	file.0000000000000001.title: "&6IsItSMP &7Questbook"
	quest.00D79A06315DF879.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Extractor&r pulls resources out of tiny block arrangements in front of it, with &ano power needed&r. Craft it from Kivi, a Port, &eAluminum Ingots&r, a &ePiston&r and &ePointed Dripstone&r."
		""
		"It reads three spots: the &btarget&r directly in front of its face, the &bcatalyst&r one block further, and the &b4 blocks around the target&r. It faces the block you click when placing it, so you place it straight onto the target; hold &bLeft Ctrl&r while placing to flip it. Items go into an inventory on its &bback&r, or wait in its own buffer. A &bredstone signal turns it off&r."
		""
		"&cThese layouts may not show up in EMI&r, so the next quest lists the useful ones. Look at the Extractor with &bJade&r to check its status."
	]
	quest.00D79A06315DF879.quest_subtitle: "Mini structures, maximum output"
	quest.00D79A06315DF879.title: "&6Rock Farmer"
	quest.00FA310EDF5F6110.quest_desc: [
		"Now for the hot stuff. &eGrout&r is the raw material for every smelting block. Combine &eSand&r, &eGravel&r and a &eClay Ball&r for &b2&r Grout."
		""
		"&aThe bulk recipe is much better:&r one &eClay Block&r with &b4 Sand&r and &b4 Gravel&r makes &b8&r Grout. A first melting setup needs &babout 34&r."
	]
	quest.00FA310EDF5F6110.quest_subtitle: "Sand, gravel, clay, repeat"
	quest.00FA310EDF5F6110.title: "&eI Am Grout"
	quest.010B9A807F2AD612.quest_desc: [
		"&eApple Juice&r counts as its own juice in the &6Fermentation Barrel&r. Pour some in and add one more &eApple Juice&r as the ingredient. No bottle is needed for this one."
		""
		"&6Apple Wine&r gives &bResistance&r. The same apple juice also makes &6Cider&r (with sugar, &bStrength&r) and &6Mead&r (with honey and sugar, &bHaste&r)."
	]
	quest.010B9A807F2AD612.quest_subtitle: "Grapes not required"
	quest.010B9A807F2AD612.title: "&aApples to Wine"
	quest.010D40929C15EDBE.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a &6Willow Fluxia Pool&r from &e5 Fluxite&r and &e1 Amethyst Shard&r. It stores &b40,000 ƒ&r and pushes &b800 ƒ/s&r to each linked target. &aLink generator → pool → altar&r, and link pools to pools to bank more."
		""
		"An empty bucket on a pool gives a &eVibrant Fluxia Bucket&r worth &b1,000 ƒ&r."
		""
		"&dPool infusion:&r throw the exact ingredients into a charged pool and they transmute. A stray extra item blocks it. The Grimoire lists every infusion."
	]
	quest.010D40929C15EDBE.quest_subtitle: "Willow Fluxia Pool"
	quest.010D40929C15EDBE.title: "&bA Basin of Current"
	quest.0122BBFBE786CBCC.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Arcane Anvil&r: &e3 Amethyst Blocks&r, a &eDiamond&r, an &eAnvil&r and &e2 Polished Deepslate&r. It does a lot:"
		""
		"&a-&r Scroll + ink matching the rarity of its next level: the scroll goes up &bone level&r."
		"&a-&r Sword, staff or certain robes + scroll: &dimbue&r it with that spell."
		"&a-&r Gear + upgrade orb: an upgrade, &bmax 3&r per item."
		"&a-&r Spell book + &eLesser Spell Slot Improvement&r (hogskin and arcane cloth): one more slot, up to &b12&r."
		"&a-&r Unique book + a higher scroll of one of its spells: that spell levels up."
		"&a-&r Anything + &eShriving Stone&r: strip upgrades and imbued spells."
	]
	quest.0122BBFBE786CBCC.quest_subtitle: "Where good gear gets great"
	quest.0122BBFBE786CBCC.title: "&dIt's Purple!"
	quest.012D19A914D19BD4.quest_desc: [
		"Sweet dough and yeast bake into proper pastries on the &6Stove&r: &eCroissants&r (sweet dough, yeast, sugar) and &eBaguettes&r (dough, sweet dough, yeast)."
		""
		"Breads give &bVitality&r, which slows how fast you get hungry."
		""
		"&7Bakery's displays and bread boxes show off your wares; four kinds of bread on a tray make a Basket of Bread on the Cutting Board.&r"
	]
	quest.012D19A914D19BD4.quest_subtitle: "Ooh la la"
	quest.012D19A914D19BD4.title: "&eFresh from the Stove"
	quest.0147199F40EF5468.quest_desc: [
		"Mix an &eEssence of Undead&r with a &eLuminous Water&r to make &eLuminous Essence&r."
		""
		"This is the &bboss key&r: one Luminous Essence summons the &cHorseman&r. It's also the &arepair material&r for the mod's three tools: the War Axe, Shatterbrand and Raubbau."
		""
		"&7Make two if you can. A spare for a rematch (or a repair) saves another tombstone run.&r"
	]
	quest.0147199F40EF5468.quest_subtitle: "Light and death, stirred together"
	quest.0147199F40EF5468.title: "&dThe Key to the Grave"
	quest.01CAB1E58580EE07.quest_desc: [
		"The &eArchevoker's Logbook&r from the fort's tower is unreadable. Some of the fort's cages hold a captive &6Wandering Trader&r who will &atranslate it&r for emeralds."
		""
		"Bring the translated logbook to a village &6Priest&r and he trades you the &eVillager Bible&r: &b10 slots&r, &b+200 mana&r, +10% holy power and +10% cast time reduction."
	]
	quest.01CAB1E58580EE07.quest_subtitle: "+10% holy power, +10% cast speed"
	quest.01CAB1E58580EE07.title: "&eLost in Translation"
	quest.01D5BDC23D4942E7.quest_desc: [
		"&6MaggoAllan&r whiskey brews from &e2 Dried Wheat&r and &eYeast&r on a copper station. Whiskey goes into a plain &eGlass Bottle&r, not a mug."
		""
		"It gives &bHealing Touch&r: your hits heal instead of hurt. &aSmack a friend to patch them up&r."
		""
		"&7Its cousins: JoJannik poisons what you hit, CristelWalker shields, Carrasconlabel regenerates, AK Reserve calls lightning and Highland Hearth pushes mobs away.&r"
	]
	quest.01D5BDC23D4942E7.quest_subtitle: "A touch of class"
	quest.01D5BDC23D4942E7.title: "&6The Spirit of the Thing"
	quest.0212DE7101DE90C2.quest_desc: [
		"Grapes become juice the old-fashioned way. Craft a &6Grapevine Pot&r from &e2 wooden slabs&r over &e3 planks&r."
		""
		"&aRight-click it with grapes&r, one per click, up to &b6 grapes of one kind&r (no mixing). Then &ajump on it &b12 times&r. Iron or better armour stomps a little faster."
		""
		"&7Change your mind before stomping? Breaking the pot gives the grapes back.&r"
	]
	quest.0212DE7101DE90C2.quest_subtitle: "Take your shoes off. Actually, don't."
	quest.0212DE7101DE90C2.title: "&6Stomping Grounds"
	quest.022E46408BE68619.quest_desc: [
		"Upgrade your Small Backpack into a &eHiking Backpack&r with &e6 Leather&r, an &eIron Ingot&r and any &eSleeping Bag&r. Your stuff comes along."
		""
		"It looks much bigger. It still holds &bexactly 24 slots&r. &7You're doing it for the look.&r"
	]
	quest.022E46408BE68619.quest_subtitle: "Bigger on the outside"
	quest.022E46408BE68619.title: "&2The Size Is a Lie"
	quest.023F8C6388B53A99.quest_desc: [
		"&dMinor Arcana&r: &8black Eclipses&r to the east and west, &8black Base glyphs&r to the north and south. &cSwapping them is the classic mistake.&r Drop &e2 Amethyst Shards&r and &e1 Block of Coal&r for &b18 Amethyst Coal&r."
		""
		"&eAmethyst Coal&r burns twice as long as coal, it's the only fuel a &eLuxinia&r accepts, and you'll need it for &eEmpyrite&r and the &6Fluxia Dynamo&r. With a stick it makes 4 &eWillow Torches&r."
	]
	quest.023F8C6388B53A99.quest_subtitle: "Minor Arcana, tier II, 300 ƒ"
	quest.023F8C6388B53A99.title: "&5Violet Embers"
	quest.02AB466094C4AC42.quest_desc: [
		"&ePhantom Glass Viewers&r are 8 glass around a &eChorus Fruit&r (8 blocks) or a &ePhantom Membrane&r (16 blocks)."
		""
		"&aPlayers, dropped items and XP orbs pass straight through&r, but every other entity bumps into it like solid glass. Build &amob-proof doorways&r, walls you can walk through, or a farm wall that lets loot out and keeps mobs in."
	]
	quest.02AB466094C4AC42.quest_subtitle: "Members only"
	quest.02AB466094C4AC42.title: "&dGhost Walls"
	quest.02AC2A751B3FF266.quest_desc: [
		"The &eRGB Lantern Lamp&r is an &eAluminum Nugget&r on top, &eglass, dye, glass&r in the middle and &eKivi, gem, Kivi&r at the bottom. The &6Stonecutter&r swaps it between lantern, cube, flush and pillar shapes."
		""
		"&aHold a dye in your off-hand while placing&r and the lamp takes that colour. The same trick colours RGB glass viewers, Aurey blocks and Soaryn Boxes."
	]
	quest.02AC2A751B3FF266.quest_subtitle: "Pick a colour, any colour"
	quest.02AC2A751B3FF266.title: "&eLamp Shade"
	quest.02CA7C0C97917332.quest_desc: [
		"You've built a machine for every colour. Celebrate with a block of each: &e9 gems&r of a colour craft into a &eXychorium Gem Storage&r block."
		""
		"They're more than a showpiece: all five, plus &eAluminum&r blocks and every &eImmortal&r block, count as &abeacon base blocks&r. A glowing rainbow pyramid is entirely allowed."
	]
	quest.02CA7C0C97917332.quest_subtitle: "Taste the rainbow (don't)"
	quest.02CA7C0C97917332.title: "&dFull Spectrum"
	quest.031D0E769EF0E2E9.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Borehead Bearing&r (wooden slab, Gearbox, Block of Industrial Iron) spins a drill head of &eRock Cutting Wheels&r (Crushing Wheel, Block of Industrial Iron, Iron Sheet), which attach without glue. The head needs &bat least one wheel and one storage block&r."
		""
		"It turns at &bquarter speed&r, reversed, and each wheel breaks blocks all around itself. Drops fill its storage; &cit stalls when full&r, so pull items from the bearing."
		""
		"&7Mount one on a car for a mobile tunnel borer.&r"
	]
	quest.031D0E769EF0E2E9.quest_subtitle: "Mole-grade mining"
	quest.031D0E769EF0E2E9.title: "&6Tunnel Vision"
	quest.03207F0DC8B9D921.quest_desc: [
		"&6Carry On&r: with an &bempty main hand&r, &asneak + right-click&r a chest, furnace or passive mob to pick it up, contents and all. Right-click to set it down. You move slower and can't attack while carrying."
		""
		"&cIt can't lift&r Sophisticated Storage, Create or Chipped blocks, Waystones, beds or doors. Use Packing Tape for Sophisticated chests."
		""
		"&7Yes, you can carry your friends.&r"
	]
	quest.03207F0DC8B9D921.quest_subtitle: "Lift with your legs"
	quest.03207F0DC8B9D921.title: "&eHeavy Lifting"
	quest.03C8FDD5EE20B842.quest_desc: [
		"Stack it up: a fuelled &6Blaze Burner&r, a &6Basin&r on top, and a &6Mechanical Mixer&r two blocks above the basin, spinning at &b30 RPM or more&r."
		""
		"Drop in &eCopper Ingots&r and &eZinc Ingots&r and each pair becomes &b2 Brass Ingots&r."
		""
		"&aBrass leads into the next Create chapter, Brass Tacks:&r brass casing, Precision Mechanisms, Deployers, Mechanical Crafters, Crushing Wheels, steam engines and trains. The Create add-ons have their own chapter too."
		""
		"&7From a hand crank to an alloy furnace. Not bad for some grey rocks.&r"
	]
	quest.03C8FDD5EE20B842.quest_subtitle: "The Andesite Age ends here"
	quest.03C8FDD5EE20B842.title: "&6Real Alloys"
	quest.0422023C88D59E8B.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Linked Typewriter&r is a flight console from the &6Mechanical Crafter&r (buttons, a Transmitter, Gold Sheets and a Precision Mechanism)."
		""
		"Right-click it and your &bmovement keys&r (plus any keys you bind) send &6Redstone Link&r frequencies. &bSneak-right-click&r opens the key setup, and right-clicking it with a &eLinked Controller&r copies that controller's frequencies."
		""
		"Wire the links to burners, gearshifts and props and fly from one seat."
	]
	quest.0422023C88D59E8B.quest_subtitle: "WASD, but for airships"
	quest.0422023C88D59E8B.title: "&6Fly-by-Wire"
	quest.042451A5C3998BFC.quest_desc: [
		"&6Iron Furnaces&r adds faster furnace tiers. The first one is cheap: eight &eCopper Ingots&r around a vanilla &6Furnace&r make a &6Copper Furnace&r (9 seconds per item instead of 10). The &6Iron Furnace&r is faster still."
		""
		"Already placed a furnace? An &eupgrade kit&r swaps it for the next tier without breaking it: &bsneak and right-click&r it with the kit. A vanilla furnace pops its contents out first, so grab them."
		""
		"&7Higher tiers and augments wait in &6Kitted Out&7.&r"
	]
	quest.042451A5C3998BFC.quest_subtitle: "Copper finally has a job"
	quest.042451A5C3998BFC.title: "&6Hotter Stuff"
	quest.044B7F0C253495E4.quest_desc: [
		"Craft &e4 Dried Green Tea&r and &e4 Dried Black Tea&r into a &6Mixed Tea Leaf Block&r and place it to dry. It becomes an &6Oolong Tea Leaf Block&r, which breaks into &e3 Dried Oolong Tea&r."
		""
		"&cLet it finish:&r breaking a Mixed block early gives back only half of what went in, either 4 plain Green Tea Leaves or 4 Dried Black Tea."
	]
	quest.044B7F0C253495E4.quest_subtitle: "Half green, half black"
	quest.044B7F0C253495E4.title: "&2Best of Both Leaves"
	quest.0495779EF48D631F.quest_desc: [
		"The &ePocket Generator&r is a generator you carry. Right-click it, add fuel, and it charges the FE items in your inventory, &aCurios slots included&r."
		""
		"The &eFuel Canister&r stores a mountain of burn time. In a furnace it spends only &b200 ticks&r per smelt, so no half-burnt coal is wasted, and it fuels the Coal Generator and Pocket Generator too. Right-click it to open, then shift-click fuel in. &cIt's one-way: items never come back out.&r"
	]
	quest.0495779EF48D631F.quest_subtitle: "Charging on the go"
	quest.0495779EF48D631F.title: "&ePower in Your Pocket"
	quest.04A8DBDC49EA5E61.quest_desc: [
		"The red machine. The &6Ignition Plate&r takes &e4 Red gems&r, Kivi, iron bars, &eNetherrack&r and a &6Machine Base&r, so you'll need a quick trip to the Nether."
		""
		"It faces away from the block you place it on. Give it a &bredstone signal&r and it lights a fire in front of that face (or lights a campfire or candle sitting there); cut the signal and the fire goes out. &aGreat for switchable fireplaces and mob traps.&r"
	]
	quest.04A8DBDC49EA5E61.quest_subtitle: "Some like it hot"
	quest.04A8DBDC49EA5E61.title: "&cFire on Demand"
	quest.04AF09A915B50574.quest_desc: [
		"&eRennet&r is what turns milk into cheese. Cook an &eEgg&r, &eAlpine Salt&r and a &eGlass Bottle&r in your Cooking Frame for &b2 Rennet&r."
		""
		"You need &b1 Rennet per cheese wheel&r, so make a few batches."
		""
		"&7A Cheesemaker villager (job block: Pine Cheese Rack) trades it too.&r"
	]
	quest.04AF09A915B50574.quest_subtitle: "Every cheesemaker has one"
	quest.04AF09A915B50574.title: "&eThe Secret Ingredient"
	quest.04DD532D35401B70.quest_desc: [
		"Feed a &eCake o' Enchanting&r to a Blaze Enchanter or Forger and it starts seething: &dSuper Enchanting&r. Compact an Egg, Sugar and Lapis into a Cake Base, then Spout &b1,000 mB&r of Liquid XP onto it. Press a Block of Super Experience for a &eSuper Enchanting Template&r."
		""
		"A seething Enchanter goes up to level &b60&r, rolls &dtreasure&r enchantments and goes one level past the normal cap. A seething Forger merges past the cap and even combines enchantments that normally conflict."
		""
		"&cSuper jobs call down lightning. Put a Lightning Rod nearby, or an open-sky machine can be destroyed. Roofed over, there is no strike, but you risk curses and higher repair costs.&r"
	]
	quest.04DD532D35401B70.quest_subtitle: "Rules were made to be broken"
	quest.04DD532D35401B70.title: "&dSeething Ambition"
	quest.04E995BAC0B8CE2A.quest_desc: [
		"The &eSmall Backpack&r (4 leather, 2 string, 1 white wool) holds &b24 slots&r. Wear it in the &bCurios back slot&r and press &bB&r to open it on the go."
		""
		"You can also place it on the ground: right-click to open, &asneak-right-click to pick it up with everything inside&r. Backpacks and shulker boxes can't go in."
		""
		"&7Other looks: the woolly Sheepbag, or the Wanderer Backpack that some Wandering Traders sell.&r"
	]
	quest.04E995BAC0B8CE2A.quest_subtitle: "Tiny packs"
	quest.04E995BAC0B8CE2A.title: "&2Pack Light"
	quest.04EC097FBB76DEEA.quest_desc: [
		"A single adult villager with &b15+ hearts&r may offer &dA Courtship&r, a four-part chain: a first gift of flowers, an evening stroll, a cake for their family, and finally a proposal paid for in gold."
		""
		"The cake step needs a relative of theirs living in the same village. Every step pays out plenty of hearts, so it is the perfect run-up to the rings. Once you are married, your spouse and children have their own quests too."
	]
	quest.04EC097FBB76DEEA.quest_subtitle: "Old-fashioned romance"
	quest.04EC097FBB76DEEA.title: "&dA Proper Courtship"
	quest.055857634ED56B07.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Winemaker&r outfit: a &eStraw Hat&r (red wool and wheat), an &eApron&r (red wool), &eLeggings&r (wool, leather and a gold ingot) and &eBoots&r (brown wool and rabbit hide)."
		""
		"&aWearing all four, Bone Meal isn't used up.&r That's a huge boost for a grape farm, or any farm really."
	]
	quest.055857634ED56B07.quest_subtitle: "Straw hat mandatory"
	quest.055857634ED56B07.title: "&eDressed for the Harvest"
	quest.0564EFA018715523.quest_desc: [
		"Four &6Let's Do&r nature mods live in this chapter:"
		"&6Meadow&r turns the mountain &bMeadow&r biome into alpine dairy country: woolly cattle, cheese and fondue."
		"&6Alpine Whispers&r dresses up &bGroves&r and &bSnowy Plains&r with Arolla Pines, Alpine Sheep and Reindeer."
		"&6Blooming Nature&r adds &b16 new biomes&r, 10 kinds of wood and a lot of flowers."
		"&6Wilder Nature&r fills the wild with animals and a &6Bounty Board&r full of hunting contracts."
		""
		"There is no guide book (Wilder Nature's Field Guide only covers animals). Recipes, including the Cookpot and Cheese Press, are in &bEMI&r. The few tricks EMI can't show (felting, truffling) are explained in these quests."
		""
		"&7The cheese line down the middle is the main road. The other three mods branch off on their own.&r"
	]
	quest.0564EFA018715523.quest_subtitle: "Four mods, one great outdoors"
	quest.0564EFA018715523.title: "&2Highlands and Wildlands"
	quest.0570C390EDD7841A.quest_desc: [
		"The &ePower Glove&r adds &b+4 melee damage&r to every hit. It's one of the best early combat artifacts, and you have &btwo&r hand slots."
		""
		"Check pillager outposts, ruined portals, big ocean ruins and some stronghold chests."
		""
		"&7Other hand picks: &eVampiric Glove&7 (heal on hit), &eFeral Claws&7 (attack speed), &eDigging Claws&7 (mine faster, even bare-handed).&r"
	]
	quest.0570C390EDD7841A.quest_subtitle: "Hands slot, +4 damage"
	quest.0570C390EDD7841A.title: "&cPack a Punch"
	quest.05967410619DBE02.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Shiraz Palace&r is the jewel of the &bdesert&r, and only about one desert find in ten is a palace. Take a &eLighthouse map&r or a &eWoodland Explorer Map&r rather than wandering."
		""
		"&cThis is one of the deadliest places in the mod.&r Its spawners hold husks in &cnetherite armour&r (some with netherite swords), Wither Skeleton archers, pillagers and cave spiders. Full enchanted diamond, Healing potions and a Totem are not overkill."
		""
		"The &eelite chests&r hold netherite helmets and boots, &enetherite ingots&r and handfuls of diamonds."
	]
	quest.05967410619DBE02.quest_subtitle: "The richest house in the desert"
	quest.05967410619DBE02.title: "&6Sultan of Sand"
	quest.05B301E4A9729BDB.quest_desc: [
		"This world has been &arenovated&r. &6YUNG's&r mods rebuild the classic dungeons, temples, mineshafts and fortresses, &6IDAS&r scatters dozens of hand-built structures around, and &6Integrated Villages&r replaces every vanilla village."
		""
		"To find things, search for the right biome with a &eNature's Compass&r, drop a waypoint on every find and activate each Waystone you pass. &6First Light&r and &6Kitted Out&r cover all three."
		""
		"Structure quests tick when you &awalk inside&r the building, not when you stand on top of it. Every loot chest is per-player (Lootr, from Kitted Out), so nobody steals your loot."
		""
		"&7Rivers now have YUNG's Bridges (some of them broken), so follow the water. The advancement screen (L) has tabs for IDAS, Integrated Villages, Better Dungeons and Cave Biomes. They make handy checklists. The giant &6When Dungeons Arise&7 builds and its pirate ships have a chapter of their own, &6Rise and Plunder&7.&r"
	]
	quest.05B301E4A9729BDB.quest_subtitle: "Here be dragons. Literally, at the end."
	quest.05B301E4A9729BDB.title: "&6Into the Unknown"
	quest.05EC882E421CA367.quest_desc: [
		"Normal propeller bearings make wobbly helicopters. The &6Gyroscopic Propeller Bearing&r &atries to keep its propeller upright&r; a redstone signal resets the tilt to zero. Facing down, it steadies top-heavy builds."
		""
		"It needs a &eGyroscopic Mechanism&r: a sequenced assembly on an Iron Sheet deploying a &eCogwheel&r, &eShaft&r and &eBrass Nugget&r. The same part makes &6Smart Propellers&r and the &6Gimbal Sensor&r."
	]
	quest.05EC882E421CA367.quest_subtitle: "Keeping your head up"
	quest.05EC882E421CA367.title: "&eWhirlybird"
	quest.05EF1CD0C3EEED3C.quest_desc: [
		"&6Haley Beer&r brews from &eHops&r, &eYeast&r and &ePopped Chorus Fruit&r (smelt chorus fruit from the End). Any station can brew it."
		""
		"Its effect lets you &afly freely&r while it lasts. Keep one in your pocket for building high, and age a few in a Big Barrel so the buzz lasts longer."
	]
	quest.05EF1CD0C3EEED3C.quest_subtitle: "One more round and I'm airborne"
	quest.05EF1CD0C3EEED3C.title: "&dFlying High"
	quest.06192B77A0D1ECA5.quest_desc: [
		"Mine some &ecobblestone&r and upgrade to a &6Stone Pickaxe&r. Eight cobblestone in a ring make a &6Furnace&r."
		""
		"No coal yet? &aSmelt a log&r into &echarcoal&r: it burns just as well and makes &etorches&r with a stick."
	]
	quest.06192B77A0D1ECA5.quest_subtitle: "Rock solid progress"
	quest.06192B77A0D1ECA5.title: "Stone Age"
	quest.0624AAC756CF2184.quest_desc: [
		"Once the &5Ender Dragon&r has fallen, craft &eObsidian&r, &eDragon's Breath&r and &eGunpowder&r into a &6Dragon Charge&r."
		""
		"Throw it and it bursts into a cloud of &cInstant Damage&r that keeps spreading until it is &b6.5 blocks&r in radius. Superb against crowds."
		""
		"&cThe cloud doesn't care whose side you're on. Throw it far.&r"
	]
	quest.0624AAC756CF2184.quest_subtitle: "Bottled breath, now throwable"
	quest.0624AAC756CF2184.title: "&5Bad Breath"
	quest.0632B9084F4C0227.quest_desc: [
		"Wine &aages in the bottle&r. Every &b24 in-game days&r is one wine year: each year adds &b10 seconds&r to its effect, and every &b6 years&r adds &ba whole effect level&r, up to &b+5&r."
		""
		"Bottles age anywhere, but in storage with &bno sky light&r (underground or fully roofed) they age &b1.5x faster&r. That's your excuse for a proper cellar."
		""
		"Store bottles in &6wine racks&r (small, mid and big, in every wood) or a &6Wine Box&r. &bShift + right-click&r opens and closes the box. The tooltip shows how many days are left until the next level."
		""
		"&7This is a long game measured in days of world time. Stock the cellar and forget about it.&r"
	]
	quest.0632B9084F4C0227.quest_subtitle: "Good things come to those who wait. A long time."
	quest.0632B9084F4C0227.title: "&5Aged to Perfection"
	quest.068DB273AE3A5664.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Fermentation Barrel&r is a &eBarrel&r on top of &e2 Sticks&r. Its screen has a &bjuice slot&r, &b3 ingredient slots&r, a &bbottle slot&r and the output."
		""
		"Each juice you pour in adds &b25%&r, up to &b100%&r. The barrel holds &cone juice type at a time&r, so brew it empty before switching to another grape."
		""
		"&7Villagers can take the barrel as a workstation and become &6Winemakers&r, who trade seeds, wine bottles, fruit bags and, at master level, a bottle of Miss Lilitu's Wine.&r"
	]
	quest.068DB273AE3A5664.quest_subtitle: "Where juice grows up"
	quest.068DB273AE3A5664.title: "&6The Magic of the Barrel"
	quest.06E168FA4BC4E782.quest_desc: [
		"Three &eplanks&r over two &esticks&r make a &6Wooden Pickaxe&r. It's flimsy, but it mines &7stone&r, and stone is the way out of the wooden age."
		""
		"&7Not sure of a shape? Hover the pickaxe in EMI and press R.&r"
	]
	quest.06E168FA4BC4E782.title: "Pick Me"
	quest.07453C3EA167CE5C.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Soaryn Box&r, named after XyCraft's author, is a small storage box: &e4 gems&r of any colour, &e2 Kivi&r and &e2 Item Ports&r make two."
		""
		"&aHold a dye in your off-hand when placing&r to colour it, which makes colour-coded storage easy. Breaking the box spills its contents on the ground, so &cempty it before you move it&r."
	]
	quest.07453C3EA167CE5C.quest_subtitle: "It's not random if you put it there"
	quest.07453C3EA167CE5C.title: "&eBoxing Clever"
	quest.07861D6B36197D41.quest_desc: [
		"&eLevitite Blend&r is &6heated mixing&r (Mixer over a Basin on a lit &6Blaze Burner&r): &b4&r End Stone Powder, &b2&r Zinc Nuggets and &b500 mB&r of Water make 500 mB of blend."
		""
		"Fill buckets with a &6Spout&r or straight from a Fluid Tank. Don't light it yet!"
	]
	quest.07861D6B36197D41.quest_subtitle: "Shake well before flying"
	quest.07861D6B36197D41.title: "&eLiquid Lift"
	quest.079BC9AC2BB20DCF.quest_desc: [
		"&eBrass Casing&r, an &eElectron Tube&r and a &eComparator&r make a &6Threshold Switch&r. Put it on a container or tank: when the contents pass the &bupper threshold&r its redstone output flips, and it stays that way until they drop to the &blower threshold&r. Perfect for switching a farm off when the chest is full."
		""
		"Swap the Comparator for an &eObserver&r and you get a &6Smart Observer&r, which reacts to filtered items or fluids in a container, belt, chute or pipe."
	]
	quest.079BC9AC2BB20DCF.quest_subtitle: "Full? Empty? It knows."
	quest.079BC9AC2BB20DCF.title: "&eKeeping Watch"
	quest.07B289256CB68062.quest_desc: [
		"Three handy sensors:"
		"&a- &6Hourglass&r (gold and glass): fill it with sand, sugar, redstone and more; each falls at its own speed, and a &bcomparator&r reads the time left. A Turn Table flips it to reset."
		"&a- &6Clock Block&r (planks and a clock): shows the time, and a comparator reads it across the day."
		"&a- &6Wind Vane&r (iron, iron bars, redstone): outputs &b1 in rain and 2 in a thunderstorm&r."
		""
		"&7Right-click with a plain vanilla Clock to read the exact time.&r"
	]
	quest.07B289256CB68062.quest_subtitle: "Tick, tock, drizzle"
	quest.07B289256CB68062.title: "&eClockwork Curios"
	quest.07C011CDCF143A83.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Modifier Worktable&r is &e3 seared blocks&r over &e4 natural stone&r. Granite, deepslate, tuff and even Create's stones all count."
		""
		"Use a &eWet Sponge&r in it to &aremove a modifier&r. You lose the materials but get the slot back. Add a matching &eslime crystal&r with the sponge and the modifier is saved into the crystal, ready for another tool."
	]
	quest.07C011CDCF143A83.quest_subtitle: "Undo button for modifiers"
	quest.07C011CDCF143A83.title: "&eClean Slate"
	quest.0814271DA54512D4.quest_desc: [
		"Once you are married with &b100+ hearts&r, open &bTalk&r with your spouse and choose &aProcreate&r. After a little dance you are holding a &eBaby Boy&r or &eBaby Girl&r (there is a &b5%&r chance of twins). The next baby can come &b3 days&r later."
		""
		"Keep the baby in your inventory (or a crib) for &b20 minutes&r until its tooltip says &a\"Ready to grow!\"&r. Then &aright-click&r to name it and place it on the ground. Your child starts at &b100 hearts&r with you."
		""
		"&cYou cannot drop a baby.&r &7Do not try. And if your spouse says they can't have children, they have the Infertile trait; no amount of hearts changes that.&r"
	]
	quest.0814271DA54512D4.quest_subtitle: "Some assembly required"
	quest.0814271DA54512D4.title: "&dNext Generation"
	quest.08537F3F1AFE9A9C.quest_desc: [
		"&eSeashells&r lie on beach sand. Break one to pick it up, then &aright-click it in the air to open it&r. Most hold &eRaw Mussel Meat&r (cook it for a snack), but some have gold, an emerald or, very rarely, a diamond."
		""
		"Hang around a beach and a &eMessage in a Bottle&r washes up on the sand every few minutes (at most two at once). Open it for paper, a blank map or, &bone time in five&r, an &aexplorer map&r, for example to buried treasure."
	]
	quest.08537F3F1AFE9A9C.quest_subtitle: "By the seashore, obviously"
	quest.08537F3F1AFE9A9C.title: "&bShe Sells Seashells"
	quest.08587D56FBC92206.quest_desc: [
		"After you beat the &5Ender Dragon&r, set the &eDragon Egg&r right on top of an &6Extractor&r that &bfaces up&r (this one only works pointing upwards). With nothing else needed, it &aslowly copies the egg&r into its output."
		""
		"A &eDragon Head&r in front of one makes &eDragon's Breath&r instead, so you don't have to chase the dragon with bottles."
		""
		"&7The egg only appears the first time the dragon dies, so this is how the rest of the server gets one.&r"
	]
	quest.08587D56FBC92206.quest_subtitle: "Mum will never notice"
	quest.08587D56FBC92206.title: "&5Egg-straction"
	quest.087456548ACAC972.quest_desc: [
		"The &eWayward Compass&r (&e4 Arcane Essence&r, &e4 Iron Ingots&r and a &eSoul Lantern&r) points to the nearest &6Catacombs&r, deep underground. &aRight-click&r it to search again."
		""
		"The Catacombs are full of trial spawners and undead, with &cthe Dead King&r waiting on his throne. Bring good armor, food and a full mana bar."
	]
	quest.087456548ACAC972.quest_subtitle: "It points down"
	quest.087456548ACAC972.title: "&eAnd So a Quest Begins"
	quest.087517D95DDC3410.quest_desc: [
		"&6Bastion Remnants&r are the vanilla piglin strongholds, still here and still dangerous: watch out for &cPiglin Brutes&r, and &awear some gold&r so regular piglins leave you alone."
		""
		"The treasure chest always has a &eNetherite Upgrade&r smithing template, and with Lootr &aevery player gets their own&r."
	]
	quest.087517D95DDC3410.quest_subtitle: "Piglins really let the place go"
	quest.087517D95DDC3410.title: "&6Those Were the Days"
	quest.0888A25B76671F89.quest_desc: [
		"Once a relic hits its &bmax level&r, the Relic tab offers &6Rank Up&r. It &cresets&r the relic's levels, abilities and points, but every rank lets abilities go higher and unlocks &drank modifiers&r, extra effects that usually arrive at ranks &b1, 3 and 5&r."
		""
		"Most relics go to rank &b5&r. The &eCut Glass Boot&r and the &eRing of Sins&r can't rank up at all."
		""
		"&7This is where the Experience Disperser earns its keep.&r"
	]
	quest.0888A25B76671F89.quest_subtitle: "Start over, but stronger"
	quest.0888A25B76671F89.title: "&6Prestige Worldwide"
	quest.08E0293D04483779.quest_desc: [
		"The &eCloud in a Bottle&r gives you a &adouble jump&r: press jump again in mid-air. The second jump wipes out the fall you had built up so far, and you get &b3&r extra blocks of safe fall distance on top."
		""
		"Look in mineshaft minecarts, pillager outposts, big ocean ruins and End cities."
		""
		"&7It takes your only belt slot. Pair it with &eBunny Hoppers&7 on your feet for silly heights.&r"
	]
	quest.08E0293D04483779.quest_subtitle: "Belt slot, double jump"
	quest.08E0293D04483779.title: "&bCloud Nine"
	quest.0906F2FF2EF765CB.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Mounted Potato Cannon&r comes from the &6Mechanical Crafter&r (Copper Sheets, Redstone, a Dried Kelp Block, a Cogwheel and Fluid Pipes). It takes the same ammo as the hand-held Potato Cannon."
		""
		"&bRotation charges it&r, a &bredstone signal fires&r, and holding the signal autofires. Load it by automation. &cRecoil pushes your ship&r."
		""
		"&7Phantoms make excellent target practice.&r"
	]
	quest.0906F2FF2EF765CB.quest_subtitle: "Spud-based air superiority"
	quest.0906F2FF2EF765CB.title: "&cBroadside"
	quest.09143D1D256DF71E.quest_desc: [
		"&cElder Guardians&r curse everyone nearby with &cMining Fatigue III&r, so you can't dig through the monument. &aDrink milk&r to clear it for a while, then hunt them down through the chambers."
		""
		"They drop wet sponges, prismarine and sometimes the &eTide&r armour trim. In this pack, one kind of Elder Guardian carries a &eHeart of the Sea&r and always drops it."
		""
		"&7Water Breathing and a good sword make this far less soggy.&r"
	]
	quest.09143D1D256DF71E.quest_subtitle: "Then defeat them"
	quest.09143D1D256DF71E.title: "&3Respect Your Elders"
	quest.0920550F2B95518B.quest_desc: [
		"&eZinc Ore&r generates in the Overworld from &bY -63 to 70&r, in stone and deepslate. It needs an &biron pickaxe&r and drops &eRaw Zinc&r; smelt it (or blast it in a lava fan) into &eZinc Ingots&r."
		""
		"&eZinc Nuggets&r work in place of Iron Nuggets in Andesite Alloy and Chain Drives."
	]
	quest.0920550F2B95518B.quest_subtitle: "Half of brass"
	quest.0920550F2B95518B.title: "&7Zinc About It"
	quest.092C59764CC7CEA9.quest_desc: [
		"&6Bolvar Wine&r ferments from &eRed Taiga Grapejuice&r with a &eHoney Bottle&r and a &eCherry&r, no bottle needed. It gives &bLava Walker&r: stroll across lava like it's a footpath."
		""
		"&7Other regional wines worth a try: &eKelp Cider&r (white savanna juice and kelp) lets you walk on water, and &eClark Wine&r (white jungle juice and sugar) gives you a double jump.&r"
	]
	quest.092C59764CC7CEA9.quest_subtitle: "The floor is lava. You don't mind."
	quest.092C59764CC7CEA9.title: "&cHot Footing It"
	quest.093BEF2B8F8A49DB.quest_desc: [
		"The &eFishing Net&r (sticks and string) scoops up floating things whole. Get within about &b1 block&r of one (a boat helps), look at it and &bhold right-click for 5 seconds&r. It works most of the time."
		""
		"&aRight-click again to empty the net.&r You get the catch plus a bonus roll: fish, emeralds, prismarine and sometimes a &eSoaked Bag&r (right-click to open) or even a &eHeart of the Sea&r."
	]
	quest.093BEF2B8F8A49DB.quest_subtitle: "Bagged and waterlogged"
	quest.093BEF2B8F8A49DB.title: "&9Net Gains"
	quest.096A3158A2DECEEA.quest_desc: [
		"The &eDiamond Lance&r (&e3 Diamonds&r) hits hardest of all at &b6.5&r, with huge knockback. It's also the heaviest, so its charge is the shortest: about &b2 seconds&r."
		""
		"&7Prefer a long gallop? The &eEmerald Lance&7 is the lightest, with a charge of about 6 seconds and plenty of durability, but it only hits for 4.&r"
	]
	quest.096A3158A2DECEEA.quest_subtitle: "Weight: yes"
	quest.096A3158A2DECEEA.title: "&bHeavy Hitter"
	quest.098615D02F726F95.quest_desc: [
		"Deep underground (&bY -60 to 40&r) you'll stumble on abandoned &6campsites&r: a plank floor, a bed, a campfire, workstations, barrels and a chest. &cAbout one in three of them has a Mimic instead of the chest.&r With Quark around, it can even look like a spruce or birch chest."
		""
		"A &6Mimic&r has &b60 health&r and bites hard, but stays asleep until you get close. Arrows bounce off it while it sits on the ground, so &afight it in melee&r. It always drops &aone random artifact&r."
		""
		"&7Real campsite chests have a smaller artifact chance, plus tools and ores.&r"
	]
	quest.098615D02F726F95.quest_subtitle: "Never trust furniture with teeth"
	quest.098615D02F726F95.title: "&cIt Was a Chest Last Time"
	quest.09989CF628D8C660.quest_desc: [
		"The &eMatchmaker's Ring&r is &e8 Iron Ingots&r in a ring, and you need &btwo&r of them in your hand to arrange a match: one is used up."
		""
		"Give it to an unmarried adult, such as your grown child, and they marry the nearest single villager within &b5 blocks&r who isn't a relative."
		""
		"&7Bring the lucky candidate along first. Nobody likes a long-distance arranged marriage.&r"
	]
	quest.09989CF628D8C660.quest_subtitle: "Make me a match"
	quest.09989CF628D8C660.title: "&dMatchmaker, Matchmaker"
	quest.09C99AFC1F16177E.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Radio&r plays Beachparty's own songs. It is a &eNote Block&r, an &eOvergrown Disc&r and another &eNote Block&r in a row."
		""
		"&cThe disc can't be crafted&r and it is rare. Each &bwoodland mansion&r chest has about a 1 in 6 chance; shipwreck, buried treasure and underwater ruin chests have a small one. Those ocean chests can even hold a finished &6Radio&r. &7The Sandy Merchant villager may sell both too.&r"
		""
		"&aRight-click&r the radio to switch it on and again to change station. &bSneak-right-click&r turns it off."
	]
	quest.09C99AFC1F16177E.quest_subtitle: "Now that's what I call ancient"
	quest.09C99AFC1F16177E.title: "&6Beach Beats"
	quest.09F681A96D53A386.quest_desc: [
		"The &eSpear&r (iron ingot, iron nugget, sticks) is a budget trident: hold right-click and release to throw it."
		""
		"&eDynamite&r comes from gunpowder, paper and string, or &e1 TNT makes 3&r. Right-click to throw. &aIn water it makes a big blast that breaks no blocks&r, which is classic dynamite fishing. &cOn land it is smaller but does break blocks.&r"
		""
		"Both also turn up in floating debris."
	]
	quest.09F681A96D53A386.quest_subtitle: "Fishing, the loud way"
	quest.09F681A96D53A386.title: "&cHarpoons and Boom Sticks"
	quest.0A18FC899F83CEF4.quest_desc: [
		"The &eEverlasting Beef&r is food that is &anever used up&r: eat it and it just goes on a &b15 s&r cooldown. Cows and mooshrooms you kill yourself have a &btiny&r chance to drop it, and it is a rare pick from Mimics and bastion hoglin stables too."
		""
		"&aCook it&r in a furnace, smoker or campfire for the &eEternal Steak&r: the same trick, better food. A cow that dies while on fire drops it ready-cooked."
		""
		"&7Pure luck, so don't farm for it. It turns up when it turns up.&r"
	]
	quest.0A18FC899F83CEF4.quest_subtitle: "The last meal you'll ever need"
	quest.0A18FC899F83CEF4.title: "&6Steak Out"
	quest.0A19A1686682CDF0.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Illager Fort&r is a stone stronghold in &bsnowy taigas, snowy plains, snowy slopes and taigas&r. Follow a map from a campsite, or search the cold forests."
		""
		"&cInside wait Evokers&r (fangs and vexes, and a &eTotem of Undying&r each when they die) and &cIllusioners&r, plus pillagers, vindicators and cave spider spawners. Bring a shield and plenty of food."
		""
		"The treasure chests are worth it: enchanted &ediamond armour&r, diamonds, Woodland Mansion loot and a pile of &eBottles o' Enchanting&r."
	]
	quest.0A19A1686682CDF0.quest_subtitle: "The illagers' winter palace"
	quest.0A19A1686682CDF0.title: "&cStorm the Fort"
	quest.0A31634E17777913.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Glimmering Weald&r is a rare, glowing biome &bbelow Y=0&r, full of &eGlow Shrooms&r, glowing lichen and extra Stonelings."
		""
		"Glow Shrooms can only be planted on deepslate; bone meal one to grow a huge mushroom. Hold one and nearby Stonelings &acome to you&r instead of running."
	]
	quest.0A31634E17777913.quest_subtitle: "Mushrooms with a night light"
	quest.0A31634E17777913.title: "&3Glow Up"
	quest.0A3B2C3531C77CEB.quest_desc: [
		"Every &b5 minutes&r something may spawn on water within about &b100 blocks&r of a player. It floats for &b8 minutes&r and breaks after &b3 loots&r."
		"&eDebris&r: planks, ingots, Dynamite, a Spear, rarely a Trident or diamond."
		"&eBooks&r: paper, feathers, enchanted books."
		"&eFish Pools&r: cod and salmon in rivers, tropical fish and pufferfish in oceans."
		""
		"&aCast any fishing rod so the bobber lands on it, then reel in.&r A &eSpyglass&r helps you spot them."
	]
	quest.0A3B2C3531C77CEB.quest_subtitle: "Debris in sight!"
	quest.0A3B2C3531C77CEB.title: "&9Flotsam and Jetsam"
	quest.0A775AD95E6D4CCC.quest_desc: [
		"&6Mix&r &b4&r &eSaplings&r, &eSugar Cane&r or &eBamboo&r with &b250 mB of Water&r in a Basin (no heat needed) for &ePulp&r, then &6press&r it into &eCardboard&r. Four Cardboard make a &eBlock of Cardboard&r."
		""
		"Cardboard starts Create's &6package logistics&r: boxing items up and posting them around your base, or across the whole server."
		""
		"&7There's cardboard armour too. Wear the full set and sneak to hide in plain sight.&r"
	]
	quest.0A775AD95E6D4CCC.quest_subtitle: "Recycling, Create-style"
	quest.0A775AD95E6D4CCC.title: "&ePulp Fiction"
	quest.0AB8D39A75C494F2.quest_desc: [
		"&6Xaero's Minimap&r sits in the corner from your first second. &bY&r opens its settings, &bB&r makes a new waypoint, &bU&r lists your waypoints and &bZ&r enlarges the map."
		""
		"&6Xaero's World Map&r opens with &bM&r and fills in as you explore. When you die, a &cdeathpoint&r waypoint appears on its own."
		""
		"&7M is shared with the FTB Chunks map, so use the sidebar buttons for claiming.&r"
	]
	quest.0AB8D39A75C494F2.quest_subtitle: "Never lose your base again"
	quest.0AB8D39A75C494F2.title: "&bYou Are Here"
	quest.0AEF39213CD751BD.quest_desc: [
		"&6Oretoises&r are slow, common turtles below Y=0 with ore on their backs: coal, copper, iron, lapis or redstone. &aMine them with a pickaxe&r to get the ore."
		""
		"&cNever punch one.&r Hitting it with anything but a pickaxe sends out a shockwave that hurts everything nearby, you included."
		""
		"Feed it &eGlow Berries&r and it may regrow its ore after a minute. &6Jade&r shows the cooldown."
	]
	quest.0AEF39213CD751BD.quest_subtitle: "Slow, steady and full of ore"
	quest.0AEF39213CD751BD.title: "&2Mine Turtle!"
	quest.0AF286F2B0963C7B.quest_desc: [
		"Everything meets here: &6Pinnacle&r lifts your cap to 100, and the &6Draconic Endshelf&r lets the table reach it. &aEnchant an item at level 100.&r"
		""
		"You've ridden the tiers from Haven to Pinnacle, rebuilt your gear from scrap, and stacked shelves from the Nether, the deep dark and the End. Few players get here."
		""
		"&7Still hungry? Two God-Fused Pearls and a Perfect Gem of the Royal Family go into the &6Enchanting Table of the Raven&r&7, which lets you set every stat by hand.&r"
	]
	quest.0AF286F2B0963C7B.quest_subtitle: "Enchant at level 100"
	quest.0AF286F2B0963C7B.title: "&6Apotheosis"
	quest.0AFE90532EEDB6D2.quest_desc: [
		"&6Apothic Spawners&r makes spawners portable: mine one with a &eSilk Touch&r tool and it keeps its mob. It costs &b100 durability&r. Hold &bShift&r over the item to see its stats."
		""
		"&cThe old upgrades with sugar, clocks or ghast tears are disabled in this pack.&r Spawners are upgraded with &dSpawner Runes&r instead."
		""
		"&7The &dCapturing&r&7 sword enchantment gives mobs a 0.5% chance per level to drop their spawn egg. Use one on a spawner to change its mob.&r"
	]
	quest.0AFE90532EEDB6D2.quest_subtitle: "Apothic Spawners"
	quest.0AFE90532EEDB6D2.title: "&7Spawner Snatcher"
	quest.0B132104F1EBC25F.quest_desc: [
		"&6Arcane Goggles&r: &e1 Astralite Ingot&r, &e2 Astralite Nuggets&r, &e2 Glass&r and &e1 Amethyst Shard&r. Wear them or hold them in either hand."
		""
		"Every Fluxia device within &b24 blocks&r shows a gauge and links appear as violet threads. Look at your altar to read its &btier, rune count, the rite it recognises, the cost and what's missing&r."
		""
		"&7When the Grimoire and the goggles disagree, trust the goggles.&r"
	]
	quest.0B132104F1EBC25F.quest_subtitle: "The goggles never lie"
	quest.0B132104F1EBC25F.title: "&bSeeing the Current"
	quest.0B32E4955ADEDD36.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Gem Cutting Table&r raises a gem one purity. Put in &btwo gems of the same type and purity&r, plus Gem Dust and a rarity material."
		""
		"Costs climb fast: Cracked to Chipped is 1 dust and 3 Scrap Metal; Normal to Flawless is 7 dust and 9 Luminous Shards (or 1 Godforged Pearl); Flawless to Perfect is 9 dust and 3 Pearls."
		""
		"&7Later, a &6Gem Case&r&7 (Ender Chest, Basalt, Glass and this table) stores thousands of gems and can cut them in place.&r"
	]
	quest.0B32E4955ADEDD36.quest_subtitle: "Gem Cutting"
	quest.0B32E4955ADEDD36.title: "&bA Cut Above"
	quest.0B47AA7FBE692900.quest_desc: [
		"&6Better Witch Huts&r rebuilds the swamp hut in three new styles (small, large and double). They appear in &bswamps and mangrove swamps&r, with a witch and her &eblack cat&r at home."
		""
		"Inside: potions, splash potions and odd brewing ingredients. &7Swamps also hide the rarer &6Witch Circle&7, and &6YUNG's Extras&7 scatters stone-brick arches through the same marshes.&r"
	]
	quest.0B47AA7FBE692900.quest_subtitle: "Wipe your feet. And check for cats."
	quest.0B47AA7FBE692900.title: "&5Hex Marks the Spot"
	quest.0B60B5D24BF7EB4A.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Mechanical Bearing&r (Wooden Slab, Andesite Casing, Shaft) rotates the glued structure in front of it. The moment it &breceives rotation&r it assembles that structure into a spinning contraption; when it stops, the blocks are placed back at the nearest grid angle."
		""
		"Other movement anchors work the same way: the &6Gantry Carriage&r slides along gantry shafts, the &6Rope Pulley&r lowers blocks, and the &6Cart Assembler&r puts builds on minecarts. Ponder shows each one."
	]
	quest.0B60B5D24BF7EB4A.quest_subtitle: "The world, on a turntable"
	quest.0B60B5D24BF7EB4A.title: "&eRound and Round"
	quest.0B9B39BD4A620C0C.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Victory Frigate&r is the largest Seven Seas ship and the hardest, with &bmore than twenty spawners&r: zombies with &cdiamond axes and swords&r, vindicators with Sharpness axes, archers, and &cpillagers in diamond chestplates with Multishot crossbows&r."
		""
		"Clear it deck by deck and break each spawner as you go. The reward is &b7 treasure chests&r with enchanted &ediamond armour&r, high-level books, diamonds and emeralds, and dozens of supply barrels."
	]
	quest.0B9B39BD4A620C0C.quest_subtitle: "The biggest gun on the water"
	quest.0B9B39BD4A620C0C.title: "&9Ship of the Line"
	quest.0BC92E394FCE51C6.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Source Relay&r (6 Gold Ingots + a Source Gem Block) moves Source up to &b30 blocks&r. Link it to jars and other relays with the &6Dominion Wand&r. A redstone signal switches it off."
		""
		"Apparatus variants: &6Splitter&r (spreads to many jars), &6Collector&r (pulls from jars within 5 blocks), &6Depositor&r (fills jars within 5) and &6Warper&r (any range, some loss past 30 blocks)."
	]
	quest.0BC92E394FCE51C6.title: "&dLong-Distance Relationship"
	quest.0BE88EBEB0F77461.quest_desc: [
		"Farm \\& Charm crops start out as &ewild plants&r. Wild tomatoes grow in plains, savannas and badlands; wild lettuce and onions turn up in plains, swamps, meadows, rivers, forests and taigas. Break them by hand for the crop."
		""
		"&aOnions are planted directly&r, like potatoes. Craft &e1 tomato&r or &e1 lettuce&r into &b3 seeds&r to start your own beds."
		""
		"&7Keep an eye out for Abandoned Fields: small overgrown plots with crops at every stage.&r"
	]
	quest.0BE88EBEB0F77461.quest_subtitle: "Salad, but make it wild"
	quest.0BE88EBEB0F77461.title: "&aForaging Season"
	quest.0C1097AC93AAD244.quest_desc: [
		"Climb to cloud height (&bY 191 to 196&r) and use an empty &eGlass Bottle&r to catch a &eCloud in a Bottle&r."
		""
		"Use it in the air to place a &atemporary cloud block&r you can stand on. Handy to start a sky bridge or catch yourself mid-build."
	]
	quest.0C1097AC93AAD244.quest_subtitle: "Head in the clouds"
	quest.0C1097AC93AAD244.title: "&fCloud Storage"
	quest.0C207832A630E7F0.quest_desc: [
		"Upgrade at a &6Smithing Table&r: &eWooden Brewing Station&r + &eCopper Ingot&r + &eSentry Armor Trim Smithing Template&r."
		""
		"Sentry templates turn up in &6pillager outpost&r chests. &aCopy it first&r (7 diamonds and cobblestone) so you keep one."
		""
		"The copper station unlocks most &6whiskeys&r and still brews every beer."
	]
	quest.0C207832A630E7F0.quest_subtitle: "Shiny kettles brew stronger stuff"
	quest.0C207832A630E7F0.title: "&6Copper Connoisseur"
	quest.0C5E92679328D6A5.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Valve&r turns a box of ordinary blocks into a giant fluid tank. Craft it from Kivi, &e2 Fluid Ports&r, &e2 gems&r and a &6Machine Base&r."
		""
		"Hover over it in your inventory and hold &bLeft Ctrl&r to see the largest tank it can handle. The next quest explains how to build one."
	]
	quest.0C5E92679328D6A5.quest_subtitle: "The heart of every tank"
	quest.0C5E92679328D6A5.title: "&9Turn the Valve"
	quest.0CC544A5158E8302.quest_desc: [
		"&cA relic's abilities do nothing until you research them.&r Put the relic in your &bmain inventory&r (not a chest or backpack) and hold &bLeft Shift&r over it to open its screen."
		""
		"Researching is a small puzzle: move over the fog to find hidden &dstars&r, then link them to match the ability's icon. The dots around a star show how many links it needs. A &bHint&r costs some player XP, and holding Shift while using it solves the whole puzzle for you (also for XP)."
		""
		"&7Hover any button on that screen for help. The first page explains the layout. The reward bottles hold relic XP: throw one at your feet to feed your relics.&r"
	]
	quest.0CC544A5158E8302.quest_subtitle: "No research, no superpowers"
	quest.0CC544A5158E8302.title: "&dConnect the Stars"
	quest.0D21C50CC3793AF7.quest_desc: [
		"Every drink makes you &bDrunk&r. From level III you sway, from V the world spins, and at VI you can &cblack out and wake up to 30 blocks away&r. Don't drink near lava or a cliff."
		""
		"The fix is fashion. Craft &ePatterned Wool&r from blue and white wool, then the &6Brewfest&r hat, top, trousers and boots. &aThe full set makes you immune to drunkenness.&r"
		""
		"&7A Breathalyzer (iron nuggets and redstone) tells you how far gone you are. Rare Brewfest Tents in the plains are built from patterned wool, so raiding one saves a lot of dyeing.&r"
	]
	quest.0D21C50CC3793AF7.quest_subtitle: "Lederhosen are load-bearing"
	quest.0D21C50CC3793AF7.title: "&9Oktoberfest Ready"
	quest.0D29F216FF233185.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Apple Press&r is an &eIron Trapdoor&r over a &eBarrel&r propped up on &eSticks&r. It works in two stages:"
		""
		"&bMashing:&r an &eApple&r becomes &eApple Mash&r in &b30 seconds&r."
		"&bFermenting:&r &eApple Mash&r plus an empty &eWine Bottle&r becomes &eApple Juice&r in &b40 seconds&r. Stack 2 Glass Bottles in a crafting grid for 4 Wine Bottles."
		""
		"&7It also squeezes a Honeycomb Block into 4 Honeycomb, and Honeycomb plus a Wine Bottle into a Honey Bottle.&r"
	]
	quest.0D29F216FF233185.quest_subtitle: "An apple a day, liquefied"
	quest.0D29F216FF233185.title: "&6Pressing Matters"
	quest.0D89F635C0997FC6.quest_desc: [
		"Press &eMilk&r and &eRennet&r into your first &eCheese Wheel&r. Plain cheese takes a regular &eMilk Bucket&r or a &eWooden Bucket of Milk&r."
		""
		"A wheel is a block you can place on a table. &aCraft it into 4 Cheese Slices&r to eat or cook with."
		""
		"&7Different milks make different wheels. Collecting all seven is this chapter's grand finale.&r"
	]
	quest.0D89F635C0997FC6.quest_subtitle: "The big wheel keeps on turning"
	quest.0D89F635C0997FC6.title: "&eSay Cheese!"
	quest.0DB1185BD8507842.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Roaster&r (iron ingots and nuggets) works just like the Cooking Pot: 6 ingredients, a bowl slot, &cheat below&r. It handles meat, fish, pancakes and the hearty plates."
		""
		"Chop a porkchop into &eBacon&r on the Cutting Board, then roast &e2 bacon&r, &e2 eggs&r and &ebutter&r in a bowl for &b3 Bacon with Eggs&r."
		""
		"&7Prepared meats like bacon and chicken parts also cook on a campfire or the Stove's grill.&r"
	]
	quest.0DB1185BD8507842.quest_subtitle: "Bring home the bacon, then roast it"
	quest.0DB1185BD8507842.title: "&6Sizzle Season"
	quest.0DB2693DBE0239B8.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Stove&r is the hub of the whole chapter. Craft it from &e3 iron ingots&r, &e5 Bricks&r (the block) and a &eCampfire&r."
		""
		"Inside it has &b3 ingredient slots&r and a fuel slot that takes any furnace fuel; a bake takes about &b12 seconds&r. The top is a &bgrill with 4 spots&r: right-click campfire food onto it, right-click to flip, sneak-right-click to take it back."
		""
		"&aThe Stove also heats a Cooking Pot or Roaster placed on top.&r Bakery's breads and Candlelight's dishes bake here too."
	]
	quest.0DB2693DBE0239B8.quest_subtitle: "The heart of every kitchen"
	quest.0DB2693DBE0239B8.title: "&6Hot Stuff"
	quest.0DCAF60678CA88EE.quest_desc: [
		"After the stomping, &aright-click the pot with an empty &eWine Bottle&r to fill it. Each bottle takes &b3 grapes&r, so &b6 grapes make 2 juices&r."
		""
		"Make Wine Bottles by stacking &e2 Glass Bottles&r in a crafting grid for &e4&r. The same bottles hold juice and finished wine."
		""
		"&a4 juices fill a Fermentation Barrel&r, which is where this is going."
	]
	quest.0DCAF60678CA88EE.quest_subtitle: "Bottled sunshine"
	quest.0DCAF60678CA88EE.title: "&dJuicy Success"
	quest.0DF81D9BBD8988CC.quest_desc: [
		"Some layouts to try (target in front, extras beside it or behind it):"
		"&e- Cobblestone, Kivi, Andesite, Diorite, Granite or Tuff&r: that block as the target with &bwater and lava&r next to it. A &6Water Block&r counts as the water. Renewable Kivi!"
		"&e- Stone&r: Cobblestone target with a &eMagma Block&r behind it, plus water and lava beside."
		"&e- Lava&r: an Extractor &bfacing up&r, a &eDripstone Block&r on top of it and lava above that. It slowly fills its internal &b1,000 mB&r tank; a tank or pipe on its back can take the lava away."
		"&e- Snowballs&r: an Extractor &bfacing down&r onto a &eCarved Pumpkin&r that sits on a Snow Block. A tiny snowman!"
		"&e- Mud&r: dirt with water beside it. &e- Calcite&r: a Bone Block with water."
		""
		"&7A waterlogged Extractor supplies its own water for many of these.&r"
	]
	quest.0DF81D9BBD8988CC.quest_subtitle: "A rock farm with no moving parts"
	quest.0DF81D9BBD8988CC.title: "&aKivi on Tap"
	quest.0E14248528F09342.quest_desc: [
		"Get each of Lili's ten treasures at least once (not all at the same time): &eBamboo Fishing Rod&r, &eFishing Net&r, &eFish Trap&r, &eSoaked Bag&r, &eSpear&r, &eDynamite&r, &eAnglers Hat&r, &ePuffer Platter&r, plus two you haven't made yet:"
		"&eFish Trophy Frame&r: planks and a gold ingot. Shows off one fish on a wall."
		"&eFish Net&r: a lead and a slime ball make 32. Sneak-right-click switches it between a bouncy net and a fence."
		""
		"The reward is &a2 Completionist Banners&r: place one for &bLuck&r to everyone within 8 blocks."
	]
	quest.0E14248528F09342.quest_subtitle: "Every lure in the box"
	quest.0E14248528F09342.title: "&6Scrap Collector"
	quest.0E375D31797D1CE1.quest_desc: [
		"Plant &eTea Blossoms&r on &6farmland&r like any crop. Bone meal speeds them up. A grown bush gives &b1 Green Tea Leaf&r and only sometimes a blossom back."
		""
		"&cA tea field shrinks on its own.&r Keep shearing flowers for fresh blossoms (bone meal on grass grows plenty), or harvest with &bFortune&r, which adds blossoms."
		""
		"&76 leaves pack into a Bag of Tea Leaves for tidy storage.&r"
	]
	quest.0E375D31797D1CE1.quest_subtitle: "Mind your blossoms"
	quest.0E375D31797D1CE1.title: "&aTea Time Starts in the Dirt"
	quest.0E942BE8E059B209.quest_desc: [
		"&aSeal the pact&r in a pool: &eBound Soul Pact&r + &eEcho Shard&r (Ancient Cities) + &e2 Astralite Ingots&r, &b25,000 ƒ&r. Throw the &eSealed Soul Pact&r into the lit gateway (another &b25,000 ƒ&r) and your familiar steps out and binds itself to the nearest altar &bwithin 24 blocks&r, so build the gateway close to home."
		""
		"Boons: &6Axolotl&r makes rites &b50%&r cheaper. &6Wisp&r (from an Allay) adds &b20,000 ƒ&r reserve. &6Frog&r gives a &b25%&r chance to double. &6Bat&r gives a little of each."
		""
		"&bOne familiar works per altar tier.&r They can't be hurt or lost. Only a &eSoul Wisp&r dismisses one."
	]
	quest.0E942BE8E059B209.quest_subtitle: "Your first familiar"
	quest.0E942BE8E059B209.title: "&dBound Company"
	quest.0E9FCFC1F3BA5F88.quest_desc: [
		"A block of &eTNT&r wrapped in &eIron Ingots&r with a piece of &eString&r makes &e4 Bombs&r."
		""
		"Throw one by hand and it &cexplodes on contact&r. Bombs hurt mobs but only break weak blocks like grass, so they &adon't crater your base&r. There's a short cooldown between throws."
		""
		"&7The &9Blue Bomb&7 can't be crafted. Find it in dungeon and stronghold chests or rare urns: it splits into five burning baby bombs.&r"
	]
	quest.0E9FCFC1F3BA5F88.quest_subtitle: "Pull pin, throw, run (no pin)"
	quest.0E9FCFC1F3BA5F88.title: "&cDa Bomb"
	quest.0EEB5BA745048FD1.quest_desc: [
		"Playing with friends? Open &6My Team&r from the sidebar, choose &aCreate a Party&r and invite them. They accept from chat."
		""
		"A party shares &bquest progress&r and &bclaims&r: one member finishing a quest completes it for the whole party, and &beach member&r claims the rewards for themselves. You can also add &aallies&r from the same screen to let other teams build in your land."
	]
	quest.0EEB5BA745048FD1.quest_subtitle: "Friendship, now with paperwork"
	quest.0EEB5BA745048FD1.title: "Better Together"
	quest.0F3AAD5F1CE5F6A2.quest_desc: [
		"&bHold right-click&r with the &eClot of Time&r and you &arewind along the path you just walked&r: a few seconds at first, much longer once it's levelled. The cooldown is as long as the rewind."
		""
		"Fell off a ledge? Walked into a creeper? &aJust take it back.&r At rank 1 you can't be hurt while rewinding."
	]
	quest.0F3AAD5F1CE5F6A2.quest_subtitle: "Ctrl+Z, but for your body"
	quest.0F3AAD5F1CE5F6A2.title: "&dRewind"
	quest.0F3D9CFB23BDA1E1.quest_desc: [
		"An &6Iron Rod&r breaks &bwhatever block is in front of it&r when a &6Piston&r pushes it. Add a clock and you have an automatic cobblestone miner or crop harvester."
		""
		"&cIt needs an End Rod&r in this pack (with 2 Iron Ingots), so it comes after your first trip to &5the End&r."
	]
	quest.0F3D9CFB23BDA1E1.quest_subtitle: "Point the business end away from you"
	quest.0F3D9CFB23BDA1E1.title: "&cRod of Destruction"
	quest.0F592991923FC22A.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Gateway Core&r takes &e4 Astralite Ingots&r, &e3 Willow Logs&r, a &eNether Star&r and a &eBlood Rune&r. That usually means a Wither fight first."
		""
		"Build a &b5x5 wall of willow logs&r (stripped is fine) with a 3x3 hole. The core replaces the middle block of the bottom row: place it first, facing the side you'll walk in from. &aLink a charged pool to it&r and right-click to open."
		""
		"Opening costs &b10,000 ƒ&r and it burns &b200 ƒ/s&r while lit. &cBreaking a frame log while it's lit collapses it.&r"
	]
	quest.0F592991923FC22A.quest_subtitle: "A door for spirits"
	quest.0F592991923FC22A.title: "&5The Soul Gateway"
	quest.0F7B130580CB44F7.quest_desc: [
		"Every tire is built around a &eShaft&r: &eSmall Tire&r with one Dried Kelp, &eTire&r with four, &eLarge Tire&r with four Mechanical Belts, and the &eMonstrous Tire&r with four Dried Kelp Blocks."
		""
		"Bigger tires climb over more. Four regular ones make a sensible first car."
	]
	quest.0F7B130580CB44F7.quest_subtitle: "Kelp: it's what's for driving"
	quest.0F7B130580CB44F7.title: "&eKicking Tires"
	quest.0F85CA5ADB99291A.quest_desc: [
		"&eInk&r comes in five rarities, and rarity decides how strong a spell you can write. Every spell's levels are split into bands: the first &b30%&r are Common, then &b25%&r Uncommon, &b20%&r Rare, &b15%&r Epic and the top &b10%&r Legendary."
		""
		"Find ink in chests, as drops from wizards, or buy it from &6Wandering Traders&r and the merchant wizards in magic towers."
	]
	quest.0F85CA5ADB99291A.quest_subtitle: "Common, Uncommon, Rare, Epic, Legendary"
	quest.0F85CA5ADB99291A.title: "&bTools of the Trade"
	quest.0FAA34786DC1891E.quest_desc: [
		"A &eNetherite Block&r on &6Shadowpulse Goo&r becomes &eRaw Eclipse Alloy Ore&r in &b24 seconds&r. Smelt the drops into &eEclipse Alloy Ingots&r."
		""
		"&cIt's pricey&r: one Netherite Block (36 Ancient Debris) gives only 3-4 raw. &aEclipse Alloy templates&r turn Celestigem gear into Eclipse gear with its upgrades intact, and save ingots on armor."
		""
		"Eclipse gear holds &b500,000 FE&r, mines at netherite level and unlocks the best upgrades: Ore X-Ray, Flight, Lava Immunity, and later Instant Break and Death Protection (both need &eTime Crystals&r)."
	]
	quest.0FAA34786DC1891E.quest_subtitle: "Tier 4 material"
	quest.0FAA34786DC1891E.title: "&5Total Eclipse of the Forge"
	quest.0FAEC18807F2EA03.quest_desc: [
		"Eight &ePaper&r around a &eClock&r (four gold ingots and a redstone) make a &6Calendar&r. Its tooltip shows the current &bseason&r and the day."
		""
		"The year has four seasons of three sub-seasons each, &b8 days&r per sub-season, so a full year is &b96 days&r. Seasons keep turning while you're offline. Only the &bOverworld&r has them, and winter brings snow and ice."
		""
		"&7Paper needs sugar cane, a summer crop: grab wild cane from riverbanks. Later, a Season Sensor (it needs Nether quartz) turns the season into a redstone signal.&r"
	]
	quest.0FAEC18807F2EA03.quest_subtitle: "Plan your harvest like a pro"
	quest.0FAEC18807F2EA03.title: "&6What Season Is It?"
	quest.0FE8A31302E66BB5.quest_desc: [
		"&6Amendments&r changes vanilla blocks rather than adding new ones. Some highlights:"
		"&a- &rplace any &elantern&r on a wall, where it sways when bumped"
		"&a- &rhang &eitems&r on hanging signs, and hang &etools&r on tripwire hooks (sneak-click)"
		"&a- &rput carpets on stairs, candles on skulls, blocks on lily pads"
		"&a- &rring a bell by clicking the chain or rope below it"
		"&a- &rhitting mobs with a torch sets them alight; fire charges can be thrown"
		""
		"&cBuilder's warning:&r a ceiling lantern &cfalls when its support breaks&r, and from high enough it smashes and &cstarts a fire&r."
	]
	quest.0FE8A31302E66BB5.quest_subtitle: "Old blocks, new tricks"
	quest.0FE8A31302E66BB5.title: "&6Vanilla, Amended"
	quest.0FEA3DCC1B20B9DC.quest_desc: [
		"Don't rebuild your gear every tier. A &eTemplate: Blazegold&r is an &eUpgrade: Blank&r plus &b5 Blazegold Ingots&r; craft one with &b2 more ingots&r to &aget two back&r."
		""
		"In a &6Smithing Table&r, template + Ferricore item + 1 Blazegold Ingot gives the Blazegold version &awith every upgrade still installed&r. Celestigem and Eclipse Alloy templates work the same way."
	]
	quest.0FEA3DCC1B20B9DC.quest_subtitle: "Keep your upgrades, change your metal"
	quest.0FEA3DCC1B20B9DC.title: "&aMoving On Up"
	quest.10019C0195920136.quest_desc: [
		"&6EMI&r is the item list on the right of any inventory screen. Hover an item and press &bR&r for its recipes, or &bU&r for everything it's used in. &bBackspace&r goes back."
		""
		"Press &bA&r to favourite an item (it pins to the left), and flip the right panel to the &acraftables&r page to see what you can make right now. On a recipe, the &b+&r button fills the crafting grid for you."
		""
		"&7Start a search with @ to filter by mod name, like @serene.&r"
	]
	quest.10019C0195920136.quest_subtitle: "The most important quest in the book"
	quest.10019C0195920136.title: "&aLook It Up"
	quest.1006FB5375FDC5E4.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Mechanical Drill&r (3 Andesite Alloy, an Iron Ingot and Andesite Casing) breaks the block in front of it; faster spin breaks faster."
		""
		"Its real job is riding a &6contraption&r: put drills on a piston or bearing and they chew through everything they run into. Build a tunnel bore or a cobblestone breaker."
	]
	quest.1006FB5375FDC5E4.quest_subtitle: "Mining, minus the mining"
	quest.1006FB5375FDC5E4.title: "&eDrill, Baby, Drill"
	quest.1032657A4D66A427.quest_desc: [
		"&6Minecraft Comes Alive&r turns every villager into a &aperson&r: a name, a face, a personality, a mood and a family tree. You can befriend them, marry one, raise children and grow a whole village."
		""
		"&aRight-click a villager&r to open the MCA menu: &bTalk&r, &bInteract&r, &bTrade&r and &bFamily Tree&r. Walking into a village also hands you the book &eRelationships and You&r, a short primer worth reading."
		""
		"&7Want a new look? A &eComb&7 changes your hair, &eNeedle and Thread&7 your clothes, and a &ePotion of Femininity&7 or &eMasculinity&7 your character. Press &bU&7 to browse the Skin Library.&r"
	]
	quest.1032657A4D66A427.quest_subtitle: "Hrmm? No. Hello!"
	quest.1032657A4D66A427.title: "&dMinecraft Comes Alive"
	quest.1032B486605B8AC7.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Ritual Brazier&r is an Arcane Pedestal, a Source Gem Block and 3 Gold Ingots. &dRituals&r are crafted &eTablets&r, each built around an Archwood log of a set colour."
		""
		"Use a tablet on the brazier, throw any augment items on top, then &aright-click with an empty hand&r to start. The tablet is used up. Rituals draw Source from jars &bwithin 6 blocks&r, and a redstone signal stops one."
		""
		"&7Favourites: Sanctuary (no hostile spawns in 32 blocks), Scrying, Flight, Cloudshaping and Harvest.&r"
	]
	quest.1032B486605B8AC7.title: "&dBrazen"
	quest.1034ECCA5AB3C6E2.quest_desc: [
		"Ascent needs a full set (4 armor + held weapon) of &aUncommon&r or better, and you must slay an &cApothic Invader&r yourself."
		""
		"Invaders replace roughly &b1 in 55&r Overworld monster spawns once you're in Frontier (a little more in the Nether), with a &b3-minute&r cooldown per player. They arrive with a loud boom, a chat message and a &bbeacon beam&r. &6Invader Dungeons&r underground hold a &cCaged Invader&r too."
		""
		"Every invader drops a boosted affix item, and sometimes a &dSigil of Malice&r. Activate Ascent to raise your enchanting cap to &b60&r."
	]
	quest.1034ECCA5AB3C6E2.quest_subtitle: "World Tier: Ascent"
	quest.1034ECCA5AB3C6E2.title: "&aBegin Your Ascent"
	quest.10722815C54F674A.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Water Wheel&r is 8 planks around a Shaft. Place it so &bflowing water&r runs past it: still source water does nothing, and covering more sides doesn't add power."
		""
		"Each wheel gives &b8 RPM&r and &b256 SU&r, and several wheels on one shaft add their capacity together. Right-click a wheel with any planks to change its wood."
		""
		"&aThis is the first power that runs while you're away.&r"
	]
	quest.10722815C54F674A.quest_subtitle: "Free spin, forever"
	quest.10722815C54F674A.title: "&bHarnessed Hydraulics"
	quest.107EC7F07B8E720D.quest_desc: [
		"When you die, your items stay in a &6corpse&r at the spot. Right-click it and press &aTransfer Items&r; curios and cosmetic armour go straight back into their slots."
		""
		"The corpse never despawns while it holds items and is safe from lava and the void. Find it with &bDeath History (U)&r, the minimap's &bdeathpoint&r, or &b/back&r."
		""
		"&cWarning:&r anyone can open your corpse. Go back quickly!"
	]
	quest.107EC7F07B8E720D.quest_subtitle: "Your stuff waits for you. Mostly."
	quest.107EC7F07B8E720D.title: "&cDeath Is Not the End"
	quest.108CBEED3179F3BD.quest_desc: [
		"&6Apothic Towers&r are tall, rare Overworld towers. The stone one stands in forests, plains and mountains; leafy ones in jungles and swamps, sandy ones in deserts, savannas and badlands, spruce ones in taiga and snowy biomes."
		""
		"Each holds one chest of enchanted books, &eFlawed&r gems and &aUncommon&r to &5Epic&r affix gear, plus &b4 gems&r in item frames."
		""
		"&cIn the stone and sand towers the chest is trapped:&r opening it lights &b4 TNT&r hidden in the floor below. Dig the TNT out from the side first, or break the chest instead of opening it. The stone tower also hides silverfish in its walls."
	]
	quest.108CBEED3179F3BD.quest_subtitle: "Mind the trapped chest"
	quest.108CBEED3179F3BD.title: "&eTower of Tomes"
	quest.109BED2924558E79.quest_desc: [
		"Soups simmer in the &6Cooking Pot&r. &eSimple Tomato Soup&r is just two tomatoes and sugar, with a bowl in the container slot."
		""
		"Then level up to &eGoulash&r: cooked beef, onion, carrot, potato and that tomato soup. It's the most filling of Farm \\& Charm's pot dishes."
		""
		"&7Other pot classics: potato, onion and barley soup, and corn grits.&r"
	]
	quest.109BED2924558E79.quest_subtitle: "A hug in a bowl"
	quest.109BED2924558E79.title: "&cSoup's On"
	quest.10A5E3AD2B4EB0DC.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Steering Wheel&r (Large Cogwheel, Andesite Casing, Shaft) gives precise rotation: &bhold right-click and move the mouse&r. Sneak to snap to &b45°&r steps, and set the max angle on its panel."
		""
		"Drive a &6Mechanical Bearing&r carrying a rudder with it, and &ctell the bearing not to disassemble&r. Or steer by thrust: an &6Analog Transmission&r slows one propeller with a redstone signal, and a &6Directional Gearshift&r can reverse it."
	]
	quest.10A5E3AD2B4EB0DC.quest_subtitle: "Turn, you magnificent beast"
	quest.10A5E3AD2B4EB0DC.title: "&eHard to Port"
	quest.10E1E15011C83598.quest_desc: [
		"Build a rectangle. Lay a &bsolid floor&r of seared blocks first, with &cno glass or tanks in the floor&r. Then build walls of seared bricks, &eSeared Glass&r, tanks and drains, and put the &6Controller&r in one wall. Interiors go up to &b14x14x64&r."
		""
		"Fill a &6Fuel Tank&r in the wall with &elava&r. Each interior block adds &b12 ingots&r of capacity. The Smeltery holds many fluids at once: click one in its screen to choose what pours next."
		""
		"&aIt also makes alloys automatically&r, and mobs that wander inside get slowly melted down."
		""
		"&7Right-click the Controller to open the screen. That completes this quest.&r"
	]
	quest.10E1E15011C83598.quest_subtitle: "Melts everything, mixes the rest"
	quest.10E1E15011C83598.title: "&6The Mighty Smeltery"
	quest.11148897663EF219.quest_desc: [
		"Stack &e2 logs&r (any wood) in a crafting grid for &e4 Grapevine Stems&r. Place one and &aright-click it with grape seeds&r (any kind except jungle) to plant them on it."
		""
		"With red or white seeds the stem grows a canopy of &6grapevine leaves&r around it. &aRight-click a mature stem to harvest&r, and it grows back. Bone meal speeds it up, and &eShears&r cut it back to bare wood."
		""
		"&7Stems are the tidy way to farm grapes: rows of them make a proper vineyard.&r"
	]
	quest.11148897663EF219.quest_subtitle: "Grapes like a little support"
	quest.11148897663EF219.title: "&2Trellis Training"
	quest.1136A0BBAB3E0D3A.quest_desc: [
		"Two mods fill this world's chests with treasure, and you &anever craft any of it&r:"
		"&6Artifacts&r are simple trinkets with fixed effects. Read the &btooltip&r and you know everything."
		"&6Relics&r are gear that &dgrows&r: you research their abilities, level them up by using them and eventually rank them up."
		""
		"Most of it is worn in your &6Curios&r slots (see &6Strapped In&r in First Light); a few pieces are held in your hand instead. Slots are tight: &bone&r head, necklace, belt and back, &btwo&r hands, feet and rings. Choosing a loadout is half the fun."
		""
		"&7Lootr (see Kitted Out) gives every player their own roll on each structure chest, so your friends can't steal your luck.&r"
	]
	quest.1136A0BBAB3E0D3A.quest_subtitle: "None of this treasure can be crafted. Go look."
	quest.1136A0BBAB3E0D3A.title: "&6Finders Keepers"
	quest.1160EAF317EE8EDC.quest_desc: [
		"Infuse a &eBlank Rune&r in a pool with one more item:"
		"&dWater Rune&r: &ePrismarine Crystals&r, &b2,500 ƒ&r. Adds &b2,000 ƒ&r to the altar's reserve."
		"&dEarth Rune&r: &eEmerald&r, &b2,500 ƒ&r. Each makes rites &b0.5%&r cheaper."
		"&dBlood Rune&r: &eGhast Tear&r, &b4,000 ƒ&r. Each adds &b0.4%&r chance of a doubled result."
		""
		"Every type still counts toward the altar tier. Cheaper and doubling each cap at &b50%&r from runes."
		"&7Bigger rites outgrow a 20,000 ƒ reserve, so plan some Water Runes.&r"
	]
	quest.1160EAF317EE8EDC.quest_subtitle: "Runes with a purpose"
	quest.1160EAF317EE8EDC.title: "&3Water, Earth and Blood"
	quest.1189A94CE96BF384.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Cash Register&r takes &eCopper Ingots&r and &eGold Ingots&r and makes two. &bSneak-right-click&r opens the drawer with a cheerful ring. Its &bfour compartments&r hold valuables: emeralds, gems, ingots, quartz and paper. A comparator can read it."
		""
		"The fun part: &aplace it on top of, next to or diagonally above a villager's workstation and right-click it&r. It reaches the villager who works there, just as if you'd clicked on them, so you can shop from behind the counter."
		""
		"&7Lili's Pottery's Clayworker uses a Pottery Table as a workstation: give your potter a shop counter.&r"
	]
	quest.1189A94CE96BF384.quest_subtitle: "Open for business"
	quest.1189A94CE96BF384.title: "&6Ka-Ching!"
	quest.11972A89EFEA73D5.quest_desc: [
		"&eWild Rooibos&r grows in &asavannas&r and &eWild Yerba Mate&r in &amountain biomes&r. Break them for &eRooibos Leaf&r and &eYerba Mate Leaf&r."
		""
		"The leaves are also seeds: &aplant them on farmland&r and you never have to travel again. &7A Nature's Compass makes finding the right biome much quicker.&r"
	]
	quest.11972A89EFEA73D5.quest_subtitle: "Pack a lunch"
	quest.11972A89EFEA73D5.title: "&6Leaves from Afar"
	quest.119B7B6B604751AA.quest_desc: [
		"Place two &6Simple Swappers&r, then right-click the first and then the second with a &eFerricore Wrench&r to link them. Each redstone pulse swaps the block in front of one with the block in front of the other. &aChests keep their contents.&r"
		""
		"They default to &bPulse&r mode, so give them a button. &aLinked swappers work across dimensions.&r"
		""
		"&7Remember that last part. It matters a lot at the end of this chapter.&r"
	]
	quest.119B7B6B604751AA.quest_subtitle: "This for that, at a distance"
	quest.119B7B6B604751AA.title: "&6Swap Meet"
	quest.11BFF2240DABAFBA.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Mincer&r is a hand-cranked grinder made from iron ingots, iron nuggets and planks. &aRight-click to put something in, then keep right-clicking to crank&r."
		""
		"&b1 wheat = 4 Flour&r, the base of every dough. It also minces beef, cuts porkchops into bacon, grinds bones into bone meal and turns rotten flesh into fertilizer."
		""
		"&7Feed it a silk-touched ore block for a few extra raw ores. Check EMI for the current numbers.&r"
	]
	quest.11BFF2240DABAFBA.quest_subtitle: "Crank it like you mean it"
	quest.11BFF2240DABAFBA.title: "&6The Daily Grind"
	quest.11E30F85F6BBE23C.quest_desc: [
		"Every tier adds slots: &bWood 27&r, &bCopper 45&r, &bIron 54&r, &bGold 81&r, &bDiamond 108&r, &bNetherite 132&r. Upgrade slots go &b1, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5&r up the same ladder."
		""
		"Two ways up: craft a Sophisticated chest with &eIngots&r, or craft a tier upgrade item like the &eBasic to Iron Tier Upgrade&r (8 iron around a lever) and &aright-click the placed chest&r - contents and upgrades stay inside."
		""
		"&7Barrels and shulker boxes climb the same ladder.&r"
	]
	quest.11E30F85F6BBE23C.title: "&6Bigger on the Inside"
	quest.11F4F779E2969800.quest_desc: [
		"&eDiamond Horse Armor&r can't be crafted, but the dungeons in this chapter are full of it: desert temple storerooms, fortress keeps and stronghold chests all hold horse armour and saddles."
		""
		"Armour your mount before you charge into anything with a sword."
	]
	quest.11F4F779E2969800.quest_subtitle: "Your horse deserves nice things too"
	quest.11F4F779E2969800.title: "&bBarded and Dangerous"
	quest.12437C7D3D921285.quest_desc: [
		"&eBarley seeds&r only come from &6wild barley&r (rivers, plains, savannas) or Abandoned Fields; there is no recipe, so grab a few when you see it. &eOat seeds&r drop from wild oats in meadows and taigas, or craft &b2 wheat seeds + 2 bone meal&r into 2."
		""
		"&eKernels&r are corn's seeds: break wild corn, or craft 1 corn into 3. Corn grows two blocks tall."
		""
		"&7Nine of most crops pack into a bag or bale for tidy storage.&r"
	]
	quest.12437C7D3D921285.quest_subtitle: "Three new grains for the granary"
	quest.12437C7D3D921285.title: "&eAmber Waves"
	quest.1266AEC24F16FC4D.quest_desc: [
		"A &eLuxinia Flower&r burns &eAmethyst Coal&r, and nothing else, for &b40 ƒ/s&r. One coal lasts &b160 seconds&r, up to &b6,400 ƒ&r. &aDrop the coal onto it&r: it picks up loose items on and just above itself, so a dropper facing down works, but a hopper doesn't (the flower has no inventory). Link it to a pool."
		""
		"It holds &b4,000 ƒ&r. If that fills mid-burn, the rest of the coal is wasted, so keep it linked."
		""
		"&cLuxinias can't be crafted or grown.&r They only come from oasis floors and Willow Huts. Don't lose them."
	]
	quest.1266AEC24F16FC4D.quest_subtitle: "Luxinia Flower"
	quest.1266AEC24F16FC4D.title: "&dThe Patient Generator"
	quest.126E3A5DCE4C23B6.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Collector&r is an &eEnder Pearl&r, &e2 Light gems&r, &eRedstone&r, Kivi and an &eItem Port&r. It mounts on the face of a block."
		""
		"It &agrabs item drops within 3 blocks&r, catching new drops before they even land as item entities. It pushes what it catches into the block it's mounted on, so stick it on a chest; right-click it to open its buffer and set a filter. A &bredstone signal turns it off&r."
	]
	quest.126E3A5DCE4C23B6.quest_subtitle: "Catch it before it lands"
	quest.126E3A5DCE4C23B6.title: "&bVacuum Seal"
	quest.127D6EFD66709306.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Diamond Backpack&r: &b108 slots&r and &b5 upgrade slots&r on your back, a storage network at home, wireless power, a web of waystones and a brewing stand bubbling away."
		""
		"You're kitted out. Time to specialise: build machines in &6Create&r, cast spells with &6Ars Nouveau&r or &6Iron's Spells&r, push enchanting further in &6Apotheosis&r, head out in &6Exploration&r, or settle down with the farming and family chapters. Pick a tab - there's no wrong answer."
	]
	quest.127D6EFD66709306.quest_subtitle: "Kitted out, top to bottom"
	quest.127D6EFD66709306.title: "&bReady for Anything"
	quest.12935D0C0B5ED225.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Tinker's Workshop&r is a rare IDAS dungeon built from &6Create&r machinery: drills, presses and fans you really shouldn't stand in front of. It shows up in &bforests, birch forests, plains and meadows&r."
		""
		"Find its &avault&r: brass, diamonds, Create parts and sometimes a &eLinked Controller&r."
		""
		"&7Its bigger sibling, the &6Tinker's Citadel&7, appears in the same biomes with a vault of its own.&r"
	]
	quest.12935D0C0B5ED225.quest_subtitle: "Health and safety violations ahead"
	quest.12935D0C0B5ED225.title: "&6Mind the Gears"
	quest.12A65EBA2CE0A1F0.quest_desc: [
		"Cheese Slices make easy crafting-table food: a &eCheese Sandwich&r (bread, cheese, bread) makes &b6&r, and &eCheesecake&r (cheese, eggs, wheat) is a placeable cake you can cut into slices."
		""
		"&7Also try Cheese Rolls and Cheese Tarts. In the Cookpot, Water Buffalo meat with cheese and salt becomes Sausage with Cheese.&r"
	]
	quest.12A65EBA2CE0A1F0.quest_subtitle: "Bread's best friend"
	quest.12A65EBA2CE0A1F0.title: "&eGrate Expectations"
	quest.12A86C8D8574C066.quest_desc: [
		"With the &eGlitchy Mantle&r on, some attacks simply &amiss you&r. At relic level 5 you leave &dglitchy copies&r that stun whatever touches them. At level 10, &dSurface Tear&r lets you &awalk on air&r. Keep moving, or you fall. Sneak to drop down safely."
		""
		"&7Back slot again: mantle or elytra, you decide.&r"
	]
	quest.12A86C8D8574C066.quest_subtitle: "End chests, back slot"
	quest.12A86C8D8574C066.title: "&5Error 404: Hit Not Found"
	quest.12B078F468743CD3.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Wooden Planter&r (&eWooden Slabs&r and &eDirt&r) or &6Stone Brick Planter&r (&eStone Brick Slabs&r and &eDirt&r) makes three. &aPlant crops straight into it&r, no hoe or farmland needed, and now and then it gives them a free growth boost."
		""
		"&7Not to be confused with Lili's Pottery's clay Planter, which holds small flowers rather than crops.&r"
	]
	quest.12B078F468743CD3.quest_subtitle: "No hoe required"
	quest.12B078F468743CD3.title: "&2Kitchen Garden"
	quest.12DD8616F37CA2E1.quest_desc: [
		"Right-click a placed &6Fluid Hatch&r with a &eBlock of Experience&r (9 Nuggets of Experience) to turn it into an &6Experience Hatch&r."
		""
		"Put it on a tank. &bRight-click&r to deposit your levels as Liquid XP and &bsneak-right-click&r to take them back. A scroll panel sets how much each click moves."
		""
		"&7Fill a bucket from the tank for a Bucket o' Enchanting, a portable 1,000 mB.&r"
	]
	quest.12DD8616F37CA2E1.quest_subtitle: "A bank account for levels"
	quest.12DD8616F37CA2E1.title: "&aSpirit-Taking"
	quest.12F16C4C8F79303C.quest_desc: [
		"Brew all &bnine&r drinks: &aGreen, Black, Oolong, Lavender, Hibiscus, Rooibos and Yerba Mate Tea&r, plus &eCoffee&r and &eMilk Coffee&r. Each one counts as soon as it lands in your inventory, so you don't need them all at once."
		""
		"Doing it earns two &6Completionist Banners&r. A placed banner gives &bAbsorption&r to players around it, so hang one in your kitchen or base."
		""
		"&7Bonus: [Let's Do] Legacy grants the Herbalist title once you have drunk 25 Herbal Brews drinks.&r"
	]
	quest.12F16C4C8F79303C.quest_subtitle: "Master of the Kettle"
	quest.12F16C4C8F79303C.title: "&6A Hug in a Cup"
	quest.133255470837DE16.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Basic Spell Turret&r (4 Source Gems, a Redstone Block, 4 Gold Ingots) casts the spell from a Spell Parchment &bwhen powered by redstone&r, like a magic dispenser. It uses Touch and Projectile spells."
		""
		"The &6Timer Spell Turret&r (add a Clock) fires on its own, and the &6Enchanted Spell Turret&r halves the Source cost. Turrets can pick up and place blocks using an adjacent inventory."
	]
	quest.133255470837DE16.title: "&dTurret Syndrome"
	quest.137C9ABBA5FA43A3.quest_desc: [
		"&6Andesite Casing&r is the shell of most machines. Place a &eStripped Log&r or Stripped Wood and &aright-click it with Andesite Alloy&r."
		""
		"Casing can also be right-clicked onto shafts, cogs and belts to encase them, which looks tidy and hides the moving parts."
		""
		"&7Here's some iron toward the next quest's Block of Iron.&r"
	]
	quest.137C9ABBA5FA43A3.quest_subtitle: "Wood, upgraded"
	quest.137C9ABBA5FA43A3.title: "&eThe Andesite Age"
	quest.139EAD4CE0F65CC7.quest_desc: [
		"Empty &eDragon's Breath&r bottles into an &6Item Drain&r (250 mB each) to get it as a fluid; pipe it to a tank and fill a bucket at your Fluid Hatch. A fan blowing through a breath source or a &eDragon Head&r does &bBulk Ending&r: Cobblestone to End Stone, Stone Bricks to End Stone Bricks, Leather to Phantom Membrane, Apples to Chorus Fruit."
		""
		"&aRenewable trick:&r it works like the lava-dripstone farm. A breath source block above a block with &ePointed Dripstone&r hanging under it slowly fills a cauldron below."
		""
		"&7You need to visit the End to collect the first bottles.&r"
	]
	quest.139EAD4CE0F65CC7.quest_subtitle: "Dragon's Breath, now in bulk"
	quest.139EAD4CE0F65CC7.title: "&dThe End Is Near(by)"
	quest.13A143470420785B.quest_desc: [
		"Three mods share this chapter. &6Vinery&r turns grapes and apples into wine, &6Brewery&r brews beer and whiskey in a bubbling kettle, and &6Apple Wood Rebarked&r gives your orchard its own wood, furniture and a moonshine."
		""
		"There is no guide book. Use &bEMI&r instead: the &bBarrel Fermentation&r, &bApple Press Mashing&r and &bFermenting&r, &bGrape Mashing&r and &bBrewing&r tabs list every recipe, and pressing &bR&r on any wine or beer shows how it is made."
		""
		"Looking at a &6Grapevine Pot&r, a wine rack or a &6Brewing Station&r kettle also shows a little info panel that tells you what it needs next."
		""
		"&7Brewing leans on Farm \\& Charm for yeast, the drying silo and rope. The &6From Farm to Table&7 chapter covers all three.&r"
	]
	quest.13A143470420785B.quest_subtitle: "Grow it, press it, brew it, age it"
	quest.13A143470420785B.title: "&5Down to the Cellar"
	quest.13B3825BBE69A553.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Simple Clicker&r uses the item in its slot like a player: right-click, left-click or hold, sneaking or not, aimed at blocks, air or chosen mobs."
		""
		"The &6Simple Sensor&r emits redstone when its target is in front of it. &aRight-click its filter slot&r to match an exact block state, like a door being open or a crop being fully grown."
	]
	quest.13B3825BBE69A553.quest_subtitle: "Robot fingers, robot eyes"
	quest.13B3825BBE69A553.title: "&6Click, Clack, Sense That"
	quest.13D2D519BB12E1BB.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Spectral Lantern&r is a vanilla lantern with a ghost inside: &eIron Nuggets&r around a &eSpectral Essence&r."
		""
		"Like any lantern it stops sanity drain within &b4 blocks&r. &aPlace a couple around your camp&r, your loot pile or anywhere you'll stand for a while."
	]
	quest.13D2D519BB12E1BB.quest_subtitle: "A night-light for grown-ups"
	quest.13D2D519BB12E1BB.title: "&6Light in the Fog"
	quest.140704D9E29D7698.quest_desc: [
		"&6Apotheosis&r turns gear into loot: monsters and chests drop &eaffixed&r weapons and armor with random stats, gems slot into them, and five &bWorld Tiers&r make the world tougher and the rewards richer as you climb."
		""
		"It comes with three modules: &6Apothic Enchanting&r (level-100 enchanting), &6Apothic Spawners&r (portable, upgradeable spawners) and &6Apothic Attributes&r (crits, life steal and friends). &6Placebo&r is just their shared library."
		""
		"&aCraft the Chronicle of Shadows&r from a &eBook&r and a &eGold Ingot&r. It covers every module."
		""
		"&7The guide often says \"see JEI\". This pack runs EMI instead, so this chapter spells out the numbers the guide leaves to JEI: infusion stats, rune effects and reforging costs.&r"
	]
	quest.140704D9E29D7698.quest_subtitle: "The Chronicle of Shadows"
	quest.140704D9E29D7698.title: "&5All Things That Should Have Been"
	quest.142767F65ACF32A1.quest_desc: [
		"On a moving contraption, regular &eWindmill Sails&r produce &blift&r at right angles to their face, more the faster you go. Enough of them and you have a &afixed-wing plane&r."
		""
		"&eSymmetric Sails&r (2 Windmill Sails make 2) only produce &bdrag&r, and none when edge-on. Use them as rudders, fins and stabilisers. They attach without glue and can be dyed."
	]
	quest.142767F65ACF32A1.quest_subtitle: "Rudders, fins and actual wings"
	quest.142767F65ACF32A1.title: "&eWing It"
	quest.142791A2592566BE.quest_desc: [
		"Three cosy Let's Do mods live in this chapter. &6Furniture&r fills your rooms, &6Hearth \\& Timber&r builds the walls and roof around them, and &6Lili's Pottery&r adds clay, kilns and painted vases."
		""
		"None of them has a guide book. &bLook at a furniture piece&r (a Fish Tank, Wardrobe, Bin, Lamp...) and a small &bHUD panel&r shows its state and controls. Hearth \\& Timber's interactive blocks explain themselves when you &bhold Shift&r over their tooltip. &bEMI&r shows every Furniture and Hearth \\& Timber recipe, but &cnot&r what the Pottery Table and Kiln make, so those quests spell it out."
		""
		"&aBuild in Oak and Red.&r The chapter's final quest counts only &eOak&r wooden pieces and &eRed&r fabric pieces, so every Furniture quest asks for those, and every piece has to be &bplaced&r at least once. Any other wood or colour works the same way once you've got the gist."
	]
	quest.142791A2592566BE.quest_subtitle: "Four walls are not a home"
	quest.142791A2592566BE.title: "&6Make Yourself at Home"
	quest.142F3992E9D10936.quest_desc: [
		"&eGlass Viewers&r are XyCraft's seamless glass. Run ordinary glass through a &6Stonecutter&r for the clear, dire and silicon styles, or use &eTinted Glass&r for the dark one."
		""
		"&eReinforced Glass Viewers&r are 2 glass and 2 iron ingots in a 2x2. Eight glass around a &eGlow Ink Sac&r gives glowing viewers, which the Stonecutter turns into the glowing-clear style. Viewers work as walls of a XyCraft tank."
	]
	quest.142F3992E9D10936.quest_subtitle: "Glass, but connected"
	quest.142F3992E9D10936.title: "&fWindow Dressing"
	quest.14487F88E59CB32D.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Item IO&r is built like the Valve but with &eItem Ports&r. Set it into a tank wall and feed it containers: it &afills or empties them&r against the tank, for example turning glass bottles into water bottles."
		""
		"&bRight-click&r it with the &6Aluminum Wrench&r to switch between &bfill&r and &bdrain&r. Don't hit it with the wrench, or you'll just pick it up."
	]
	quest.14487F88E59CB32D.quest_subtitle: "Fill 'er up"
	quest.14487F88E59CB32D.title: "&eBottle Service"
	quest.144B632B65F382ED.quest_desc: [
		"An &eAndesite Propeller&r is a Create &ePropeller&r over a wooden slab over a &eShaft&r. Spin it and it pushes your contraption."
		""
		"&bReverse the rotation&r (or hit it with a &6Wrench&r) to flip the thrust. Thrust drops as you speed up and as you climb, so bring a few. Each needs &b4 SU per RPM&r."
		""
		"&7The Wooden Propeller is the same thing in a nicer coat; convert between them in a crafting grid.&r"
	]
	quest.144B632B65F382ED.quest_subtitle: "Spin to win"
	quest.144B632B65F382ED.title: "&ePropeller Heads"
	quest.1452077CDB9BDE86.quest_desc: [
		"&eDungarees&r can't be crafted: an experienced &bFarmer&r villager sells them for emeralds once you've levelled up their trades."
		""
		"Wear them and you &astop trampling farmland&r, plus you can see how well-fed your animals are."
		""
		"&7They also look very fetching on a Scarecrow.&r"
	]
	quest.1452077CDB9BDE86.quest_subtitle: "Every farmer's dream wardrobe"
	quest.1452077CDB9BDE86.title: "&9Overall Excellent"
	quest.14C60B448CABD889.quest_desc: [
		"Any explosion that hits a spawner makes it unstable. &cA few seconds later it blows up again&r, dropping its mob and &b48-64&r &eSpawner Chains&r. Stand well back."
		""
		"Rogue Spawners in caves and dungeon spawners are perfect targets. Silk Touch the ones you want to keep, since a blown-up spawner is gone for good."
		""
		"&7The chains are fire- and blast-proof, so the second boom won't destroy them.&r"
	]
	quest.14C60B448CABD889.quest_subtitle: "Spawner Chains"
	quest.14C60B448CABD889.title: "&cChain Reaction"
	quest.14DEF8F48EB82AFA.quest_desc: [
		"A &eBlank Runestone&r can't be crafted from scratch. Look in chests: stronghold libraries, End Cities and Ancient Cities give the best odds, Nether fortresses and bastions are decent. Or buy them from the captive trader some Evoker Forts hold."
		""
		"Surround one with &e8&r of a school's focus to make that school's rune, or with &e8 Arcane Essence&r for an &eArcane Rune&r. Runes turn Wizard armor into school armor and fill upgrade orbs."
		""
		"&7Wrong rune? Craft it with a &eShriving Stone&r&7 (raw iron and an amethyst shard) to wipe it blank again.&r"
	]
	quest.14DEF8F48EB82AFA.quest_subtitle: "Every school has its sigil"
	quest.14DEF8F48EB82AFA.title: "&eWritten in Stone"
	quest.152F4C7C62C27406.quest_desc: [
		"Surround a Water Wheel with 8 more planks to get a &6Large Water Wheel&r. It turns at only &b4 RPM&r but gives &b512 SU&r, double a small wheel."
		""
		"Gear it up with Large-to-small cogs if your machines need more speed."
	]
	quest.152F4C7C62C27406.quest_subtitle: "Slower, but beefier"
	quest.152F4C7C62C27406.title: "&bBigger Splash"
	quest.159EB5A1152B16B2.quest_desc: [
		"Fabric furniture comes in all 16 wool colours. Red is the one the finale counts."
		""
		"&6Sofa&r: &eRed Wool&r and &eSticks&r, makes three. Sofas placed side by side join into one long couch. &6Pouffe&r: three &eRed Wool&r in a row. It's a &btrampoline&r too: you bounce, and you take only &bhalf fall damage&r. &6Curtains&r open and close with a right-click or a &bredstone signal&r."
		""
		"&6Lamp&r: &bSneak-right-click&r to switch it on or off. &aClick a wall with it to place a wall lamp.&r The recipe makes two, so try both. Either kind counts for the finale."
	]
	quest.159EB5A1152B16B2.quest_subtitle: "Soft furnishings, loud colour"
	quest.159EB5A1152B16B2.title: "&cSeeing Red"
	quest.15BB3043AAB27789.quest_desc: [
		"In a &6Smithing Table&r, combine the template, a &eBlaze Burner&r and an &eEnchanting Table&r to make the &6Blaze Enchanter&r."
		""
		"Pipe &eLiquid Experience&r into it (a Mechanical Arm can also feed it XP items), set the enchanting level on its value panel (up to &b30&r), then insert an item. Put an item in the panel's filter slot and it instead writes enchantments suited to that item onto a blank &eEnchanting Template&r (press a Block of Experience to make one)."
		""
		"&7Higher isn't always better: some enchantments stop appearing at high levels. Blaze machine advancements go to whoever placed the machine.&r"
	]
	quest.15BB3043AAB27789.quest_subtitle: "An enchanting table that never sleeps"
	quest.15BB3043AAB27789.title: "&6Blaze of Glory"
	quest.15DE39C4F654FAD7.quest_desc: [
		"&e8 Dragonfly Wings&r around a &eBlank Runestone&r make an &eAstral Rune&r. The &6Astromancer&r also trades one for &e6 Mithril Scrap&r."
		""
		"Combine a &6Wizard armor&r piece (the hood, not the hat), an Astral Rune and an Arcane Essence for &eAstral armor&r, with &b+10%&r astral power per piece. Eight runes fill an &eAstral Upgrade Orb&r."
	]
	quest.15DE39C4F654FAD7.quest_subtitle: "Starlight, set in stone"
	quest.15DE39C4F654FAD7.title: "&9Written in the Stars"
	quest.1618F4883C133514.quest_desc: [
		"Pour the blend into a mould and &aadd heat&r: Flint and Steel, a Torch, a Campfire, Magma or a lit Blaze Burner. The crystal spreads through all of the fluid. &dSoul fire&r makes pink &dPearlescent Levitite&r."
		""
		"Enough &dLevitite&r on a contraption keeps it &bafloat&r, and it resists slow movement like a sky anchor. It can't climb on its own, so keep a propeller or balloon."
		""
		"&cLevitite can't be picked back up: mining it destroys it.&r Cast it straight into your ship. Clay, mud and coarse dirt moulds dissolve when it sets."
	]
	quest.1618F4883C133514.quest_subtitle: "Rocks are not supposed to do that"
	quest.1618F4883C133514.title: "&dUnidentified Floating Object"
	quest.164513214AA6BC3B.quest_desc: [
		"Put an &eIron Block&r against any face of an awake &6Primogel Goo&r. After &b2 minutes&r it becomes &eRaw Ferricore Ore&r. Mine it and smelt the &eRaw Ferricore&r into &eFerricore Ingots&r."
		""
		"&aOne goo works all six faces at once&r, so surround it with iron blocks. Don't pull a block out halfway, or that face starts over."
		""
		"&cThe raw block drops only 3-4 raw, with no Fortune bonus.&r Nine ingots in, three or four out. Silk Touch just gives the block back."
	]
	quest.164513214AA6BC3B.quest_subtitle: "Your first goo conversion"
	quest.164513214AA6BC3B.title: "&eIron, Re-Gooed"
	quest.167B646EA5C4768E.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Globe&r can't be crafted. Buy one from the &eWandering Trader&r, or find one in shipwreck treasure and galleon chests."
		""
		"It shows a tiny randomly generated planet, &bunique to each world&r, and using it tells you your &bcoordinates&r. Right-click to spin it; &aclick it fast enough&r and it really gets going."
		""
		"&7Antique Ink turns it into a Sepia Globe; Soap turns it back.&r"
	]
	quest.167B646EA5C4768E.quest_subtitle: "Like a record, baby"
	quest.167B646EA5C4768E.title: "&dYou Spin Me Round"
	quest.1686665BBF260706.quest_desc: [
		"The &eSeed Pouch&r holds &b640&r of one kind of seed: seeds, saplings, mushrooms, berries, kelp, sugar cane, nether wart, even &dArs Nouveau&r pods. Craft it from &eLeather&r, &eString&r and a seed of your choice."
		""
		"Right-click seeds onto it to fill it. While you hold it, it &apicks up matching seeds&r on its own. Use it on farmland to plant, or &bsneak&r to plant a &b3x3&r patch at once."
		""
		"&7It also carries Bone Meal and fertilises 3x3 the same way.&r"
	]
	quest.1686665BBF260706.quest_subtitle: "Ten stacks, one pocket"
	quest.1686665BBF260706.title: "&ePocket Garden"
	quest.16C6D4CEE4A1147D.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Modern Foundry's Anvil&r is &bthree blocks&r of an alloy on top of &e4 seared blocks&r, laid out like a vanilla anvil. You can also build it around your old Station. It takes on the colour of the metal."
		""
		"Allowed metals: rose gold, slimesteel, pig iron, amethyst bronze, manyullyn, netherite and others. &aCreate's Brass Blocks also count&r (see the Create chapters)."
		""
		"It has &bfive input slots&r, which lets you build &abroad tools&r and apply five-ingredient modifiers."
	]
	quest.16C6D4CEE4A1147D.quest_subtitle: "Room for five"
	quest.16C6D4CEE4A1147D.title: "&6Anvil-ution"
	quest.16DDA24F87471AB5.quest_desc: [
		"Serve a full &6dinner menu&r: eat a &estarter&r, a &emain course&r and a &edessert&r from a set table, with no more than &b5 minutes&r between courses."
		""
		"Finish all three for &bFull menu!&r: five more minutes of Well Served, plus &bRefreshed&r (your next harvests cost no tool durability and may drop extra)."
		""
		"Farm \\& Charm soups and salads make good starters, lasagne or a Farmer's Breakfast a main, and Bakery cake slices or cupcakes a dessert."
		""
		"&7In the evening, nearby villagers may wander over to a set table and help themselves. They'll thank you with a discount on trades for a day.&r"
	]
	quest.16DDA24F87471AB5.quest_subtitle: "Starter, main, dessert. Repeat."
	quest.16DDA24F87471AB5.title: "&6A Three-Course Affair"
	quest.170CF438E5E50FA4.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Mechanical Saw&r (Iron Sheets, an Iron Ingot and Andesite Casing) fells whole trees on a contraption or when it faces one."
		""
		"Point it &bupward&r and it processes items dropped on top: logs into stripped logs and planks, stonecutter recipes, and &eAndesite Alloy into 6 Shafts&r (better than crafting). Set its filter to pick an output."
	]
	quest.170CF438E5E50FA4.quest_subtitle: "Timber!"
	quest.170CF438E5E50FA4.title: "&eWorkshop's Most Feared"
	quest.1744E2941513F0D8.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Energy Transmitter&r powers every FE block in its area &awirelessly&r. Feed it from a generator and set the area like an advanced machine."
		""
		"It sends up to &b1,000 FE/t&r and loses &c1% per block&r of distance. Transmitters in each other's range share power &awith no loss&r, so a chain of them makes a base-wide grid."
	]
	quest.1744E2941513F0D8.quest_subtitle: "Wires are so last tier"
	quest.1744E2941513F0D8.title: "&6Power Over Ether"
	quest.17E8015D127099FF.quest_desc: [
		"Golden Furnace, &eDiamonds&r and &eGlass&r make a &6Diamond Furnace&r. The line goes on: &6Emerald&r or &6Crystal&r, then &6Obsidian&r, then &6Netherite&r."
		""
		"Slot &eAugments&r into the furnace's Augments tab: &eSpeed&r (sugar) halves cook time but burns twice the fuel, &eFuel&r (coal) stretches fuel, &eBlasting&r and &eSmoking&r only take those recipes, and &eFactory&r turns it into a multi-slot machine running on &bFE&r."
	]
	quest.17E8015D127099FF.quest_subtitle: "2.5x faster than vanilla"
	quest.17E8015D127099FF.title: "&bDiamond-Hot"
	quest.17F00CE6FD29E799.quest_desc: [
		"Roll &eBamboo&r or &ePaper&r in the Rolling Mill to make a &eStraw&r. Right-click a &6Blaze Burner&r with it to make a liquid-fuelled burner, then fill it by bucket or pipe."
		""
		"Per bucket: &eLava&r keeps it heated for &b20,000 ticks&r, &eSeed Oil&r for 4,800, and &eBioethanol&r &asuperheats&r it for 24,000. That means superheating without hand-feeding Blaze Cakes."
		""
		"&7Seed Oil comes from compacting seeds in a Press and Basin. Biofuel takes a few more mixing steps: see Ponder.&r"
	]
	quest.17F00CE6FD29E799.quest_subtitle: "Blazes prefer it liquid"
	quest.17F00CE6FD29E799.title: "&eThrough a Straw"
	quest.180D617B589DCA66.quest_desc: [
		"Tools come with &bmodifier slots&r. Most have &b3 upgrade slots&r and &b1 ability slot&r. Put the tool and an ingredient in the &6Station&r to apply a modifier."
		""
		"Easy first picks: &eRedstone&r for &bHaste&r (45 dust per level, so use blocks), &eQuartz&r for &bSharpness&r, a &eDiamond&r for +500 durability and diamond mining tier, or a &eBook and Quill&r for a bonus upgrade slot."
		""
		"&7The Station only takes three ingredients at once. Five-ingredient modifiers such as Silky need the Anvil.&r"
	]
	quest.180D617B589DCA66.quest_subtitle: "Redstone makes it go faster"
	quest.180D617B589DCA66.title: "&bUpgrade Path"
	quest.1818151F9A3FFAC0.quest_desc: [
		"Set a &6Mechanical Generator&r to &eLimestone&r and pull its output (funnel or chute) straight into &6Crushing Wheels&r. Each Limestone has a chance to drop &eQuartz&r and &eLapis Lazuli&r. Switch it to &eScoria&r and the crushing drops &eBlaze Powder&r, which compacts into Blaze Rods."
		""
		"That is quartz, lapis and blaze rods from nothing but rotation. &aYour factory now feeds itself.&r"
		""
		"&7Other Ultimate Factory crushing recipes: Nether Bricks sometimes give Netherite Scrap, Blackstone a Wither Skeleton Skull, Soul Sand Glowstone Dust.&r"
	]
	quest.1818151F9A3FFAC0.quest_subtitle: "A quarry with no hole"
	quest.1818151F9A3FFAC0.title: "&6Something From Nothing"
	quest.18228E8017A42FE8.quest_desc: [
		"A rare IDAS dungeon hidden in the &bdesert&r. Like the desert temple, it gives you &cMining Fatigue&r while its master lives, so you can't dig through the walls."
		""
		"Fight your way past the husks and strays to the tomb and slay the &cPharaoh of the Labyrinth&r, a husk with a diamond sword and shield. That lifts the curse, and the tomb holds diamonds, emeralds and golden apples."
	]
	quest.18228E8017A42FE8.quest_subtitle: "Left, left, left... wait"
	quest.18228E8017A42FE8.title: "&eLost in the Labyrinth"
	quest.182DAA7E87B32C42.quest_desc: [
		"Four logs in a diamond shape make 4 &eHollow Logs&r. &bSneak&r while walking toward the open side to &acrawl inside&r; stand one upright and you can climb up through it."
		""
		"Fallen trees in the wild are often hollow already. Perfect for secret tunnels and fairy-tale cottages."
	]
	quest.182DAA7E87B32C42.quest_subtitle: "Cosy. Slightly damp."
	quest.182DAA7E87B32C42.title: "&2Crawling in my Bark"
	quest.18783BA3906145FA.quest_desc: [
		"A &ePattern&r is a blank wooden stencil. Put &e2 Planks&r and &e2 Sticks&r in a checkerboard to get &b6&r of them."
		""
		"Every table in this mod is built from Patterns, and the &6Part Builder&r uses &bone Pattern up for each part&r it makes. Keep a stack around."
	]
	quest.18783BA3906145FA.quest_subtitle: "Stencils for everything"
	quest.18783BA3906145FA.title: "&ePattern Recognition"
	quest.1879B1ADAA2A35E3.quest_desc: [
		"Your first &6Sequenced Assembly&r. Press a &eGold Ingot&r into a &eGolden Sheet&r and send it along a belt under three Deployers holding a &eCogwheel&r, a &eLarge Cogwheel&r and an &eIron Nugget&r, in that order."
		""
		"The sheet needs that trio &b5 times&r (15 deploys in all), so loop the belt back on itself. Each finished item is a &6Precision Mechanism&r &b80%&r of the time; the other &c20%&r is scrap like nuggets, shafts or even a clock."
		""
		"&aAt the end of each lap, divert anything that isn't an Incomplete Precision Mechanism&r (a filtered Brass Funnel or Tunnel does it). Keep the Deployers topped up with funnels on their backs."
	]
	quest.1879B1ADAA2A35E3.quest_subtitle: "Five laps, one gamble"
	quest.1879B1ADAA2A35E3.title: "&6Clockwork Precision"
	quest.188B3FC091302690.quest_desc: [
		"&6Ars Polymorphia&r adds the &6Polymorph&r recipe picker to the &6Storage Lectern&r's crafting grid."
		""
		"When your ingredients match more than one recipe, a button appears by the output slot. Click it and &apick the result you actually want&r."
	]
	quest.188B3FC091302690.title: "&6Ars Polymorphia&r: Pick a Card"
	quest.189BB88A164E2AE8.quest_desc: [
		"The three &6Heavenly&r warships float at &by 200&r over jungles, forests, deserts, plains and savannas. Find the &6Heavenly Rider&r and the &6Heavenly Conqueror&r."
		""
		"&cWither Skeletons ride Hoglins&r on deck while archers on phantoms circle the hull. A knock-off at this height is fatal, so carry a &ewater bucket&r or &dSlow Falling&r, and an Elytra if you have one."
		""
		"The holds hold piles of diamonds and gold, strong Healing potions and a real chance of a &eTotem of Undying&r."
	]
	quest.189BB88A164E2AE8.quest_subtitle: "Two hundred blocks of nope"
	quest.189BB88A164E2AE8.title: "&bCastles in the Air"
	quest.18A9BAFFFE43AF05.quest_desc: [
		"&eImmortal Stone&r is a cloud Kivi block of one colour in the centre, &e4 Obsidian&r on the edges and &e4 Aluminum Ingots&r in the corners. A cloud Aluminum block in the centre gives &eImmortal Aluminum&r instead."
		""
		"These blocks have a blast resistance of &b9001&r, and &aonly players can break them&r. Withers, the Ender Dragon, creepers and anything else just bounce off. You can still mine them yourself with a pickaxe."
		""
		"&7The quest asks for the blue one; a Light, Red, Green or Dark centre gives that colour instead. Ideal for boss arenas, bunkers and anything you don't want blown up.&r"
	]
	quest.18A9BAFFFE43AF05.quest_subtitle: "Wither? Never heard of her"
	quest.18A9BAFFFE43AF05.title: "&5Built to Last"
	quest.18B172510081C94C.quest_desc: [
		"Put a &eCoffee&r and a &eMilk Bucket&r in the kettle at &b50% heat&r. This one needs no water and no Glass Bottle."
		""
		"&aMilk Coffee&r gives the same &aDeeprush&r as plain coffee but lasts longer, &b2:10&r instead of 1:30."
	]
	quest.18B172510081C94C.quest_subtitle: "Milk, no bottle"
	quest.18B172510081C94C.title: "&fMocha Moment"
	quest.18E0E0964F8C56A4.quest_desc: [
		"Two more ocean finds. The &6Undead Pirate Ship&r is crewed by &cskeleton spawners&r (some of them ride dolphins) and carries diamonds, emeralds and enchanted books."
		""
		"The &6Typhon&r is a huge stone-and-magma &bsea monster statue on the sea floor&r. Nothing guards it, but you'll need to dive: bring &dWater Breathing&r for its chests."
	]
	quest.18E0E0964F8C56A4.quest_subtitle: "Some sailors never left"
	quest.18E0E0964F8C56A4.title: "&3Davy Jones' Locker"
	quest.190C2C2C3E868329.quest_desc: [
		"&6Smoker&r turns smoking into a craft. Build a &6Smoking Station&r from planks, stone bricks and a regular Smoker. &7In this pack the vanilla Smoker runs the same new rules.&r"
		""
		"It has a food slot and a &eplanks&r slot: the planks are both fuel and flavour. The food stays the same item but gains a &bSmoked&r bonus to hunger and saturation."
		""
		"&cSmoke food that's already cooked&r: cook meat in a furnace, on a campfire or on the Stove's grill first."
	]
	quest.190C2C2C3E868329.quest_subtitle: "Smoker fires up the flavour"
	quest.190C2C2C3E868329.title: "&6Where There's Smoke"
	quest.19131D7C629B1AF0.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Source Jar&r (6 Archwood Slabs + 2 Glass) holds &b10,000 Source&r. Machines pull from jars nearby, and a comparator reads how full one is."
		""
		"To move Source, break the jar and carry it (it keeps its contents) or, later, use &6Source Relays&r. Put a jar right next to your Imbuement Chamber."
	]
	quest.19131D7C629B1AF0.quest_subtitle: "No, you can't bucket it"
	quest.19131D7C629B1AF0.title: "&6Not a Fluid"
	quest.191E624E908911FA.quest_desc: [
		"&6XyCraft&r comes in parts: &6World&r adds &eKivi&r stone, glowing &eXychorium&r crystals in five colours, &eAluminum&r and a huge set of connected-texture building blocks. &6Machines&r turns them into simple, unpowered gadgets: colour-coded utility blocks, an &6Extractor&r, an autocrafter and &6tanks built from ordinary blocks&r."
		""
		"There is &cno guide book&r yet. Use &bEMI&r for crafting recipes, and look at a tank or an Extractor to read its contents or status in the &bJade&r overlay. The XyCraft &bModifier Key&r is &bLeft Ctrl&r by default (Controls, XyCraft category); holding it over some items shows extra tooltip info."
		""
		"&7Some items in the creative tab (Gauntlet, Modules, pipes, Hover Pack) are unfinished or hidden behind experimental settings. This chapter only covers what works.&r"
	]
	quest.191E624E908911FA.quest_subtitle: "Aesthetic technology, no batteries required"
	quest.191E624E908911FA.title: "&6Welcome to XyCraft"
	quest.1922F54AB5F4305E.quest_desc: [
		"Cheat the seasons: any &eglass&r block within &b16 blocks directly above&r a crop makes it grow at full speed all year round."
		""
		"Crops &bbelow Y=48&r that can't see the sky are always in season too, so a lit underground farm works as well."
		""
		"&aSmelt sand&r for glass and roof your field."
	]
	quest.1922F54AB5F4305E.quest_subtitle: "Summer, indoors, all year"
	quest.1922F54AB5F4305E.title: "Glass Half Full"
	quest.1950DADFFCAFE77B.quest_desc: [
		"&6Dark Brew&r is brewed on a netherite station from three whiskeys: &eJoJannik&r, &eLilitu Single Malt&r and &eMaggoAllan&r. &cThrow it&r and a &6Booze&r beer elemental bursts out where it lands."
		""
		"Botched brews spawn them too. Defeat one: they drop pub food and patterned wool, and very rarely a Brewfest Hat."
	]
	quest.1950DADFFCAFE77B.quest_subtitle: "A beer that fights back"
	quest.1950DADFFCAFE77B.title: "&cFoam Wars"
	quest.19735FE28D981938.quest_desc: [
		"Ports are the connectors inside XyCraft's logistics blocks. An &eItem Port&r is a &eChest&r and &e2 Gold Nuggets&r, shapeless; Create's &eBrass Nuggets&r work too. A &eFluid Port&r is a &eBucket&r and &e2 Aluminum Nuggets&r. Each recipe makes four."
		""
		"You'll need them for the &6Extractor&r, the &6Valve&r, the &6Soaryn Box&r and nearly everything else from here on."
	]
	quest.19735FE28D981938.quest_subtitle: "Ins and outs"
	quest.19735FE28D981938.title: "&6Port Authority"
	quest.19827B375291AD0F.quest_desc: [
		"The &dEnd Portal Stabilizer&r fixes one Unstable End Portal Frame per charge, and it has &b12 charges&r: exactly one portal. &aRight-click a frame&r with it and let the sparks settle."
		""
		"There are two ways to make one, and both take the best your base can do:"
		"&d- Ars Nouveau:&r an &6Enchanting Apparatus&r with a &eNether Star&r in the middle and a &eWilden Tribute&r, 2 &eNetherite Ingots&r, 2 &eEcho Shards&r, 2 &eEyes of Ender&r and a &eSource Gem Block&r on the pedestals (&b10,000 source&r)."
		"&6- Create:&r a &6sequenced assembly&r on a &eNether Star&r: &b3 loops&r of Netherite Ingot, Precision Mechanism, Eye of Ender, &b1,000 mB&r Liquid Experience and an Echo Shard, then a press."
		""
		"&7It can't be enchanted or repaired. Frames that are already stable are skipped without using a charge.&r"
	]
	quest.19827B375291AD0F.quest_subtitle: "Twelve charges, one portal"
	quest.19827B375291AD0F.title: "&dHold It Together"
	quest.19B1BBA873A3D569.quest_desc: [
		"Put the three parts in the &6Modern Foundry Station&r and take out a &ePickaxe&r. If the slots look wrong, pick the Pickaxe layout from the &bbuttons on the left&r of the screen."
		""
		"Each material adds a &btrait&r. Stone is &bstonebound&r (it speeds up as it wears down), flint is &bjagged&r and copper is &bdwarven&r. Mix and match."
		""
		"&aTo repair it&r, put the tool and some of its &ehead material&r in the Station. A broken tool doesn't vanish. It just stops working until you fix it."
	]
	quest.19B1BBA873A3D569.quest_subtitle: "Your very first custom tool"
	quest.19B1BBA873A3D569.title: "&aPick and Mix"
	quest.19C221B9DC0194E9.quest_desc: [
		"Beer goes with food. Cook a &eBeer&r and a &ePorkchop&r on the Farm \\& Charm &6Stove&r for &e4 Pork Knuckles&r."
		""
		"Brewery's pub dishes give &bStoutheart&r: knockback resistance and slow healing. &7Look up Pretzels, Sausages and Dumplings in EMI for more.&r"
	]
	quest.19C221B9DC0194E9.quest_subtitle: "Never drink on an empty stomach"
	quest.19C221B9DC0194E9.title: "&6Pub Grub"
	quest.19CC1210A35376FA.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Fondue Pot&r (Iron Ingots and Sticks) melts cheese. &cIt needs a heat source below it&r, just like the Cookpot, so set it on your Tiled Stove."
		""
		"A whole &eCheese Wheel&r fills &b3 portions&r, a single slice fills 1. Then &aright-click the pot with Bread&r to dip it and get a &eCheese Stick&r."
		""
		"&7Fondue night is better with friends. Bring bread.&r"
	]
	quest.19CC1210A35376FA.quest_subtitle: "Dip responsibly"
	quest.19CC1210A35376FA.title: "&6Melting Pot"
	quest.1A213869D5CCF571.quest_desc: [
		"&dInfusion&r: place the item in the enchanting table. If your stats fit its recipe, the &bthird slot&r turns into an infusion for &b3 Lapis&r and some levels."
		""
		"Infused shelves give &b5 Eterna&r up to &b60&r. Upgrade them with Glowstone, Fire Charges and Blaze Powder, Prismarine Crystals or a Heart of the Sea for more Eterna, Quanta or Arcana."
		""
		"Enchant at level 60. That needs &6Ascent&r active."
	]
	quest.1A213869D5CCF571.quest_subtitle: "Enchant at level 60"
	quest.1A213869D5CCF571.title: "&dInfused With Power"
	quest.1A239E7CAE296BE7.quest_desc: [
		"With Amendments, the &6Cauldron&r holds &bany liquid&r: honey, milk, potions and dye."
		""
		"&aClick dye into a water cauldron&r to colour it; mix dyes for custom shades. Dip leather armour and other dyeable items in to colour them (4 per layer). You can also &dmix potions&r in it, up to &b8 effects&r, but opposite effects cancel out."
		""
		"Scoop dyed water out with a &eGlass Bottle&r to get a &eDye Bottle&r. Craft it with a dyeable item to apply that exact colour."
		""
		"&cA cauldron over a heat source boils, and boiling liquid hurts.&r"
	]
	quest.1A239E7CAE296BE7.quest_subtitle: "Something's brewing, and it's teal"
	quest.1A239E7CAE296BE7.title: "&dCauldron Chemistry"
	quest.1A44B57A6BD4A606.quest_desc: [
		"&b3 Flax&r in a vertical column make &e3 Rope&r. There is no String recipe for rope in this pack, so flax it is."
		""
		"Hang rope under ceilings, fences and walls, or stick it to block sides. Vertical rope is &aclimbable&r, and &asliding down it cancels fall damage&r. Stretch it sideways and you can tightrope-walk across."
		""
		"&bUse rope on a hanging rope&r to extend it downward, and &bShift + right-click with an empty hand&r to haul it back up, along with any block tied to the end."
		""
		"&cRope burns fast&r, and breaking it drops everything hanging below."
	]
	quest.1A44B57A6BD4A606.quest_subtitle: "Climb it, slide it, hang things from it"
	quest.1A44B57A6BD4A606.title: "&eRope Trick"
	quest.1AD6061FF39DA212.quest_desc: [
		"&e4 Andesite Casings&r around a &eLarge Cogwheel&r make &b2&r &6Chain Conveyors&r. Right-click two of them with &eChains&r to link them, up to &b32 blocks&r apart. Packages ride the links, and so can you: &bright-click a chain while holding a Wrench&r."
		""
		"A &6Package Frogport&r is a &eSlimeball&r, an &eItem Vault&r (a Barrel between two Iron Sheets) and &eAndesite Alloy&r in a column. Right-click a conveyor with it first, then place it within &b5 blocks&r and give it an address."
		""
		"A frog works with the inventory (or Packager) below it: packages addressed elsewhere get &asent off along the chain&r, and packages for its own address get &asnatched off the chain&r and dropped in."
	]
	quest.1AD6061FF39DA212.quest_subtitle: "Ribbit-based logistics"
	quest.1AD6061FF39DA212.title: "&aTongue Twister"
	quest.1AD67BF0D07F614B.quest_desc: [
		"&eArchwood&r is the mod's building wood. It comes in four colours: &9Cascading&r, &cBlazing&r, &aFlourishing&r and &5Vexing&r. A lone tree can turn up in almost any overworld biome, and the rare &bArchwood Forest&r is full of them, plus magical creatures and fruit."
		""
		"Any colour makes &eArchwood Planks&r. Grab a few saplings of each colour: several ritual tablets later want a &bspecific&r log."
		""
		"&7The Dowsing Rod (Gold Ingot + 2 Archwood Planks) reveals Budding Amethyst and makes magical creatures glow within 75 blocks.&r"
	]
	quest.1AD67BF0D07F614B.quest_subtitle: "Four flavours of magic wood"
	quest.1AD67BF0D07F614B.title: "&aBarking Up the Right Tree"
	quest.1AF2EF3402560251.quest_desc: [
		"Your first rite. Draw &f4 white Base glyphs&r one block out from the altar on its &bfour sides&r (north, south, east, west). Drop &e1 Amethyst Shard&r and &e1 Bone Meal&r inside, then &aright-click the altar&r: you get &e4 Amethyst Shards&r back."
		""
		"A bare altar is &btier I&r and can only cast this and &dMinor Binding&r (light grey Base glyphs on the &bcorners&r instead; String + Copper Ingot for 12 Glowstone Dust)."
		""
		"&7Leftover chalk from an old circle can make the altar lock onto the wrong rite. Rub it out first.&r"
	]
	quest.1AF2EF3402560251.quest_subtitle: "Minor Focus, tier I, 20 ƒ"
	quest.1AF2EF3402560251.title: "&dThe Apprentice's Circle"
	quest.1AF84958217B88C7.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Mini Fridge&r (&e5 Iron Ingots&r and &e1 Redstone&r) freezes things, no ice biome or Silk Touch needed. Put one item in its slot and wait:"
		"&eWater Bottle&r to &eIce&r, &eIce&r to &ePacked Ice&r, &ePacked Ice&r to &eBlue Ice&r, and a &eWater Bucket&r to a &ePowder Snow Bucket&r."
		""
		"&aEvery cocktail needs Ice&r, so keep the fridge busy. &7Blue Ice also makes a fast boat road.&r"
	]
	quest.1AF84958217B88C7.quest_subtitle: "Ice ice baby"
	quest.1AF84958217B88C7.title: "&bCold Comfort"
	quest.1B036D50868526B2.quest_desc: [
		"With 8 runes underneath, your altar is &btier II&r. Now &eFluxite&r becomes renewable."
		""
		"&dMagicka Solidificus&r (&b150 ƒ&r): &9blue Triads&r on the four corners and &eyellow Serpents&r on the four sides, all one block out. Drop &e6 Stone&r, &e1 Diamond&r and &e1 Lily of the Valley&r inside for &b24 Fluxite&r."
		""
		"Tier II also opens &dMinor Arcana&r, &dFlame Bloom&r (blaze rods), &dCrystallized Fertilization&r (amethyst farmland), &dThe Written Pact&r and the &dVigils&r of the Verdant Tide and Clear Skies, which hold the altar for many minutes."
		""
		"&7Here's a diamond for your next cast.&r"
	]
	quest.1B036D50868526B2.quest_subtitle: "Tier II: Magicka Solidificus"
	quest.1B036D50868526B2.title: "&dStone Taught to Remember"
	quest.1BBF80282594103E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Nature's Compass&r (a compass ringed with saplings and logs): right-click, choose a biome and press &bStart Search&r. It points the way and the top-left of your screen shows coordinates and distance."
		""
		"It finds modded biomes too - handy for cherry groves, mushroom fields or that one biome a recipe needs."
	]
	quest.1BBF80282594103E.title: "&aWhere the Wild Things Grow"
	quest.1C209590A3A4FD48.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Hose Pulley&r (&eCopper Casing&r, a &eDried Kelp Block&r and a &eCopper Sheet&r) lowers a hose to drain or fill a body of fluid. Give it rotation to lower the hose, then pump the fluid away through pipes on its other side."
		""
		"A lake of &b10,000 or more blocks&r counts as &ainfinite&r: it never runs dry and the world isn't touched. That works for water and for &clava&r, so a Nether lava sea can feed Blaze Cakes and Sturdy Sheets forever."
	]
	quest.1C209590A3A4FD48.quest_subtitle: "The bottomless bucket"
	quest.1C209590A3A4FD48.title: "&cLava on Tap"
	quest.1C3BAFD6A4BF67F0.quest_desc: [
		"&6Supplementaries&r adds about a hundred vanilla-style gadgets: rope, jars, sacks, safes, cannons, flutes, globes, slingshots, quivers, redstone toys and a lot of decor. Its companion &6Amendments&r teaches vanilla blocks new tricks, and the add-on &6Supplementaries Squared&r brings extra variants."
		""
		"There is &cno guide book&r. Instead, &bhover over an item&r and read its &btooltip hint&r, and use &bEMI&r for recipes (including the odd ones, like the Safe and Rope Arrow)."
		""
		"This chapter is a guided tour. The main path follows the rope all the way to a &cpirate galleon&r; the side branches cover storage, travel, gadgets, home and the add-ons."
		""
		"&7Moonlight is the library underneath. It has no items or quests of its own.&r"
	]
	quest.1C3BAFD6A4BF67F0.quest_subtitle: "A junk drawer full of good ideas"
	quest.1C3BAFD6A4BF67F0.title: "&6Odds \\& Ends"
	quest.1C583E591EAE5EDA.quest_desc: [
		"The next lift upgrade starts with &eEnd Stone&r, &6crushed&r into &eEnd Stone Powder&r with Crushing Wheels."
		""
		"End Stone normally means a trip to the End. Can't wait? &6Ars Nouveau&r's &dConjuration Essence&r turns ordinary stone into End Stone in a crafting grid (see the Ars Nouveau chapter)."
	]
	quest.1C583E591EAE5EDA.quest_subtitle: "Grinding the End down to size"
	quest.1C583E591EAE5EDA.title: "&eStardust"
	quest.1CC11A25B1C4AE3E.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Swivel Bearing&r (wooden slab, Block of Industrial Iron, Cogwheel) grabs the block in front of it; glue on whatever else should swing. Power its cog and that group assembles into its own contraption on a &bphysics joint&r."
		""
		"A shaft passes straight through and keeps turning, redstone &bunlocks&r it to spin freely, and it tops out at &b96 RPM&r. Rotating propeller pods, turrets, drawbridges."
	]
	quest.1CC11A25B1C4AE3E.quest_subtitle: "Turrets, pods and very fancy doors"
	quest.1CC11A25B1C4AE3E.title: "&eSwivel Chair"
	quest.1CCFD27EC00D45E6.quest_desc: [
		"&6Lili's Pottery&r turns clay into vases, pots and urns. &cEMI doesn't show what the Pottery Table and Kiln make&r, so here's how they work."
		""
		"Craft the &6Pottery Table&r from an &eIron Ingot&r, &eLeather&r, &eRedstone&r, a &eCauldron&r and &ePlanks&r. It works like a &bstonecutter&r: put in a &eClay Ball&r, pick a shape, and &b1 clay ball becomes 1 piece&r."
		""
		"There are nine shapes: Vase, Bud Vase, Cupella, Garden Pot, Square Pot, Plant Bowl, Planter, Urn and Amphore. Plain clay gives terracotta-coloured pieces. &7Garden and Square Pots hold flowers, even tall ones.&r"
	]
	quest.1CCFD27EC00D45E6.quest_subtitle: "Lili's Pottery: get your hands dirty"
	quest.1CCFD27EC00D45E6.title: "&6Table for Two Hands"
	quest.1CDAACCBA23A2F3D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Wild strawberries&r grow almost everywhere: plains, meadows, rivers, forests, taigas, savannas and jungles."
		""
		"Crafting a strawberry gives only &b1 seed&r. Chop it on a &6Cutting Board&r or crank it through a &6Mincer&r for &b4&r instead."
		""
		"&aYou'll want plenty:&r they go into jam, tea, salads, oatmeal and Grandma's famous cake."
	]
	quest.1CDAACCBA23A2F3D.quest_subtitle: "The sweetest thing in the hedgerow"
	quest.1CDAACCBA23A2F3D.title: "&cBerry Good"
	quest.1CE312B9C35EB217.quest_desc: [
		"A second template, a &eBlaze Burner&r and an &eAnvil&r in a Smithing Table make the &6Blaze Forger&r. Pick its mode on the side panel:"
		""
		"&aMerge&r combines two matching items or books with no repair cost. &aApply&r puts a filled Enchanting Template onto an item. &aExtract&r pulls one enchantment off an item, book or template onto a blank template."
		""
		"Blank &eEnchanting Templates&r come from pressing a &eBlock of Experience&r in a &6Mechanical Press&r."
	]
	quest.1CE312B9C35EB217.quest_subtitle: "The anvil, minus the grumbling"
	quest.1CE312B9C35EB217.title: "&6Forged in Fire"
	quest.1D13727DA9E66510.quest_desc: [
		"&eShatterbrand&r is the Hollow's sword: &b9&r attack damage, and every hit leaves its target briefly &cInfected&r."
		""
		"It only comes from &eLoot Bags&r, and it's the rarest item in them. Open every bag you get."
	]
	quest.1D13727DA9E66510.quest_subtitle: "The rarest thing in the bag"
	quest.1D13727DA9E66510.title: "&5Shatterbrand"
	quest.1D20F21FCF643CA4.quest_desc: [
		"&bAir pressure&r drops with height, so balloons lift less and propellers push less up high. The &6Altitude Sensor&r (Paper, Iron Sheet, Andesite Casing) gives a signal by elevation; set the range in its UI, or invert it."
		""
		"Wear goggles to read pressure and exact height. Wire an inverted sensor to the burner and it can hold a cruising altitude for you."
		""
		"For hands-on control, the &6Throttle Lever&r (Stick on Brass Casing) sets &b0-15&r by dragging."
	]
	quest.1D20F21FCF643CA4.quest_subtitle: "The higher you go, the less you get"
	quest.1D20F21FCF643CA4.title: "&bThin Air"
	quest.1D56F0B5766AD135.quest_desc: [
		"&6Mountain Towers&r stand in mountains, groves, ice spikes and snowy plains. The &6Cryomancer&r inside is &aneutral&r: ink, ice scrolls, a map to the &6Impaled Icebreaker&r, and an &eIce Rune&r for &e2 Icy Fangs&r."
		""
		"Icy Fangs come from &cIce Spiders&r in snowy biomes. Strays drop &eFrozen Bones&r, the ice focus."
		""
		"&7The Icebreaker's captain kept a &ePermafrost Shard&r&7, the heart of the Ice Staff.&r"
	]
	quest.1D56F0B5766AD135.quest_subtitle: "The Cryomancer is in"
	quest.1D56F0B5766AD135.title: "&bA Cold Reception"
	quest.1D8DE6C04B68AEF6.quest_desc: [
		"&eBlazebloom Goo&r is a &ePrimogel Goo&r surrounded by &e4 Blaze Powder&r, &e2 Redstone&r and &e2 Nether Wart&r. Wake it with &eNether Wart&r or &eBlaze Powder&r."
		""
		"It works &b2x&r faster than Primogel and still does every Primogel conversion. Higher goo always covers the lower recipes, faster."
	]
	quest.1D8DE6C04B68AEF6.quest_subtitle: "Tier 2, from the Nether"
	quest.1D8DE6C04B68AEF6.title: "&cFeeling the Bloom"
	quest.1DB21866D2727996.quest_desc: [
		"A &eCopper Sheet&r, a &eBarrel&r and another &eCopper Sheet&r in a column make a &6Fluid Tank&r. Tanks merge into one: up to &b3x3&r wide and &b32&r blocks tall, &b8 buckets&r per block."
		""
		"&cYou can't empty buckets into a tank by hand in survival&r, so fill it through pipes and pumps. To pour in a bucket, empty it into an &6Item Drain&r and pipe it across. A Wrench toggles the window."
		""
		"&7Four tanks is also the smallest possible boiler. Hint, hint.&r"
	]
	quest.1DB21866D2727996.quest_subtitle: "8 buckets a block"
	quest.1DB21866D2727996.title: "&bTanks a Lot"
	quest.1DC1598292DD94A0.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Merchant Campsite&r is a ring of tents in the &bplains, meadows and sunflower plains&r, with a lone merchant villager and an &aIron Golem&r keeping watch. Nothing here wants to hurt you."
		""
		"Check the &emap chest&r: it always holds an explorer map to an &6Illager Campsite&r or an &6Illager Fort&r. That's your way into the illager branch."
	]
	quest.1DC1598292DD94A0.quest_subtitle: "A friendly face on the road"
	quest.1DC1598292DD94A0.title: "&eTents and Trinkets"
	quest.1E0D75D892AE31CE.quest_desc: [
		"Craft an &eEngagement Ring&r from &e7 Gold Ingots&r and a &eDiamond&r, or use 7 rose gold ingots for the rose gold ring."
		""
		"Gift it to a villager with &b50+ hearts&r and you are &aengaged&r. Hugs and kisses land more often from here on. Villagers already engaged or married to someone else, and your own relatives, will turn you down."
	]
	quest.1E0D75D892AE31CE.quest_subtitle: "Down on one knee"
	quest.1E0D75D892AE31CE.title: "&ePut a Ring on It"
	quest.1E11F5EB8888BD44.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Field Guide&r can't be crafted. It is the reward of the Guild Commission &e\"Welcome to WilderNature\"&r: take it from the board when it shows up and explore a &bPlains&r."
		""
		"The guide lists each animal's temper, health, favourite food, where it spawns, and whether you can breed or tame it."
	]
	quest.1E11F5EB8888BD44.quest_subtitle: "First Edition"
	quest.1E11F5EB8888BD44.title: "&aKnow Your Neighbours"
	quest.1E5D075E2955D689.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Cheese Press&r is made from &eWooden Slabs&r and &eSticks&r. (Its id and advancement call it a Cheese Form, and EMI files it under Cheese Forming.)"
		""
		"Put in &b1 milk bucket&r and &b1 Rennet&r and wait &b90 seconds&r. You get a cheese wheel and the empty bucket back."
		""
		"&aIt is hopper-friendly:&r Rennet in from the top, milk from the side, cheese out of the bottom."
	]
	quest.1E5D075E2955D689.quest_subtitle: "Form your future"
	quest.1E5D075E2955D689.title: "&6Press Pass"
	quest.1ECCEBBA69434E4F.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Fish Trap&r (bamboo and string) catches fish on its own. &aPlace it in water&r, or hang it from a &eRope&r or a Fish Net Fence. Right-click it with bait, wait for the bubbles, then collect with an empty hand."
		""
		"&cBaits are not shown in EMI:&r"
		"&eWheat Seeds&r: 3 Cod. &eSweet Berries&r: 3 Salmon."
		"&eMelon Seeds&r: 2 Tropical Fish. &eBeetroot Seeds&r: 2 Pufferfish."
		"&7Each catch uses one bait and takes about a minute.&r"
	]
	quest.1ECCEBBA69434E4F.quest_subtitle: "Fishing while you're AFK"
	quest.1ECCEBBA69434E4F.title: "&9Trap Set, Fish Get"
	quest.1EDC99E543E0B6B8.quest_desc: [
		"&eBrass Sheets&r, &eAndesite Alloy&r, a &ePrecision Mechanism&r and &eBrass Casing&r build a &6Mechanical Arm&r. It picks items up and sets them down anywhere within &b5 blocks&r."
		""
		"&cSet it up before you place it.&r Hold the arm and right-click targets: once for &bblue (take from)&r, again for &byellow (put into)&r, left-click to clear. It handles belts, depots, funnels, basins, crafters, deployers, blaze burners and more, but &cchests need a funnel&r."
		""
		"&7Its value panel sets how it shares items between outputs (Round Robin, Forced Round Robin or Prefer First); a redstone signal pauses it.&r"
	]
	quest.1EDC99E543E0B6B8.quest_subtitle: "Point, click, delegate"
	quest.1EDC99E543E0B6B8.title: "&6Armed and Ready"
	quest.1F03FE98E7E0BABA.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Storage Lectern&r (Lectern + 4 Chests on the Apparatus) is a storage terminal with a crafting grid. &aWand chests to it&r within &b30 blocks&r; named inventories become tabs."
		""
		"It needs &6Bookwyrms&r: &beach one gives access to 8 inventories&r. Get their charms from a &dRitual of Awakening&r augmented with a &eBook and Quill&r, and use them on the lectern."
		""
		"&7Repositories (4 Archwood Logs + 4 Gold Nuggets) are double chests that keep their names.&r"
	]
	quest.1F03FE98E7E0BABA.quest_subtitle: "Bookwyrms not included (yet)"
	quest.1F03FE98E7E0BABA.title: "&6Library Card"
	quest.1F0C82E411F40D08.quest_desc: [
		"&b4 Iron Ingots and 4 Glass&r make &b8&r &eFramed Glass&r, the cleanest window in the game (stained and pane versions too). &b8 Iron Ingots&r make &b24&r &eIron Plates&r; surround a water bucket with plates for the &eRusty&r kind."
		""
		"Pair them with &eGlass Item Frames&r: the frame vanishes once filled, and a map in one &aupdates live&r."
	]
	quest.1F0C82E411F40D08.quest_subtitle: "Rivets not included"
	quest.1F0C82E411F40D08.title: "&fHeavy Metal Decor"
	quest.1F198698B3F8F1C0.quest_desc: [
		"Mesh a &eLarge Cogwheel&r diagonally with a small one. Large driving small &adoubles the speed&r; small driving large halves it."
		""
		"This is how you turn a Water Wheel's &b8 RPM&r into &b16&r, then &b32 RPM&r. Remember the stress rule: the faster machine also costs more."
		""
		"&cNever let two sources fight&r (opposite directions, or a gear loop). Create breaks a block to settle the argument."
	]
	quest.1F198698B3F8F1C0.quest_subtitle: "Two times faster, two times hungrier"
	quest.1F198698B3F8F1C0.title: "&eShifting Gears"
	quest.1F1C611A76328D31.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Lost Caves&r (&6YUNG's Cave Biomes&r) lie under the &bhottest, driest land&r: dig down below deserts and badlands. Ancient sandstone, prickly vines and &cregular sandstorms&r that slow you down and narrow your view."
		""
		"Right-click a fruiting cactus to pick a &ePrickly Peach&r. &6Sand Snappers&r love them: hold a peach to lure one, &aright-click to feed it&r, and it goes digging for a gift, sometimes a pottery sherd or an armour trim."
		""
		"&7Don't poke a cactus that has no fruit. It pokes back.&r"
	]
	quest.1F1C611A76328D31.quest_subtitle: "Bring a scarf"
	quest.1F1C611A76328D31.title: "&eSand in Your Boots"
	quest.1F2F26A9498356A1.quest_desc: [
		"Right-click a placed &eBrass Casing&r with a &eSturdy Sheet&r to make &6Train Casing&r (a Deployer can do it too)."
		""
		"It's the heart of the railway: it builds &bbogeys&r, &6Train Stations&r, &6Train Controls&r, &6Signals&r, &6Observers&r and train doors."
	]
	quest.1F2F26A9498356A1.quest_subtitle: "Brass casing, reinforced"
	quest.1F2F26A9498356A1.title: "&eLocomotive Ambitions"
	quest.1F57537DD1409C11.quest_desc: [
		"&aRight-click a fully grown crop&r (wheat, carrots, potatoes, beetroot, nether wart, cocoa) and Quark harvests it and replants it for you. An empty hand works fine."
		""
		"A &eHoe&r also clears grass, crops and leaves in a &b3-wide&r swath, or &b5-wide&r with diamond and netherite hoes."
		""
		"&7Feed a Poisonous Potato to a baby animal for a small chance it stays tiny forever.&r"
	]
	quest.1F57537DD1409C11.quest_subtitle: "Grab, replant, repeat"
	quest.1F57537DD1409C11.title: "&aCrop Til You Drop"
	quest.1F645E8DC11F634F.quest_desc: [
		"&6Sleepy Hollows&r adds one haunted biome: a dark pine forest under a black sky, thick with fog, tombstones and glowing pumpkins. It hides a &6Cemetery&r where you can summon the &cHorseman&r."
		""
		"Look in the &bmiddle of big Old Growth Pine Taiga&r areas, away from rivers and coasts. A &eNature's Compass&r (from &6Kitted Out&r) can search for the biome by name."
		""
		"&7The mod has no guide book. This chapter is the guide, EMI has every recipe, and the mod's advancement tab tracks a few milestones.&r"
	]
	quest.1F645E8DC11F634F.quest_subtitle: "Is it foggy in here, or is it just me?"
	quest.1F645E8DC11F634F.title: "&5Into the Hollow"
	quest.1FA894D1CEB786FF.quest_desc: [
		"Put a &eLightning Rod&r on top of a &eBlock of Experience&r and wait for a thunderstorm. When lightning hits the rod, the block below becomes a &eBlock of Super Experience&r, and the charge can spread to XP blocks next to it."
		""
		"&7Lay out a 3x3 of XP blocks with the rod in the middle to make the most of each strike.&r"
	]
	quest.1FA894D1CEB786FF.quest_subtitle: "Wait for a storm"
	quest.1FA894D1CEB786FF.title: "&eLightning in a Block"
	quest.1FB0A77FCDA59217.quest_desc: [
		"Bake &eDough&r and a &eWater Bucket&r on the &6Stove&r for &b3 Farmer's Bread&r."
		""
		"It's a placeable loaf: &aset it on a table and everyone can eat it by the slice&r. Any bread counts for a Farmer's Breakfast, but this one is the proper farmhouse kind."
	]
	quest.1FB0A77FCDA59217.quest_subtitle: "Crusty outside, fluffy inside"
	quest.1FB0A77FCDA59217.title: "&eOur Daily Bread"
	quest.1FCE2B65EA6A85A5.quest_desc: [
		"&eNether Wart&r grows on &eSoul Sand&r in the little wart gardens inside Nether Fortresses."
		""
		"It is the base of almost every potion, so &aplant it on Soul Sand back home&r and you will never have to hunt for it again."
	]
	quest.1FCE2B65EA6A85A5.quest_subtitle: "It grows on you"
	quest.1FCE2B65EA6A85A5.title: "&cWart Hunting"
	quest.20173946B50CB89F.quest_desc: [
		"Wear the &eKinetic Belt&r and &bhold jump&r in the air to &aglide&r: less gravity, more momentum, softer landings. Its other ability adds extra &bcharm&r slots."
		""
		"&7It has an electric synergy with the &eGlitchy Mantle&7, listed on the relic's Synergies tab. Wear both and see.&r"
	]
	quest.20173946B50CB89F.quest_subtitle: "Who needs an elytra?"
	quest.20173946B50CB89F.title: "&bGliding Gracefully"
	quest.206A599E229153D3.quest_desc: [
		"Power, stone and magic: your factory has it all. Now break the rules."
		""
		"Get a &6Blaze Forger&r seething with a &eCake o' Enchanting&r, set it to &aMerge&r, and combine two items or books that already share a maxed enchantment. The result goes &done level past the cap&r."
		""
		"&bPick the enchantment carefully:&r Apothic Enchanting raises many caps in this pack (Efficiency goes to IX), and Mending and Infinity can't be pushed at all. Two &bSilk Touch&r books (cap: I) are the easy route."
		""
		"&cKeep a Lightning Rod close by. The advancement goes to the player who placed the Forger.&r"
		""
		"&7Electric power, endless stone and enchantments that ignore the rules. Create would be proud.&r"
	]
	quest.206A599E229153D3.quest_subtitle: "Caps are merely suggestions"
	quest.206A599E229153D3.title: "&6Overclocked"
	quest.208C561A80F3E9C7.quest_desc: [
		"&ePlate Armor&r is built in the &6Station&r from a &eplating&r part and &eMaille&r. Cast the plating from metal. Maille can be cast too, or shaped in the Part Builder from leather, vines or copper."
		""
		"&cMake plating sand casts in the Part Builder&r, with sand in the pattern slot, since you have no plating to press into a cast yet. Each piece has &b3 defense&r and &b2 upgrade&r modifier slots."
	]
	quest.208C561A80F3E9C7.quest_subtitle: "Proper armor, finally"
	quest.208C561A80F3E9C7.title: "&ePlated and Grated"
	quest.20A2D91B74D16B7A.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Imbuement Chamber&r (6 Archwood Planks + 2 Gold Ingots) soaks items in &dSource&r to transform them. It is the main way to make Source Gems."
		""
		"It &aslowly gathers Source by itself&r, so it works before you own a single jar. Once you have jars, it also draws from &6Source Jars&r within &b2 blocks&r, so it no longer waits on its own slow trickle."
		""
		"Place an item inside by right-clicking. The reward will get you started."
	]
	quest.20A2D91B74D16B7A.title: "&6Steeped in Magic"
	quest.20C5C5C8E0C51EB7.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Portable Storage Interface&r is Andesite Casing plus a Chute. Put one on your contraption and one on the ground, lined up with a &b1 or 2 block gap&r."
		""
		"When they meet, the contraption pauses and the ground side exposes &aall its storage&r to funnels and chutes. Unload the harvest without stopping the machine for good."
	]
	quest.20C5C5C8E0C51EB7.quest_subtitle: "Pit stop!"
	quest.20C5C5C8E0C51EB7.title: "&eDrive-by Exchange"
	quest.20DA68DCB802120A.quest_desc: [
		"Forge the full empyrite set (&b24 ingots&r: Helm, Cuirass, Tassets and Greaves), &dawaken all four&r and wear them together."
		""
		"Two awakened pieces grant &6Emberproof&r: fire immunity and half lava damage. All four grant &6Radiant Aegis&r: &b15%&r less damage, attackers that hit you in melee catch fire, and your awakened gear resonates twice as fast."
		""
		"&7From here: Resonance V, an imbuement on every piece, and the tier V rites. The circle never really closes.&r"
	]
	quest.20DA68DCB802120A.quest_subtitle: "Crowned in current"
	quest.20DA68DCB802120A.title: "&6The Empyrean Regalia"
	quest.210448F2F700E4F6.quest_desc: [
		"The &eMidnight Mantle&r is the deepest relic: four abilities that unlock at relic levels &b0, 5, 10 and 15&r, a first level that costs ten times the usual relic XP, and up to &brank 7&r."
		""
		"&dLunar Phase&r scales with the moon in the sky: switch between &bfull moon&r (damage and attack speed) and &bnew moon&r (health and regeneration) in the &bLeft Alt&r menu. Later it hides you in darkness, scatters constellations when you're hit and calls down &dfalling stars&r when you attack."
		""
		"Find it in &6End city&r or &6Better Stronghold&r chests. Research it, wear it, and start the long climb."
	]
	quest.210448F2F700E4F6.quest_subtitle: "Wear the night sky"
	quest.210448F2F700E4F6.title: "&9Over the Moon"
	quest.2147A88670739AAD.quest_desc: [
		"&b3 Bamboo&r in a column make a &6Flute&r. &aRight-click a tamed pet or horse&r to bind it; one flute holds up to &b5 animals&r."
		""
		"Play the flute and every bound animal within &b64 blocks&r teleports to you, unless it's sitting. Horses, camels, llamas, donkeys, dogs, cats and parrots all answer."
		""
		"&7You must bind animals first: an unbound flute does nothing here.&r"
	]
	quest.2147A88670739AAD.quest_subtitle: "Here boy! Here horse!"
	quest.2147A88670739AAD.title: "&aThe Pied Piper"
	quest.218A12D4AF1334F0.quest_desc: [
		"&eIron Ore&r is common in stone and deepslate. Mine it for &eRaw Iron&r and &asmelt it&r in your furnace into &eIron Ingots&r."
		""
		"Iron goes into tools, armour, buckets, rails and half the machines in this pack. You'll never have enough."
		""
		"&7Grab any &eCopper&7 you pass too. The next furnace upgrade wants it.&r"
	]
	quest.218A12D4AF1334F0.quest_subtitle: "The metal everything wants"
	quest.218A12D4AF1334F0.title: "&fIron Age"
	quest.21BD62B4F639E38D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Simple Storage Network&r links your chests into one searchable inventory. Lay &eNetwork Cable&r (iron and stone slabs), then craft the &6Storage Network Root&r from a diamond, &eNether Quartz&r and cable."
		""
		"&cOnly one Root per network.&r Each &eLink Cable&r (cable and a chest) connects one inventory - a chest, a barrel or a Sophisticated chest."
		""
		"The network only runs while the &bRoot's chunk is loaded&r, so force-load it on the &6FTB Chunks&r map. Craft a book with a cable for the &eNetwork Guide Book&r."
	]
	quest.21BD62B4F639E38D.quest_subtitle: "Every chest, one screen"
	quest.21BD62B4F639E38D.title: "&6The Heart of the Network"
	quest.221835575611F04D.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Aluminum Wrench&r is three &eAluminum Ingots&r and one &eXychorium gem&r of any colour, laid out in the shape of a wrench."
		""
		"Hit a XyCraft machine with it to &apick the block up instantly&r. &bHold attack&r to keep grabbing more. &bRight-click&r with it to rotate or configure machines, such as flipping an &6Item IO&r between fill and drain."
	]
	quest.221835575611F04D.quest_subtitle: "The actuator"
	quest.221835575611F04D.title: "&7Twist and Shout"
	quest.22359A592E3D201A.quest_desc: [
		"Open &b100 Lootr containers&r. The advancement itself hands you the &eCentennial Trophy&r, a little statue for your mantelpiece."
		""
		"&7By now you've seen more of this world than most. Show it off.&r"
	]
	quest.22359A592E3D201A.quest_subtitle: "A trophy for the trophy hunter"
	quest.22359A592E3D201A.title: "&6A Hundred Lids Lifted"
	quest.2242AFC6A0DD8A48.quest_desc: [
		"Craft &e9 Green Tea Leaves&r into a &6Green Tea Leaf Block&r and &aplace it anywhere&r, indoors or out. It dries in stages over just under &b4 minutes&r while the chunk is loaded. Once it has become a &6Dried Green Tea Leaf Block&r, break it for &e3 Dried Green Tea&r."
		""
		"&cDon't break a block while it is still drying:&r it drops its ingredients and starts over. Placing a few blocks side by side keeps a batch going."
	]
	quest.2242AFC6A0DD8A48.quest_subtitle: "Patience is the secret ingredient"
	quest.2242AFC6A0DD8A48.title: "&2Hang Them Out to Dry"
	quest.2253116026ABCF99.quest_desc: [
		"Use a &eHeart of Diamond&r on plain stone and a &atame Stoneling&r builds itself a new body. It carries an item for you and follows anyone holding a &eGlow Shroom&r."
		""
		"&7You'll want a second heart for this, since the first belongs in your Pickarang.&r"
	]
	quest.2253116026ABCF99.quest_subtitle: "A new body for an old heart"
	quest.2253116026ABCF99.title: "&7Young Dreamer"
	quest.225614A6D4788B6D.quest_desc: [
		"&6FTB Essentials&r gives everyone a few handy commands:"
		"&b/sethome&r and &b/home&r (one home), &b/spawn&r, &b/back&r (your last teleport &aor death spot&r), &b/tpa <player>&r to ask to teleport to a friend, and &b/trashcan&r to void junk."
		""
		"&b/rtp&r throws you somewhere random &b500 to 25,000&r blocks from the centre of the world. It has a &c10 minute cooldown&r and can drop you inside someone else's claim."
	]
	quest.225614A6D4788B6D.quest_subtitle: "Commands for the weary traveller"
	quest.225614A6D4788B6D.title: "No Place Like /home"
	quest.2273E696FCA9C53B.quest_desc: [
		"The &cPharaoh&r is a husk decked out in gold, with an enchanted golden sword, a shield and &b30 hearts&r of health. Defeat him to lift the &cMining Fatigue&r from that temple for good."
		""
		"His tomb chests hold gold, emeralds, &ediamonds&r, enchanted books and sometimes an &eEnchanted Golden Apple&r. &7Bring food, armour and a decent sword.&r"
	]
	quest.2273E696FCA9C53B.quest_subtitle: "Put the Pharaoh back to bed"
	quest.2273E696FCA9C53B.title: "&6Mummy Issues"
	quest.227B0D678EE9E82C.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Windmill Bearing&r turns whatever is attached in front of it. Build a frame of &eWindmill Sails&r (any &ewool&r block counts as a sail too), then &bright-click the bearing&r to start it. Right-click again to stop and edit."
		""
		"You need at least &b8 sails&r. Speed is &b1 RPM per 8 sails&r, up to &b16 RPM&r at 128 sails, and each RPM is worth &b512 SU&r. Sails stick to each other, but other blocks need &eSuper Glue&r."
		""
		"&7Going for 128 sails earns the 'A strong Breeze' advancement.&r"
	]
	quest.227B0D678EE9E82C.quest_subtitle: "Big sails, big numbers"
	quest.227B0D678EE9E82C.title: "&bA Mild Breeze"
	quest.22966980BA2BDA76.quest_desc: [
		"&eSmall Connectors&r (Copper Rod, Andesite Alloy and a Slime Ball make 3) sit on machines. Right-click one with a &eCopper Spool&r, then another, to string a wire up to &b16 blocks&r. Each carries &b1,000 FE/t&r and links to up to &b4&r others."
		""
		"&bWrench a connector&r to cycle its mode: a generator needs &aPull&r, a consumer needs &aPush&r, and None just relays. Right-click both ends with an &eEmpty Spool&r to reel the wire back in."
		""
		"&7The Redstone Relay passes power only while it has a redstone signal.&r"
	]
	quest.22966980BA2BDA76.quest_subtitle: "Push, pull or politely relay"
	quest.22966980BA2BDA76.title: "&aMaking Connections"
	quest.22ED0868097AB8F1.quest_desc: [
		"A &eSolrosa&r makes &b4 ƒ/s&r forever with no fuel at all. Pick one up from the oasis floor and &alink it straight to your altar&r with the staff. That's enough for your first rite."
		""
		"They're renewable: &adrop a &ePrismarine Shard&a onto a placed &eWither Rose&r and the rose turns into a Solrosa. With &6Create&r, a fan blowing through soul fire haunts Poppies into Wither Roses (a recipe from this pack's Ultimate Factory add-on), so no Wither needed."
	]
	quest.22ED0868097AB8F1.quest_subtitle: "Solrosa"
	quest.22ED0868097AB8F1.title: "&eThe Free Trickle"
	quest.230342E5AD171391.quest_desc: [
		"&eWild Coffee&r grows in &ajungles&r. Break it for &eCoffee Beans&r and plant them on farmland. A grown bush can be &aright-clicked&r for beans, like sweet berries."
		""
		"Brew &eCoffee Beans&r with a &eGlass Bottle&r at &b50% heat&r. &aDeeprush&r gives &bHaste&r to the other players near you, and the deeper you stand the stronger it gets. &cAbove Y 50 it does nothing&r, so share it in the mines."
		""
		"&7Your first sip also hands you 12 Coffee Beans and a Milk Bucket. Funny, that.&r"
	]
	quest.230342E5AD171391.quest_subtitle: "A round for the mining crew"
	quest.230342E5AD171391.title: "&6Espresso Yourself"
	quest.2322131793D1E165.quest_desc: [
		"A ruined arena in the &bplains, meadows and sunflower plains&r. The &6Coliseum&r has no chests: &athe loot is on the gladiators&r."
		""
		"&cThe gladiator is a giant Phantom&r ridden by a heavily armoured skeleton archer with a &bPower V&r bow and &cLevitation&r arrows. Shoot the phantom down, then deal with the rider. Defeated gladiators drop diamonds, emeralds, iron and gold."
		""
		"&7Don't wait for sunrise: this phantom has Fire Resistance and won't burn. Keep a water bucket handy for the Levitation.&r"
	]
	quest.2322131793D1E165.quest_subtitle: "The crowd wants blood. Preferably not yours."
	quest.2322131793D1E165.title: "&6Are You Not Entertained?"
	quest.2341C23096A9A104.quest_desc: [
		"&aAccept&r a bounty to get its contract: &bHunt&r (track down and kill a creature), &bGather&r (hold items), &bObserve&r (look at an animal through a &eSpyglass&r) or &bExplore&r (visit a biome)."
		""
		"You can hold &bonly one contract at a time&r. When it is done, put the contract in the board's turn-in slot and press &aClaim&r for loot and XP."
		""
		"&7Watch for Guild Commissions: special contracts with unique rewards.&r"
	]
	quest.2341C23096A9A104.quest_subtitle: "One contract at a time"
	quest.2341C23096A9A104.title: "&eSigned, Sealed, Delivered"
	quest.239A39634EFFB38C.quest_desc: [
		"Put &bfour Wheel Mounts&r under a glued chassis, drive them from a &6Portable Engine&r through shafts and gearboxes, add a seat and assemble it with the &6Physics Assembler&r."
		""
		"Steer by sending redstone into the &bsides&r of the front mounts with &6Redstone Links&r and a &6Linked Typewriter&r or Linked Controller. A &6Redstone Inductor&r eases the signal in and out for gentler steering."
		""
		"&cSharp turns at full speed can roll a car over.&r Ease off the RPM."
		""
		"&7Handy maths: one engine at 32 RPM supplies exactly what four mounts need at that speed (4 x 16 SU per RPM).&r"
	]
	quest.239A39634EFFB38C.quest_subtitle: "Are we there yet?"
	quest.239A39634EFFB38C.title: "&aRoad Trip!"
	quest.23A57524B0B4DF33.quest_desc: [
		"Fill a &6Feeding Trough&r with &eseeds&r and animals within &b8 blocks&r wander over, eat and &abreed on their own&r. A &6Water Trough&r, filled with a water bucket, shortens their breeding cooldown when they drink."
		""
		"Set both up in your pens and the herd grows while you're off adventuring."
		""
		"&7It takes plantable seeds (vanilla and Farm \\& Charm), melon and pumpkin seeds, plus carrots, potatoes and onions.&r"
	]
	quest.23A57524B0B4DF33.quest_subtitle: "Love is in the hay"
	quest.23A57524B0B4DF33.title: "&6Feed and Water"
	quest.23CF6F91CC240BF3.quest_desc: [
		"Chests in &bforest and jungle biomes&r favour the &eLeafy Mantle&r strongly. It lets you &aslip through leaves&r, land on them safely and heal while you're surrounded by foliage. At relic level 5 it can &acancel a killing blow&r by eating the leaves around you."
		""
		"&7It takes the back slot, the same one your elytra and backpack want.&r"
	]
	quest.23CF6F91CC240BF3.quest_subtitle: "Forest chests, back slot"
	quest.23CF6F91CC240BF3.title: "&2Turn Over a New Leaf"
	quest.23D76C906C218B0B.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Redstone Coil&r is a two-block-tall zapper turret made from a comparator, an iron block, a redstone block and a redstone torch."
		""
		"&bIt needs a redstone signal&r: the stronger the signal, the more damage and range. Right-click to switch target: &bFishes&r, &bMonsters&r, &bPlayers&r (not your team) or &bNone&r. It hits targets in water or in iron armour harder."
		""
		"&7Shields that block its zaps lose durability.&r"
	]
	quest.23D76C906C218B0B.quest_subtitle: "Rudimentary, reliable, very slow"
	quest.23D76C906C218B0B.title: "&cShock and Trawl"
	quest.2421C0DF003105FD.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Heavenly Challenger&r is the deadliest of the three sky ships, also at &by 200&r. Its Wither Skeletons wear netherite and swing &cnetherite swords&r and axes, and phantom and hoglin riders back them up."
		""
		"The treasure is the best in the overworld skies: &enetherite helmets, boots and pickaxes&r, netherite ingots and Enchanted Golden Apples."
		""
		"&7All three Heavenly ships can also spawn over the End's outer islands. Remember that for the next quest.&r"
	]
	quest.2421C0DF003105FD.quest_subtitle: "The admiral is not taking visitors"
	quest.2421C0DF003105FD.title: "&cDreadnought"
	quest.24296DB5FCD0047B.quest_desc: [
		"&6When Dungeons Arise: Seven Seas&r adds &bfive ships&r that sit on the surface of any &bocean&r. They're spread out, roughly one per 1,000 blocks of open water, so a fast boat and a spyglass help."
		""
		"Start with the &6Small Yacht&r: a few vindicators or a pillager with a &cMultishot&r crossbow, and a villager on board. The treasure has an enchanted book, diamonds or emeralds, and enchanted chainmail."
		""
		"&7No advancements for these ships: the quests tick when you step aboard.&r"
	]
	quest.24296DB5FCD0047B.quest_subtitle: "Yo ho ho and a bottle of potion"
	quest.24296DB5FCD0047B.title: "&3Set Sail"
	quest.2432B5B63C0D9B38.quest_desc: [
		"Craft &e4 Barrels&r in a square for a &6Big Barrel&r. It holds &b9&r beers or whiskeys: right-click with a drink to put it in, &bShift + right-click&r takes the last one out."
		""
		"Every &b7 in-game days&r inside, a drink gains a quality level, up to a fourth level when the barrel turns golden. Aged drinks last longer, hit harder and &amake you less drunk&r."
	]
	quest.2432B5B63C0D9B38.quest_subtitle: "Patience, in oak"
	quest.2432B5B63C0D9B38.title: "&6Barrel-Aged"
	quest.24C3D397B153516D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Crabs&r scuttle along beaches and pinch anyone who gets too close. Use a &eWater Bucket&r on one to scoop it up."
		""
		"They breed with &eWheat&r, &eChicken&r or any &eFish&r. Kill them for &eCrab Legs&r (cook them for a hearty meal) and, sometimes, a &eCrab Shell&r: brew it into an Awkward Potion for a &dPotion of Stability&r (Resilience, knockback resistance)."
	]
	quest.24C3D397B153516D.quest_subtitle: "Snip snip"
	quest.24C3D397B153516D.title: "&cFeeling Crabby"
	quest.24D57EE5C30ACA0E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Create Crafts \\& Additions&r brings &belectricity&r (Forge Energy, FE) to Create. It starts with the &6Rolling Mill&r: craft it from &eIron Sheets&r, two &eShafts&r, &eAndesite Alloy&r and an &eAndesite Casing&r."
		""
		"Give it rotation, drop ingots or sheets on top, then right-click to take the output. &aIngots roll into 2 rods, sheets into 2 wires.&r A belt with funnels automates it."
	]
	quest.24D57EE5C30ACA0E.quest_subtitle: "Crafts \\& Additions, step one"
	quest.24D57EE5C30ACA0E.title: "&aRolling Thunder"
	quest.250E8DD145FC34CB.quest_desc: [
		"&eManyullyn&r is the classic Tinkers summit. In a smeltery fuelled with &eBlazing Blood&r, melt &eCobalt&r and &eAncient Debris&r together: &b3 ingots&r of molten cobalt and &b1 ingot&r of molten debris make &b4 Manyullyn Ingots&r."
		""
		"Make a &eBlock of Manyullyn&r and then put it to use: build a tool with a manyullyn head. It mines at &bnetherite tier&r, and its &bambush&r trait hits harder when you or your target is at full health."
		""
		"&aYou've mastered the Foundry.&r Melted, cast, alloyed and hammered: every tool from here on is your own design."
	]
	quest.250E8DD145FC34CB.quest_subtitle: "The purple endgame"
	quest.250E8DD145FC34CB.title: "&5Manyullyn Masterpiece"
	quest.251316F431356DAB.quest_desc: [
		"The real treasure is in the galleon's &6Safe&r. Its password is simply &e\"Key\"&r, so the ship's own Key &aor any freshly crafted, un-renamed Key&r opens it."
		""
		"Inside: diamonds, emeralds, gold, spectral arrows, sea-themed enchanted books, maybe a &9Blue Bomb&r, and usually the &dBlast Armor Trim&r smithing template. It is the &conly place&r that template comes from."
		""
		"Copy it like any vanilla template: the template, &e7 Diamonds&r and a &eCobblestone&r make two, so you never need to sail out again."
		""
		"&7No template in this safe? It's a chance, not a promise. Another galleon is out there.&r"
	]
	quest.251316F431356DAB.quest_subtitle: "X marks the safe"
	quest.251316F431356DAB.title: "&6Plunder the Plunderers"
	quest.251DF967B1D9FBD4.quest_desc: [
		"Treasure enchantments like &dMending&r never appear in the table... unless a &6Deepshelf of Arcane Treasures&r is in range. Make it from 2 Deepshelves, Diamonds, Gold Blocks and an Emerald Block."
		""
		"&cCurses count as treasure too.&r Load a &6Seashelf of Aquatic Filtration&r with Curse books to ban them, or wash curses off afterwards with a &ePrismatic Cobweb&r in an anvil."
	]
	quest.251DF967B1D9FBD4.quest_subtitle: "Deepshelf of Arcane Treasures"
	quest.251DF967B1D9FBD4.title: "&6Mending, Finally"
	quest.254956BC5F50F76C.quest_desc: [
		"&dConjure Magelight&r is a cheap first glyph: just a &eTorch&r and a &eLantern&r at the Scribe's Table. Cast on a block it leaves a permanent magic light; cast on yourself it gives Night Vision."
		""
		"Right-click a glyph item to learn it. &cThe glyph is used up when you learn it&r, so let this quest tick before you read it."
		""
		"&7Other cheap Tier I picks: Craft (a Crafting Table), Item Pickup (2 Hoppers), Amplify (a Diamond Pickaxe).&r"
	]
	quest.254956BC5F50F76C.title: "&dLet There Be Light"
	quest.2559929169258CC8.quest_desc: [
		"&eAstralite Ore&r generates in every overworld biome between &bY -64&r and &bY 42&r. Mine it for &eRaw Astralite&r (Fortune works) and smelt or blast it into &eAstralite Ingots&r. Nine nuggets make an ingot."
		""
		"&cQuirk in this version:&r the ore is tagged so a &cdiamond pickaxe gets no drop&r. Use an iron or netherite one."
		""
		"You'll need a lot of it: runes, goggles, the cauldron and nearly every device. &7Later the cauldron doubles your ore.&r"
	]
	quest.2559929169258CC8.quest_subtitle: "Astralite"
	quest.2559929169258CC8.title: "&9Star-Metal"
	quest.25611303498B6180.quest_desc: [
		"A &eScroll&r holds a single &dspell&r. Find them in the same chests as essence, buy them from &6Wandering Traders&r, or hunt &cNecromancers&r, which spawn in the dark like any other Overworld monster and sometimes drop one."
		""
		"&aRight-click&r a scroll to cast its spell once with no mana and no cooldown. The scroll is used up."
		""
		"&7Better idea: keep it. Written into a spell book, the same spell can be cast forever.&r"
	]
	quest.25611303498B6180.quest_subtitle: "Read once, then gone"
	quest.25611303498B6180.title: "&eWords of Power"
	quest.25DDF695E8D312D2.quest_desc: [
		"Wild &6grape bushes&r grow in patches in plains, forests, rivers, swamps, meadows and the mountains. &aRight-click a ripe bush&r to pick its grapes and keep the bush. &aBreak it&r and a ripe one drops &b2-3 seeds&r instead."
		""
		"Any grape also crafts into &b1 seed&r, so even a single bunch can start a vineyard. Seeds grow into new bushes on any solid block and take bone meal."
		""
		"&7No luck? The &6Wandering Winemaker&r sometimes visits with his mules and sells every grape seed for an emerald each.&r"
	]
	quest.25DDF695E8D312D2.quest_subtitle: "Somewhere a bush is waiting"
	quest.25DDF695E8D312D2.title: "&aWild Harvest"
	quest.25F0F4B19EAC7DA6.quest_desc: [
		"Four &dTier Runes&r overhaul a spawner's core stats. The &eFrontiersman's&r rune (Timeworn Fabric from salvaged Uncommon gear, Clocks, Flint) sets &b7&r mobs per spawn with a 150-600 tick delay."
		""
		"Wayfarer's needs Luminous Shards and any spawn egg, Mountaineer's an Infused Rune, a Sigil of Malice and a Warden Tendril. Thundering, the best, sets &b16&r mobs every &b20 ticks&r."
		""
		"&cTier runes set values, they don't add.&r A lower rune on an already upgraded spawner downgrades it, so only ever go up."
	]
	quest.25F0F4B19EAC7DA6.quest_subtitle: "Tier Runes"
	quest.25F0F4B19EAC7DA6.title: "&aFrontiersman's Upgrade"
	quest.26093DA16B0C3200.quest_desc: [
		"A &eFurnace&r surrounded by four &eMud Bricks&r makes the &6Kiln&r. It &apaints pottery&r: load a pottery piece, any &eDye&r and normal furnace fuel. The menu shows a live preview of the colour."
		""
		"&bFire it again with another dye to blend the colours.&r The paint stays on when you place and break the piece."
		""
		"&7A painted vase is still the same item, so tick this off yourself once you've fired one.&r"
	]
	quest.26093DA16B0C3200.quest_subtitle: "Paint by fire"
	quest.26093DA16B0C3200.title: "&cTurn Up the Heat"
	quest.2623FCB0A62AAE83.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Oak Base Cabinet&r is storage with style: &eOak Slabs&r, &eSticks&r and a &eChest&r make two. Craft a Cabinet together with an &6Oak Desk&r (&eOak Planks&r and &eSticks&r) and you get a &6Dresser&r."
		""
		"The &6Coffer&r (&eWool&r and two &eIron Nuggets&r) is a little chest that &akeeps its contents when you break it&r, like a shulker box. Perfect for moving house."
		""
		"&7Desks placed side by side join into one long desk. The finale wants a placed Oak Desk too, so make a spare.&r"
	]
	quest.2623FCB0A62AAE83.quest_subtitle: "A place for everything"
	quest.2623FCB0A62AAE83.title: "&6Cabinet Maker"
	quest.26500EC58A1FD912.quest_desc: [
		"Fish meals are crafted with a &eBowl&r, which you get back after eating. &eSalmon Rolls&r (salmon and kelp) are ready to eat. &eCod Meal&r (cod, kelp, potato) and &ePuffer Platter&r (pufferfish, potato) must be &acooked first&r: raw ones give Hunger or Poison."
		""
		"&aSalmon Rolls&r and &aCooked Cod Meal&r give &bLuck&r for a few minutes, which means better fishing loot. A cooked Puffer Platter gives one random effect."
		""
		"&7Cook them on a Camping Grill for extra food value.&r"
	]
	quest.26500EC58A1FD912.quest_subtitle: "Feeling lucky?"
	quest.26500EC58A1FD912.title: "&aCatch of the Day"
	quest.2653B6F065CE1091.quest_desc: [
		"The &eBlazejet Wand&r (Blazegold and Ferricore) fires an &bAir Burst&r that launches you wherever you look."
		""
		"While it's in your hand you &atake no fall damage&r, and it has Lava Repair like other Blazegold gear."
		""
		"&7Later it upgrades into the Voidshift Wand (teleport where you look) and the Eclipsegate Wand (briefly opens a hole through the blocks you click).&r"
	]
	quest.2653B6F065CE1091.quest_subtitle: "No fall damage, no problem"
	quest.2653B6F065CE1091.title: "&eJet Set"
	quest.266501CB41F0ADD0.quest_desc: [
		"Blow a fan's air through a &bcatalyst&r and every item caught in the stream beyond it gets processed: dropped items, items on a &6Depot&r, or on a belt."
		"&bWater&r: Washing. Gravel gives Flint and &eIron Nuggets&r, and a Magma Block becomes Obsidian."
		"&bFire or a Campfire&r: Smoking. Cooks food."
		"&bLava&r: Blasting. Smelts ores and sand &awith no fuel&r, but &cburns food and anything it can't smelt&r."
		"&bSoul Fire or a Soul Campfire&r: Haunting."
		""
		"&7EMI doesn't list fan recipes in this pack. Hold W over an Encased Fan to see Ponder's processing scenes.&r"
	]
	quest.266501CB41F0ADD0.quest_subtitle: "Wash, smoke, blast, haunt"
	quest.266501CB41F0ADD0.title: "&bProcessing by Particle"
	quest.26729217FECE73FD.quest_desc: [
		"&6Bounty Boards&r turn up in villages, or craft one from oak planks, logs, paper and a &ediamond&r. Right-click it and take a bounty: bring items or hunt mobs &cbefore the timer runs out&r."
		""
		"New bounties appear every &b45 seconds&r or so. Everyone sees the same board but takes their own copy - great for groups."
	]
	quest.26729217FECE73FD.quest_subtitle: "Inquire within"
	quest.26729217FECE73FD.title: "&6Help Wanted"
	quest.26B6C1D8F7C7A481.quest_desc: [
		"Put a &eSource Gem&r in the &6Imbuement Chamber&r and 3 themed items on pedestals &bwithin 1 block&r of it. For &b2000 Source&r you get an essence. &aThe pedestal items are not used up.&r"
		""
		"&eEarth&r: Iron Ingot, Seeds, Dirt. &eManipulation&r: Stone Button, Redstone, Clock. Also &eFire&r, &eWater&r and &eAbjuration&r from everyday items (see EMI)."
		""
		"&cTwo need mob drops:&r &eAir&r takes a &eWilden Wing&r, and &eConjuration&r a &eWilden Horn&r plus a &eStarbuncle Token&r."
		""
		"&7Manipulation Essence recolours Archwood saplings, so one colour of tree is enough.&r"
	]
	quest.26B6C1D8F7C7A481.quest_subtitle: "Seven flavours of essence"
	quest.26B6C1D8F7C7A481.title: "&dElemental, My Dear"
	quest.26BBDC2B0FC40EC2.quest_desc: [
		"&6Supplementaries Squared&r is an add-on full of variants:"
		"&a- &6Copper&r, &6Brass&r and &6Crimson Lanterns&r that you can &aswitch on and off&r. Copper uses &eCopper and Blaze Powder&r; Brass needs Create brass."
		"&a- &6Plaques&r: 3 iron, gold or copper ingots make 3 wall plates with &beditable text&r. Perfect storage labels."
		"&a- &6Coloured Sacks&r (a sack plus dye), &6Gold Candle Holders&r, &6Metal Frames&r and Daub stairs and slabs."
		""
		"&7Coloured sacks still count towards being Overencumbered.&r"
	]
	quest.26BBDC2B0FC40EC2.quest_subtitle: "More of everything, squared"
	quest.26BBDC2B0FC40EC2.title: "&6Supplementaries Squared"
	quest.26D67D75741F33A9.quest_desc: [
		"The witches keep prisoners. Look for small &ewooden cages&r hanging on chains from posts beside the houses, each holding a captured swamp villager with no job yet. Not every village has one. The cage walls are trapdoors, so &aflip one or break it&r to let them out, but only once the witches are dealt with."
		""
		"&7Like every villager in this pack it becomes an &6MCA&7 villager. A boat is the easiest way to get it across the bog; back home, give it a bed and a job block.&r"
	]
	quest.26D67D75741F33A9.quest_subtitle: "Somebody has to let them out"
	quest.26D67D75741F33A9.title: "&aJailbreak"
	quest.275994DBDF37C35D.quest_desc: [
		"Place your painted piece and &aright-click it with a Honeycomb&r to glaze it. Each honeycomb adds a coat, up to &b8 layers&r, for a deeper shine."
		""
		"&cOnly plain-clay pieces count for this quest&r, so glaze a painted terracotta-coloured one, not a Red Vase."
		""
		"&7Changed your mind? Hold a Brush on a piece for about 5 seconds to strip the paint off.&r"
	]
	quest.275994DBDF37C35D.quest_subtitle: "...and on, and on"
	quest.275994DBDF37C35D.title: "&eWax On, Wax On"
	quest.275CAA5DAE97F13F.quest_desc: [
		"Mix &e3 Raw Gold&r and &e1 Raw Copper&r into &b4&r &eRose Gold Dust&r, then smelt the dust into &eRose Gold Ingots&r."
		""
		"Both romance rings have a &6rose gold&r version that works exactly the same, so your proposal costs a quarter less gold. Rose gold also goes into the &6Villager Tracker&r (find a villager by name) and the &6Civil Registry&r (a book of village events)."
	]
	quest.275CAA5DAE97F13F.quest_subtitle: "Budget bling"
	quest.275CAA5DAE97F13F.title: "&dPink Is the New Gold"
	quest.278D01E079B7783F.quest_desc: [
		"Every overworld wood, the Let's Do woods included, gets structural pieces. &6Beams&r come from two &eStripped Logs&r, &6Supports&r from &ePlanks&r and a &eStick&r, and &6Railings&r from &eSlabs&r and &eSticks&r."
		""
		"&aRight-click a Support or Railing with an Axe&r to switch its shape (a Railing goes full, half or quarter height). &aRight-click a Support with a Board&r to brace it (not on its extended shape). &6Boards&r (one slab makes two) stack in layers when you add more, and an Axe takes one off."
	]
	quest.278D01E079B7783F.quest_subtitle: "Load-bearing aesthetics"
	quest.278D01E079B7783F.title: "&6Up to Code"
	quest.279858C6FEB893ED.quest_desc: [
		"The biome has its own soundtrack, and you can take it home: the &eMusic Disc&r plays &7Elias Thornwick - Into the Hollows&r."
		""
		"&6Coffins&r in a Cemetery have a &b10%&r chance to hold one. Or do it the classic way: get a &cCreeper&r killed by a &cSkeleton&r."
	]
	quest.279858C6FEB893ED.quest_subtitle: "Spooky beats to fight bosses to"
	quest.279858C6FEB893ED.title: "&dGrave Grooves"
	quest.27A99280DDF68521.quest_desc: [
		"&6Hearth \\& Timber&r is Furniture's sibling for walls, roofs and everything structural. It has no advancements, so this branch is all crafting."
		""
		"A ring of &e8 Sticks&r makes two &6Timber Frames&r, and adding more sticks gives the &6Cross&r, &6Diagonal&r and &6Grid&r patterns. &aRight-click a frame with any full block to fill it&r: plaster, bricks, planks, stone. The block is used up. &bRight-click with a Pickaxe&r to take it back out."
		""
		"&7A row of filled frames over a stone base is the classic half-timbered cottage.&r"
	]
	quest.27A99280DDF68521.quest_subtitle: "Hearth \\& Timber: the outside matters too"
	quest.27A99280DDF68521.title: "&6Framed!"
	quest.28210AD37A98F119.quest_desc: [
		"The &eShield of Retaliation&r is held, not worn. &bHold right-click&r to open a short &bparry window&r: a hit from the front during it is blocked. &cIf you parry nothing, the next hit hurts more.&r At rank 1 it can catch projectiles and throw them back."
		""
		"The same Nether chests hold the &eSphere of Self-Sacrifice&r (pay a third of your health, get twice that back over time) and the &eGhostly Mantle&r (suffocating mist, and a last-second escape at level 10)."
	]
	quest.28210AD37A98F119.quest_subtitle: "Timing is everything"
	quest.28210AD37A98F119.title: "&cPerfect Parry"
	quest.2844561D5D793B8E.quest_desc: [
		"A &eStaff&r casts your selected spell with a plain &aright-click&r. The &eGraybeard Staff&r is a &eWooden Shovel&r, an &eIron Ingot&r and one &eArcane Essence&r."
		""
		"It adds &b10%&r spell power and &b25%&r mana regeneration while held."
		""
		"&7Fancier staffs come later, most of them tuned to one school.&r"
	]
	quest.2844561D5D793B8E.quest_subtitle: "+10% spell power, +25% mana regen"
	quest.2844561D5D793B8E.title: "&aNo Longer Short-Staffed"
	quest.285D496E2F135F58.quest_desc: [
		"Drop &eBlaze Ember&r into Polymorphic Fluid for &eUnrefined Blaze Ember Fuel&r, then let &6Blazebloom Goo&r refine the source into &eBlaze Ember Fuel&r."
		""
		"The &6Simple Fuel Generator&r (Blazegold, Redstone, Buckets and a Blast Furnace) burns it at &b450 FE per mB&r. One ember makes one bucket, so that's &b450,000 FE&r, about double what the same ember gives in the coal generator."
		""
		"&7Later: Voidflame Coal dropped into Blaze Ember Fuel, refined by VoidShimmer Goo, gives Voidflame Fuel (1,300 FE/mB). Eclipse Ember into Voidflame Fuel plus Shadowpulse Goo gives Eclipse Ember Fuel (4,000 FE/mB).&r"
	]
	quest.285D496E2F135F58.quest_subtitle: "Twice the power, half the coal"
	quest.285D496E2F135F58.title: "&6Liquid Courage"
	quest.2878612E1EC9DE00.quest_desc: [
		"Find a wild &6Whirlisprig&r in a forest and &agrow a tree near it&r to earn its token. Its charm also wants a &eMagebloom&r, a &eMagebloom Seed&r, a Diamond and some saplings on the pedestals. Use the charm on any &eflower&r with a chest beside it and Source nearby."
		""
		"It produces logs, crops, seeds and flowers based on the plants within &b10 blocks&r of its flower, without harvesting them. A bigger, more varied garden makes it happier and more productive (its mood can take a few minutes to update)."
	]
	quest.2878612E1EC9DE00.title: "&aGreen Thumbs Up"
	quest.289713AE1A6338DC.quest_desc: [
		"Point an &6Encased Fan&r through &ePowder Snow&r for &bBulk Freezing&r (or use a Freezing Catalyst from Create: Connected)."
		""
		"It turns &eBlaze Rods&r into &eBreeze Rods&r, steps Ice up to Packed and then Blue Ice, and turns Magma Cream into Slime Balls. &aNo Trial Chamber needed.&r"
	]
	quest.289713AE1A6338DC.quest_subtitle: "Blaze, meet breeze"
	quest.289713AE1A6338DC.title: "&bIce Ice Breezy"
	quest.2899A11208C360EE.quest_desc: [
		"A &eGold Block&r on &6Blazebloom Goo&r becomes &eRaw Blazegold Ore&r in &b60 seconds&r. Smelt the raw drops into &eBlazegold Ingots&r."
		""
		"Blazegold tools mine at diamond level with &b1,440&r durability and have &aLava Repair&r: drop the item into a lava source and it comes back fully repaired. &cThe lava turns to obsidian&r, so bring a bucket."
		""
		"Blazegold also unlocks swappers, wands, fluids and the &eHammer&r upgrade (3x3 mining)."
	]
	quest.2899A11208C360EE.quest_subtitle: "Fireproof bling"
	quest.2899A11208C360EE.title: "&6Blazegold Rush"
	quest.28B8FC92A7AFB524.quest_desc: [
		"&6Create: Enchantment Industry&r turns experience into a fluid: &b1 mB&r of &eLiquid Experience&r is 1 XP point. Start with the &6Mechanical Grindstone&r: 8 &eAndesite Alloy&r around a &eShaft&r."
		""
		"It works like a grindstone and sandpaper in one, and &astrips enchantments&r off gear. Right-click an &6Item Drain&r with it to make a &6Grindstone Drain&r, then put a second Mechanical Grindstone on top: what it grinds (XP nuggets, disenchanted gear) collects below as Liquid XP."
		""
		"&7XP sources: Nuggets of Experience from crushing ores, and mobs killed by Deployers (and sometimes Crushing Wheels) now drop nuggets too.&r"
	]
	quest.28B8FC92A7AFB524.quest_subtitle: "Create: Enchantment Industry"
	quest.28B8FC92A7AFB524.title: "&aGrind Your Gears"
	quest.28E44721BBE2CCA8.quest_desc: [
		"&6Create: Dragons Plus&r adds fluids and fan processes, and it is the base for Enchantment Industry. Its first block is the &6Fluid Hatch&r: a &eCopper Ingot&r and an &eItem Drain&r, crafted together."
		""
		"Put it on a &6Fluid Tank&r. Right-click with a full container to &apour it in&r, and &bsneak-right-click&r with an empty one to fill it from the tank."
	]
	quest.28E44721BBE2CCA8.quest_subtitle: "Create: Dragons Plus"
	quest.28E44721BBE2CCA8.title: "&aHatch a Plan"
	quest.28F7A6514344EDCE.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Seared Melter&r is &e5 Seared Bricks&r and a &eSeared Fuel Gauge&r (4 bricks and 5 glass). It has &b3 item slots&r and holds &bone fluid at a time&r. It can't make alloys."
		""
		"Place it on top of a &6Seared Heater&r (a ring of 8 bricks) that burns normal furnace fuel at &b800°C&r. That is hot enough for &ecopper, gold and iron&r."
		""
		"&7A Seared Fuel Tank filled with lava runs at 1000°C, which you'll need for cobalt and obsidian later.&r"
	]
	quest.28F7A6514344EDCE.quest_subtitle: "A pot that's always on the boil"
	quest.28F7A6514344EDCE.title: "&6Meltdown"
	quest.28F7C22DC24A97B0.quest_desc: [
		"Put it together: a balloon over a &6Hot Air Burner&r on a lever, a &6Portable Engine&r driving your propellers, a seat for the pilot. Glue it all and assemble."
		""
		"To land, come down &aclose to the ground&r, slow to under &b5 m/s&r and level within &b4°&r, then pull any &6Physics Assembler&r's lever. The blocks snap back onto the grid."
		""
		"&7If something renders oddly in the air, try with shaders off: Iris is a known trouble spot.&r"
	]
	quest.28F7C22DC24A97B0.quest_subtitle: "Your first airship"
	quest.28F7C22DC24A97B0.title: "&aLift Off!"
	quest.29161AEF496F359A.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Salvaging Table&r breaks affix gear into &b1-4&r rarity materials: Common into &eMysterious Scrap Metal&r, Uncommon &eTimeworn Fabric&r, Rare &eLuminous Crystal Shards&r, Epic &eArcane Sands&r, Mythic &eGodforged Pearls&r."
		""
		"Gems become dust, and plain iron, diamond or netherite gear gives some of its metal back. Hoppers can feed it."
		""
		"&aTip:&r upgrade smithing templates (slate, stone and one rarity material) step a great roll up a material, &awithout losing its affixes&r: stone tools or chainmail to iron, iron to gold, gold to diamond."
	]
	quest.29161AEF496F359A.quest_subtitle: "Salvaging Table"
	quest.29161AEF496F359A.title: "&6Waste Not"
	quest.2947A481FBE8FB68.quest_desc: [
		"The &eContraption Diagram&r is &ePaper&r plus a whole &6Physics Assembler&r (yes, it eats one). Hang it on an assembled contraption and right-click: it draws every &bforce arrow&r and marks the &bcentre of mass&r."
		""
		"Weight matters. Wool, envelopes and wooden slabs weigh &b0.25&r, planks and logs &b0.5&r, most blocks &b1&r, stone &b2&r, storage blocks like Iron Blocks &b4&r. Build hulls from wood, not stone."
		""
		"&7If your ship tilts, the diagram tells you which end to put a counterweight on.&r"
	]
	quest.2947A481FBE8FB68.quest_subtitle: "Where is the middle, exactly?"
	quest.2947A481FBE8FB68.title: "&eBalance Sheet"
	quest.296E9E4A611F5D96.quest_desc: [
		"&eSourceberry&r bushes grow wild in &bTaiga&r and &bArchwood Forest&r biomes. Eating the berries gives &dMana Regeneration&r, and they brew into a Mana Regen potion."
		""
		"Plant a patch near home: a summoned &6Starbuncle&r will harvest ripe bushes for you, and Sourceberry foods are prime fuel for a Mycelial Sourcelink later."
	]
	quest.296E9E4A611F5D96.title: "&aBerry Magical"
	quest.2971AFDA1F741525.quest_desc: [
		"&6Shadowpulse Goo&r turns a &eBudding Amethyst&r into a &dBudding Time Crystal&r, so place the goo right next to one in a geode. &cThe result can never be picked up&r, not even with Silk Touch, so it grows where it stands."
		""
		"It must charge in three places in order: the &bOverworld&r (blue particles), then &bthe Nether&r (orange), then &bthe End&r (green, buds start growing). It changes colour when a stage is done. Move it with linked &6Swappers&r, which work across dimensions."
		""
		"Only a full &eTime Crystal Cluster&r drops a &eTime Crystal&r; breaking a smaller bud wastes it. Growing buds drain the charge, and an empty crystal goes back to the Overworld to start again. &cMoving it on its own shatters its buds&r, so harvest first."
		""
		"Nine crystals make a &eTime Crystal Block&r, and that block plus Shadowpulse Goo makes another budding crystal."
		""
		"&7No geode nearby? Apothic Enchanting's infusion and Ars Nouveau's Amethyst Golem can both make Budding Amethyst. Carrying crystals randomly gives you Speed or Slowness for a few seconds.&r"
	]
	quest.2971AFDA1F741525.quest_subtitle: "A crystal that has been everywhere"
	quest.2971AFDA1F741525.title: "&dWibbly Wobbly, Timey Wimey"
	quest.2976A5159059EC69.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Curios&r slots open from the button on your inventory screen or with &bG&r. You can wear your backpack in the &bback&r slot."
		""
		"With &6Elytra Slot&r, an &eElytra&r goes in that same back slot, so you can fly and still wear a chestplate. There is only &cone back slot&r though: backpack or elytra."
		""
		"&aTip:&r a backpack works fine from your inventory, so keep the back slot free for wings later."
	]
	quest.2976A5159059EC69.quest_subtitle: "One back, many wishes"
	quest.2976A5159059EC69.title: "Strapped In"
	quest.298EDE1B047F0DBA.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Mechanical Harvester&r collects &bfully grown&r crops it passes and replants them. The &6Mechanical Plough&r tills soil into farmland, clears grass and flowers, and flings mobs out of the way."
		""
		"Mount a row of harvesters on a piston or bearing that sweeps over your field."
	]
	quest.298EDE1B047F0DBA.quest_subtitle: "Farming on autopilot"
	quest.298EDE1B047F0DBA.title: "&aCrop Circles"
	quest.29A699F58619AB00.quest_desc: [
		"Cast a &6Foundry Controller&r by pouring &b1000 mB&r of molten &eObsidian&r (one melted obsidian block) over a &eScorched Bricks&r block in a basin."
		""
		"Build it like a Smeltery, but &ccorners and edges are required&r. The Foundry &bcan't alloy&r, so nothing mixes by accident. It also gives &aore byproducts&r: iron ore yields bonus &esteel&r, gold yields cobalt, and copper yields gold."
		""
		"&7Open the Foundry's screen to finish.&r"
	]
	quest.29A699F58619AB00.quest_subtitle: "Ore in, bonus out"
	quest.29A699F58619AB00.title: "&6The Fantastic Foundry"
	quest.29E791D3683F25EE.quest_desc: [
		"&eVoidShimmer Goo&r is a &eBlazebloom Goo&r with &e4 Ender Pearls&r, &e2 End Stone&r and &e2 Dragon's Breath&r. Feed it an &eEnder Pearl&r or &eChorus Fruit&r."
		""
		"Dragon's Breath is bottled from the Ender Dragon's breath attack, so bring Glass Bottles to the fight in &6the End&r. Already beaten her? &aFour End Crystals on the exit portal respawn her.&r VoidShimmer works &b5x&r faster than Primogel."
	]
	quest.29E791D3683F25EE.quest_subtitle: "Tier 3, courtesy of a dragon"
	quest.29E791D3683F25EE.title: "&dShimmer and Shine"
	quest.2A086CE35B6E90B5.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pyromancer Towers&r rise in hills, forests, plains and swamps. The &6Pyromancer&r who lives there is &aneutral&r and trades ink, fire scrolls, Fire Ale and a map to the &6Mangrove Hut&r."
		""
		"He also swaps &e4 Chained Books&r for a &eFire Rune&r, once per restock. Chained Books only turn up on the bookshelves of the Nether &6Citadel&r, so for now &e8 Blaze Rods&r around a blank rune is the easier way."
		""
		"&cWizards guard their stuff:&r open a chest or barrel near any neutral wizard and they turn hostile."
	]
	quest.2A086CE35B6E90B5.quest_subtitle: "The Pyromancer is in"
	quest.2A086CE35B6E90B5.title: "&cSmoke Signals"
	quest.2A4FC1EBBCD37302.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Small Blimp&r is one of the most common Dungeons Arise builds: it floats about &b20 blocks above&r most land biomes. A few skeleton spawners are on board."
		""
		"&aPillar up&r with scaffolding (here's some) and search the treasure chests: dungeon loot, enchanted iron gear and a chance of a map to the &6Plague Asylum&r or the &6Mining Complex&r."
		""
		"&7Bigger ships fly much higher. Treat this one as practice.&r"
	]
	quest.2A4FC1EBBCD37302.quest_subtitle: "Look up for once"
	quest.2A4FC1EBBCD37302.title: "&bLoftier Ambitions"
	quest.2A8B4A98EC575D5D.quest_desc: [
		"&eTrain Casing&r and an &eElectron Tube&r make &b4&r &6Train Signals&r. Place one beside a selected track: signals cut the line into &bsegments&r, and only one train may be in a segment at a time."
		""
		"Scheduled trains won't pass a signal from behind, so &atwo-way track needs signals facing both ways&r. Before a junction, wrench a signal into a &bcross signal&r: it only lets a train in if it can leave straight away, so a queue never blocks the junction."
		""
		"&7Redstone forces a signal red, and Nixie Tubes can be attached to show its state.&r"
	]
	quest.2A8B4A98EC575D5D.quest_subtitle: "One train per block"
	quest.2A8B4A98EC575D5D.title: "&cRed Light, Green Light"
	quest.2A9922308B582900.quest_desc: [
		"Two new flowers grow in the wild. &dLavender&r grows in mountain biomes like &ameadows&r and &acherry groves&r. &cHibiscus&r grows in &ajungles&r."
		""
		"&cThey drop the opposite way around:&r &aShear Lavender&r to get &eLavender Blossom&r, but &abreak Hibiscus by hand&r to keep the flower. Shears turn Hibiscus into a Tea Blossom."
		""
		"&aBone meal on a placed Lavender or Hibiscus pops out a spare flower&r, like vanilla tall flowers, so one of each is enough to start a bed."
	]
	quest.2A9922308B582900.quest_subtitle: "Shears in, shears out"
	quest.2A9922308B582900.title: "&dBlooms for Brewing"
	quest.2A9CAD5533E4B98A.quest_desc: [
		"&6Alpine Sheep&r roam taigas, groves, snowy plains and snowy slopes. &aShear one&r for &b1-3 Homespun Wool&r, and breed them with &eWheat&r."
		""
		"Homespun Wool makes the &eWinter Hat&r (4 wool), the Arolla Pine bed and sofa, and Homespun Carpet."
		""
		"&7Ordinary sheep and cows don't spawn in these biomes. These fellows replace them.&r"
	]
	quest.2A9CAD5533E4B98A.quest_subtitle: "Itchy, but in a cosy way"
	quest.2A9CAD5533E4B98A.title: "&fHomespun Craft"
	quest.2AA45D73A9AF9070.quest_desc: [
		"Both blaze machines need a &eBlaze Upgrade Smithing Template&r. Every &cBastion Remnant&r treasure chest has one, and its other chests have a small chance. A Dead Lord's House (Structures Arise) has the same treasure loot."
		""
		"&aDon't spend it!&r Put it in the top middle of a crafting grid, &eNetherrack&r in the centre and &b7&r &eBlaze Rods&r around it to get &b2&r templates back."
	]
	quest.2AA45D73A9AF9070.quest_subtitle: "Some upgrades are found, not made"
	quest.2AA45D73A9AF9070.title: "&cTreasure of the Bastion"
	quest.2AEE116EA925AB86.quest_desc: [
		"The &bbadlands&r are bandit territory: the only big Dungeons Arise finds there are the &6Bandit Village&r and the &6Bandit Towers&r."
		""
		"The village has &choglins with Wither Skeleton riders&r and husks in mixed armour. The towers are tall, with husks and skeletons in Thorns gear guarding lots of chests: the treasure has enchanted diamond gear, diamonds and sometimes a &emap to a Foundry&r."
	]
	quest.2AEE116EA925AB86.quest_subtitle: "Wanted: dead or alive. Mostly dead."
	quest.2AEE116EA925AB86.title: "&6Outlaw Country"
	quest.2AF51CA1DED6E50D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Quark&r is not one big system. It is &bover a hundred small features&r that feel like they always belonged in Minecraft: new blocks, smarter storage, handy tools, a few new critters and some deep-cave surprises."
		""
		"Press &bEsc&r and click the little &bq&r button on the Pause menu (it is on the Title screen too). It lists every Quark feature with a short description. Recipes are in &6EMI&r."
		""
		"This chapter is a guided tour. Branch out in any direction: &afarming&r, &astorage&r, &abuilding&r, &aautomation&r and &acritters&r. The main road goes &cbelow Y=0&r, toward the &ePickarang&r."
		""
		"&7Zeta is the library underneath. It has no items of its own.&r"
	]
	quest.2AF51CA1DED6E50D.quest_subtitle: "Small things, big difference"
	quest.2AF51CA1DED6E50D.title: "&6Bit by Bit"
	quest.2B33181E1F26AF17.quest_desc: [
		"The &ePickarang&r is a boomerang pickaxe: &b2 Diamonds&r, &b2 Planks&r and your &eHeart of Diamond&r. &bRight-click&r to throw it. It &amines whatever it hits and flies back with the drops&r."
		""
		"It digs like a diamond pickaxe, chops like an axe, shovels like a shovel and has &b800 durability&r. It can't break obsidian."
		""
		"Enchant it: &dEfficiency&r, &dFortune&r or &dSilk Touch&r, &dUnbreaking&r, &dMending&r and &dPiercing&r (hits several blocks per throw). Perfect for ores in a ravine wall or ceiling."
	]
	quest.2B33181E1F26AF17.quest_subtitle: "What goes around comes around"
	quest.2B33181E1F26AF17.title: "&6Somehow, Pickarang Returned"
	quest.2B9CF933F70672C8.quest_desc: [
		"&eAlpine Salt Ore&r only grows inside &eLimestone&r, the pale stone in the ground under a Meadow. Mine it and &asmelt or blast&r it into &eAlpine Salt&r."
		""
		"Salt is the spice of this whole chapter: it goes into &eRennet&r, &eAmethyst Milk&r and most Cookpot meat dishes."
		""
		"&aTip:&r once you have a cooking station, boiling smooth &eLimestone&r or even &eCalcite&r also gives salt, so you never have to come back."
	]
	quest.2B9CF933F70672C8.quest_subtitle: "Worth its salt"
	quest.2B9CF933F70672C8.title: "&fA Pinch of Alpine"
	quest.2BA44A551E71EE71.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Mechanical Piston&r pushes and pulls glued structures in a straight line. Put &ePiston Extension Poles&r behind it: the number of poles is how far it travels."
		""
		"Rotation direction decides push or pull, and faster input moves it faster. Add a Slimeball for a &6Sticky Mechanical Piston&r."
	]
	quest.2BA44A551E71EE71.quest_subtitle: "Poles apart"
	quest.2BA44A551E71EE71.title: "&eExtend Yourself"
	quest.2BA9DE49AD948F70.quest_desc: [
		"The &eGenerator Augment&r (paper, stone, redstone, repeater) makes a furnace stop smelting and &aburn its fuel into FE&r instead: &b40 FE/t&r for Iron, &b160&r for Gold, &b240&r for Diamond, up to &b1000&r for Netherite."
		""
		"&cIt only pushes power out of sides set to Output&r: press &bOpen Config&r in the furnace GUI and set one."
		""
		"&7With a Blasting augment it burns spare ingots and gems; with Smoking, food.&r"
	]
	quest.2BA9DE49AD948F70.quest_subtitle: "Your first FE"
	quest.2BA9DE49AD948F70.title: "&6Fire Makes Power"
	quest.2BAFE0EEBF1A9FEF.quest_desc: [
		"&6Wilder Nature&r adds deer, bison, boars, elephants, squirrels and many more animals. Its heart is the &6Bounty Board&r (6 planks, 2 sticks)."
		""
		"Right-click it to see the current bounties. They are shared by the whole server and &brefresh every 3 in-game days&r."
		""
		"&7Lost a contract? The board restores it for 1 Emerald.&r"
		""
		"&7This is not the &6Bountiful&7 board from the &6Kitted Out&7 chapter. The two keep separate contracts and rewards, so you can work both.&r"
	]
	quest.2BAFE0EEBF1A9FEF.quest_subtitle: "Wilder Nature"
	quest.2BAFE0EEBF1A9FEF.title: "&6Wanted: Wildlife"
	quest.2BD13E51BECF1A98.quest_desc: [
		"JDT fluids are made by &adropping an item into a fluid source block&r. Craft &ePolymorphic Catalyst&r from a Blazegold Ingot and Nether Wart, then throw it into &bwater&r to get &ePolymorphic Fluid&r."
		""
		"Each drop converts &bone source block&r, one item per block. Polymorphic Fluid is the base of JDT's crafted fluids: liquid fuels, Portal Fluid and, much later, &dTime Fluid&r. Keep a small pool of it."
	]
	quest.2BD13E51BECF1A98.quest_subtitle: "Just add catalyst"
	quest.2BD13E51BECF1A98.title: "&bShape-Shifting Water"
	quest.2BDF6905C3B4E487.quest_desc: [
		"Surround a &eSource Gem&r with 8 &eStone&r to get 8 &eSourcestone&r, the mod's magic building block."
		""
		"An &6Arcane Pedestal&r is 4 Sourcestone, a Source Gem and 4 Gold Nuggets. Pedestals hold ingredients for the Imbuement Chamber and the Enchanting Apparatus. &aAim for 8 eventually&r: the bigger apparatus recipes use that many."
		""
		"&7The Arcane Platform is a 1:1 swap that can face any direction.&r"
	]
	quest.2BDF6905C3B4E487.title: "&6Put It on a Pedestal"
	quest.2C24AD98ECDE164B.quest_desc: [
		"Melt &eIron&r, &eSkyslime Balls&r and &eGrout&r (for Seared Stone) together in a lava-fuelled Smeltery. Each iron ingot, slime ball and half a grout make &b2 Slimesteel Ingots&r."
		""
		"Slimesteel heads mine at &bdiamond tier&r and have huge durability. They also come with &boverslime&r, a second blue durability bar that wears down before the real one."
		""
		"&aA slimesteel pickaxe can mine cobalt.&r"
	]
	quest.2C24AD98ECDE164B.quest_subtitle: "Steel with a bounce"
	quest.2C24AD98ECDE164B.title: "&bSlime Time"
	quest.2C508E9E78AEED63.quest_desc: [
		"Trap a mob inside an &6Alchemist Cauldron&r. It takes damage every second, and each hit adds &b250 mB&r of blood. &aFill glass bottles&r to get &eBlood Vials&r."
		""
		"A plain cauldron over a lit &ecampfire&r works the same way."
		""
		"Vials are the &dblood&r focus, and blood brewed with Hogskin makes &eBloody Vellum&r for the Vampiric Spell Book."
	]
	quest.2C508E9E78AEED63.quest_subtitle: "The blood focus"
	quest.2C508E9E78AEED63.title: "&4Out for Blood"
	quest.2C69874270ACD66F.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Experience Holder&r banks your levels (&b+/-&r buttons, Shift for 10). It can also hold nearby players at a &btarget level&r, perfect for enchanting at exactly 30, and vacuum up XP orbs."
		""
		"It's a tank of &eXP Fluid&r too, and keeps its XP when broken. &7Create: Enchantment Industry (see the Bolt-On Brilliance chapter) accepts JDT XP Fluid as experience.&r"
	]
	quest.2C69874270ACD66F.quest_subtitle: "Saving levels for a rainy day"
	quest.2C69874270ACD66F.title: "&aLevel Headed"
	quest.2C9AFF2BFCDB171B.quest_desc: [
		"&eXychorium&r ore comes in five colours: &9Blue&r, &cRed&r, &aGreen&r, &8Dark&r and &fLight&r. Each colour spawns &btwo small veins per chunk&r between &bY -24 and 56&r, most often around &bY 16&r, in stone, deepslate and inside Kivi blobs."
		""
		"A &bstone pickaxe&r is enough. Each ore drops &b1-3 gems&r, and &aFortune&r adds more."
		""
		"&7Each colour has a job: blue makes water, red makes fire, green grows plants, light stops mob spawns and dark deletes fluids. You'll want all five.&r"
	]
	quest.2C9AFF2BFCDB171B.quest_subtitle: "Collect the whole set"
	quest.2C9AFF2BFCDB171B.title: "&dFive Shades of Shiny"
	quest.2CACE31018F83F9C.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Feeding Trough&r is &ePlanks&r around &eWheat&r. Put animal food in it and nearby animals walk over, eat and &abreed on their own&r."
		""
		"It works within &b10 blocks&r, stops if more than &b32 animals&r are crowded nearby, and gives &cno XP&r. Feed it from a hopper, a Copper Pipe or &6Pipez&r for a hands-off ranch."
		""
		"&7Not to be confused with the trough from Let's Do Farm and Charm.&r"
	]
	quest.2CACE31018F83F9C.quest_subtitle: "Self-service for cows"
	quest.2CACE31018F83F9C.title: "&6Breakfast Is Served"
	quest.2D2954A1647426D4.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Kisegi Sanctuary&r is another sunken temple, &b32 blocks down&r under &bplains, hills and cherry groves&r. Same rules as the Infested Temple: &cTrial Spawners&r, keys and &b4 vaults&r (normal, treasure and their ominous versions). &cWither Skeletons in netherite chestplates&r guard the halls."
		""
		"Its loot holds two rare enchantments. &dEnsnaring&r can slow enemies hard and summon evoker fangs. &cCurse of Lolth&r can heal you as you hit, but &ccave spiders burst out of your victims&r and hitting spiders hurts you back."
		""
		"&7Bring a Brush: suspicious sand and gravel here hide pottery sherds and more.&r"
	]
	quest.2D2954A1647426D4.quest_subtitle: "Don't touch the webs. Or the swords."
	quest.2D2954A1647426D4.title: "&5Weaver's Sanctum"
	quest.2D34C88EA5E92EF0.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Street Lantern&r is a &eFroglight&r (Ochre or Verdant) plus an &eIron Ingot&r, and makes four. The &6Plated Street Lantern&r needs a &ePearlescent Froglight&r and a &eGold Ingot&r, and makes two."
		""
		"&aFroglights:&r a Frog that eats a small &eMagma Cube&r drops one. The colour depends on the frog: &bwarm (white) frogs give Pearlescent&r, temperate (orange) Ochre, cold (green) Verdant. Mangrove Swamps are home to warm frogs."
		""
		"Lanterns stack into tall lamp posts and hang on walls when you place them against one. &7Any one Street Lantern, standing or on a wall, counts for the finale.&r"
	]
	quest.2D34C88EA5E92EF0.quest_subtitle: "Frogs did the hard part"
	quest.2D34C88EA5E92EF0.title: "&eLight Up the Street"
	quest.2D5A6ED92D7D0475.quest_desc: [
		"A &eGolden Sheet&r, &eAndesite Alloy&r and a &eBlock of Copper&r in a column make a &6Steam Engine&r. Place it on a &6Fluid Tank&r (the smallest working boiler is &b4 tank blocks&r), then &bright-click the engine with a Shaft&r to give it an output."
		""
		"The tank becomes a &6boiler&r once it has &bheat&r (fuelled Blaze Burners under it, like the one from Spin Cycle) and &bwater&r (a pump feeding it). Its power level is the &blowest&r of three limits: 1 level per &b4 tank blocks&r, per &b10 mB/tick&r of water, and per heated burner."
		""
		"&aEach level runs one engine at full power: 64 RPM and 16,384 SU.&r Wear &6Goggles&r and look at the tank to see whether size, water or heat is holding you back."
		""
		"&7No burners? Magma, lava or a campfire make a weak passive boiler: one engine at 16 RPM.&r"
	]
	quest.2D5A6ED92D7D0475.quest_subtitle: "Real power, finally"
	quest.2D5A6ED92D7D0475.title: "&6Let Off Some Steam"
	quest.2D6C8611A76387DD.quest_desc: [
		"Arrange &e5 small flowers&r in a U shape to make a &eBouquet&r. Gift it to a villager you have at least &b10 hearts&r with and they become &a\"In love with\"&r you: promised, but not engaged yet."
		""
		"Not everyone is interested in every character. If a villager says you are not right for each other, that is just them; try someone else."
		""
		"&7A bouquet is also a very nice gift for anybody.&r"
	]
	quest.2D6C8611A76387DD.quest_subtitle: "The first step"
	quest.2D6C8611A76387DD.title: "&dSay It With Flowers"
	quest.2D7E21D8105D8554.quest_desc: [
		"&eGem Dust&r goes into nearly every Apotheosis recipe. For your very first batch, &adrop a gem on the ground and drop an Anvil on it&r. Each gem crushed this way becomes &b1&r dust."
		""
		"Surround one dust with &b8 Deepslate&r for &b8 Gem-Fused Slate&r, the base of most sigils, the upgrade templates and spawner runes."
		""
		"&7After this, the Salvaging Table does it better: 1-2 dust from a Cracked gem, up to 10 from a Perfect one.&r"
	]
	quest.2D7E21D8105D8554.quest_subtitle: "Gem Dust"
	quest.2D7E21D8105D8554.title: "&7Anvil Therapy"
	quest.2D9E1FE4D0EA5AD9.quest_desc: [
		"The &eNovice Spell Book&r is a shapeless craft: a &eBook&r (or your Tattered Tome) with a &eFerricore Sword&r, &ePickaxe&r, &eAxe&r and &eShovel&r from Just Dire Things. Create Ars Compact swaps these in for Ars Nouveau's usual iron tools, so iron ones won't work."
		""
		"No Ferricore yet? See &eIron, Re-Gooed&r in the Just Dire Things chapter."
		""
		"&cThe tools are used up&r, so craft fresh ones rather than sacrificing your enchanted gear."
		""
		"It holds &b10 spells&r of up to &b10 glyphs&r each, and can cast &dTier I&r glyphs. You already know five starter glyphs: &dProjectile&r, &dTouch&r, &dSelf&r, &dBreak&r and &dHarm&r."
	]
	quest.2D9E1FE4D0EA5AD9.quest_subtitle: "Four Ferricore tools walk into a book"
	quest.2D9E1FE4D0EA5AD9.title: "&dSpellbook, Novice Edition"
	quest.2DA8DE355A97588B.quest_desc: [
		"A rare IDAS stronghold crawling with &cillagers&r (pillagers, vindicators, evokers and even ravagers), found in &bplains, meadows, taigas and flower forests&r."
		""
		"It's a real fight, so bring a shield, armour and a Totem if you have one. The jail chests can hold the &eSentry&r and &eVex&r armour trims, and the library has enchanted books."
	]
	quest.2DA8DE355A97588B.quest_subtitle: "Turnabout is fair play"
	quest.2DA8DE355A97588B.title: "&cPillage the Pillagers"
	quest.2DD0D03DF14B0F53.quest_desc: [
		"&ePrimogel Goo&r is &e4 Clay Balls&r in the corners, &e2 Sugar&r, &e2 Rotten Flesh&r and a &eDirt&r block in the centre."
		""
		"&cPlaced goo starts dormant.&r Right-click it with its food, &eSugar&r or &eRotten Flesh&r, to wake it up. One item is eaten."
		""
		"&7Every conversion has a 10% chance to send it back to sleep. If it stops working, feed it again.&r"
	]
	quest.2DD0D03DF14B0F53.quest_subtitle: "It's alive! Well, after lunch"
	quest.2DD0D03DF14B0F53.title: "&aGoo Goo, Ga Ga"
	quest.2DDFC3A968FBA50C.quest_desc: [
		"&6Blooming Nature&r adds &b16 biomes&r, from Aspen Forests to Desert Oases, and brings fog, fireflies and falling leaves to many vanilla biomes."
		""
		"Even early on it helps: &eTwigs&r and &ePebbles&r lie on the ground in many biomes. Pick them up: each Twig crafts into a &eStick&r and &b4&r Pebbles make a &eCobblestone&r."
		""
		"&7Now and then a &6Wandering Gardener&r visits with his camel, trading the mod's flowers and saplings.&r"
	]
	quest.2DDFC3A968FBA50C.quest_subtitle: "Blooming Nature"
	quest.2DDFC3A968FBA50C.title: "&aStop and Smell the Flowers"
	quest.2E2AA633E4C9A943.quest_desc: [
		"Crush &eObsidian&r into &ePowdered Obsidian&r. Then run a short &6Sequenced Assembly&r: a &6Spout&r adds &b500 mB of Lava&r, and a &6Mechanical Press&r presses it &btwice&r."
		""
		"&eSturdy Sheets&r are the bones of the railway: every Train Casing needs one, and so do Train Schedules."
	]
	quest.2E2AA633E4C9A943.quest_subtitle: "Obsidian, but flat"
	quest.2E2AA633E4C9A943.title: "&eRock Solid"
	quest.2E37076C1B5C26E6.quest_desc: [
		"&6Sourcelinks&r generate &dSource&r into jars within &b5 blocks&r. Each is 2 Source Gems, 2 Gold Ingots and a themed centre item."
		""
		"The &6Agronomic Sourcelink&r (Wheat centre) earns Source whenever crops and trees grow within &b15 blocks&r, with a bonus for Mageblooms, Sourceberries and Archwood saplings. &cBone meal growth doesn't count.&r"
		""
		"&7The others: Mycelial (eats food), Volcanic (burns fuel), Vitalic (mob deaths and breeding) and Alchemical (drinks potions from Potion Jars).&r"
	]
	quest.2E37076C1B5C26E6.quest_subtitle: "Grow plants, get magic"
	quest.2E37076C1B5C26E6.title: "&dTapping the Source"
	quest.2E40C88FD8145F5D.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Scroll Forge&r makes scrolls to order: &e3 Polished Deepslate&r and &e4 Crying Obsidian&r (ruined portals, piglin bartering)."
		""
		"Insert &eink&r, &epaper&r and a school &efocus&r, then pick a spell of that school. You get the lowest level of the ink's band. Spells the ink is too weak for are greyed out."
		""
		"&bFoci:&r Blaze Rod (fire), Frozen Bone (ice), Bottle o' Lightning (lightning), Divine Pearl (holy), Ender Pearl (ender), Blood Vial (blood), Emerald (evocation), Poisonous Potato (nature)."
	]
	quest.2E40C88FD8145F5D.quest_subtitle: "Write your own spells"
	quest.2E40C88FD8145F5D.title: "&6New Age Librarian"
	quest.2EA28A2B79770C66.quest_desc: [
		"&6Fur Armor&r is made from &eLeather&r and &eRabbit Hide&r, with &eFeathers&r on the helmet and chestplate."
		""
		"Wear the full set for a bonus of &b+2 Knockback Resistance&r, so hits push you around less."
		""
		"&7The look says mountain guide. Wear it on cold-weather trips.&r"
	]
	quest.2EA28A2B79770C66.quest_subtitle: "Warm, fluffy and slightly stubborn"
	quest.2EA28A2B79770C66.title: "&6Dressed for Success"
	quest.2ED2120FC1F73064.quest_desc: [
		"From the day you place it, a child becomes an &aadult&r in &b16 days&r (about &b5 hours and 20 minutes&r of loaded play), or sooner with golden apples."
		""
		"Adults lead their own lives: they take jobs, make friends and might even fall in love on their own. You can still call them with the whistle."
	]
	quest.2ED2120FC1F73064.quest_subtitle: "Sniff"
	quest.2ED2120FC1F73064.title: "&6They Grow Up So Fast"
	quest.2F15414360C3E0D3.quest_desc: [
		"Sew &b7 Flax&r and a piece of &eString&r into a &6Sack&r. It holds &b9 slots&r and keeps its contents when picked up, like a tiny shulker box. Place it down to open it."
		""
		"&cHeavy load:&r carrying &bmore than 2 packed sacks&r makes you &cOverencumbered&r, so no sprinting. Every 2 more makes it worse, cutting your jump and walking speed. Coloured sacks count too."
		""
		"&7Placed sacks fall like sand, so don't build them into a ceiling.&r"
	]
	quest.2F15414360C3E0D3.quest_subtitle: "A shulker box for peasants"
	quest.2F15414360C3E0D3.title: "&eSack It Up"
	quest.2F2517347F688FDC.quest_desc: [
		"&6Illager Campsites&r turn up in &bplains, meadows, windswept hills and snowy plains&r: tents, a campfire, a couple of pillagers and a vindicator. A gentle first fight."
		""
		"Some camps keep a zombie villager prisoner. &aCure it&r with a &eSplash Potion of Weakness&r and a &eGolden Apple&r and it becomes a villager (see &6Starting a Family&r)."
		""
		"Its map chest always holds a map to an &6Illager Fort&r or an &6Illager Corsair&r."
	]
	quest.2F2517347F688FDC.quest_subtitle: "They didn't bring marshmallows"
	quest.2F2517347F688FDC.title: "&cUnhappy Campers"
	quest.2F25AE36BDDEC7C6.quest_desc: [
		"Sigils are used in a &6Smithing Table&r. A &dSigil of Socketing&r adds one socket, but only to an item that has fewer than &b2&r sockets."
		""
		"Its siblings: the &dSigil of Withdrawal&r pops out every gem and gives back both item and gems, and the &dSigil of Unnaming&r strips the long affix name."
		""
		"&7All three are crafted around Gem-Fused Slate. Socketing and Withdrawal also take Gem Dust, Unnaming just Flint.&r"
	]
	quest.2F25AE36BDDEC7C6.quest_subtitle: "Sigils"
	quest.2F25AE36BDDEC7C6.title: "&dSocket to Me"
	quest.2F52A96493AC9ED9.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Flux Controller&r (flux block, core and dust) on your network unlocks &bWireless Charging&r: open its tab, pick slots (hotbar, hands, armour, curios), toggle it on and press &bApply&r."
		""
		"FE-powered items in those slots now top up while the network has power - &aperfect for Building Gadgets&r. A &eBasic Flux Storage&r (&b2M FE&r) makes a good buffer."
	]
	quest.2F52A96493AC9ED9.quest_subtitle: "Wireless charging, Minecraft edition"
	quest.2F52A96493AC9ED9.title: "&6Charging in Thin Air"
	quest.2F8917F333049753.quest_desc: [
		"Goo also upgrades fuel. A &eBlock of Coal&r, or JDT's own &eCharcoal Block&r (9 Charcoal), against &6Primogel Goo&r turns into raw ore that drops &ePrimal Coal&r directly."
		""
		"Primal Coal burns &b3x&r as long as coal and makes twice the FE per tick in a JDT generator. It's also the start of the coal ladder: every goo tier refines the previous coal's block into the next."
		""
		"&7Each coal block only gives 3-4 Primal Coal, so you'll need about three to collect the 9 for a Primal Coal Block.&r"
	]
	quest.2F8917F333049753.quest_subtitle: "Burns longer, brags louder"
	quest.2F8917F333049753.title: "&eCoal with Ambition"
	quest.2F9BA69479540306.quest_desc: [
		"Infuse a blank rune at &b70 Eterna, 30%+ Quanta and 50%+ Arcana&r: Summit active and a table built up with Deepshelves for an &dInfused Spawner Rune&r. It powers the strongest runes:"
		""
		"&eStupor&r (Chorus Fruit, a Potion of Mining Fatigue brewed from Haste and a Fermented Spider Eye) removes mob AI. &eDefiance&r (Conduit) ignores spawn rules. &eSolitude&r (Nether Star) runs with nobody nearby. &eEchoes&r (8 Echo Shards) adds an extra copy of the drops, up to 3 times."
		""
		"&7No-AI farms are much kinder to the server. Your fellow players thank you.&r"
	]
	quest.2F9BA69479540306.quest_subtitle: "Infused Spawner Rune"
	quest.2F9BA69479540306.title: "&dRunes, Infused"
	quest.2FB9D3060C818C43.quest_desc: [
		"&6HT's TreeChop&r changes trees: breaking a log only &achops&r it, and after enough chops the &bwhole tree falls&r and drops its logs. Any tool works, an &eaxe&r is just faster."
		""
		"&bSneak&r to break a single log the normal way. Logs with no natural leaves attached are never chopped, so your log cabin is safe."
		""
		"Turn the logs into &eplanks&r and craft a &6Crafting Table&r. Everything starts here."
	]
	quest.2FB9D3060C818C43.quest_subtitle: "Every journey starts with a tree"
	quest.2FB9D3060C818C43.title: "&aTimber!"
	quest.2FC3A3C4FF955E0C.quest_desc: [
		"Your first backpack came from &6First Light&r. Craft it with &eIngots&r around it to upgrade it, contents and all: &bCopper 45&r slots, &bIron 54&r, &bGold 81&r, &bDiamond 108&r. The &bNetherite 120&r tier is made at a &6Smithing Table&r. Higher tiers also take more upgrades."
		""
		"&7Going Leather, Copper, then Iron costs 4 iron instead of 8.&r"
		""
		"&7About 1 in 100 zombies, skeletons, creepers, piglins and other monsters spawns wearing a loot-stuffed backpack - and tougher gear to match.&r"
	]
	quest.2FC3A3C4FF955E0C.quest_subtitle: "More pockets, please"
	quest.2FC3A3C4FF955E0C.title: "&6Pack Mule"
	quest.2FF44A4F493D8E70.quest_desc: [
		"Own all &b7 Meadow wools&r. The needle gets you every one without leaving the Overworld:"
		"&fWhite&r to Plaid, &7Light Gray&r to Linen, &8Gray&r to Jacquard, Brown to Rustic, &9Blue&r to Chambray, Black to Tweed and &3Cyan&r to Warped."
		""
		"&aTip:&r Blooming Nature's flowers craft into plenty of dyes, so dyeing white wool first is easy."
	]
	quest.2FF44A4F493D8E70.quest_subtitle: "Fifty shades of tweed"
	quest.2FF44A4F493D8E70.title: "&dThe Wool Enthusiast"
	quest.303920E5BBBE36C0.quest_desc: [
		"&6Simple&r machines need &ano power&r and act on the one block in front of them. Each is &e4 Ferricore&r, &eLapis&r, &eRedstone&r and a vanilla part: an Observer and Diamond for the &6Block Breaker&r, a Dispenser and Diamond for the &6Block Placer&r."
		""
		"All share a &bRedstone mode&r (Ignored, Low, High, Pulse) and a &bSpeed&r in ticks, 20 by default. &cThe Breaker needs a tool in its slot and wears it out&r like a player would."
	]
	quest.303920E5BBBE36C0.quest_subtitle: "Automation without the power bill"
	quest.303920E5BBBE36C0.title: "&6Break It, Place It"
	quest.3079E243885490A2.quest_desc: [
		"&6Jade&r is the little box at the top of your screen. It names whatever block or mob you're looking at and which &bmod&r it comes from. Hold &bShift&r for extra detail, press &bkeypad 0&r for its settings."
		""
		"&6AppleSkin&r adds hunger and &esaturation&r values to every food tooltip, and previews on your hunger bar how much a bite will restore."
		""
		"&aTip:&r high-saturation food like &esteak&r keeps your health regenerating far longer than snacks."
	]
	quest.3079E243885490A2.quest_subtitle: "Information at a glance"
	quest.3079E243885490A2.title: "&bWhat Am I Looking At?"
	quest.30FBD369F7A448CF.quest_desc: [
		"&6YUNG's Better Mineshafts&r are long tunnel networks between about &by -55 and y 30&r. There are &b13 styles&r that match the biome they sit in: sandstone in deserts, ice in frozen peaks, moss in lush caves and so on."
		""
		"Check the &adead ends&r for free ore deposits (sometimes even diamond), and look for abandoned workstations. Chest minecarts are Lootr carts too."
		""
		"&cWatch for TNT minecarts&r and bring shears or a sword for the cobwebs. &6YUNG's Better Caves&r also reshapes the caves around them: tame near the surface, huge and wild deep down."
	]
	quest.30FBD369F7A448CF.quest_subtitle: "Mind the gap. And the TNT."
	quest.30FBD369F7A448CF.title: "&6Down the Shaft"
	quest.3119A239AE226DDB.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Mechanical Nest&r hangs at &by 190&r over &bswamps, mangroves and forests&r. You have to go &ainside&r it for this quest."
		""
		"&cIts traps are the danger.&r Get within 4 blocks of one and it throws &cSlowness III and Mining Fatigue III&r with a &clightning strike&r. Deeper in, a &cRavager carries a charged Creeper&r. Have a way down ready (a water bucket or Slow Falling) and drink the milk when the traps catch you."
		""
		"Its treasure chests hold &dVoltaic Shot&r and &dDischarge&r crossbows, swords and books, diamond and emerald blocks, and netherite scrap."
	]
	quest.3119A239AE226DDB.quest_subtitle: "Clockwork, lightning and very bad ideas"
	quest.3119A239AE226DDB.title: "&eShock and Awe"
	quest.31227418F3BA80B0.quest_desc: [
		"Each &6Advanced&r machine is its Simple version plus &e4 Celestigem&r, &e3 Eyes of Ender&r and &eRedstone&r. They &cneed FE&r, but work on a whole &barea&r (Render Area previews it, Rad sets the radius, Off the offset) and have proper &ballow/deny filters&r."
		""
		"They also &acharge FE tools placed inside them&r, so an Advanced Block Breaker keeps a Celestigem pickaxe topped up."
		""
		"&7A Machine Settings Copier copies one machine's setup onto another: shift-right-click to copy, right-click to paste.&r"
	]
	quest.31227418F3BA80B0.quest_subtitle: "Same machine, whole area"
	quest.31227418F3BA80B0.title: "&6Going Pro"
	quest.315D81E63A13AF37.quest_desc: [
		"&eThatch&r has no recipe. &aUse a Water Bottle on a placed Hay Bale&r to make a &eWet Hay Block&r, then leave it under open sky in a &bhot biome&r (beach, desert, savanna, badlands or the Nether). It dries into &eThatch&r in a minute or so. Elsewhere it just dries back into hay."
		""
		"Top off the hut with a &6Beach Parasol&r (wool and palm planks). &7Standing near one even takes a tiny bit off fire damage.&r"
		""
		"&7More water bottle tricks: Gravel becomes Sand, and Sand becomes Sandwaves. Beachparty's Thatch is not Hearth \\& Timber's wheat-crafted Thatch Block from &6Make Yourself at Home&7; they are different blocks.&r"
	]
	quest.315D81E63A13AF37.quest_subtitle: "Island living, hay included"
	quest.315D81E63A13AF37.title: "&6Tiki Hut"
	quest.317065A03B9446BF.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Frosted Caves&r sit under the &bcoldest, snowiest&r parts of the world: icicles, creeping ice and &6Ice Cube&r mobs. &cFalling icicles hurt&r, so don't loiter under them."
		""
		"Mine the glowing &eEnchanted Ice&r set inside the big icicles for a burst of &b15 to 53 XP&r (Silk Touch keeps the block instead). Pick a &eFrost Lily&r too: brewed into an Awkward Potion it makes a &dPotion of Frost&r."
	]
	quest.317065A03B9446BF.quest_subtitle: "Look up. Then look up again."
	quest.317065A03B9446BF.title: "&bIce to Meet You"
	quest.3190D271A3A54144.quest_desc: [
		"Weaken a &eWitch&r to &bhalf health or less&r, then hit it with a &dDispel&r spell (Dispel glyph: Abjuration Essence + 3 Milk Buckets). It turns into a &eWixie Token&r. Craft the charm on the Apparatus and use it on a &6Cauldron&r."
		""
		"Show the Wixie Cauldron the item you want, and it &aautocrafts it&r from nearby chests for a little Source. It also brews potions into Potion Jars."
	]
	quest.3190D271A3A54144.title: "&dCauldron Confidential"
	quest.320905E423258886.quest_desc: [
		"A &eRepair Kit&r is a part like any other: a Pattern and &b2&r units of material in the &6Part Builder&r, or cast from metal later."
		""
		"Click it onto a tool in your inventory, or combine the two in a crafting grid, to restore &btwo ingots'&r worth of durability. Use a kit made of the tool's head material. &aUseful when the Station is back at base.&r"
	]
	quest.320905E423258886.quest_subtitle: "Field repairs"
	quest.320905E423258886.title: "&ePatch Job"
	quest.323B7572E1658AD2.quest_desc: [
		"Put a vanilla &eClock&r inside a frame of &eSticks&r over an &eOak Slab&r to make an &6Oak Clock&r. Stand that Clock on &eOak Planks&r for an &6Oak Grandfather Clock&r. You'll need two vanilla Clocks for both."
		""
		"&aRight-click a clock to read the exact time.&r The Grandfather Clock ticks, &bchimes at dawn&r and &bstrikes twelve at midnight&r, loud enough to startle nearby mobs."
	]
	quest.323B7572E1658AD2.quest_subtitle: "Tick, tock, BONG"
	quest.323B7572E1658AD2.title: "&6Time Flies"
	quest.3242B10AFFE5D950.quest_desc: [
		"&6Better Strongholds&r are sprawling: armouries, bunk rooms, crypts, prisons, a &egrand library&r, a treasure room and plenty of traps. Explore before you head for the portal room; the loot is worth it."
		""
		"The &6End Portal Frames&r in its portal room are &5unstable&r, though. Read the next quest &cbefore&r you put an eye anywhere near them. &7Rumour says a secret room holds a very special sword.&r"
		""
		"&7Two spare eyes, in case the first batch shattered.&r"
	]
	quest.3242B10AFFE5D950.quest_subtitle: "Libraries, prisons and the odd trap"
	quest.3242B10AFFE5D950.title: "&2A Stronger Hold"
	quest.324B57D5A297E8D9.quest_desc: [
		"&eTrain Casing&r and a &eCompass&r make &b2&r &6Train Stations&r. Select a track, then place the station beside it, and give it a name in its screen."
		""
		"Stations are where trains are &abuilt&r (Assembly Mode), where they &astop&r, and what schedules point to. Trains only pull in from the direction the station marker shows."
	]
	quest.324B57D5A297E8D9.quest_subtitle: "Please mind the gap"
	quest.324B57D5A297E8D9.title: "&aNext Stop"
	quest.327FC2BEF31968BE.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Kinetic Battery&r stores rotation. Craft it with a &ePrecision Mechanism&r, a &eBrass Casing&r, Iron Sheets and Redstone."
		""
		"Unpowered, it &acharges&r from rotation on its front. Give it a &bredstone signal&r and it discharges at a steady &b64 RPM&r. It holds &b512 SU-hours&r and only spends what your machines actually use."
		""
		"It &akeeps its charge as an item&r, so a Deployer or Mechanical Arm can swap in fresh batteries. A Comparator reads its level."
	]
	quest.327FC2BEF31968BE.quest_subtitle: "Rotation, to go"
	quest.327FC2BEF31968BE.title: "&6Fully Charged"
	quest.3360C5764C7588B7.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a &eRitual of Binding&r tablet (Vexing log, Blank Parchment, Ender Pearl, Source Gems) and perform it &anear a Starbuncle&r. It becomes a &eBound Script&r. Use the script to learn the familiar."
		""
		"Summon it from your spell book (&bC&r) on the &bFamiliars&r tab. Each gives a perk: Starbuncle grants Speed, Wixie lengthens potions, Whirlisprig halves Earth glyph costs, Bookwyrm pulls in items and XP, Drygmy boosts Earth damage, Amethyst Golem halves knockback."
	]
	quest.3360C5764C7588B7.quest_subtitle: "A pocket-sized sidekick"
	quest.3360C5764C7588B7.title: "&dThis Seems Familiar"
	quest.3375563F20D5EE2E.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Building Gadget&r (iron, redstone, lapis, diamond): &asneak + right-click&r a block to pick it, then right-click to place whole rows, walls or floors. Hold &bG&r for its settings, &bU&r undoes."
		""
		"It runs on &bFE&r (&b50 FE&r per block) and &cmay arrive empty&r: charge it wirelessly with a &6Flux Controller&r (this chapter), or later with a &6Tesla Coil&r (Create Expansions) or a &6Pocket Generator&r (Just Dire Things)."
		""
		"Its siblings are the &eExchanging&r, &eCopy-Paste&r, &eCut-Paste&r and &eDestruction&r gadgets. A book, a clay ball and lapis make the guide."
	]
	quest.3375563F20D5EE2E.quest_subtitle: "Building Gadgets 2"
	quest.3375563F20D5EE2E.title: "&6Measure Twice, Build Once"
	quest.33F84EB2FE66D4C1.quest_desc: [
		"A &eBlank Sand Cast&r is just one &eSand&r in a crafting grid, and it makes &b4&r casts. Red sand works the same way."
		""
		"To get shaped casts you can carry, put &eSand&r (or a blank cast) in the &6Part Builder's&r pattern slot and pick the part. One sand makes &b4 Pick Head Sand Casts&r."
		""
		"You can also shape one in place: put a blank cast on a &6Casting Table&r and &bright-click it with a tool part&r, such as your Pick Head. The part isn't used up, so take it back before you pour."
		""
		"&7Sand casts break after one pour, and a shaped cast turns back into a blank one if you pick it up off the table.&r"
	]
	quest.33F84EB2FE66D4C1.quest_subtitle: "Disposable, but dirt cheap"
	quest.33F84EB2FE66D4C1.title: "&eSand Box"
	quest.340197AD7E06DADA.quest_desc: [
		"&eKivi&r is a smooth, pale stone that generates in &bbig blobs&r anywhere in the Overworld between &bY 0 and 60&r. It drops itself, so there's no cobbled version to deal with."
		""
		"Nearly every XyCraft machine and decorative block eats Kivi, so &agrab a stack or two&r. Later, an &6Extractor&r can make it renewable."
	]
	quest.340197AD7E06DADA.quest_subtitle: "The pale stone that pays the bills"
	quest.340197AD7E06DADA.title: "&fKivi Country"
	quest.340AEDBD78F59C0E.quest_desc: [
		"Craft the &eStaff of Life&r from a &eNether Star&r, an &eEnd Rod&r and the &eScythe&r."
		""
		"Fallen villagers are buried in the village graveyard. &aRight-click a headstone&r with the staff to bring them back, healthy and cured. Its tooltip counts the &buses left&r, so save it for someone who matters. Keep a free plot in the graveyard so the next one has somewhere to rest."
	]
	quest.340AEDBD78F59C0E.quest_subtitle: "Death is only a setback"
	quest.340AEDBD78F59C0E.title: "&dSecond Chances"
	quest.344BDBC656E9E57D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Alpine Whispers&r gives the vanilla &bGrove&r and &bSnowy Plains&r a winter makeover: &eArolla Pine&r trees, &eAlpine Gneiss&r rocks, icicles, snow drifts and a soft snow fog."
		""
		"Chop some &eArolla Pine&r. Its planks build the mod's furniture: a Smoker, Sink, Bathtub, Wardrobe and more. &7Hold Shift over a piece to read what it does.&r"
		""
		"&7It also adds Christmas decor: wreaths, garlands, fairy lights and tree baubles.&r"
	]
	quest.344BDBC656E9E57D.quest_subtitle: "Alpine Whispers"
	quest.344BDBC656E9E57D.title: "&bA Whiff of the Alps"
	quest.347A7728F20E7E3B.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Train Schedule&r (a &eSturdy Sheet&r and &ePaper&r make 4) is a list of instructions: &bTravel to Station&r (with * wildcards) or &bDeliver&r and &bRetrieve Packages&r, each with wait conditions like a delay, time of day, cargo or a redstone signal."
		""
		"Seat a &bmob&r (a lead helps) or a &6Blaze Burner&r right in front of the Controls, then right-click it with the finished schedule. &aIt drives for you, even through unloaded chunks.&r"
		""
		"&7Put a schedule into a Station and it copies itself to every train that stops there. Package instructions need Postboxes: right-click a Station with one, then place it nearby.&r"
	]
	quest.347A7728F20E7E3B.quest_subtitle: "Hire a chicken"
	quest.347A7728F20E7E3B.title: "&eWho's Driving?"
	quest.3497D1112A6F75DC.quest_desc: [
		"A &eGold Ingot&r over two &eGold Nuggets&r makes a &6Key&r."
		""
		"A key's password is &bits name&r. A fresh one is just \"Key\", so &arename it in an anvil&r to make your own lock. Click a Safe, Lock Block or Netherite Door with it to bind them."
		""
		"The key works from &banywhere in your inventory&r or your &bCurios belt slot&r. Keep a plain spare too: pirates are not very imaginative with passwords."
	]
	quest.3497D1112A6F75DC.quest_subtitle: "The password is... whatever you call it"
	quest.3497D1112A6F75DC.title: "&eKey Moment"
	quest.34BCBFFE5BF229D9.quest_desc: [
		"Potatoes are a spring crop. Plant the ones you've got, harvest a crop and &asmelt&r them into &eBaked Potatoes&r: cheap, filling, and a fine first food supply. Out of season? Village farms often grow them too."
		""
		"&cDon't waste bone meal&r on out-of-season crops: it gets used up but works only about one time in six."
	]
	quest.34BCBFFE5BF229D9.quest_subtitle: "In season and in the oven"
	quest.34BCBFFE5BF229D9.title: "Hot Potato"
	quest.350EEC7532CCCFD2.quest_desc: [
		"First the sauce: &eBolognese&r in the &6Roaster&r from tomato soup, minced beef, bacon, onion, carrot, a bowl and a &dpotion or red wine&r."
		""
		"Then bake &eBolognese&r, &eRaw Pasta&r and &eMozzarella&r on the &6Stove&r for &eLasagne&r."
		""
		"&aPlace it and serve it by the slice.&r"
	]
	quest.350EEC7532CCCFD2.quest_subtitle: "Garfield would approve"
	quest.350EEC7532CCCFD2.title: "&cLayer Cake, Italian Style"
	quest.35189D1844FE9987.quest_desc: [
		"A &eLoot Bag&r holds &b2-4&r random goodies: sanity food, essence, Hollow Planks and, if you're lucky, &eHauntbound&r armour or one of the three weapons. &aRight-click to open it&r."
		""
		"Raising a tombstone gives one now and then (&b10%&r). The &cHorseman&r always drops &b3&r, so every boss kill is a small haul."
	]
	quest.35189D1844FE9987.quest_subtitle: "Grave goods, gift-wrapped"
	quest.35189D1844FE9987.title: "&eWhat's in the Bag?"
	quest.35AB18A9774726E7.quest_desc: [
		"&6Ars Nouveau&r is magic you build yourself. You write spells from &dglyphs&r in a spell book and pay for them with &dmana&r. Around that sit &dSource&r (the mod's power), crafting altars, &drituals&r, helpful magical creatures, familiars, magic armor and a boss."
		""
		"Your guide is the &eTattered Tome&r, which every player gets on first login (lost it? a &eBook&r plus &eLapis Lazuli&r makes another). It has a search bar for words like \"Ritual\" or \"Familiar\"."
		""
		"&aBest trick:&r hover any Ars item in an inventory and press &bLeft Ctrl&r to jump straight to its page. EMI also has Ars categories for the Scribe's Table, Imbuement Chamber and Enchanting Apparatus."
	]
	quest.35AB18A9774726E7.quest_subtitle: "Some assembly of spells required"
	quest.35AB18A9774726E7.title: "&5Glyphs \\& Sourcery"
	quest.361FE79CC9E4172C.quest_desc: [
		"Wooden &6road signs&r stand out in the wilderness, pointing the way to a &evillage&r with the distance written on them. Find one and step into it."
		""
		"Make your own: &b1 vanilla Sign&r crafts into &b2 Way Signs&r of the same wood (this quest wants &eOak&r). Put them on fences or walls, up to two arms per post. &aClick one with a Compass&r to point it at world spawn or a lodestone, and &bShift-click&r to flip it."
		""
		"&7Map tip: click a map on a bed, banner, beacon or lodestone to add a marker.&r"
	]
	quest.361FE79CC9E4172C.quest_subtitle: "This must be the place"
	quest.361FE79CC9E4172C.title: "&aFollow the Signs"
	quest.3630C5E138346C9A.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Seashelf&r is a Bookshelf in Prismarine Bricks with a &eWater Bottle&r and a &ePufferfish&r. Each gives &b3 Eterna&r (up to 45) and &b+3% Arcana&r."
		""
		"No pufferfish? Apothic adds a recipe: &aany fish plus bamboo&r."
		""
		"An &dInfused Seashelf&r needs &b45 Eterna, 15% Quanta and 10% Arcana&r, so again with &6Frontier&r active."
	]
	quest.3630C5E138346C9A.quest_subtitle: "Seashelves bring Arcana"
	quest.3630C5E138346C9A.title: "&bThe Path of Water"
	quest.364BBBF46EE6A925.quest_desc: [
		"Brew &eDried Black Tea&r with &eSugar&r and a &eGlass Bottle&r at &b50% heat&r (stove plus one Blaze Powder)."
		""
		"&aTough&r does nothing while you're healthy. When you drop to &b4 hearts or less&r it kicks in with &bRegeneration&r and &bResistance&r. Drink one before a risky fight and forget about it."
	]
	quest.364BBBF46EE6A925.quest_subtitle: "The emergency cuppa"
	quest.364BBBF46EE6A925.title: "&8Black Tea"
	quest.3653EC1454E22BFC.quest_desc: [
		"A third ring of &b24 runes&r brings the foundation to &b48&r and the altar to &btier IV&r."
		""
		"That opens &dAwakening Empyrite&r and its ten &dimbuements&r, &dGrand Convergence&r (an Iron Golem) and the &dVigil of the Open Way&r into the Spirit Realm."
		""
		"&7A fourth ring (80 runes in all) reaches tier V: Draconic Ascension makes a Dragon Egg, and Shrouded Conclave summons three Withers. Bring friends.&r"
	]
	quest.3653EC1454E22BFC.quest_subtitle: "Tier IV: 48 runes"
	quest.3653EC1454E22BFC.title: "&5Three Rings Deep"
	quest.365811F1F14B4DB2.quest_desc: [
		"&eVertical Slabs&r fill the half-block gaps regular slabs can't: 3 slabs in a column make 3. &eWooden Posts&r are thin beams that run along any axis (&b3 Wood&r, the bark block, make &b8&r) and hold chains and lanterns."
		""
		"Every wood and most stones get them. Also try &eHedges&r, &eLeaf Carpets&r and &eVertical Planks&r."
		""
		"Builder tips: &bK&r (default; Iris shaders also use K, so check Controls) locks the facing of blocks you place, and you can place a block &abehind or below&r the one you look at (great for bridging)."
	]
	quest.365811F1F14B4DB2.quest_subtitle: "Slabs, but sideways"
	quest.365811F1F14B4DB2.title: "&eStand Up Straight"
	quest.366D17775E704EB0.quest_desc: [
		"You have a roof, a furnace and a backpack. This chapter is the &atoolbox&r: the mods almost everyone on the server ends up using, whatever they specialise in later."
		""
		"The branches are independent, so do them in any order: &6storage&r, &6pipes&r, &6power&r, &6building tools&r, &6travel&r and &6bounties&r, plus the vanilla mid-game (diamonds, enchanting, the Nether, brewing)."
		""
		"Stuck on a recipe? Hover an item and press &bR&r in &6EMI&r for its recipe, &bU&r for its uses."
	]
	quest.366D17775E704EB0.quest_subtitle: "You survived. Now get comfortable."
	quest.366D17775E704EB0.title: "&bKitted Out"
	quest.369F33CA661C89FA.quest_desc: [
		"When the dragon dies, an &6End Gateway&r opens near the island. Throw an &eEnder Pearl&r into it to reach the outer islands, where &6End Cities&r tower above the void."
		""
		"&cShulkers&r shoot bullets that make you levitate, so keep blocks handy and fight near the ground. Their &eShulker Shells&r make Shulker Boxes."
	]
	quest.369F33CA661C89FA.quest_subtitle: "Purple, pointy and full of shulkers"
	quest.369F33CA661C89FA.title: "&dThe City at the End"
	quest.36BA400FE8B48A9C.quest_desc: [
		"Put &bthree identical potions&r in the middle row with &e6 Blaze Powder&r around them for a &6Potion Charm&r. &aRight-click to toggle it&r. While it's on, in your inventory or Curios charm slot, it keeps the effect running and wears down slowly."
		""
		"New brews from Awkward Potions: Shulker Shell for Resistance, Golden Apple for Absorption, Mushroom Stew for Haste, Sweet Berries for Healing Boost, and a Bottle o' Enchanting for &dAncient Knowledge&r (x4 XP)."
		""
		"&7At Pinnacle, infusion makes a charm unbreakable.&r"
	]
	quest.36BA400FE8B48A9C.quest_subtitle: "Potion Charms"
	quest.36BA400FE8B48A9C.title: "&dCharmed, I'm Sure"
	quest.36E2FECB470E3281.quest_desc: [
		"A &eSpyglass&r on &eSticks&r makes a &6Telescope&r. &aRight-click to look through it&r, &bscroll&r to zoom from &b2.5x&r up to &b50x&r, and press &bShift&r to stop. Walk more than 3 blocks away and you stop looking."
		""
		"Its HUD panel shows the &bmoon phase&r and a &bweather forecast&r. Look at the night sky long enough and you may catch a &bshooting star&r. Make a wish!"
	]
	quest.36E2FECB470E3281.quest_subtitle: "Look up"
	quest.36E2FECB470E3281.title: "&9Eyes on the Skies"
	quest.3715BBB37FF125DF.quest_desc: [
		"Surround a block of &eWool&r with &e8 Arcane Essence&r to weave &eArcane Cloth&r."
		""
		"It goes into better spell books, &6Wizard armor&r and the spell-slot upgrades. &aStart stockpiling essence&r: a full Wizard set alone takes 24 cloth."
	]
	quest.3715BBB37FF125DF.quest_subtitle: "Wool, but make it magic"
	quest.3715BBB37FF125DF.title: "&eWoven Wonders"
	quest.3776B9C81D0EABA7.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Foundry&r is buried around &by -10&r under jungles, forests, taigas, deserts, plains, savannas and mountains. Bandit Towers maps and Woodland Explorer Maps can lead here."
		""
		"&cIt's a Nether fortress in disguise&r: Blazes, Magma Cubes, Wither Skeletons with Power bows and a &cPiglin Brute in netherite&r. Bring &dFire Resistance&r and a shield."
		""
		"The treasure is &eBastion-grade&r: diamond blocks, &enetherite scrap&r and high-level enchanted books."
	]
	quest.3776B9C81D0EABA7.quest_subtitle: "Smelting, with extra screaming"
	quest.3776B9C81D0EABA7.title: "&6Hellfire Ironworks"
	quest.37A7AEA9DA6784F5.quest_desc: [
		"A &eBlank Spawner Rune&r is 5 Chains, 2 Gem Dust and 2 Gem-Fused Slate (makes 2). The dust comes from crushing gems, see the gems branch. Add 4 of something to set its effect, then &aright-click a spawner&r with it."
		""
		"Pistons: &b+2 spawn range&r. Comparators: &bredstone control&r. Soul Lanterns: &bignore light&r. Wool: silent mobs. Turtle Eggs: babies. Campfires: mobs spawn burning. Pointed Dripstone: &b-16%&r starting health."
		""
		"&aNether Quartz in your off hand reverses a stat rune&r, and the quartz is kept."
	]
	quest.37A7AEA9DA6784F5.quest_subtitle: "Spawner Runes"
	quest.37A7AEA9DA6784F5.title: "&7Runic Tinkering"
	quest.37B5594D5A0D8BF8.quest_desc: [
		"Quark's &eBackpack&r is worn in the &bchestplate slot&r and gives &b3 extra rows&r of inventory. It needs &eRavager Hide&r, which &cRavagers&r drop during &craids&r, plus Leather, a Chest and an Iron Ingot."
		""
		"&cYou can't take it off while it holds items&r, and it gives no armour."
		""
		"&7Most players use Sophisticated Backpacks. This one is a fun raid trophy.&r"
	]
	quest.37B5594D5A0D8BF8.quest_subtitle: "Raid tested, adventurer approved"
	quest.37B5594D5A0D8BF8.title: "&cRavager Leather"
	quest.38245D9198D238D6.quest_desc: [
		"&eShadowpulse Goo&r is a &eVoidShimmer Goo&r with &e4 Sculk&r, &e2 Sculk Shriekers&r and &e2 Echo Shards&r. Wake it with &eSculk&r or a &eSculk Catalyst&r."
		""
		"Echo Shards come from &6Ancient City&r chests in the Deep Dark. &cTread quietly: the Warden hears everything.&r"
		""
		"At &b10x&r Primogel speed this is the last goo you'll ever need."
	]
	quest.38245D9198D238D6.quest_subtitle: "Tier 4, raided from an Ancient City"
	quest.38245D9198D238D6.title: "&5Echoes of the Deep"
	quest.385535AC640E7952.quest_desc: [
		"Put a &eDispenser&r between &e3 Iron Ingots&r on top and &e3 Planks&r below to build a &6Cannon&r."
		""
		"It has two slots: a &eprojectile&r and &eGunpowder&r. Pick a &bpower level from 1 to 4&r; each shot burns &bthat much gunpowder&r. Light it with flint and steel, a gunpowder trail or &bredstone&r, or use its aiming mode to steer the barrel before firing."
		""
		"A Cannon fires &aanything&r: blocks land and place themselves, TNT is lit on the way out. Proper &eCannonballs&r (5 Blocks of Iron in a plus make 8) smash through blocks depending on how fast they hit."
		""
		"&7The rare &cRed Merchant&7 trader also sells cannons, bombs and rope.&r"
	]
	quest.385535AC640E7952.quest_subtitle: "If it fits in the barrel, it flies"
	quest.385535AC640E7952.title: "&6Fire in the Hole"
	quest.3887DAB32F01006B.quest_desc: [
		"Craft &b9 Fertilizer&r into &6Fertilized Soil&r, or dry &ePodzol&r in the Silo for a free block. Craft a &ePitchfork&r (an iron nugget on two sticks)."
		""
		"&aUse the pitchfork on the soil&r and crops within &b5 blocks&r get a chance to grow. &aHoe a full block&r for &6Fertilized Farmland&r, which gives the crop on it an extra growth boost now and then."
		""
		"&7Fertilized Farmland even survives being jumped on, so no more trampled beds.&r"
	]
	quest.3887DAB32F01006B.quest_subtitle: "Dirt, but premium"
	quest.3887DAB32F01006B.title: "&2Rich Pickings"
	quest.38A09840DF0A3D8D.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Fabricator&r is an autocrafter: &e4 gems&r, Kivi, a &eCrafting Table&r, a &eChest&r and a &6Machine Base&r."
		""
		"Set a recipe in its grid and it &acrafts automatically&r from its own buffer and the inventories next to it. Ctrl-click (&bModifier Key&r) a recipe slot for &bStrict Mode&r, so only that exact item is used. The GUI sets the redstone mode: &bAlways On, High Signal or Pulse&r."
		""
		"&7Pull the finished items out with a hopper or pipe.&r"
	]
	quest.38A09840DF0A3D8D.quest_subtitle: "Crafting tables, but lazy"
	quest.38A09840DF0A3D8D.title: "&6Fab-ulous Crafting"
	quest.38AD2602BD4B6E8F.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Thornborn Towers&r hang high above &bforests&r. Some of the skeletons wear &cThorns&r armour, so hits can sting back, and skeleton archers patrol the sky on phantoms."
		""
		"Climb to the top for high-level enchanted books, diamonds and emeralds, and a small chance of a &6Mining Complex&r map."
	]
	quest.38AD2602BD4B6E8F.quest_subtitle: "So does every skeleton here"
	quest.38AD2602BD4B6E8F.title: "&2Every Rose Has Its Thorns"
	quest.38D36C2DCF7DE90B.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Alteration Table&r (Scribe's Table + 4 Magebloom Fiber) fits &dThreads&r into your magic armor's slots. Put the armor on the stand, use threads on the tablet, then take the armor off to apply. Use the display with an empty hand to remove a thread."
		""
		"Threads are made on the Apparatus around a &eBlank Thread&r (6 Fiber + 3 Gold Nuggets). A thread only counts once across your whole set. &aMagic Capacity&r (+10% max mana per level) is a great first pick."
	]
	quest.38D36C2DCF7DE90B.title: "&6Tailor Made"
	quest.38EAEBF5FB175ED9.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Basin&r (5 Andesite Alloy) holds items and fluids; right-click it with a bucket to pour fluids in. Above it, &btwo blocks up&r with one air gap, goes a &6Mechanical Mixer&r (Cogwheel, Casing and a &eWhisk&r made from Alloy and Iron Sheets)."
		""
		"The mixer runs any &bshapeless&r crafting recipe plus its own: Flour and Water into &eDough&r, and &eAndesite Alloy at half price&r."
		""
		"&cIt needs at least 30 RPM.&r Below that it spins but makes nothing, so gear a water wheel up twice."
	]
	quest.38EAEBF5FB175ED9.quest_subtitle: "Minimum 30 RPM, no exceptions"
	quest.38EAEBF5FB175ED9.title: "&6Mixing It Up"
	quest.39166397EF7810D4.quest_desc: [
		"Press &bC&r to open your spell book. Every spell starts with exactly one &dForm&r (how it travels: Projectile, Touch, Self), then one or more &dEffects&r (what it does), each followed by its &dAugments&r."
		""
		"Try &dProjectile&r → &dBreak&r for a ranged mining spell, save it, and right-click with the book to cast. &bX&r / &bZ&r cycle spells and &bV&r opens a radial menu."
		""
		"Your &dmana&r bar sits at the bottom left. If a spell fizzles, check you have the mana, a Form first and at least one Effect. &7Every new glyph you learn adds +15 max mana.&r"
		""
		"&7These are the default keys, and several are shared with other mods in this pack. The Too Many Keys quest in First Light shows how to sort out clashes.&r"
	]
	quest.39166397EF7810D4.quest_subtitle: "Hello, world (it explodes slightly)"
	quest.39166397EF7810D4.title: "&aForm, Then Function"
	quest.396CB00A6DB0D678.quest_desc: [
		"&6Create: Connected&r adds the parts you always wished Create had. Start with gearboxes: a Gearbox plus a &eLarge Cogwheel&r makes a &6Parallel Gearbox&r. Unlike a normal Gearbox, shafts &baround a corner&r keep the same direction (straight through still reverses). A Gearbox plus two Large Cogwheels makes a &6Six-Way Gearbox&r, with shafts on all six sides (top and bottom spin at &bhalf speed&r)."
		""
		"&7Also worth a look: the Brass Gearbox (wrench each side's direction), the Cross Connector, and Crank Wheels that mesh like cogs.&r"
	]
	quest.396CB00A6DB0D678.quest_subtitle: "Create: Connected"
	quest.396CB00A6DB0D678.title: "&aGear Pressure"
	quest.399A26F91BF719FF.quest_desc: [
		"An &eIron Handle&r is an &eIron Nugget&r on &eAndesite Alloy&r. &bHold right-click&r to hang on and move yourself around it; &bsneak&r while holding to drag the whole contraption; &bscroll&r to change your reach."
		""
		"Great for nudging small builds into place. Dye them, or add a Copper Nugget for a copper one."
		""
		"&7Grabbing a handle mid-fall is a perfectly valid landing strategy.&r"
	]
	quest.399A26F91BF719FF.quest_subtitle: "Mind the gap"
	quest.399A26F91BF719FF.title: "&eGet a Grip"
	quest.39A38D47AD996509.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Thornrose Staff&r (&e6 Sticks&r + &e1 Amethyst Shard&r) draws &dFluxia links&r. &aRight-click the source, then the target.&r Sneak + right-click forgets the stored source."
		""
		"Links are &bone-way&r and both ends must be in the same dimension. Generators and pools can feed many targets at once."
		""
		"&7Nothing moves Fluxia by touch. If a machine sits idle next to a full pool, it's missing a link.&r"
	]
	quest.39A38D47AD996509.quest_subtitle: "The Thornrose Staff"
	quest.39A38D47AD996509.title: "&dSource First, Target Second"
	quest.39B75E0E43D97A08.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Felting Needle&r (Sticks and an Iron Ingot) turns plain wool into patterned wool. &cEMI doesn't show this, so here's how:&r"
		""
		"Hold vanilla &eWool&r in your &boff-hand&r and the needle in your main hand, then &bhold right-click for 6 seconds&r. Let go early and nothing happens. Each felt costs 1 durability."
		""
		"&eWhite Wool&r becomes &ePlaid&r. Make one to get the hang of it."
	]
	quest.39B75E0E43D97A08.quest_subtitle: "Patience, poke, plaid"
	quest.39B75E0E43D97A08.title: "&dNeedle Point"
	quest.39F0E45AD882A72C.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Lighthouse&r stands on &bbeaches and plains&r. Climb to the top: that chest has a &b50%&r chance of a map to the &6Shiraz Palace&r, the richest place in the desert, and a rare copy of the music disc &e11&r."
		""
		"The &6Fishing Hut&r sits on &bbeaches&r too, with a spawner of &czombie fishermen&r. Its barrels hold &dLuck&r potions, enchanted fishing rods and books and, very rarely, a &eTrident&r."
	]
	quest.39F0E45AD882A72C.quest_subtitle: "Lights on, nobody home"
	quest.39F0E45AD882A72C.title: "&eKeepers of the Coast"
	quest.3A0EE8AD083BAE22.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Chicken Coop&r (iron ingots, slabs and a Chicken Nest made from wheat) houses up to &b3 chickens&r and stores up to &b9 eggs&r. Chickens move in on their own; right-click to collect, use a pitchfork to let them out."
		""
		"&eChicken Feed&r is assembled on the &6Cutting Board&r from wheat, a carrot and wheat seeds. It gives chickens &bCluck&r: more eggs and feathers."
		""
		"&7The board also makes Horse Fodder, Dog Food and Cat Food; fill a Pet Bowl and your pets eat at mealtimes.&r"
	]
	quest.3A0EE8AD083BAE22.quest_subtitle: "Which came first?"
	quest.3A0EE8AD083BAE22.title: "&eHen House"
	quest.3A137C1C5BA0A743.quest_desc: [
		"&6Copper Casing&r works like brass casing: right-click a &eStripped Log&r with a &eCopper Ingot&r. Put copper casing over &eDried Kelp&r for a &6Spout&r."
		""
		"Pipe fluid into the Spout and it &afills items on a Depot or Belt below&r: bottles, buckets, and every Create recipe that needs a splash of fluid. Its cousin the &6Item Drain&r (casing plus &eIron Bars&r) empties fluid items rolled across it."
		""
		"&7Spouts work as sequenced assembly steps too. You'll need one for Blaze Cakes and Sturdy Sheets.&r"
	]
	quest.3A137C1C5BA0A743.quest_subtitle: "Copper's finest hour"
	quest.3A137C1C5BA0A743.title: "&eFill 'Er Up"
	quest.3A697D1EC63AAEFF.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Volcanic Sourcelink&r (Lava Bucket centre) burns fuel items dropped next to it or sitting on nearby pedestals. &eArchwood logs&r give bonus Source, and &cBlazing&r Archwood gives the most."
		""
		"&cIts heat slowly turns nearby stone into magma and then lava.&r Don't build it on a stone floor you care about."
	]
	quest.3A697D1EC63AAEFF.title: "&cHot Springs Eternal"
	quest.3A75230A2094E753.quest_desc: [
		"Inside the biome a &bSanity&r bar appears. It starts at 100 and drains every 5 seconds: 1 point by day, 2 at night. From full that's about &b8 minutes&r of daylight, or 4 after dark."
		""
		"It stops draining within &b4 blocks&r of a placed &eLantern&r, Soul Lantern or Jack o'Lantern (the Spectral Lantern and Spectral Jack o'Lantern count too). &cTorches don't&r, and neither does a lantern in your hand. Leave the biome and you recover 5 points every 5 seconds."
		""
		"Hit 0 and you go &cInsane&r for 60 seconds: blind, running wild and taking extra damage. Low sanity also thickens the fog and fills the woods with whispers."
	]
	quest.3A75230A2094E753.quest_subtitle: "The fog gets into your head"
	quest.3A75230A2094E753.title: "&dKeep It Together"
	quest.3A83D076F04C7772.quest_desc: [
		"Three cased helpers built on &6Andesite Casing&r:"
		"&6Gearbox&r (4 Cogwheels): relays rotation to all four sides, perfect for tight corners."
		"&6Clutch&r (Shaft and Redstone): a redstone signal &bdisconnects&r the line."
		"&6Gearshift&r (Cogwheel and Redstone): a redstone signal &breverses&r it."
		""
		"&7An Encased Chain Drive (Casing plus Iron Nuggets) relays rotation along a row, same direction all the way.&r"
	]
	quest.3A83D076F04C7772.quest_subtitle: "Corners, off switches and reverse"
	quest.3A83D076F04C7772.title: "&eTransmission Toolkit"
	quest.3A864D7D2438DC1F.quest_desc: [
		"The &eCrystal Heart&r gives you &b+10 max health&r, which is five extra hearts. It goes in the belt slot."
		""
		"&6Bastion treasure&r chests have an artifact &b65%&r of the time, and the Heart is in that pool, along with the &eGolden Hook&r (more XP from mobs) and the &eCross Necklace&r. End cities and outposts can have it too."
		""
		"&cDon't drop gold-ish artifacts near piglins.&r They pick up the Golden Hook, Cross Necklace, Antidote Vessel and Universal Attractor."
	]
	quest.3A864D7D2438DC1F.quest_subtitle: "+5 hearts, no strings attached"
	quest.3A864D7D2438DC1F.title: "&dHeart of Glass"
	quest.3AA2F1C6BAE4A44E.quest_desc: [
		"&6When Dungeons Arise&r scatters huge hand-built structures across the world: camps, fortresses, palaces, mines, temples and airships. They are &bspread out&r: roughly &bone big one per 800 by 800 blocks&r, and the &bbiome&r decides which one you get. Badlands and swamps only have two candidates each, so they're the easiest to hunt. Plains, forests and deserts are crowded, so any one building there is rare."
		""
		"&aFollow the maps.&r The friendly places (camps, temples, the Lighthouse) keep &eexplorer maps&r to the dangerous ones. A Cartographer's &eWoodland Explorer Map&r leads to the nearest of six of the rarest builds here (or a Woodland Mansion). Loot is per-player, so &aevery player gets their own map&r."
		""
		"&cThe big ones are guarded by spawners&r full of mobs in enchanted gear. Break the spawners as you go. The advancement screen (L) has a &6When Dungeons Arise&r tab that works as a checklist."
		""
		"&7The usual dungeons (YUNG's, IDAS) are in &6Into the Unknown&7. The add-on &6Seven Seas&7 puts pirate ships on the ocean.&r"
	]
	quest.3AA2F1C6BAE4A44E.quest_subtitle: "An adventure log for the long road"
	quest.3AA2F1C6BAE4A44E.title: "&cRise and Plunder"
	quest.3AB032AB02D4A23A.quest_desc: [
		"Every ability in the mod starts as an &eUpgrade: Blank&r, &b4 Ferricore Ingots&r in a diamond shape."
		""
		"Add themed items around a blank to make a real upgrade: two Iron Pickaxes for &eOre Miner&r, two Diamond Axes for &eTree Feller&r, Amethyst and Redstone for &eOre Scanner&r. The guide lists them all."
	]
	quest.3AB032AB02D4A23A.quest_subtitle: "Every ability starts here"
	quest.3AB032AB02D4A23A.title: "&eBlank Slate"
	quest.3AC3643F78251A5E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Create Aeronautics&r is three mods in one jar: &6Simulated&r turns your builds into free-moving physics objects, &6Aeronautics&r makes them fly, and &6Offroad&r puts them on wheels."
		""
		"Everything starts with the &ePhysics Assembler&r: a &eLever&r on an &eAndesite Casing&r with &eAndesite Alloy&r either side. Its manual is &6Ponder&r: hover an item and hold &bW&r."
		""
		"&7You'll want the Create chapters under your belt first: every part here is built from Create machinery.&r"
	]
	quest.3AC3643F78251A5E.quest_subtitle: "Physics, now with you aboard"
	quest.3AC3643F78251A5E.title: "&6Cleared for Takeoff"
	quest.3ACCCE0D709F4626.quest_desc: [
		"Mix &eCake Dough&r in the Crafting Bowl (egg, milk, flour and sugar) and place it on the &6Caking Station&r to get a blank cake. &aSpread strawberry jam&r on it and it's done."
		""
		"Cakes are blocks: right-click to pick one up, &acut it with a knife&r (a Bread Knife, any sword or shears), sneak-right-click to eat a slice. You can stick &bup to 4 candles&r on top and light them."
		""
		"&7Chocolate truffles and chocolate spread make the darker cakes.&r"
	]
	quest.3ACCCE0D709F4626.quest_subtitle: "Make a wish"
	quest.3ACCCE0D709F4626.title: "&dLet Them Eat Cake"
	quest.3AD061214671D2F1.quest_desc: [
		"The finest shelf in the cellar holds one bottle from every craft:"
		""
		"&6Mojang Noir&r: &eRed Grapejuice&r with a &eHoney Bottle&r, a &eCherry&r and a whole &eRed Wine&r. It boosts the experience you collect."
		"&6Smokey Reverie&r: &e2 Dried Oats&r and &eYeast&r on the netherite station. Nearby monsters may burst into flames."
		"&6Awoo Pie Moonshine&r: the apple orchard's finest."
		""
		"&aYou've mastered the vineyard, the brewhouse and the orchard. Pour yourself one. Responsibly.&r"
	]
	quest.3AD061214671D2F1.quest_subtitle: "A tasting flight to remember"
	quest.3AD061214671D2F1.title: "&6The Cellar Master"
	quest.3B172871FE9B4F4D.quest_desc: [
		"&e4 Iron Ingots&r and &e2 Redstone&r around a &eBlock of Cardboard&r make a &6Packager&r. Put it against a chest and give it a &bredstone pulse&r: the chest's contents come out as a package."
		""
		"It works backwards too: &apackages pushed into a Packager get unpacked&r into its inventory, as long as everything fits. Put a &bsign&r on the Packager to write an address on its packages."
		""
		"&7Package Filters (a Zinc Nugget and Wool) sort packages by address; * works as a wildcard.&r"
	]
	quest.3B172871FE9B4F4D.quest_subtitle: "Bubble wrap not included"
	quest.3B172871FE9B4F4D.title: "&eThinking Inside the Box"
	quest.3B4AEA2FCCE864ED.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a &eShulker Box&r with a &eNetherite Ingot&r to make a &6Safe&r. Anything already in the shulker box carries over."
		""
		"Bind it by clicking with your &6Key&r. From then on, only someone carrying a key with the &bsame name&r can open it. Like a shulker box, it keeps its contents when broken."
		""
		"&cOn the server:&r anyone can still pick a safe up and carry it off (it stays locked, but it's gone). Put it inside your &aclaimed chunks&r."
	]
	quest.3B4AEA2FCCE864ED.quest_subtitle: "Netherite-plated peace of mind"
	quest.3B4AEA2FCCE864ED.title: "&6Safe and Sound"
	quest.3B4BE5CC750149CF.quest_desc: [
		"&6Brewery&r brews in a &6Brewing Station&r: an &eIron Ingot&r in the top corner, a &eFurnace&r and &e2 Cauldrons&r across the middle, and &e3 Planks&r along the bottom."
		""
		"Placing it builds a small multiblock: a &6Brew Kettle&r, an &6Oven&r, a &6Timer&r and a &6Whistle&r. &cThe kettle is two blocks tall&r, so give it some headroom and clear space around it."
		""
		"Look at the kettle to see its &binfo panel&r: what's in the kettle, what's missing (water, heat) and what you could brew right now."
	]
	quest.3B4BE5CC750149CF.quest_subtitle: "Kettle, oven, timer, whistle"
	quest.3B4BE5CC750149CF.title: "&6First Sip"
	quest.3BC6C2A10B6F37FD.quest_desc: [
		"Build &b3 Obsidian pillars&r, each at least &b2 blocks&r tall, around an &eEmerald Block&r. At &bnight&r, light the top of each pillar, then light the emerald block and step back."
		""
		"The &cGrim Reaper&r flies, teleports, blinds you and shuffles your inventory. &cArrows and poison do nothing&r, and hitting it while it blocks sends it behind you. Hurt it badly and it rises into the air to heal while minions keep you busy; each later heal is weaker and comes a few minutes apart."
		""
		"It drops the &eScythe&r, and its defeat is required for the Monarch rank."
	]
	quest.3BC6C2A10B6F37FD.quest_subtitle: "Literally"
	quest.3BC6C2A10B6F37FD.title: "&cBeat Death"
	quest.3C30F84FAF9967E3.quest_desc: [
		"&cWither Skeletons&r drop their skull only &b2.5%&r of the time (&b+1%&r per Looting level), so you will need patience. Better Fortresses spawn them &bin packs&r inside the fortress, so farm there."
		""
		"Three skulls and four soul sand (or soul soil) are enough to summon the &cWither&r. &7Here's the sand. The skulls are up to you.&r"
	]
	quest.3C30F84FAF9967E3.quest_subtitle: "Ahead of the game"
	quest.3C30F84FAF9967E3.title: "&8Spooky Scary Skulls"
	quest.3C8C29F0AC0F9137.quest_desc: [
		"Visit &ball 16 Blooming Nature biomes&r: the forests, glades, savannas, marshes, rivers, the Fen and the Desert Oasis."
		""
		"&cThey only generate in new chunks&r, so if your area was explored before, travel somewhere fresh."
		""
		"&aThe advancement gives 500 XP and 2 Completionist Banners.&r A placed banner gives &bLuck II&r within &b8 blocks&r."
	]
	quest.3C8C29F0AC0F9137.quest_subtitle: "Sixteen postcards"
	quest.3C8C29F0AC0F9137.title: "&dBlooming Horizons"
	quest.3CC2F5350ECE5CBC.quest_desc: [
		"Reach &b50 hearts&r with one villager. The heart meter in their menu shows where you stand."
		""
		"Fifty is also the number an &eEngagement Ring&r needs, so if this is someone special, you are halfway down the aisle already. You also receive the book &eBeware the Infection!&r."
		""
		"&7Here are a couple of gold ingots to get the ring fund started.&r"
	]
	quest.3CC2F5350ECE5CBC.quest_subtitle: "50 hearts and counting"
	quest.3CC2F5350ECE5CBC.title: "&aFriendship Found"
	quest.3D105D97013E1F34.quest_desc: [
		"Brew &eDried Green Tea&r with a &eGlass Bottle&r. It needs &b40% heat&r: a stove plus one &eBlaze Powder&r does it."
		""
		"&aBalanced&r keeps refreshing a little &bAbsorption&r on you for 1:30, a free extra layer of hearts."
		""
		"&cTo drink, use it while aiming at open air.&r Clicking a block places the cup as decoration. Break it to pick it back up."
	]
	quest.3D105D97013E1F34.quest_subtitle: "Balanced, like all things should be"
	quest.3D105D97013E1F34.title: "&aGreen Tea"
	quest.3D790BC98E82B79C.quest_desc: [
		"An &6Andesite Funnel&r (Alloy over Dried Kelp) moves items in and out of inventories and belts. Placed normally it &bpulls out&r; &bsneak-place&r it to &binsert&r. Redstone pauses it. Andesite funnels have no filter."
		""
		"An &6Andesite Tunnel&r covers a belt. Give it side outputs and it splits &bone item&r off each passing stack to each side."
		""
		"&7Funnels can't pass items straight between two chests; put a belt or chute in between.&r"
	]
	quest.3D790BC98E82B79C.quest_subtitle: "Departures, arrivals, baggage claim"
	quest.3D790BC98E82B79C.title: "&eAirport Aesthetic"
	quest.3DAEEA52D178D4F3.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Paradox Machine&r (Eclipse Alloy, 3 Time Crystals, a Time Crystal Block and a bucket of Time Fluid, so &b13 crystals&r in all) rewinds an area. Set its area, put &eore blocks&r and/or mobs in it, and press &bSnapshot&r. Later, it brings back whatever you removed."
		""
		"Each block or mob restored costs &b250,000 FE&r and &b50 mB&r of Time Fluid. Pair it with goo Raw blocks for a renewable ore farm, within limits. &7Restored mobs might not be quite the same ones.&r"
		""
		"&cEvery restore builds Paradox Energy.&r Let it reach the limit and a &5Paradox&r appears that devours blocks, items and mobs. &aThrow a Time Crystal into it to seal it.&r"
		""
		"You started with a lump of goo and ended up editing time. Not bad for some dire things."
	]
	quest.3DAEEA52D178D4F3.quest_subtitle: "Rewind, replay, regret"
	quest.3DAEEA52D178D4F3.title: "&5Grandfather Clause"
	quest.3DC11EAE1A18C3FE.quest_desc: [
		"Leave smoked food sitting in the output while the station &bkeeps burning&r. After about &b12 minutes&r it becomes &dPerfectly smoked&r: it glints, and its bonuses are &b1.5x&r. &cLeave it far too long&r and it loses the status again."
		""
		"&cThe fire must not go out&r, or the timer starts over. The station only burns while there is food in the input and planks in the fuel slot, and each plank lasts &b10 seconds&r, so stock about &ba stack and a bit&r of planks and some food to smoke meanwhile."
		""
		"Some woods add an effect: &ejungle&r gives Regeneration, &ecrimson&r Fire Resistance and &ewarped&r Absorption. Acacia and dark oak add a little healing."
	]
	quest.3DC11EAE1A18C3FE.quest_subtitle: "Good things come to those who wait"
	quest.3DC11EAE1A18C3FE.title: "&dPerfectly Smoked"
	quest.3DCBFD6F77EA86E2.quest_desc: [
		"&ePlanks&r around an &eEmerald&r make a &6Speaker Block&r. Type a message of up to &b32 characters&r and pick how it appears: chat, status bar, title or &bnarrator voice&r."
		""
		"On a redstone pulse it broadcasts the message to everyone in range; set the range in its screen, up to &b64 blocks&r. Rename it in an anvil to change the speaker's name."
		""
		"&aGreat for shop doorbells, farm alarms and spawn announcements.&r"
	]
	quest.3DCBFD6F77EA86E2.quest_subtitle: "Attention shoppers"
	quest.3DCBFD6F77EA86E2.title: "&dNow Hear This"
	quest.3DD6E7FE0C83D348.quest_desc: [
		"Mix &eall six cocktails&r. They don't have to be in your bag at the same time. Every one needs &eIce&r, plus:"
		"&eSweet Berry&r: Sugar and Sweet Berries."
		"&eCocoa&r: Cocoa Beans and Sugar."
		"&eMelon&r: a Melon Slice and Sugar."
		"&eHoney&r: Honeycomb and a Milk Bucket."
		"&ePumpkin&r: a Pumpkin, Sugar and a Milk Bucket."
		""
		"&7The Melon Cocktail's Luck helps with fishing on the next branch over.&r"
	]
	quest.3DD6E7FE0C83D348.quest_subtitle: "Happy hour, all six of them"
	quest.3DD6E7FE0C83D348.title: "&dThe Big Sip"
	quest.3E47091FA59E5BFC.quest_desc: [
		"A &eCrib&r is &e4 fences&r, a &ecarpet&r and &e3 planks&r. There is one for every vanilla wood and carpet colour, so pick one that suits the nursery."
		""
		"&aRight-click the crib with a baby&r to lay it down. The baby keeps growing in there, so you are not stuck carrying it around for twenty minutes."
	]
	quest.3E47091FA59E5BFC.quest_subtitle: "Hands free at last"
	quest.3E47091FA59E5BFC.title: "&eRock-a-Bye"
	quest.3E61005C394E3A21.quest_desc: [
		"A row of &eCopper Sheet&r, &eCopper Ingot&r, &eCopper Sheet&r makes &b4&r &6Fluid Pipes&r. A pipe plus a &eCogwheel&r makes a &6Mechanical Pump&r."
		""
		"Pumps push fluid the way their &barrow&r points (&ba Wrench reverses it&r) through pipes up to &b16 blocks&r away, and faster rotation means faster flow. &aAn open pipe end pulls in the water source in front of it&r, and a vanilla infinite-water pool refills it, so a pump in a small pool can keep a boiler supplied."
		""
		"&7Wrench a straight pipe to give it a window.&r"
	]
	quest.3E61005C394E3A21.quest_subtitle: "Pipes carry, pumps push"
	quest.3E61005C394E3A21.title: "&bPipe Dreams"
	quest.3EB7214C9835A190.quest_desc: [
		"&eBlank Parchment&r is 8 Magebloom Fiber around a Paper. To write on it, place it on the &6Scribe's Table&r, select a spell in your book, then &bsneak-use the book&r on the table."
		""
		"&eSpell Parchment&r feeds turrets, runes and the Reactive enchantment."
		""
		"&7Team tip: the Annotated Codex (Blank Parchment + Leather) records every glyph you know, for a little XP per glyph. A teammate who uses it learns them all, and the codex is used up.&r"
	]
	quest.3EB7214C9835A190.title: "&ePut It in Writing"
	quest.3EC4087AFC2200BC.quest_desc: [
		"Drop a &eTime Crystal&r into Polymorphic Fluid to get &dTime Fluid&r. The &eTime Wand&r (Blazegold, Ferricore and a Time Crystal) runs on FE plus Time Fluid; right-click a Time Fluid source to fill it."
		""
		"Right-click a furnace, crop or machine to tick it &b2x&r faster for &b30 seconds&r. Click again for 4x, 8x... up to &b256x&r. &cEach step doubles the cost&r in FE and fluid."
	]
	quest.3EC4087AFC2200BC.quest_subtitle: "Fast-forward, at a price"
	quest.3EC4087AFC2200BC.title: "&dHurry Up and Wait"
	quest.3ECFA6E6A13C770C.quest_desc: [
		"&eAndesite Alloy&r goes into almost every early Create part. Craft it from &e2 Andesite&r and &e2 Iron Nuggets&r in a checkerboard. &eZinc Nuggets&r work in place of iron."
		""
		"&aTip:&r once you own a &6Mechanical Mixer&r, the same alloy costs only &b1 Andesite and 1 Nugget&r. Half price!"
	]
	quest.3ECFA6E6A13C770C.quest_subtitle: "The grey stuff that runs the world"
	quest.3ECFA6E6A13C770C.title: "&eSturdier Rocks"
	quest.3ECFDCDD3342D98A.quest_desc: [
		"&6Ars Technical&r bridges Source and &bForge Energy (FE)&r. Imbue a Source Gem with an Iron Ingot, a Redstone Block and a Clock on pedestals to make &eMachine Essence&r."
		""
		"The &6Mana Fabricator&r (Diamond centre on the Apparatus with Gold, Iron, Earth, Manipulation and Machine Essence: &b10 pedestals&r) &aturns FE into Source 1:1&r, up to &b200 Source a second&r, into a jar within 5 blocks. Feed it from an Alternator (see &6Bolt-On Brilliance&r) for a Source farm."
		""
		"&cThe Mana Generator goes the other way at a terrible 20:1 loss.&r &7It also adds two Tier II glyphs: Bulldozer (scoops a block into your inventory) and Generator (charges FE items).&r"
	]
	quest.3ECFDCDD3342D98A.quest_subtitle: "Forge Energy in, Source out"
	quest.3ECFDCDD3342D98A.title: "&6Ars Technical&r: Plug and Pray"
	quest.3F1DD1F8BC20B0C4.quest_desc: [
		"&cDragonflies&r drop up to two &eDragonfly Wings&r each. Wings are the &dAstral&r focus: put them in the &6Scroll Forge&r to write astral scrolls."
		""
		"&aSmelt spare wings&r into &eLumine Dust&r, then mix the dust with quartz or amethyst shards for &eLumine&r and &eUmbral Lumine&r building blocks."
		""
		"&7Sniffers sometimes dig up Mothspawn, a throwable egg that can hatch Lunar Moths.&r"
	]
	quest.3F1DD1F8BC20B0C4.quest_subtitle: "The astral focus"
	quest.3F1DD1F8BC20B0C4.title: "&9Wings of the Night"
	quest.3F3A0E2A5C471922.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Steam Vent&r is a &eGold Sheet&r on a &eBlock of Copper&r. It sits on a Create &6boiler&r and fills a balloon with steam: up to &b5000 m³&r, ten times a burner."
		""
		"Like a steam engine it needs &bheat, water and boiler space&r, and it's redstone-powered. That means carrying a heated Fluid Tank on board: heavy, but it is how you lift a flagship."
	]
	quest.3F3A0E2A5C471922.quest_subtitle: "Ten burners in a trench coat"
	quest.3F3A0E2A5C471922.title: "&6Up in Steam"
	quest.3FC2271EE35AF354.quest_desc: [
		"Pour &b1 ingot&r of molten &eRose Gold&r over a &eCobweb&r on a Casting Table to get &eSilky Cloth&r."
		""
		"Five cloths and a tool in the &6Anvil&r give you the &dSilky&r ability: &aSilk Touch&r. It uses the tool's ability slot, so choose carefully. Luck and Autosmelt also need the Anvil."
	]
	quest.3FC2271EE35AF354.quest_subtitle: "Silk Touch, Foundry-style"
	quest.3FC2271EE35AF354.title: "&eSmooth Operator"
	quest.3FD8AC3888E73941.quest_desc: [
		"Approach the bell tower and the &cEnder Dragon&r rises. The &eEnd Crystals&r on the pillars heal her, so &ashoot them out first&r (climb up to any that are caged). Bring arrows, blocks, slow falling and plenty of food."
		""
		"The kill counts for the team that lands the final blow. Missed it? Place &b4 End Crystals&r on the four bedrock blocks inside the tower to summon her again."
		""
		"&7There's only one Dragon Egg per world. Resummoned dragons don't drop another.&r"
	]
	quest.3FD8AC3888E73941.quest_subtitle: "The bell tolls for thee"
	quest.3FD8AC3888E73941.title: "&5Free the End"
	quest.4013D7E9497FBA27.quest_desc: [
		"&6Elevators&r: &e8 Wool&r around an &eEnder Pearl&r. Place two in the same column, up to &b384 blocks&r apart with anything in between. &aJump&r to go up, &asneak&r to go down. No XP cost."
		""
		"Re-dye them any colour; colours don't need to match. Right-click one with a block to &acamouflage&r it."
	]
	quest.4013D7E9497FBA27.quest_subtitle: "*ding*"
	quest.4013D7E9497FBA27.title: "&fGoing Up!"
	quest.40159A69B0537956.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Void Container&r is a &eDark gem&r surrounded by &eAluminum Nuggets&r on top of &e3 Kivi&r. It deletes every item, fluid and bit of energy you push into it, so it makes a perfect trash can."
		""
		"&cWarning:&r it also &cpulls items, fluids and energy out of the block it's mounted on&r and destroys them. Only mount it on something you want emptied, never on a chest you care about."
	]
	quest.40159A69B0537956.quest_subtitle: "A black hole, contained (mostly)"
	quest.40159A69B0537956.title: "&8Event Horizon"
	quest.4028F73D2A8BE74C.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Table Cloth&r (&eAndesite Alloy&r and &eWool&r) turns your stock network into a shop. Interact with your Stock Keeper while holding a cloth to set up a trade, place the cloth, and put the &bprice item&r in its side slot."
		""
		"Customers click the cloth for a &eShopping List&r, hand it to the keeper, and the goods arrive as a package. &aPayment piles up inside the Stock Ticker&r."
		""
		"&7Price it in Bronze or Silver Coins and you've got a real server shop. Table Cloths can be clicked inside FTB Chunks claims, but &cyour keeper may be protected from outsiders&r&7, so test checkout with a player from another team.&r"
	]
	quest.4028F73D2A8BE74C.quest_subtitle: "Coins welcome"
	quest.4028F73D2A8BE74C.title: "&eMarket Day"
	quest.402FE9BD52E87124.quest_desc: [
		"&eWild Hops&r grow in &6taiga&r biomes, and breaking one drops &eHops&r. Hops are their own seed: &aplant them on farmland&r."
		""
		"The vine grows &b2 blocks&r tall on its own, or &b4 blocks&r if you &aright-click it with Farm \\& Charm &eRope&r. It needs decent light and takes bone meal. &aRight-click a ripe vine to harvest it.&r"
	]
	quest.402FE9BD52E87124.quest_subtitle: "They climb, if you let them"
	quest.402FE9BD52E87124.title: "&2Hop to It"
	quest.404DB238AC810B0C.quest_desc: [
		"Open &bTalk&r and try to &aChat&r, tell a &aJoke&r or tell a &aStory&r. A success usually adds about &b5 hearts&r with that villager; a flop costs a few."
		""
		"&aHover the villager's personality&r for a hint about what they like: Upbeat villagers love jokes, Flirty ones welcome flirting, and &cSensitive&r villagers lose twice as many hearts when you get it wrong. A good mood helps too."
		""
		"&7Talk too long and they get tired of you. Take a walk and come back in a few minutes.&r"
	]
	quest.404DB238AC810B0C.quest_subtitle: "Read the room first"
	quest.404DB238AC810B0C.title: "&aSmall Talk"
	quest.405E950D64AB0795.quest_desc: [
		"&eIron&r, &ePlanks&r and &eWooden Slabs&r make a &6Pulley Block&r; a &eStick&r and &eStone&r make a &6Crank&r."
		""
		"Load the pulley with &eRope&r or &eChain&r, then &aturn it with a Crank&r (or a Turn Table on its axis). It lowers or raises the line and &apulls whatever is tied to the end&r."
		""
		"One pulley drags &bup to 8 blocks&r (rope doesn't count), and &bpulleys turning together pool their strength&r, so two ropes can lift a wide platform. That's a real &6elevator&r."
		""
		"&7Quark's Rope Coil also works in a pulley.&r"
	]
	quest.405E950D64AB0795.quest_subtitle: "Elevator music not included"
	quest.405E950D64AB0795.title: "&6Pulling Your Weight"
	quest.40636DB37FF184B9.quest_desc: [
		"Two &6Oak Base Cabinets&r craft into an &6Oak Wardrobe&r, two blocks tall. &aRight-click it with armour to hang it up&r, and &bSneak-right-click&r to take it back out. Hang up one piece to finish this quest."
		""
		"The &6Mirror&r (&eSticks&r, &eTinted Glass&r and an &eOak Slab&r) shows a &blive reflection&r. &7If your FPS dips near a wall of mirrors, turn off enableReflections in Furniture's config.&r"
		""
		"&cNever right-click a Mirror with paper renamed \"Mirror, Mirror\".&r Asking who is the fairest of them all summons a lit Creeper right behind you."
	]
	quest.40636DB37FF184B9.quest_subtitle: "Mirror, mirror, on the wall..."
	quest.40636DB37FF184B9.title: "&eNothing to Wear"
	quest.40641CC0CE89599A.quest_desc: [
		"Press some gold into &eGolden Sheets&r for two essential tools."
		""
		"The &6Wrench&r (3 Golden Sheets, a Cogwheel and a Stick) rotates Create blocks with right-click and &apicks them up instantly with sneak-right-click&r."
		""
		"&6Engineer's Goggles&r (String, Glass and a Golden Sheet) show speed and stress readouts when you look at machines. They fit your helmet slot or the &bCurios head slot&r."
	]
	quest.40641CC0CE89599A.quest_subtitle: "Look the part, fix the part"
	quest.40641CC0CE89599A.title: "&eDressed to Wrench"
	quest.40974294A392FEC2.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Storage Crate&r is a chest wrapped in &eIron Ingots&r and &ePlanks&r. It holds &b640 items&r no matter how they stack."
		""
		"That makes it &cpoor for bulk&r (cobblestone fills it fast) and &agreat for unstackables&r: tools, potions, enchanted books, or a hundred different odd blocks."
		""
		"&7For serious storage, see Sophisticated Storage in the &6Kitted Out&7 chapter.&r"
	]
	quest.40974294A392FEC2.quest_subtitle: "For the odds and ends"
	quest.40974294A392FEC2.title: "&6Crate Expectations"
	quest.409C2D38F335E43E.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Infested Temple&r is buried about &b32 blocks underground&r in &btaigas, hills, snowy biomes and cherry groves&r. It works like a Trial Chamber: &cTrial Spawners&r of spiders, cave spiders, Wither Skeletons and &cinvisible, floating skeleton archers&r, and no other mobs spawn inside."
		""
		"Beat a spawner for an &eInfested Temple Key&r and open the &6vault&r. That vault always gives a key for the higher vault, with &dPurification&r (armour that can shrug off poison and wither) and a good chance of &eEnchanted Golden Apples&r."
		""
		"&7One spawner drops an Ominous Bottle. Drink it and the spawners turn ominous, with an ominous vault of their own. Vaults are per-player.&r"
	]
	quest.409C2D38F335E43E.quest_subtitle: "The walls have legs"
	quest.409C2D38F335E43E.title: "&8Something Skittering"
	quest.40A8C1B55C11EDCE.quest_desc: [
		"Draw a 9x9 circle with &bone glyph of every colour&r (the Grimoire's eye icon shows which shape goes where), drop &eone of each of the 16 chalks&r inside and pay &b5,000 ƒ&r. Out comes &dOmni Chalk&r with &b512 uses&r."
		""
		"&bSneak + scroll&r to choose a rite (&bsneak + right-click the air&r flips to the next chapter), then &aright-click an altar and it draws the whole circle for you&r. &bSneak + right-click the altar&r rubs a circle out. Each glyph it draws costs one use."
		""
		"&7Close to essential for the 120-glyph Shrouded Conclave at tier V.&r"
	]
	quest.40A8C1B55C11EDCE.quest_subtitle: "The last circle you draw by hand"
	quest.40A8C1B55C11EDCE.title: "&dThe Whole Spectrum"
	quest.4132717CB29CCC2D.quest_desc: [
		"Smoke your first piece of food. The &ewood type&r decides how long it takes and what you gain."
		""
		"&eOak&r is a balanced all-rounder, &espruce&r leans to saturation, &echerry&r to nutrition, and &ebamboo&r is the quickest. Woods from other mods add their own flavours; check EMI's smoker tab."
		""
		"&cEach food can only be smoked once.&r"
	]
	quest.4132717CB29CCC2D.quest_subtitle: "Every wood tastes different"
	quest.4132717CB29CCC2D.title: "&7Hickory Dickory Smoke"
	quest.41709EEDEFB6AD60.quest_desc: [
		"Perform &dSummon Wilden&r with a &eSpike&r, &eHorn&r and &eWing&r thrown on the brazier and the &5Wilden Chimera&r answers. The mod recommends &dTier II&r spells and gear, plus buffs, Dispel and mobility. It resists cold damage."
		""
		"&cThe ritual destroys blocks around the brazier, and in this pack the Chimera's dive bomb breaks blocks too.&r Fight it far away from your base."
		""
		"It drops a &eWilden Tribute&r, the key to the Archmage's book."
	]
	quest.41709EEDEFB6AD60.quest_subtitle: "Three Wilden in a trench coat"
	quest.41709EEDEFB6AD60.title: "&5Chimera Obscura"
	quest.42047FDCBB9C4C26.quest_desc: [
		"&6Apple trees&r and &6Dark Cherry trees&r grow wild in plains and meadows, but they are &crare&r. The &6Wandering Winemaker&r sells their saplings, which is usually the easier route."
		""
		"&aRight-click leaves that show fruit&r to pick &eApples&r or &eCherries&r. The leaves grow new fruit and take bone meal."
		""
		"Cherries go into several wines, and dark cherry gives a full wood set with its own furniture and wine racks."
	]
	quest.42047FDCBB9C4C26.quest_subtitle: "Life is a bowl of them"
	quest.42047FDCBB9C4C26.title: "&cCherry Picker"
	quest.424068CCA81E31AE.quest_desc: [
		"&eSugar&r and an &eEgg&r make 4 &eMarshmallows&r. Put one on a &eStick&r and &bhold right-click on a lit Campfire&r. It goes Warmed, &aMelted&r, Charred, then Totally Burnt."
		""
		"&aLet go at Melted&r for a short burst of &bSpeed&r. &cCharred and burnt ones give Hunger.&r"
		""
		"&7No patience? Cook a plain marshmallow on a campfire or grill for a Roasted Marshmallow.&r"
	]
	quest.424068CCA81E31AE.quest_subtitle: "Not too much, not too little"
	quest.424068CCA81E31AE.title: "&dGolden Brown"
	quest.42572791E06E1378.quest_desc: [
		"&eQuicklime&r comes from &asmelting Calcite&r, the white stone layer inside every amethyst geode. Surround one &eDye&r with &e8 Quicklime&r for &b8&r blocks of &6Plaster&r in that colour. All 16 colours exist."
		""
		"Plaster is the classic filling for Timber Frames. Keep spare Quicklime too: the rubblestone quest needs it."
	]
	quest.42572791E06E1378.quest_subtitle: "Geodes: not just for amethyst"
	quest.42572791E06E1378.title: "&fLime and Plaster"
	quest.426260191C63DF08.quest_desc: [
		"&aUse Shears on a Spectral Pumpkin&r to carve it, then put a &eSpectral Essence&r under the carved pumpkin to get a &6Spectral Jack o'Lantern&r. Lazy? The pumpkin piles have a few ready-made ones to pick up."
		""
		"It's a sanity light too, and you can wear it as a spooky helmet. The Infected Zombies clearly agree."
	]
	quest.426260191C63DF08.quest_subtitle: "Every pumpkin has a face inside"
	quest.426260191C63DF08.title: "&6Carve Your Own Ghost"
	quest.42775BE93FCD259C.quest_desc: [
		"The advancement says \"start a family\", but it actually wants &bthree children&r. Wait &b3 days&r between babies, and place each baby before you ask for the next one."
		""
		"Your reward is the book &eManaging Your Family Vol. XI&r. To see who is related to whom, use the &bFamily Tree&r button on any villager, or craft a &eFamily Tree&r from a book and an oak sapling."
	]
	quest.42775BE93FCD259C.quest_subtitle: "Settling In"
	quest.42775BE93FCD259C.title: "&aA Full House"
	quest.4292A7DC7DB110FB.quest_desc: [
		"Dig &cbelow Y=0&r. Down there you'll meet small &6Stonelings&r: tiny stone creatures carrying an item. They &brun away unless you sneak&r up on them (a Glow Shroom also lures them)."
		""
		"Break one and it always drops a &eHeart of Diamond&r, plus whatever it held. You need that heart for the &ePickarang&r."
		""
		"&cThe deep is busy&r: Oretoises, Forgotten skeletons, and Monster Boxes that burst open with a pack of mobs when you get close."
	]
	quest.4292A7DC7DB110FB.quest_subtitle: "Below zero, things get interesting"
	quest.4292A7DC7DB110FB.title: "&bShape of My Heart"
	quest.4296B98C6A6C2EDA.quest_desc: [
		"&6Farm \\& Charm&r is the heart of this chapter: new crops, hand-cranked kitchen stations, smarter livestock and a whole menu of hearty dishes. &6Bakery&r, &6Candlelight&r and &6Smoker&r all plug into its kitchen, so start here."
		""
		"There is no guide book. &bEMI&r has a tab for every station (&bStove&r, &bPot Cooking&r, &bRoaster&r, &bCrafting Bowl&r, &bMincer&r, &bCutting Board&r, &bDrying&r). Looking at a station shows a little info panel, and many items explain themselves when you &bhold Shift&r."
		""
		"&cImportant:&r when a recipe asks for \"water\", it means a &eWater Bucket&r, not a bottle. You get the bucket back."
	]
	quest.4296B98C6A6C2EDA.quest_subtitle: "Wipe your boots, dinner's on"
	quest.4296B98C6A6C2EDA.title: "&6The Country Kitchen"
	quest.42C6FB42DCA61CE1.quest_desc: [
		"Giant-mushroom homes grow in &bforests&r. The &6Mushroom House&r and the &6Mushroom Village&r are held by &cpiglins with crossbows and Piglin Brutes&r with golden swords, a nasty surprise in the overworld (and they don't turn into zombie piglins)."
		""
		"The village has emeralds, gold and iron. The house's treasure chests can hold a &emap to the Mushroom Mines&r."
	]
	quest.42C6FB42DCA61CE1.quest_subtitle: "There's not mushroom in here"
	quest.42C6FB42DCA61CE1.title: "&cFun Guys"
	quest.42E27B7A7085D352.quest_desc: [
		"Finish the bounty and right-click the board to cash in. Rewards are mostly &eEmeralds&r, plus food, gear and the odd rare prize - spend the emeralds with villagers."
		""
		"Each board tracks your &breputation&r there, which grows with every bounty you turn in. Hang &eDecrees&r on a board (up to &b3&r) to choose its theme: farmer, armorer, librarian and more."
	]
	quest.42E27B7A7085D352.quest_subtitle: "For honest work"
	quest.42E27B7A7085D352.title: "&6Honest Pay"
	quest.4340DC5E5919265C.quest_desc: [
		"Lay track straight into a &eNether Portal&r and the matching track is built on the other side. Every block travelled in the Nether counts as &b8&r in the Overworld, so a Nether line is a huge shortcut between far-off bases."
		""
		"&cThe Nether is not friendly to commuters.&r Wall the line in: Ghasts don't read timetables."
	]
	quest.4340DC5E5919265C.quest_subtitle: "Eight blocks for the price of one"
	quest.4340DC5E5919265C.title: "&cNether Express"
	quest.4348042B2F5025A1.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Scorched Alloyer&r is &e5 Scorched Bricks&r with a scorched gauge. Its gauges use &eQuartz&r instead of glass."
		""
		"Place it on a heater or fuel tank and put &btanks&r of the input metals around it. More tanks means more metals to mix. &aIt alloys continuously&r, with no Smeltery needed, and hotter fuel unlocks better alloys."
	]
	quest.4348042B2F5025A1.quest_subtitle: "Alloys without the Smeltery"
	quest.4348042B2F5025A1.title: "&6Alloy, Alloy"
	quest.434D90B8532D82B0.quest_desc: [
		"Craft any vanilla &eBoat&r together with a &6Cannon&r to mount the gun on deck. The keys to fire, aim and dismount show on screen while you ride."
		""
		"Every wood works (and a Bamboo Raft becomes a cannon raft); this quest wants the &eOak&r one."
		""
		"&cWatch the horizon:&r pillagers know how to sail cannon boats too, and raids can now arrive by sea."
	]
	quest.434D90B8532D82B0.quest_subtitle: "Your very own navy, crew of one"
	quest.434D90B8532D82B0.title: "&9Man-o'-War"
	quest.4357784E95DB5C6F.quest_desc: [
		"For &dTier 3&r, put the Tier 2 piece back in the Apparatus with &e2 Ender Pearls&r and a &eChorus Fruit&r, and have &b5000 Source&r ready."
		""
		"Tier 3 gives every piece a third slot, and every &6Sorceror's&r piece a &blevel 3&r slot. The best threads want one: &dGliding&r (elytra flight) and &dUndying&r (a totem that recharges when you sleep) need level 3, and &dRepairing&r in a level 3 slot makes your magic armor unbreakable."
	]
	quest.4357784E95DB5C6F.quest_subtitle: "Tier 3, dressed to kill"
	quest.4357784E95DB5C6F.title: "&5Haute Couture"
	quest.43589E4AE089D241.quest_desc: [
		"The &eApprentice's Spell Book&r takes &e3 Gold Ingots&r, &e4 Arcane Essence&r and &e2 Hogskin&r. It holds &b8 spells&r and adds &b+50 mana&r and 15% cast time reduction."
		""
		"&eHogskin&r drops from &cHoglins&r in the Nether's crimson forests."
		""
		"&aFarm tip:&r the Apothecarist (in swamp Mangrove Huts) sells a &dNetherward Tincture&r that stops a hoglin from zombifying in the Overworld, and its piglets inherit the protection."
	]
	quest.43589E4AE089D241.quest_subtitle: "8 slots, +50 mana, +15% cast speed"
	quest.43589E4AE089D241.title: "&eGetting the Hang of It"
	quest.438F8D981B5187AC.quest_desc: [
		"The &eSpectral War Axe&r ignores &bhalf of its target's armour&r and makes them &bglow&r for 6 seconds, so nothing hides in the fog."
		""
		"The tombstone skeletons carry them and drop one now and then. &eLoot Bags&r have them too. Like all three Hollow weapons it has &b2031&r durability and is repaired with &eLuminous Essence&r."
	]
	quest.438F8D981B5187AC.quest_subtitle: "Halfway through the plate, every time"
	quest.438F8D981B5187AC.title: "&cArmour? What Armour?"
	quest.43D618DBF294BF5A.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Slingshot&r is a &eLead&r and &eLeather&r on a frame of &eSticks&r. It fires snowballs, eggs, flint, clay, slime balls, iron or gold nuggets, chorus fruit, fire charges and firework stars."
		""
		"&7Two rare treasure enchantments exist for it: &dAlchemistry&r&7 fires potions, &dHeavy Lifting&r&7 fires the block in your off-hand. You can only have one.&r"
	]
	quest.43D618DBF294BF5A.quest_subtitle: "Aim for the bullseye"
	quest.43D618DBF294BF5A.title: "&aApple of My Eye"
	quest.43EA21DDB3A695A3.quest_desc: [
		"The &eReins of the Spectral Horse&r drop from every Horseman. &aRight-click a block&r to summon a &6Spectral Horse&r: tamed, saddled and yours. It doesn't despawn."
		""
		"It's a solid horse with a little armour of its own, and like a donkey it can carry a &eChest&r. Hold a &eSpectral Essence&r and it will follow you."
		""
		"&cThe reins are used up&r, so pick a good spot to summon."
	]
	quest.43EA21DDB3A695A3.quest_subtitle: "Comes pre-tamed, pre-saddled, pre-dead"
	quest.43EA21DDB3A695A3.title: "&bSteed of the Damned"
	quest.440BCA9C11F80442.quest_desc: [
		"An &6Urn&r is one clay ball on the Pottery Table. It's handy storage, but it has a secret: &acarry an Urn (or Amphore) when you die&r and one of them is placed at your death spot and &bswallows your whole inventory&r, armour and offhand included. Open or break it to get everything back."
		""
		"&7It only works with keepInventory off. Treat it as a cosy backup to the pack's usual death handling, not a replacement.&r"
	]
	quest.440BCA9C11F80442.quest_subtitle: "Grave goods, but for the living"
	quest.440BCA9C11F80442.title: "&5Urn Your Keep"
	quest.4416F174410E5202.quest_desc: [
		"Bottle the dragon's breath, then infuse it at &b80 Eterna, 15-30% Quanta and 60%+ Arcana&r (Pinnacle) for &b3&r &dInfused Dragon's Breath&r."
		""
		"That goes into an &6Endshelf&r (5 Eterna, max &b90&r). Add a &eDragon Head&r from an End Ship and 5 Ender Pearls for the &6Draconic Endshelf&r: &b+20 Eterna&r, max &b100&r."
	]
	quest.4416F174410E5202.quest_subtitle: "Endshelves"
	quest.4416F174410E5202.title: "&5Here Be Dragons"
	quest.441962DA9A640B35.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Hand Crank&r is your first power source: three planks over one Andesite Alloy. Attach it to a shaft and &bhold right-click&r to turn it; sneak to turn the other way."
		""
		"It gives &b32 RPM&r and &b256 SU&r of capacity, but only while you crank, and it slowly drains your &chunger&r."
		""
		"&7There is a hidden advancement for cranking until you collapse. We don't recommend it.&r"
	]
	quest.441962DA9A640B35.quest_subtitle: "Power, by hand"
	quest.441962DA9A640B35.title: "&eElbow Grease"
	quest.4430294FC86DE6EE.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Inscription Table&r writes scrolls into spell books. Craft it from a &eBook&r, &e3 wooden slabs&r and &e2 fences&r."
		""
		"Put your spell book in the top slot and a scroll below it, then click to &ainscribe&r. Select a spell in the book and take it out to get the scroll back, which also removes the spell from the book."
		""
		"&7Nothing is wasted while you experiment: swap spells in and out as often as you like.&r"
	]
	quest.4430294FC86DE6EE.quest_subtitle: "Ink and a steady hand"
	quest.4430294FC86DE6EE.title: "&6Quaint Scribe"
	quest.4442AD8BE5B436F5.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Electric Motor&r is the reverse of the Alternator. Mechanical-craft it from &eAndesite Alloy&r, &eBrass Sheets&r, &eCopper Spools&r, an &eIron Rod&r and a &eCapacitor&r (a Zinc Sheet, Copper Sheet and Redstone Torch in a column; press a Zinc Ingot for the sheet)."
		""
		"Scroll the panel on its back to set the speed, up to &b256 RPM&r either way. It draws &b480 FE/t&r at full speed and gives &b64 SU per RPM&r, so turning it down also cuts its stress capacity."
		""
		"&cAn Alternator feeding a Motor loses a quarter of the energy. No free power here.&r"
	]
	quest.4442AD8BE5B436F5.quest_subtitle: "FE in, RPM out"
	quest.4442AD8BE5B436F5.title: "&6Motor Mouth"
	quest.4452454FA584E978.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a &eWooden Bucket&r from planks and a wooden slab. It carries water (not lava) and, most importantly, &amilks animals&r."
		""
		"Use it on a Cow or &6Highland Cattle&r for a &eWooden Bucket of Milk&r. &cEvery special milk needs a wooden bucket:&r Sheep, Goats and Water Buffalo give their own milk only this way. An iron bucket gets plain milk at best, and nothing at all from a sheep."
		""
		"&7Cows and sheep are scarce in snowy, swampy and savanna biomes here. Plains and Meadows are your best bet.&r"
	]
	quest.4452454FA584E978.quest_subtitle: "Milk, but rustic"
	quest.4452454FA584E978.title: "&6Wooden You Know It"
	quest.445DA0934EA70840.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Palm Bar&r is your cocktail station. &e7 Palm Planks&r make three of them."
		""
		"&aRight-click it&r to open four ingredient slots and an output. Put in the ingredients and the bar shakes the drink for a few seconds. Recipes are under &bTiki Bar Mixing&r in EMI. Every one needs &eIce&r, so the next step is a way to make it."
		""
		"&7The Palm Bar is also the job site of the Sandy Merchant, Beachparty's beach villager.&r"
	]
	quest.445DA0934EA70840.quest_subtitle: "Open bar"
	quest.445DA0934EA70840.title: "&6Five O'Clock Somewhere"
	quest.4478918789CEBAF8.quest_desc: [
		"&6Groutless Rubblestone&r generates in big blobs deep underground, between &bY -64 and 0&r, mostly among the deepslate. You can't craft it, so go mining."
		""
		"It comes in four looks: &eGroutless&r, &ePointed&r, &ePlastered&r and &eCovered&r. &aRight-click it with a Pickaxe&r to chip it one step barer, and &aright-click with Quicklime&r to go one step back. &cOnly vanilla stone, iron, gold, diamond and netherite pickaxes chip it&r; wooden and modded ones don't. Or craft it: 1 Groutless and 3 Quicklime make four Covered."
		""
		"&7Stairs, slabs and walls keep their shape while you chip them. Mix Groutless with Gravel for Splitstone, which a pickaxe turns into garden paths.&r"
	]
	quest.4478918789CEBAF8.quest_subtitle: "Dig deep, build rustic"
	quest.4478918789CEBAF8.title: "&8Rubble Rouser"
	quest.447E99666109CD33.quest_desc: [
		"&6Chipped&r adds thousands of block variants through seven workbenches: &6Mason Table&r (stone, bricks), &6Carpenters Table&r (wood), &6Loom Table&r (wool), &6Glassblower&r, &6Botanist Workbench&r, &6Tinkering Table&r (lamps, lanterns) and &6Alchemy Bench&r (metal and gem blocks). Put blocks in and pick a variant; EMI shows them all."
		""
		"Six have handheld versions - a Mason Table and an iron ingot make a &eChisel&r. There are backpack upgrades for them too."
		""
		"&7With &6Reintegrated Chipped&7, variants also turn up in villages, shipwrecks and dungeons.&r"
	]
	quest.447E99666109CD33.quest_subtitle: "Thousands of new looks"
	quest.447E99666109CD33.title: "&dA Chip Off the Old Block"
	quest.44D5BD82BC407B6D.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Propeller Bearing&r (wooden slab, Iron Sheet, Brass Casing) turns a structure in front of it into a big propeller. Any build counts if it has at least &b2 sail blocks&r, and &amore sails are more efficient&r."
		""
		"Goggles show its thrust and how much it can lift. Big ships want big props."
		""
		"&7Windmill Sails or Symmetric Sails both count as blades.&r"
	]
	quest.44D5BD82BC407B6D.quest_subtitle: "Size does matter"
	quest.44D5BD82BC407B6D.title: "&6Bigger Blades"
	quest.44EDEE0583144401.quest_desc: [
		"Quark lets &6Pistons&r move blocks with contents: &achests, furnaces and hoppers ride along&r (spawners, ender chests and a few others stay put). A &eChain&r attached to a moving block drags along whatever hangs on its other end."
		""
		"When you need a block that never moves, use &eSturdy Stone&r (made from cobblestone): pistons can't budge it."
		""
		"&7Also try Iron and Gold Buttons (long and very short pulses) and the Redstone Randomizer.&r"
	]
	quest.44EDEE0583144401.quest_subtitle: "Furniture included"
	quest.44EDEE0583144401.title: "&eMove It, Move It"
	quest.45311802B2278C05.quest_desc: [
		"Tie &eBread&r to a &eFishing Rod&r for a &6Bread on a Stick&r, then &aride an Alpine Sheep&r with it, like a carrot on a stick on a pig."
		""
		"&cDon't actually hand them the bread.&r They love it, and a few seconds later it hurts them."
	]
	quest.45311802B2278C05.quest_subtitle: "Sheep love bread. Bread does not love sheep."
	quest.45311802B2278C05.title: "&eMean Little Snack"
	quest.4543E39635D5D64B.quest_desc: [
		"Three ways to show off:"
		"&a- &6Item Shelf&r (3 Oak Slabs make 2; other woods give matching shelves from Supplementaries Squared): sits on a wall and holds one item."
		"&a- &6Pedestal&r (stone bricks and slabs): displays an item. &dAn End Crystal on a pedestal counts as 3 bookshelves&r for enchanting."
		"&a- &6Notice Board&r (planks and paper): pin up a &ewritten book&r or map. A redstone pulse turns the page."
		""
		"&aA Notice Board makes a perfect town board for server rules and trade offers.&r"
	]
	quest.4543E39635D5D64B.quest_subtitle: "A place for your favourite things"
	quest.4543E39635D5D64B.title: "&6Show and Tell"
	quest.4575E2BCCF0800E8.quest_desc: [
		"Quests pay in &6Gear Coins&r. &e9 bronze&r make &ea silver&r, &e4 silver&r make &ea gold&r, and every exchange works backwards too."
		""
		"Most quests pay bronze, big ones pay silver, and every other chapter's final quest pays a single, rare &6gold coin&r."
		""
		"Coins are the server's currency: &atrade them with other players&r."
	]
	quest.4575E2BCCF0800E8.quest_subtitle: "Nine makes one"
	quest.4575E2BCCF0800E8.title: "&ePocket Change"
	quest.458981CE90E61330.quest_desc: [
		"&6Create Cobblestone&r adds the &6Mechanical Generator&r: rotation in, stone out, with no lava or water in the world. Craft it from Brass Ingots, an Electron Tube, a Brass Casing, a Mechanical Drill and a bucket each of Water and Lava."
		""
		"&bRight-click it with a block&r to choose Cobblestone, Stone, Basalt, &eLimestone&r or &eScoria&r. It makes &b1 block per tick for every 8 RPM&r and costs &b8 SU per RPM&r."
		""
		"&7It holds 256 blocks and stops when full. Pulling items out is the real bottleneck, so try a Brass Chute from Create: Connected.&r"
	]
	quest.458981CE90E61330.quest_subtitle: "Create Cobblestone"
	quest.458981CE90E61330.title: "&6Rock On"
	quest.45AF2B40DCC62BA7.quest_desc: [
		"&eEmpyrite&r has no ore. Brew it in the cauldron: &e4 Astralite Ingots&r, &e1 Condensed Fluxia Conversion Dust&r, &e2 Amethyst Coal&r and &b3,000 mB&r of Fluxia, for &b16,000 ƒ&r."
		""
		"Conversion dust is crafted from a &eDiamond&r, &eLapis&r and &eRedstone&r. Four of it plus &e5 Emeralds&r make the condensed version at a crafting table, or the cauldron condenses &e2 dust&r with Fluxia, no emeralds needed."
		""
		"Empyrite tools and armor (&6Helm&r, &6Cuirass&r, &6Tassets&r, &6Greaves&r) outclass netherite, and the tools are hafted with astralite instead of sticks."
	]
	quest.45AF2B40DCC62BA7.quest_subtitle: "Both halves of the mod meet here"
	quest.45AF2B40DCC62BA7.title: "&6Above the Nether"
	quest.45B1D031400D8F8E.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Greenwood Pub&r is a big inn in &bdark forests, forests and sunflower plains&r, packed with &bwell over a dozen villagers&r. A &cvindicator&r or two may be drinking with them, and zombie and skeleton spawners lurk in the back rooms, so clear those first."
		""
		"The barrels hold bottles, brewing odds and ends and the odd strangely named brew. &aTrade with the regulars&r once the troublemakers are gone."
	]
	quest.45B1D031400D8F8E.quest_subtitle: "The locals are friendly. Mostly."
	quest.45B1D031400D8F8E.title: "&6Last Orders"
	quest.45BC4F60A36C5DEE.quest_desc: [
		"Your first &agrandchild&r. Once your child is married, &aGift a Cake&r to one of the couple and they start expecting."
		""
		"You get the book &eDeath, and How to Cure It!&r, which leads to the darker side of village life: infection, graves and the &cGrim Reaper&r."
		""
		"From one villager and a bouquet to three generations. &7Not bad for someone who used to trade them paper for emeralds.&r"
	]
	quest.45BC4F60A36C5DEE.quest_subtitle: "Grandparent of the year"
	quest.45BC4F60A36C5DEE.title: "&6Back In My Day..."
	quest.45ED2B4D46E84314.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Hydro Pump&r is a &6Water Block&r and a &eFluid Port&r with &eAluminum Nuggets&r. Mount it on a fluid container, such as a tank's &6Valve&r, and it &apumps in free water&r: &b100 mB&r per cycle, or &b1,000 mB&r if the pump is waterlogged."
		""
		"&7Pair it with a big tank and you'll never run short of water again.&r"
	]
	quest.45ED2B4D46E84314.quest_subtitle: "Never carry a bucket again"
	quest.45ED2B4D46E84314.title: "&9Free Refills"
	quest.45F1B4E9741F0926.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Brewing Cauldron&r (&e5 Iron Ingots&r, &e2 Sticks&r) merges potions. Add &b3 potions&r and a &dHerbal Infusion&r as catalyst, then wait &b60 seconds&r for a &eFlask&r holding all three effects."
		""
		"The &dHerbal Infusion&r takes &e3 Dried Green&r, &e3 Dried Black&r and &e3 Dried Oolong Tea&r, so keep plenty of leaf blocks drying. Teas don't go in; only real potions."
		""
		"&aOne Flask instead of three bottles saves hotbar space before a big fight.&r &7The Witch Hat and Top Hat (wool, plus gold for the Witch Hat) cut magic damage by 40% if a boss likes potions.&r"
	]
	quest.45F1B4E9741F0926.quest_subtitle: "Three potions, one Flask"
	quest.45F1B4E9741F0926.title: "&5Potion Perfected"
	quest.461E6AFD2B2D1C52.quest_desc: [
		"&e8 Glass&r around &e1 Oak Plank&r makes 8 &6Oak Windows&r, and stacked windows join into one tall pane. &cWindows only come in eight woods:&r Oak, Spruce, Birch, Jungle, Acacia, Dark Oak, Mangrove and Cherry."
		""
		"A &6Window Casing&r frames it. &aRight-click the bottom front with a Flower Pot&r for a window box, and right-click the bottom part with an Axe to toggle it on or off."
		""
		"The &6Sliding Stable Door&r (&eSpruce Planks&r and &eIron Ingots&r) slides open. &aRight-click with any planks to recolour it&r, or with an &eIron Ingot&r to reinforce it. Barn and Hayloft doors are made from Stable Doors."
	]
	quest.461E6AFD2B2D1C52.quest_subtitle: "Windows, window boxes and barn doors"
	quest.461E6AFD2B2D1C52.title: "&bLet the Light In"
	quest.467C9F0BB2E18AC1.quest_desc: [
		"Craft &eRose Quartz&r from &e1 Nether Quartz&r and &e8 Redstone&r, and &eSand Paper&r from &ePaper&r and &eSand&r."
		""
		"Hold the Rose Quartz in your &boffhand&r and &bhold right-click&r with the Sand Paper to polish it. &ePolished Rose Quartz&r on top of an &eIron Sheet&r makes one &6Electron Tube&r."
		""
		"&aTubes go into nearly every smart brass block&r: crafters, funnels, tunnels, deployers, signals and display boards."
	]
	quest.467C9F0BB2E18AC1.quest_subtitle: "Polish first, glow later"
	quest.467C9F0BB2E18AC1.title: "&eRose-Tinted Tubes"
	quest.467CEC13E02BA1D3.quest_desc: [
		"The blue machine. The &6Water Block&r is &e4 Blue gems&r, Kivi, iron bars, &e2 Water Buckets&r and a &6Machine Base&r."
		""
		"It is an &ainfinite water source in block form&r. Right-click it with an empty bucket or tank item to fill it. Many &6Extractor&r layouts accept it as their water, and the &6Hydro Pump&r is built around one."
	]
	quest.467CEC13E02BA1D3.quest_subtitle: "Is it full? It's always full"
	quest.467CEC13E02BA1D3.title: "&9Schrodinger's Water"
	quest.469C45ADB951FD64.quest_desc: [
		"&6Wizard armor&r is made from &eArcane Cloth&r alone (hood or hat 5, robes 8, leggings 7, boots 4). Each piece adds &b+125 max mana&r and &b+5%&r spell power, and you can dye it."
		""
		"It's also the base for &dschool armor&r: put a school rune, a Wizard piece and an Arcane Essence in a &6Smithing Table&r (or crafting grid) for &b+10%&r of that school's power on top."
		""
		"&7A Netherite Upgrade template and a Netherite Ingot turn any Wizard piece into Netherite Battlemage armor.&r"
	]
	quest.469C45ADB951FD64.quest_subtitle: "+125 mana, +5% spell power per piece"
	quest.469C45ADB951FD64.title: "&5Dressed for Sorcery"
	quest.46B5B56E18891EEC.quest_desc: [
		"The &eRing of the Seven Deadly Sins&r has seven double-edged powers: Pride, Envy, Wrath, Sloth, Greed, Gluttony and Lust. &dSloth&r makes you immortal if you stand still long enough, but &dGreed&r can &cdestroy&r a drop, and &dLust&r gives extra offspring at the cost of animals that die within minutes unless you breed them again."
		""
		"&cWarning: once it's in a ring slot, clicking it out hurts you and fails. Assume it's stuck.&r It also can't rank up."
		""
		"&7This quest only needs it in your inventory. Think before you wear it.&r"
	]
	quest.46B5B56E18891EEC.quest_subtitle: "One ring to curse them all"
	quest.46B5B56E18891EEC.title: "&4Seven Deadly Sins"
	quest.4742225337990211.quest_desc: [
		"This chapter covers the pack's &6Create&r add-ons (Aeronautics has its own chapter). Each branch is one add-on: &6electricity&r, odd gearboxes, &6copycats&r, &6liquid experience&r, endless stone and more."
		""
		"The manual for most of them is &6Ponder&r: hover a machine and hold &bW&r. Copycats+, Framed, Create Cobblestone and Ultimate Factory have no Ponder scenes, so their quests explain them here. &cMachine recipes&r (pressing, mixing, rolling, charging...) don't show in EMI in this pack, so these quests name the machine and the key ingredients in words."
		""
		"&7Do the two Create chapters (Spin Cycle and Brass Tacks) first. Almost everything here assumes you know shafts, belts, Brass and Mechanical Crafters.&r"
	]
	quest.4742225337990211.quest_subtitle: "Your factory, accessorised"
	quest.4742225337990211.title: "&6Aftermarket Parts"
	quest.4752907932C34042.quest_desc: [
		"Open &bInteract&r, press &bGift&r, then &ahold an item and right-click&r. About &ba third&r of the item's value turns into hearts."
		""
		"Gold, emeralds and diamonds are always welcome, and jobs have favourites: a librarian loves books, a toolsmith loves a bell, a fisherman loves a fishing rod. Children adore sweets and flowers."
		""
		"&cMix it up.&r Hand over the same thing again and again and its value drops until you hear \"Not another one of these!\". It recovers after a day."
	]
	quest.4752907932C34042.quest_subtitle: "Mostly. Diamonds help."
	quest.4752907932C34042.title: "&eIt's the Thought That Counts"
	quest.47598CADFB7789C4.quest_desc: [
		"&6Evoker Forts&r hide in forests, hills, plains, deserts and savannas, and the &cArchevoker&r at the top is hostile from the start. Village &6Priests&r sell a map to one."
		""
		"He drops essence, ink, an evocation scroll, half the time an &eEvocation Rune&r, and very rarely the &eGrimoire of Evokation&r, a unique book with three locked evocation spells (ordinary Evokers can drop it too)."
		""
		"&7Free the caged villagers while you're there, and check the tower for a logbook.&r"
	]
	quest.47598CADFB7789C4.quest_subtitle: "This wizard does not trade"
	quest.47598CADFB7789C4.title: "&cFort Knocks"
	quest.4774A79C57FE05D4.quest_desc: [
		"&eCoconuts&r grow hanging under palm leaves. When ripe they &cdrop and hurt whatever stands below&r, so don't nap under a palm."
		""
		"&aRight-click a Coconut to throw it.&r It cracks open on landing into &e2 Open Coconuts&r, with a good chance of a &ePalm Sprout&r as well. A thrown coconut also bonks mobs for a little damage."
		""
		"Open Coconuts go into the &eCoconut Cocktail&r later on."
	]
	quest.4774A79C57FE05D4.quest_subtitle: "Mind your head"
	quest.4774A79C57FE05D4.title: "&6Coco-Nuts"
	quest.4786F688B2610A2C.quest_desc: [
		"&6Beachparty&r hides wearable beach &eArtifacts&r in buried treasure, shipwreck and underwater ruin chests (not the same thing as the Artifacts mod). They go in your &bCurios&r slots:"
		"&eCrocs&r: sprint across water. &eRubber Rings&r: swim faster and stay afloat. &eSwim Wings&r: halve fall damage. &eSunglasses&r and the &eBeach Hat&r: a little less fire damage."
		""
		"&cThe Beach Hat and Pool Noodle don't count here&r, but the &eBeach Ball&r and &eFloaty Boat&r do."
		""
		"&7Right-click an artifact in your inventory to hide its 3D model. Collect all twelve for the advancement \"The Treasure of the Sandy Madre\".&r"
	]
	quest.4786F688B2610A2C.quest_subtitle: "Beachwear, found not bought"
	quest.4786F688B2610A2C.title: "&dSandy Treasures"
	quest.47A815327DF8164D.quest_desc: [
		"Crush &eNetherrack&r into &eCinder Flour&r, then &6compact&r it (Mechanical Press over a Basin) with an &eEgg&r and &eSugar&r into a &eBlaze Cake Base&r. Have a &6Spout&r fill the base with &b250 mB of Lava&r."
		""
		"Feed the &eBlaze Cake&r to a Blaze Burner and it goes &cSuperheated&r for &b2 min 40 s&r. A superheated burner counts as &b2 heat&r in a boiler, and while it's on cake it refuses ordinary fuel."
		""
		"&7Superheated mixing turns each Cobblestone into 50 mB of Lava: a lava supply that pays for its own cakes.&r"
	]
	quest.47A815327DF8164D.quest_subtitle: "Extra crispy"
	quest.47A815327DF8164D.title: "&cHot Cakes"
	quest.47C205C11109E2F4.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Monastery&r is a quiet retreat in &btaigas, hills and mountains&r. Only a villager and an &aIron Golem&r live here, so don't start trouble."
		""
		"Climb to the top and open the &emap chest&r. Half the time it holds a map to the &6Thornborn Towers&r. &7The other map, meant for the Infested Temple, comes out blank in this version: use a Woodland Explorer Map for that one.&r"
	]
	quest.47C205C11109E2F4.quest_subtitle: "Please keep your voice down"
	quest.47C205C11109E2F4.title: "&fVow of Silence"
	quest.47FF56092BB720BE.quest_desc: [
		"&eGold Casts&r are reusable. Put a part, or any ingot, on an &bempty&r Casting Table and pour &b1 ingot&r (90 mB) of molten gold over it. &cThe part or ingot is used up&r to make the mold."
		""
		"The &eIngot Cast&r is the important one: it turns any molten metal into ingots. Pour 1 ingot of gold onto a &eBook&r instead and you get the &eEncyclopedia&r, every tool, material and modifier in one book."
		""
		"&aBrick tip:&r melt Grout to get Seared Stone fluid and cast it with the Ingot Cast. That gives &b2 Seared Bricks per Grout&r instead of 1."
	]
	quest.47FF56092BB720BE.quest_subtitle: "Casts that last forever"
	quest.47FF56092BB720BE.title: "&eThe Golden Rule"
	quest.480102E0C65C7E5A.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Corsair Corvette&r is crewed by skeletons with golden axes and a Punch archer, and carries &bbarrels of gunpowder and flint&r. &cSome skeletons spawn with a creeper riding on their heads&r, so don't let them get close."
		""
		"The &6Pirate Junk&r has vindicators, a firework-shooting pillager and can have &cIllusioner&r spawners. Its treasure holds enchanted diamond helmets and boots, diamonds and emeralds, plus lots of supply barrels."
	]
	quest.480102E0C65C7E5A.quest_subtitle: "Two crews, no manners"
	quest.480102E0C65C7E5A.title: "&3Scallywags"
	quest.481C73A835C6C7A9.quest_desc: [
		"&eRooibos Tea&r needs only a stove's &b30%&r heat and gives a short burst of &bRegeneration&r."
		""
		"&eYerba Mate Tea&r (leaf plus &eSugar&r) is the fussiest brew: it needs &b75% heat&r. Keep &b2 or more Blaze Powder&r in the heat slot of a kettle that sits on a stove."
		""
		"Its &aBonding&r effect gives &bAbsorption&r and &bRegeneration&r to the &aother players&r near you, not to you. Brew it for the group."
	]
	quest.481C73A835C6C7A9.quest_subtitle: "One for you, one for the team"
	quest.481C73A835C6C7A9.title: "&6Rooibos and Yerba Mate"
	quest.4849368F0F0DDC94.quest_desc: [
		"The &eEnchanted Spell Book&r needs &e2 Diamonds&r, &e4 Hogskin&r, &e2 Arcane Cloth&r and any &eenchanted book&r. It holds &b10 spells&r and adds &b+100 mana&r."
		""
		"Keep an eye out for &dunique&r books too: Blazes rarely drop the &eBlaze Instruction Manual&r, and the &eRotten Spell Book&r turns up in chests and catacombs. A Rotten book, arcane cloth and a few natural treasures craft the &eDruidic Tome&r."
	]
	quest.4849368F0F0DDC94.quest_subtitle: "10 slots, +100 mana"
	quest.4849368F0F0DDC94.title: "&bMaster Enchanter"
	quest.486235BCCA101E17.quest_desc: [
		"Illagers have taken over a windmill in the &bplains&r. The &6Illager Windmill&r is mostly guarded by pillagers, sometimes with a vindicator or a witch, and its wheat fields are worked by &bzombie villager&r farmhands."
		""
		"&aCure them&r (Weakness plus a Golden Apple each) and you've got the start of a village. The chests have enchanted iron gear and emeralds, and the barrels can hide a &esaddle&r."
	]
	quest.486235BCCA101E17.quest_subtitle: "The miller has been replaced"
	quest.486235BCCA101E17.title: "&eTilting at Windmills"
	quest.48C57D2769BB8B06.quest_desc: [
		"Put any &eSeeds&r on the Apparatus with &e4 Source Gems&r on pedestals to get a &eMagebloom Seed&r. Plant it on farmland."
		""
		"A grown crop drops &dMagebloom&r flowers, and each one crafts into &b4&r &eMagebloom Fiber&r: the magic cloth behind parchment, threads, armor and illusion blocks. &aStart a proper farm&r, ideally inside an Agronomic Sourcelink's range for bonus Source."
	]
	quest.48C57D2769BB8B06.title: "&dFlower Power"
	quest.48D99F6219EA5AE4.quest_desc: [
		"&6Create: Framed&r colours in Create's glass. Surround a dye with &b8&r &eFramed Glass&r, or stonecut stained glass for framed, tiled, vertical and horizontal versions. Craft it with any wooden door or trapdoor to get a matching glass door or trapdoor."
		""
		"&eMetal Windows&r: 3 Brass, Copper or Zinc Nuggets on the top and sides of a block of &eGlass&r make 2. A fan through water washes the dye back off."
		""
		"&7Feeling silly? A Deployer holding a fish turns a Block of Cardboard into Karpboard.&r"
	]
	quest.48D99F6219EA5AE4.quest_subtitle: "Create: Framed"
	quest.48D99F6219EA5AE4.title: "&bWindow Shopping"
	quest.4904DC9993D71B59.quest_desc: [
		"&6Wisp \\& Willow&r is cosy ritual magic. You draw coloured &dchalk glyphs&r around a &6Willow Altar&r, drop reagents on the ground and pay in &dFluxia&r (ƒ), a current that flowers and machines produce."
		""
		"The &eWisp \\& Willow Grimoire&r was handed to you on first join. &cIt can't be crafted&r, so keep it safe. Its ritual pages have an &beye icon&r that projects the circle into the world. Hold &bW&r over the altar or a chalk for &6Ponder&r scenes on casting and runes; every rite has its own scene under the &bRituals&r tag in the Ponder index."
		""
		"&cEMI only shows this mod's ordinary crafting and smelting recipes here.&r Rites, pool infusions and cauldron brews live in the Grimoire and Ponder only."
		""
		"&7Some Grimoire numbers are out of date and its ritual pages never say which altar tier a rite needs. This chapter gives the real numbers.&r"
	]
	quest.4904DC9993D71B59.quest_subtitle: "Wisp \\& Willow"
	quest.4904DC9993D71B59.title: "&dA Willow, a Wisp and a Lot of Chalk"
	quest.492F861FBA32EBBC.quest_desc: [
		"&eNether Grout&r is &eMagma Cream&r, &eSoul Sand&r (or Soul Soil) and &eGravel&r, for 2. The bulk recipe is a &eMagma Block&r with 4 soul sand or soil and 4 gravel, for 8. Craft one with a &eBook&r to get &eFantastic Foundry&r."
		""
		"Smelt more Nether Grout into &eScorched Bricks&r. They build the Alloyer and the Foundry."
	]
	quest.492F861FBA32EBBC.quest_subtitle: "Book four: Fantastic Foundry"
	quest.492F861FBA32EBBC.title: "&eNether Smelting"
	quest.499FB2FF0665E0AB.quest_desc: [
		"&eHoney Glue&r is made by &6Spouting&r &b500 mB&r of honey onto an &eIron Sheet&r (empty Honey Bottles in an &6Item Drain&r for the fluid)."
		""
		"Click two endpoints to glue the box between them (up to &b48 blocks&r a side), &bCtrl+Scroll&r to grow or shrink it, and hold &bAlt&r to place a corner in mid-air. Perfect for big hulls."
		""
		"&cIt only works for Simulated Contraptions&r, not normal Create contraptions."
	]
	quest.499FB2FF0665E0AB.quest_subtitle: "Super Glue's sticky cousin"
	quest.499FB2FF0665E0AB.title: "&eSweet Connections"
	quest.49B500AF39C121E3.quest_desc: [
		"Coloured clay replaces normal clay, sand and gravel in &briverbeds, lake bottoms and shallow patches&r of certain biomes. Mined without Silk Touch, a block drops &b4 balls&r."
		""
		"&cRed&r: badlands and rivers. &eYellow&r: savanna and rivers. &fWhite&r: snowy plains, snowy taiga, ice spikes, frozen rivers. &9Blue&r: taiga, windswept hills, rivers, and lush caves. &8Black&r: swamps only."
		""
		"&aEvery colour shows up in Swamps and Mangrove Swamps.&r Swamps are rarer than usual in this pack (the Willow Fen takes many of their spots), so a &eNature's Compass&r helps. &7Renewable trick: stack Water, then Red, Yellow, White, Blue or Black Terracotta, then a hanging Pointed Dripstone. Leave one block of air under the tip, and the Sand, Gravel or Clay below that slowly turns into clay of the terracotta's colour.&r"
	]
	quest.49B500AF39C121E3.quest_subtitle: "Five clays, five biomes"
	quest.49B500AF39C121E3.title: "&6Earth Tones"
	quest.49EAD947A40D3B1E.quest_desc: [
		"Switch a station to &bAssembly Mode&r and click the highlighted track with &eTrain Casing&r to place &bbogeys&r. Build your carriage on them, wrap it in &eSuper Glue&r, and add &6Train Controls&r (&eLever&r, &eTrain Casing&r, &ePrecision Mechanism&r) facing &bforward&r. The front bogey goes on the station marker, on straight track."
		""
		"Assemble, then right-click the Controls to drive: &bWASD&r to move, &bscroll&r to cap your speed, &bhold Space&r to pull into a nearby station."
		""
		"&aFurnace fuel in a chest or barrel on board makes it about 40% faster.&r &cTrains can only be disassembled at a station.&r"
	]
	quest.49EAD947A40D3B1E.quest_subtitle: "Some glue required"
	quest.49EAD947A40D3B1E.title: "&6The Little Engine That Could"
	quest.4A03DB744F43B735.quest_desc: [
		"Four Iron Sheets around Andesite Alloy make a &ePropeller&r; stack a Shaft, Andesite Casing and the Propeller for an &6Encased Fan&r."
		""
		"Its spin direction decides whether it &bpushes or pulls&r. Faster fans reach further, from about &b5 blocks at 32 RPM&r to &b20 at 256&r, but don't work any faster."
		""
		"&aA fan at the bottom or top of a Chute blows items upward.&r"
	]
	quest.4A03DB744F43B735.quest_subtitle: "Big fan energy"
	quest.4A03DB744F43B735.title: "&fWind Maker"
	quest.4A095A6BCAB3C35D.quest_desc: [
		"Familiars are spirit companions that boost your altar. They start with paper."
		""
		"&eAmethyst Sugar Cane&r: &e3 Sugar Cane&r + &e2 Amethyst Shards&r. It grows like cane (faster on &eSnad&r). Three of it make 3 &eAmethyst Paper&r."
		""
		"&dThe Written Pact&r is a tier II rite (&b500 ƒ&r, 7x7): &e4 Amethyst Paper&r, &e1 Soul Sand&r and &e2 Amethyst Shards&r give &b4 Soul Pacts&r. The Grimoire's eye icon shows the 12-glyph layout."
		""
		"&7Have a Ghast Tear for the next step.&r"
	]
	quest.4A095A6BCAB3C35D.quest_subtitle: "Familiars, part one"
	quest.4A095A6BCAB3C35D.title: "&dThe Written Pact"
	quest.4A0F640153DEEB48.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Storage Controller&r (stone, planks, two comparators and a wooden Sophisticated chest or barrel) joins every Sophisticated storage touching it, or touching storage that touches it, up to &b15 blocks&r away, into one big inventory."
		""
		"&aRight-click&r the controller with a stack to store it; &adouble right-click&r to dump every matching item. A pipe or hopper on the controller reaches the whole wall."
		""
		"&eStorage Links&r (ender pearl, stone, planks, repeater) bring in chests that aren't touching the wall: place one against them, then link it to the controller with a &eStorage Tool&r (ender pearl, iron, sticks, redstone torch)."
		""
		"&7Comparators need Nether Quartz, so this one waits for your first Nether trip.&r"
	]
	quest.4A0F640153DEEB48.quest_subtitle: "One block to rule them all"
	quest.4A0F640153DEEB48.title: "&6The Wall of Storage"
	quest.4A1C546CB7893227.quest_desc: [
		"&6Flux Networks&r sends power wirelessly, and it starts with a ritual. Stack it up: &eBedrock&r, a one-block gap with &eRedstone&r dropped into it, then &eObsidian&r on top. &aLeft-click the obsidian&r and each redstone becomes &eFlux Dust&r."
		""
		"&cBig batches can crack the obsidian into cobblestone.&r Bedrock lines the bottom of the Overworld and the floor of the Nether. Once you have a &6Flux Block&r, it works in place of bedrock anywhere."
	]
	quest.4A1C546CB7893227.quest_subtitle: "Bedrock, redstone, obsidian"
	quest.4A1C546CB7893227.title: "&cRock Bottom"
	quest.4A51E81B32ED6473.quest_desc: [
		"Mine &eObsidian&r with a &eDiamond Pickaxe&r (or pour water onto a lava source to make it). A portal frame is &b4 wide and 5 tall&r; the corners are optional, so &b10 Obsidian&r is enough. Light it with &eFlint and Steel&r."
		""
		"The Nether is where mid-game ingredients come from: &eNether Quartz&r (comparators, the Storage Network Root), &eGlowstone&r, &eBlaze Rods&r and &eNether Wart&r."
		""
		"&cBeds explode in the Nether.&r If things go wrong, your &6Corpse&r waits where you fell."
	]
	quest.4A51E81B32ED6473.quest_subtitle: "Pack fire resistance. Or at least pack."
	quest.4A51E81B32ED6473.title: "&cHighway to the Nether"
	quest.4A75F032D3C08DF5.quest_desc: [
		"&6Legacy&r keeps a journal of your adventure. Open it with the &bTitles \\& Milestones&r button in your inventory."
		""
		"&bJourney&r records your firsts, &bTitles&r unlock from what you do and can be shown above your name, and &bMilestones&r are &aserver world-firsts&r: who entered the Nether first, and on which day."
		""
		"&7Race your friends.&r"
	]
	quest.4A75F032D3C08DF5.quest_subtitle: "Firsts, titles and bragging rights"
	quest.4A75F032D3C08DF5.title: "Living Legend"
	quest.4AA795E203B06DFF.quest_desc: [
		"Place the &6Physics Assembler&r against your build, then &eSuper Glue&r everything you want to take along (right-click two corners to glue the box between them)."
		""
		"Now look at the Assembler, &bhold right-click and drag&r its lever. The blocks become a &6Simulated Contraption&r with real mass and momentum, and it stays fully usable: walk on it, open chests, sit in seats, run machines."
		""
		"&7Break off a piece and it splits into its own contraption. A Slime Ball glues two back together.&r"
	]
	quest.4AA795E203B06DFF.quest_subtitle: "Glue, lever, physics"
	quest.4AA795E203B06DFF.title: "&aIt Moves!"
	quest.4AF6FC84535C90BF.quest_desc: [
		"&eFluxite&r, the stone every Fluxia device is built from, &chas no crafting recipe&r. The rite that makes it needs a tier II altar, and getting there takes about &b13&r fluxite you don't have yet (5 for a pool, 8 for runes). So go find a &6Fluxia Oasis&r."
		""
		"Oases are rare underground caverns with the floor between &bY -38&r and &bY 6&r, roughly one per 1,000 x 1,000 block area in any overworld biome. Look for calcite and amethyst walls around a glowing pool under a leaning willow. &aMine the &eFluxite&a out of the walls&r and pick up the &eSolrosas&r and &eLuxinia Flowers&r on the mossy floor."
		""
		"&7A Willow Hut (savannas only) is worth a detour too: its placed Willow Fluxia Pool saves you 5 fluxite, and it has a potted Luxinia.&r"
	]
	quest.4AF6FC84535C90BF.quest_subtitle: "The real first step"
	quest.4AF6FC84535C90BF.title: "&bA Light Under the Hill"
	quest.4B0210FCC78F6CD6.quest_desc: [
		"Press &ball 7 cheese wheels&r: plain, Sheep, Goat, Buffalo, Grain, Amethyst and Warped. Each one is &b1 Rennet&r plus its milk in the Cheese Press."
		""
		"That means mountain meadows, savanna rivers, a Silk Touch geode trip and a visit to the Warped Forest. It is the whole chapter in one cheese board."
		""
		"&aThe advancement gives you 2 Completionist Banners.&r A placed banner gives &bHaste II&r to everyone within &b8 blocks&r. Hang one over your mine or workshop."
	]
	quest.4B0210FCC78F6CD6.quest_subtitle: "From the peaks to the Nether, for cheese"
	quest.4B0210FCC78F6CD6.title: "&6The Ultimate Cheese Connoisseur"
	quest.4B09B6A7CF8C2BD9.quest_desc: [
		"Roll &eCopper Sheets&r into &eCopper Wire&r. For spools, stack an &eIron Sheet&r, an &eIron Rod&r and another &eIron Sheet&r in a column: that makes &b24&r &eEmpty Spools&r."
		""
		"Surround an Empty Spool with &b4&r Copper Wire for a &eCopper Spool&r. It strings &blow-current&r wire between connectors, and most electric machines eat a few in their recipe: the Alternator alone takes &b4&r."
	]
	quest.4B09B6A7CF8C2BD9.quest_subtitle: "Wire you like this?"
	quest.4B09B6A7CF8C2BD9.title: "&eSpool Me Once"
	quest.4B2CE9063FE012B9.quest_desc: [
		"&eSpectral Essence&r is the mod's basic ingredient. &cInfected Zombies&r drop &b0-2&r each, and they roam the biome &cday and night&r in groups. Coffins and tombstones give some too."
		""
		"&cWatch your step:&r flowers with a &dpurple mist&r around them are &cinfected&r. Walking through one gives you &cInfected&r, which hurts and drains sanity."
		""
		"&7Cooking essence on a campfire gives Rotten Flesh. Don't.&r"
	]
	quest.4B2CE9063FE012B9.quest_subtitle: "Ectoplasm, now in convenient drops"
	quest.4B2CE9063FE012B9.title: "&dA Slimy, Weird Thing"
	quest.4B9EA39E408D3580.quest_desc: [
		"Build a spawner with the &eThundering&r rune (Infused Rune, Godforged Pearls, Infused Dragon's Breath, a Nether Star and a &dPerfect Endersurge&r gem, an End-only gem), plus &eControl&r, &eStupor&r, &eDefiance&r and &eSolitude&r."
		""
		"The Infused Dragon's Breath means an 80-Eterna table at &6Pinnacle&r, the same infusion as the Endshelf step."
		""
		"The result spawns every &b20 ticks&r, needs no player nearby, ignores light and spawn rules, keeps its mobs still and only runs while it gets a &bredstone signal&r."
		""
		"&7Give it a proper kill chamber before you flip the switch.&r"
	]
	quest.4B9EA39E408D3580.quest_subtitle: "Mob factory, fully tuned"
	quest.4B9EA39E408D3580.title: "&6The Ultimate Spawner"
	quest.4BA516B829B1A8C8.quest_desc: [
		"In &bswamps and mangrove swamps&r, half of all big finds are &6Keep Kayra&r, a ruined castle with a library and a garden. A couple of dozen frogs live here; the garrison is less friendly: skeletons and &cWither Skeletons in diamond chestplates&r, and creepers riding slimes."
		""
		"It has &bdozens of treasure chests&r. Expect &ehigh-level enchanted books&r, enchanted diamond gear and, rarely, a piece of &enetherite armour&r."
	]
	quest.4BA516B829B1A8C8.quest_subtitle: "A castle for the frogs"
	quest.4BA516B829B1A8C8.title: "&2Croak and Dagger"
	quest.4C35726CB71F147C.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Mining Complex&r is a deep industrial mine &bburied around y -5&r, in most land biomes. Small Blimp, Abandoned Temple and Thornborn maps lead here."
		""
		"&cSkeleton miners&r patrol the tunnels, some with &cMaces&r and netherite chestplates or a Fire Aspect flint and steel, plus a pillager firing fireworks. &aSmash the decorated pots&r: a few hide a &eMining Complex Treasure Key&r that opens the &6vault&r."
		""
		"The vault holds &dVoltaic Shot&r (exploding crossbow bolts that fly straight) and &dDischarge&r books and gear, diamond blocks and a chance of an &eEnchanted Golden Apple&r."
	]
	quest.4C35726CB71F147C.quest_subtitle: "The miners are still on shift"
	quest.4C35726CB71F147C.title: "&7Clocking In"
	quest.4C5A1A3548506764.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a &6Brewing Stand&r from a &eBlaze Rod&r and &e3 Cobblestone&r (any cobble-type stone works), and fuel it with &eBlaze Powder&r."
		""
		"Water bottles plus &eNether Wart&r make an &eAwkward Potion&r, the base for almost everything; add a second ingredient for the effect. &6EMI&r lists every brew."
		""
		"&aNice to know:&r the Sophisticated Backpacks &eAlchemy Upgrade&r drinks potions for you, and the Chipped &6Alchemy Bench&r is built from a Brewing Stand and an Enchanting Table."
	]
	quest.4C5A1A3548506764.quest_subtitle: "Toil and trouble"
	quest.4C5A1A3548506764.title: "&dDouble, Double"
	quest.4C639D14F3E912F6.quest_desc: [
		"Quark adds new stones: red &eJasper&r, pale &eLimestone&r and grey-blue &eShale&r. All three generate &bunderground everywhere&r from Y 0 to 60, and in big surface patches: Jasper in badlands and deserts, Limestone in swamps and oceans, Shale in cold biomes."
		""
		"Each comes as polished, bricks, stairs, slabs, walls and vertical slabs, via crafting or the &6Stonecutter&r. They even make &astone tools&r."
		""
		"&7Permafrost caps the Frozen Peaks, and Myalite waits in the outer End.&r"
	]
	quest.4C639D14F3E912F6.quest_subtitle: "Stone, but with personality"
	quest.4C639D14F3E912F6.title: "&7Rock Collection"
	quest.4C76C2E33FB50717.quest_desc: [
		"&ePacking Tape&r is a slime ball and paper. Use it on a Sophisticated chest, then break the chest: it drops as &aone item with everything still inside&r."
		""
		"&cCarry On can't lift Sophisticated Storage&r, so tape is how you move it."
		""
		"&7Breaking an untaped chest that would spill more than 200 stacks of items is blocked unless you sneak.&r"
	]
	quest.4C76C2E33FB50717.quest_subtitle: "Pack it up, pack it in"
	quest.4C76C2E33FB50717.title: "&eMoving Day"
	quest.4C89439153344310.quest_desc: [
		"&eAluminum Ore&r forms large veins between &bY -34 and 56&r and drops &eRaw Aluminum&r. &aSmelt or blast it&r into &eAluminum Ingots&r. One ingot crafts into nine &eAluminum Nuggets&r, which several machines need."
		""
		"&cDon't feed raw aluminum or aluminum ore to Create's Crushing Wheels.&r The &eCrushed Raw Aluminum&r they make has no working smelting or washing recipe in this pack. It's a dead end. Stick to the furnace, or melt it in the &6Modern Foundry&r smeltery."
	]
	quest.4C89439153344310.quest_subtitle: "Light, shiny, everywhere"
	quest.4C89439153344310.title: "&7Pale Metal"
	quest.4C988F3E687D673B.quest_desc: [
		"The plain cobblestone monster room got an upgrade: &6Better Dungeons&r small dungeons have banners, skulls, one or two chests and sometimes &eore blocks&r tucked into the corners."
		""
		"They are one of the most common finds underground, anywhere between &by -50 and y 50&r. &aLight up or break the spawner&r before you start looting."
	]
	quest.4C988F3E687D673B.quest_subtitle: "The humble spawner room, now with interior design"
	quest.4C988F3E687D673B.title: "&7Home Improvement"
	quest.4CB92BC5D0E301B8.quest_desc: [
		"A &eRope Winch&r (Iron Sheet, Shaft, Block of Industrial Iron) and a &eRope Connector&r tie together with a &eRope Coupling&r, up to &b40 blocks&r apart. Spin the winch to reel in or let out."
		""
		"Tow cargo, lower a lift basket or moor your ship. Shears cut the rope."
		""
		"&7Right-click a rope with a Wrench to zipline down it.&r"
	]
	quest.4CB92BC5D0E301B8.quest_subtitle: "Tow, moor, zipline"
	quest.4CB92BC5D0E301B8.title: "&eLearning the Knots"
	quest.4CF40A0188CA3080.quest_desc: [
		"&6Create: Structures Arise&r scatters &b28&r Create-themed builds across the world: lost train stations, windmills, sky villages, a steampunk pillager airship and more. They are &crare&r, so keep your eyes open."
		""
		"The most common one is the &6Dead Lord's House&r in the Nether. Its chests use Bastion treasure loot, so you will find a &eBlaze Upgrade Smithing Template&r inside."
		""
		"&7Some builds have mob spawners. Bring armour.&r"
	]
	quest.4CF40A0188CA3080.quest_subtitle: "Create: Structures Arise"
	quest.4CF40A0188CA3080.title: "&cDead Lord's Hospitality"
	quest.4D5315C854E43378.quest_desc: [
		"&6Bakery&r adds breads, pastries, jams, cakes and cookies. It has &cno oven of its own&r: everything bakes in the Farm \\& Charm &6Stove&r and mixes in the &6Crafting Bowl&r."
		""
		"Its workbench is the &6Caking Station&r (wooden slabs, flour and bricks), where you shape dough, cut cupcakes and decorate cakes."
		""
		"&7EMI has Baking Station and Jam Pot tabs.&r"
	]
	quest.4D5315C854E43378.quest_subtitle: "Bakery joins the kitchen"
	quest.4D5315C854E43378.title: "&6Bake It Happen"
	quest.4D57336BF30A0546.quest_desc: [
		"The &eWedding Ring&r is &e8 Gold Ingots&r in a ring (or 8 rose gold ingots). Your partner accepts it at &b100 hearts&r, so keep chatting, gifting and kissing until the meter gets there."
		""
		"Gift the ring and you are &amarried&r. No ceremony, no seating chart, no awkward speeches."
		""
		"Your spouse is family now, so their menu gains &bInventory&r and &bWork&r, and &bInteract&r lets you hand them &bArmor&r, ask them to &bFollow Me&r and set their &bLocations&r."
		""
		"&7If it ever goes wrong, any other cleric can give you &eDivorce Papers&7. Let's hope it never comes to that.&r"
	]
	quest.4D57336BF30A0546.quest_subtitle: "You may now kiss the villager"
	quest.4D57336BF30A0546.title: "&d'Til Death Do Us Part"
	quest.4DC67DCE9B3E6E58.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Modern Foundry Station&r is &e3 Patterns&r over &e4 Planks&r arranged like legs. The odd name comes from the port. Old Tinkers players know it as the Tinker Station."
		""
		"It &acombines parts into tools&r, applies &bmodifiers&r, repairs tools and swaps parts. It has &bthree input slots&r, so it can only build tools made of up to three parts. Bigger tools need an Anvil, later in this chapter."
	]
	quest.4DC67DCE9B3E6E58.quest_subtitle: "The Tinker Station, for veterans"
	quest.4DC67DCE9B3E6E58.title: "&6Station to Station"
	quest.4E0D3D26FD663A8D.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Unicorn Galleon&r is a grand sailing ship taken over by &czombies in chainmail&r with swords, axes and Fire Aspect flint and steel, while skeleton archers fly around it on bats."
		""
		"Its treasure is like the Pirate Junk's (enchanted diamond pieces, diamonds, emeralds), and around 20 supply barrels keep the crew fed. &7A parrot keeps them company.&r"
	]
	quest.4E0D3D26FD663A8D.quest_subtitle: "Majestic. Also full of zombies."
	quest.4E0D3D26FD663A8D.title: "&fThe Unicorn Rides the Waves"
	quest.4E56B30212417FCC.quest_desc: [
		"Put a &eBlock of Primal Coal&r against &6Blazebloom Goo&r and it becomes ore that drops &eBlaze Ember&r: &b14,400&r ticks of burn time, &b240 FE/t&r in the coal generator."
		""
		"Blaze Ember is also the base of JDT's &aliquid fuel&r, next door."
	]
	quest.4E56B30212417FCC.quest_subtitle: "Coal, tier two"
	quest.4E56B30212417FCC.title: "&cEmber Alert"
	quest.4EA11629C5D1ECBC.quest_desc: [
		"Somewhere in the world, a fleet of airships hangs about &b100 blocks above the ground&r. The &6Airship Village&r can appear over any overworld biome but is &cvery rare&r, so keep an eye on the sky while you travel."
		""
		"Don't expect a staircase to the ground. &aBring a stack of blocks&r to pillar up, or fly in once you have wings."
	]
	quest.4EA11629C5D1ECBC.quest_subtitle: "The rarest village floats"
	quest.4EA11629C5D1ECBC.title: "&bHigh Society"
	quest.4EE56E8124E8D605.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Cooking Frame&r is a &btwo-block-tall&r kettle over its own fire, made from &eSticks&r, &eIron Ingots&r and a &eCampfire&r. It needs &ano extra heat source&r, so it is the easy start."
		""
		"Every recipe uses water. Put it in the water slot: a &eWater Bucket&r fills &b50%&r, a &eWater Bottle&r &b25%&r. The tooltip shows the water level."
		""
		"EMI lists its recipes under &bCooking Cauldron&r."
	]
	quest.4EE56E8124E8D605.quest_subtitle: "A kettle over an open flame"
	quest.4EE56E8124E8D605.title: "&6Framed for Cooking"
	quest.4F151916C762CEFB.quest_desc: [
		"Stack a &eBrass Sheet&r, a &eSpout&r and a &eBlock of Iron&r for the &6Printer&r. It sits above a Depot or belt like a Spout. Put the original in its filter slot."
		""
		"With &eLiquid Experience&r it &acopies Enchanted Books&r. With &eLiquid Black Dye&r it copies Written Books, train schedules, clipboards and package addresses. Any dye prints names and banner patterns."
	]
	quest.4F151916C762CEFB.quest_subtitle: "Ctrl+C for enchanted books"
	quest.4F151916C762CEFB.title: "&eHot Off the Press"
	quest.4F1804A6ECEF8A8B.quest_desc: [
		"&dEldritch&r spells can't be forged until you learn them. Gather &eAncient Knowledge Fragments&r (three in every Ancient City chest, often one to three in stronghold library chests, now and then in End Cities, and Wandering Traders sell them) and surround an &eEcho Shard&r with &e8&r of them."
		""
		"&aRight-click the Eldritch Manuscript&r to learn one of seven eldritch spells. One manuscript, one spell."
		""
		"After that, the &6Scroll Forge&r makes that spell with an Echo Shard as the focus."
	]
	quest.4F1804A6ECEF8A8B.quest_subtitle: "The school nobody teaches"
	quest.4F1804A6ECEF8A8B.title: "&3Forbidden Lore"
	quest.4F1ABD82E4790B53.quest_desc: [
		"&eIron Ingots&r and a &eStick&r make a &6Faucet&r. Put it on the side of a &6Jar&r, barrel or other container and right-click the handle to open or close it."
		""
		"When open it &adrains liquid&r into a container below, and &adrips items&r out of the inventory behind it, one at a time. &bA redstone signal flips it&r open or closed."
		""
		"&7Water from a faucet also turns dirt into mud and concrete powder into concrete.&r"
	]
	quest.4F1ABD82E4790B53.quest_subtitle: "Drip, drip, drip"
	quest.4F1ABD82E4790B53.title: "&bTap That"
	quest.4F4736F6E221235C.quest_desc: [
		"The Labyrinth hides &eDisc Fragments&r in its chests, its tomb and its suspicious sand (bring a &eBrush&r). Craft &b9 fragments&r into the music disc &dSlither&r."
		""
		"&7A second disc, &dCalidum&7, can turn up in Labyrinth chests and in the desert Bazaar.&r"
	]
	quest.4F4736F6E221235C.quest_subtitle: "Nine pieces, one tune"
	quest.4F4736F6E221235C.title: "&dNine Pieces of Slither"
	quest.4F652B79BBCA3F4B.quest_desc: [
		"Getting the full Hauntbound set earns two &6Completionist Banners: Sleepy Hollows&r."
		""
		"&aPlace one&r and everyone within &b8 blocks&r gets &dMental Fortitude&r: no sanity drain at all. Plant one at the Cemetery for a calm boss arena, or at a base inside the biome."
		""
		"&7Want more? A Smithing Table turns a banner, a Netherite Upgrade and a Netherite Ingot into two.&r"
	]
	quest.4F652B79BBCA3F4B.quest_subtitle: "Plant it and keep your head"
	quest.4F652B79BBCA3F4B.title: "&dFlag of Fortitude"
	quest.4F93A59DF7E5C23F.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Empty Fan Catalyst&r (a ring of 4 Brass Ingots and 4 Iron Bars) is a tidy fan-processing block. Fill it and the fan processes as if it blew through the real thing, with &ano flowing water and no fire spread&r."
		""
		"Right-click or Spout it full: a &eWater Bucket&r for washing, &eLava&r for blasting, &eNetherrack&r for smoking, &eSoul Sand&r for haunting. &ePowder Snow&r and &eDragon's Breath&r unlock the Dragons Plus processes too."
		""
		"&7Craft a filled catalyst on its own to empty it again.&r"
	]
	quest.4F93A59DF7E5C23F.quest_subtitle: "Fan processing, no fire required"
	quest.4F93A59DF7E5C23F.title: "&eCatalytic Converter"
	quest.4FABA66CF8E92297.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Ancient Mines&r are dwarven halls dug into &bhills and mountains&r. Expect cave spiders near the bottom."
		""
		"Read the &elore books&r you find there, and keep an eye out for golden apples and a music disc."
	]
	quest.4FABA66CF8E92297.quest_subtitle: "They are coming"
	quest.4FABA66CF8E92297.title: "&7Drums in the Deep"
	quest.4FBBF39DD34818BB.quest_desc: [
		"Right-click a placed &eStripped Log&r (or Stripped Wood) with a &eBrass Ingot&r and it becomes &6Brass Casing&r. A &6Deployer&r can do the same job later."
		""
		"While you're at it, run some ingots through your &6Mechanical Press&r for &eBrass Sheets&r: hands, arms and smart chutes all want them."
		""
		"&7Casing is the shell of almost every brass machine, so keep a stack handy.&r"
	]
	quest.4FBBF39DD34818BB.quest_subtitle: "Brass on bark"
	quest.4FBBF39DD34818BB.title: "&eCasing the Joint"
	quest.4FC5A8E7DCAEDCFC.quest_desc: [
		"The &cHorseman&r has &b180 HP&r and 26 armour, hits for 16 and shrugs off knockback. Every so often he calls &cSoulfire&r: when \"Soulfire rises!\" appears, &amove&r, because the spirals set you alight."
		""
		"Take him down to 66% and 33%, catch his head each time, and after the second head he &cenrages&r with &b30%&r more speed. Finish him off."
		""
		"He drops 250 XP, &b3 Loot Bags&r and, every time, the &eReins of the Spectral Horse&r."
		""
		"&7The quest counts for whoever lands the killing blow, and their team. Another Luminous Essence summons him again, so everyone can get a turn.&r"
	]
	quest.4FC5A8E7DCAEDCFC.quest_subtitle: "Darkness falls, a boss to dread"
	quest.4FC5A8E7DCAEDCFC.title: "&4The Horseman Rides No More"
	quest.4FF77810D61818ED.quest_desc: [
		"&6Chutes&r (Iron Sheet, Iron Ingot, Iron Sheet, makes 4) drop items straight down between inventories. Place them against each other's sides to go diagonal."
		""
		"Put an &6Encased Fan&r at the top or bottom and items travel &bupward&r instead. Your Goggles show which way a chute is flowing."
	]
	quest.4FF77810D61818ED.quest_subtitle: "What goes up must come down"
	quest.4FF77810D61818ED.title: "&eVertical Logistics"
	quest.4FF7E341EA3319B9.quest_desc: [
		"A powered &6Magnet&r pushes blocks made of &biron or copper&r away on one side and pulls them in on the other: iron blocks, raw ore blocks, anvils, cauldrons, hoppers and more."
		""
		"Its force is the &bredstone signal minus the distance&r, and the strongest magnet wins. Moved &eHoppers&r drop one item per block travelled (and &aplant seeds&r), and a moved &eStonecutter&r cuts the block above it."
		""
		"&cThe recipe needs a Chorus Fruit&r, so this is an End-game toy. Moving farms, sliding doors, auto-planters: the automation branch is complete."
	]
	quest.4FF7E341EA3319B9.quest_subtitle: "Opposites attract. So does iron."
	quest.4FF7E341EA3319B9.title: "&6Magnetic Personality"
	quest.501C6718F70BCB52.quest_desc: [
		"A zombie bite can &cinfect&r a villager: they turn green and slur their words, and after &b3 days&r they become a zombie."
		""
		"&aGift a Golden Apple&r to cure them on the spot. A villager who has already turned needs a &eSplash Potion of Weakness&r first, then a golden apple, and a few minutes to recover. An &6Infirmary&r in the village makes infection less likely."
	]
	quest.501C6718F70BCB52.quest_subtitle: "Keeps the zombie away"
	quest.501C6718F70BCB52.title: "&cAn Apple a Day"
	quest.502C438742122F1B.quest_desc: [
		"Every storage upgrade starts as an &eUpgrade Base&r (iron and planks). Add logs for a &eStack Upgrade Tier 1&r: every slot holds &b2x&r as much."
		""
		"Higher tiers go &b3x, 4x, 8x, 16x&r and &b32x&r using copper, iron, gold, diamond and netherite. A chest takes at most &b2&r stack upgrades."
		""
		"Other upgrades worth a look: &ePickup&r, &eMagnet&r, &eHopper&r, &eVoid&r, &eCompacting&r and &eCrafting&r. Backpack upgrades convert to storage ones with planks."
	]
	quest.502C438742122F1B.quest_subtitle: "Same chest, more stuff"
	quest.502C438742122F1B.title: "&6Stack 'Em High"
	quest.505DA514D8E4A6F8.quest_desc: [
		"A placed baby grows through &bBaby, Toddler, Child, Teen&r and finally &bAdult&r, &b4 days&r per stage. It reaches &aChild&r about &b8 days&r after you place it."
		""
		"In a hurry? &aGift a Golden Apple&r to skip a day. Children only age while their chunk is loaded, so keep them close to home."
		""
		"&7Here's a fishing rod for your little one's first job.&r"
	]
	quest.505DA514D8E4A6F8.quest_subtitle: "Toddler on the loose"
	quest.505DA514D8E4A6F8.title: "&aWhat a Handful"
	quest.50642F6B33333278.quest_desc: [
		"&aPlace a Luminous Essence on the Pedestal&r (right-click it). A &b7.5-second&r ritual begins: souls swirl, a heart beats, then lightning strikes and the &cHorseman&r appears about &b5 blocks north&r. The essence is used up."
		""
		"Pack first: good armour, plenty of food, &eSplash Luminous Water&r, sanity snacks and lanterns, and a way to chase a fast target (a horse or a bow)."
		""
		"&cWater won't save you:&r he turns nearby water sources into gravestone. &7Only one Horseman can ride within 64 blocks at a time.&r"
	]
	quest.50642F6B33333278.quest_subtitle: "Knock, knock. Who's there? Nobody"
	quest.50642F6B33333278.title: "&dSomething Stirs"
	quest.5067BD43429AD55F.quest_desc: [
		"&6Better Dungeons&r has three big dungeons:"
		"&6Catacomb&r: zombie halls with a &astaircase entrance&r leading down from the surface. Its tombstones hide diamonds, and the other chests can even hold an &eEnchanted Golden Apple&r."
		"&6Fortress of the Undead&r: skeleton spawners and skulls, deep down at &by -50 to -30&r."
		"&6Spider Cave&r: webs, spiders and an egg room full of potions."
		""
		"&7Bring torches, food and a bow. You can find them in any order.&r"
	]
	quest.5067BD43429AD55F.quest_subtitle: "Bones, brains and cobwebs"
	quest.5067BD43429AD55F.title: "&cCrypt Crawler"
	quest.50C6BB85F6B49702.quest_desc: [
		"Armour on, food growing, land claimed, bags packed and a waystone or two on the map. You've made it through day one!"
		""
		"Next stop: &6Kitted Out&r, the must-haves chapter right below this one. It covers the mods that make everyday life easier, from better furnaces to backpack upgrades."
		""
		"After that, pick any mod chapter that looks fun. &7Duff believes in you.&r"
	]
	quest.50C6BB85F6B49702.quest_subtitle: "Day one: survived"
	quest.50C6BB85F6B49702.title: "&6Settled In"
	quest.50ED0CA668B94F67.quest_desc: [
		"&6Jousting&r adds &elances&r for mounted combat. Craft a &eWooden Lance&r from logs, planks and a stick."
		""
		"Lances only work &bwhile riding&r a horse, donkey, camel or other mount. &bHold right-click&r to lower the lance and charge: your mount speeds up and everything in your path takes a hit and gets knocked back. Let go and there's a short cooldown."
		""
		"&aAnything riding a mount without a lance gets knocked right off it&r, spider jockeys and skeleton riders included. &7Here's a saddle to get you started.&r"
	]
	quest.50ED0CA668B94F67.quest_subtitle: "Couch your lance, good sir"
	quest.50ED0CA668B94F67.title: "&6Joust Do It"
	quest.50FDBCAFC275A7BF.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Blunderbuss&r comes only from the Guild Commission &e\"Big Game Hunter\"&r: hunt &b8 Elephants&r while you hold the contract."
		""
		"&eFlint Ammunition&r (Flint and Gunpowder) fires &b4-8 pellets&r, deadly up close. &eDiamond Ammunition&r fires one &b12-damage&r shot. Repair it with &eIron Ingots&r."
		""
		"&7Commissions come and go with the board's refresh, so check back if it isn't there yet.&r"
	]
	quest.50FDBCAFC275A7BF.quest_subtitle: "Blunder forward"
	quest.50FDBCAFC275A7BF.title: "&cBig Game Hunter"
	quest.51088EBC45A3FB05.quest_desc: [
		"&eMithril Ore&r sits deep: &bY -63 to -38&r, and never touching air, so caves won't show it. Strip-mine or tunnel. It needs a &cNetherite Pickaxe&r."
		""
		"&aBlast&r Raw Mithril into &eMithril Scrap&r (blast furnace only), and craft &e4 scrap&r into an ingot."
		""
		"&7Mithril goes into rings, upgrade orbs, portal frames and the best gear.&r"
	]
	quest.51088EBC45A3FB05.quest_subtitle: "Deep, hidden and stubborn"
	quest.51088EBC45A3FB05.title: "&bTruesilver"
	quest.511B9126C80A1E00.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Steam Vent&r (5 &eIron Nuggets&r, makes two) is an extractor hood. It &aswitches itself on above a lit heat source&r within &b4 blocks&r: campfires, furnaces, smokers, and the stoves and pots from &6Farm \\& Charm&r, &6Candlelight&r and the other Let's Do kitchen mods. Right-click it to keep it always on."
		""
		"&6Steam Pipes&r (&eIron Nuggets&r, makes four) connect in every direction. &aRun pipes from a vent into a Chimney&r and smoke puffs out of the top. The &6Brick Chimney&r takes &eBricks&r and &eBrick Slabs&r. &bSneak-right-click&r a Chimney to cycle none, moderate and thick smoke."
		""
		"&7Chimneys get sooty over time. Right-click a sooty one with a Brush for Black Dye. Stone Brick and Copper Chimneys exist too, but any one chimney counts for the finale.&r"
	]
	quest.511B9126C80A1E00.quest_subtitle: "Every kitchen needs a hood"
	quest.511B9126C80A1E00.title: "&7Something's Cooking"
	quest.512570655D2D3AD2.quest_desc: [
		"Craft &eplanks&r into &6Wooden Silos&r and stack them: they join into one silo up to &b3x3 wide and 9 tall&r. Right-click with an item to load it, &bright-click with an empty hand&r to open the hatch, &bsneak-right-click&r to take out what's dried."
		""
		"Dry &ebone meal&r or &erotten flesh&r into &eFertilizer&r, which feeds several nearby crops at once."
		""
		"&7Brewery dries its grains here as well; see &6The Cellar&7 chapter.&r"
	]
	quest.512570655D2D3AD2.quest_subtitle: "Waste not, grow lots"
	quest.512570655D2D3AD2.title: "&6Silo Story"
	quest.51276E6FBB85E29E.quest_desc: [
		"The &eHelium Flamingo&r lets you &aswim through the air&r for &b8 seconds&r, then recharge for &b15&r. A meter shows the charge."
		""
		"Its key is unbound by default, so it uses &bSprint while in mid-air&r. Bind \"Activate Helium Flamingo\" under Options > Controls if you prefer."
		""
		"Find it in &6End cities&r, ancient cities and some stronghold chests."
		""
		"&7That ends this list, not the Artifacts: dozens more are out there. Keep opening chests and killing Mimics.&r"
	]
	quest.51276E6FBB85E29E.quest_subtitle: "Swimming, but in the sky"
	quest.51276E6FBB85E29E.title: "&dFlamingo Flight"
	quest.516BBF7063C1E654.quest_desc: [
		"&eDiamonds&r live in the &bdeepslate&r layers near the bottom of the world. You need an &eIron Pickaxe&r or better to mine them."
		""
		"In this pack they unlock a lot: the &6Enchanting Table&r, the &6Building Gadget&r, the &6Storage Network Root&r, the &6Bounty Board&r, the &6Diamond Furnace&r and the top backpack and chest tiers."
		""
		"&7Tip: make a Diamond Pickaxe early - you need one to mine Obsidian.&r"
	]
	quest.516BBF7063C1E654.quest_subtitle: "Dig deeper. No, deeper."
	quest.516BBF7063C1E654.title: "&bShiny Business"
	quest.51AD57CE613EEA10.quest_desc: [
		"&6Better Desert Temples&r turns the old pyramid into a huge tomb with &bpuzzles, traps and parkour&r. Look for it in &bdeserts&r."
		""
		"&cThe temple curses you with Mining Fatigue&r while its Pharaoh lives, so you can't tunnel around anything. Explore the library, the lab and the storerooms (saddles and horse armour!) and find your way to the tomb."
		""
		"&7On the way you will pass &6YUNG's Extras&7 wells, obelisks and ruins. Some wells hide treasure at the bottom.&r"
	]
	quest.51AD57CE613EEA10.quest_subtitle: "Wipe your feet on the way in"
	quest.51AD57CE613EEA10.title: "&eSandstone Secrets"
	quest.51DAF82501F5392E.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Cookpot&r (Copper and Iron Ingots) uses the same recipes as the Cooking Frame, but it &conly cooks with a heat source under it&r. &cA plain Campfire does not count.&r"
		""
		"Build a &6Tiled Stove&r from &eLimestone Bricks&r and &eIron Ingots&r, then place the pot on top. &cMined Limestone drops Cobbled Limestone:&r smelt it back into Limestone before crafting bricks. The Fireplace and Smoker-lid versions of the stove also work."
		""
		"&7The stoves from Farm \\& Charm, Candlelight and Herbal Brews heat it as well.&r"
	]
	quest.51DAF82501F5392E.quest_subtitle: "Proper Swiss kitchen"
	quest.51DAF82501F5392E.title: "&6Stoked"
	quest.51E9DBA1157D9C14.quest_desc: [
		"Craft the &6Alchemical Cauldron&r (&e3 Astralite Ingots&r + &e4 Fluxite&r), then build its ring: a diamond of &b12 Fluxite&r in the floor around the pot, &b4 Willow Log pillars&r (unstripped) two high on the corners of a 5x5, each capped with a &eBlock of Astralite&r, and two blocks of air above. Ponder shows it."
		""
		"&aLink a charged pool to it&r and right-click to light it for &b2,000 ƒ&r. Pour in &eVibrant Fluxia Buckets&r for its tank."
		""
		"&7Astralite Leaching turns 1 raw astralite into 2 ingots. The Grimoire lists every brew.&r"
	]
	quest.51E9DBA1157D9C14.quest_subtitle: "Alchemical Cauldron"
	quest.51E9DBA1157D9C14.title: "&5The Pot Boils"
	quest.523323717A54527B.quest_desc: [
		"Place &aevery kind of Furniture piece at least once&r. Remember: &conly Oak wood and Red fabric count&r, and each piece has to be &bplaced&r, not just crafted."
		""
		"If you've followed this chapter you have almost all of it. Commonly missed: an &6Oak Desk&r (yours became a Dresser), an &6Oak Shutter&r (6 Oak Slabs, makes four), the &6Coffer&r and the four workshop pieces. For Lamps, Fish Tanks, Chimneys, Planters and Street Lanterns, &aany one of each kind&r is enough."
		""
		"Not needed: the Pells dummy, Canvas paintings, patterned fabrics, Trash Bags and discs. &7Hover over Interior Designer in your advancements screen to see how many of the 32 you've placed.&r"
	]
	quest.523323717A54527B.quest_subtitle: "Home is where you put the furniture"
	quest.523323717A54527B.title: "&6Interior Designer"
	quest.5238D3A4DE2D97A6.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a &6Conduit&r from a &eHeart of the Sea&r and &e8 Nautilus Shells&r. Placed in a frame of prismarine blocks underwater, it gives you &bwater breathing, night vision and fast mining&r nearby."
		""
		"&7No heart from the Elder Guardians? Buried treasure has one every time; shipwreck maps lead to it.&r"
	]
	quest.5238D3A4DE2D97A6.quest_subtitle: "Underwater, but make it comfy"
	quest.5238D3A4DE2D97A6.title: "&bConduit Power"
	quest.527DDF53C9DBC9AB.quest_desc: [
		"Add &eGunpowder&r to Luminous Water for &eSplash Luminous Water&r. Throw it to cleanse infected plants within &b4 blocks&r, cure &cInfected&r and give everyone it hits &b+6 sanity&r."
		""
		"It also deals &b20 damage&r to the &cHorseman&r. That doesn't work while his head is loose, so save your throws for when he's vulnerable."
	]
	quest.527DDF53C9DBC9AB.quest_subtitle: "Throw light at the problem"
	quest.527DDF53C9DBC9AB.title: "&bHoly Splash"
	quest.528E416D85B7921C.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Crushing Wheel&r is a &6Mechanical Crafting&r recipe: a 5x5 grid minus its corners (&b21 crafters&r) holding &e16 Andesite Alloy&r, &e4 Planks&r and a &eStone&r in the centre. It makes &b2 wheels&r."
		""
		"Place two side by side, spinning &binto each other&r, and drop items in from above. &aSilk-touched ore blocks beat raw ore&r: Iron Ore gives a Crushed Raw Iron plus a &b75%&r chance of a second, while Raw Iron gives just one (and a chance of XP). Wash crushed ore with an &6Encased Fan&r through water for &b9 nuggets&r and a chance of a byproduct."
		""
		"&7They also turn Netherrack into Cinder Flour and Obsidian into Powdered Obsidian. Each wheel costs 8 SU per RPM, so bring real power.&r"
	]
	quest.528E416D85B7921C.quest_subtitle: "Grind it fine"
	quest.528E416D85B7921C.title: "&6Wheels of Fortune"
	quest.52941ECF410EFD1D.quest_desc: [
		"&eGems&r drop from about &b4%&r of monsters you kill, and turn up in chests, towers and invader loot. Each gives a bonus that depends on what it's socketed into."
		""
		"To socket one, &apick up the gem and right-click it onto an item&r with a free socket, or use a &6Smithing Table&r. A &dUnique&r gem can only be socketed once per item."
		""
		"Purity runs &bCracked, Chipped, Flawed, Normal, Flawless, Perfect&r. Some gems only drop in the Nether or the End."
	]
	quest.52941ECF410EFD1D.quest_subtitle: "Apothic Gems"
	quest.52941ECF410EFD1D.title: "&bShiny Rocks, Big Bonuses"
	quest.52E19D506056C8A6.quest_desc: [
		"&6Beachparty&r turns the plain vanilla &bBeach&r biome into a holiday spot: &ePalm Trees&r, &eSeashells&r and rippled &eSandwaves&r generate there and only there. Snowy and stony beaches don't count."
		""
		"Find a beach and chop some &ePalm Logs&r. One log makes 4 &ePalm Planks&r, and the full wood set is there: doors, boats, signs, plus &ePalm Glass&r and floorboards."
		""
		"&7Grab a few Palm Sprouts from the leaves too. They grow on any sand block, so you can build a beach at home.&r"
	]
	quest.52E19D506056C8A6.quest_subtitle: "No shirt, no shoes, no problem"
	quest.52E19D506056C8A6.title: "&eLife's a Beach"
	quest.530079768834BC26.quest_desc: [
		"The &5Archmage Spell Book&r is the end of the road: your Mage's Spell Book, the &eWilden Tribute&r, a &eNether Star&r, a &eTotem of Undying&r, 3 &eEnder Pearls&r and 2 &eEmeralds&r."
		""
		"It unlocks every &dTier III&r glyph: Blink, Burst, Linger, Wall, Lightning, Fangs, Summon Undead, Split, Orbit, Glide, Wither and more. Each costs 160 XP points at the Scribe's Table, so bring levels."
		""
		"&aYou are now, officially, an Archmage.&r &7The Ritual of Challenge can start a raid if you still need a Totem.&r"
	]
	quest.530079768834BC26.quest_subtitle: "Tier III, the full alphabet"
	quest.530079768834BC26.title: "&5Magnum Opus"
	quest.53536D1A03DBFA74.quest_desc: [
		"&eIron Bars&r, &eIron Ingots&r and a &eWooden Slab&r make a &6Cage&r. Click a small mob to capture it, right-click to let it out, and &bShift + right-click&r to place the cage as a block."
		""
		"It fits chickens, rabbits, foxes, parrots, cats, bats, armadillos and the &bbabies&r of cows, sheep, pigs and goats. &cPets must be tamed first.&r"
		""
		"&7Perfect for carrying pets and young livestock across the server.&r"
	]
	quest.53536D1A03DBFA74.quest_subtitle: "Moving house? Bring the cat"
	quest.53536D1A03DBFA74.title: "&aPet Carrier"
	quest.5391A904E11F1D99.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Grill&r is &e3 Iron Ingots&r, a &eCampfire&r and &e4 Iron Nuggets&r. Right-click raw food onto it: it holds &b4 items&r and cooks anything a campfire can."
		""
		"Grilled food gets &a+25% nutrition and saturation&r. That includes Lili's fish meals and Beachparty's mussels."
		""
		"&cDon't stand on a lit grill.&r"
	]
	quest.5391A904E11F1D99.quest_subtitle: "Beach barbecue"
	quest.5391A904E11F1D99.title: "&6Flame Grilled"
	quest.53A3F76EFD642204.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Item Collector&r is an unpowered vacuum. Stick it on a chest and it pulls dropped items in its area straight into that inventory, with filters and a speed setting. &7Perfect next to a farm or a Block Breaker.&r"
		""
		"The &6Simple Fluid Collector&r (a Dispenser and a Bucket in the usual Ferricore frame) does the same for fluids: it sucks up the source in front of it, holds &bone fluid&r at a time and fills a bucket or Fluid Canister in its slot."
		""
		"&7Its partners, the Simple Fluid Placer and Simple Dropper, put fluids and items back into the world.&r"
	]
	quest.53A3F76EFD642204.quest_subtitle: "Nothing left on the floor"
	quest.53A3F76EFD642204.title: "&6Hoover Duty"
	quest.53F5F115EF6DC506.quest_desc: [
		"&6Lootr&r makes loot chests, barrels, minecarts and more in structures &aper-player&r: everyone gets their own roll, even teammates. Chests you've already opened look different."
		""
		"Open any structure's loot chest to finish. &7Loot containers only break while sneaking - leave them for the next player. The &6Into the Unknown&7 chapter has places to look.&r"
	]
	quest.53F5F115EF6DC506.quest_subtitle: "No more empty chests"
	quest.53F5F115EF6DC506.title: "&6Loot for Everyone"
	quest.5433ADCB5A41E3CC.quest_desc: [
		"Melt &eCopper&r and &eGold&r in the same Smeltery and they combine into molten &eRose Gold&r on their own: 1 ingot of each makes 2. Pour the result through your &eIngot Cast&r."
		""
		"&cAlloying is automatic.&r Melt copper and gold together and you get rose gold whether you wanted it or not."
		""
		"A rose gold head &amines very fast&r but at a low tier, and its &benhanced&r trait gives a bonus upgrade slot. Rose gold is also one of the easiest metals for building the &6Anvil&r."
	]
	quest.5433ADCB5A41E3CC.quest_subtitle: "Copper + gold = love"
	quest.5433ADCB5A41E3CC.title: "&eComing Up Roses"
	quest.54506DCF008A2FCB.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Accumulator&r stores &b2,000,000 FE&r per block and merges into a multiblock up to &b3 wide and 5 tall&r. Craft it with a &eCopper Rod&r, two &eCapacitors&r, a &eBrass Casing&r and &eElectrum Wire&r. Give it an input connector and an output connector."
		""
		"For long runs use &eLarge Connectors&r (2 Andesite Alloy, a Slime Ball and a Gold or Electrum Rod make 2): &b5,000 FE/t&r, up to &b32 blocks&r, but they take only &eGold&r or &eElectrum Spools&r."
		""
		"&aYou now have a real power grid.&r FE is the pack's shared energy, so it can feed other mods' machines too."
		""
		"&7Want power on a moving contraption? The Portable Energy Interface works like a Portable Storage Interface for FE.&r"
	]
	quest.54506DCF008A2FCB.quest_subtitle: "Two million FE a block"
	quest.54506DCF008A2FCB.title: "&6Grid Expectations"
	quest.549C738712D70ED4.quest_desc: [
		"&eUpgrade: Flight&r (Blank, End Crystal, Feather, Phantom Membrane) fits only the &eEclipse Alloy Chestplate&r. It lets you fly freely, &cpaid for in FE&r, so don't run dry mid-air."
		""
		"A fresh chestplate costs 8 ingots. A &eCelestigem Chestplate&r + &eTemplate: Eclipse Alloy&r (5 ingots) + one more ingot in a Smithing Table costs 6, and its upgrades come along."
	]
	quest.549C738712D70ED4.quest_subtitle: "Creative flight, survival rules"
	quest.549C738712D70ED4.title: "&dFly Me to the Moon"
	quest.551A358EBAD361AF.quest_desc: [
		"Fish Tanks are two blocks long. The &6Copper Fish Tank&r takes &eCopper Ingots&r and &eGlass&r, the &6Iron Fish Tank&r &eIron Ingots&r and &eGlass&r. Either one counts for the finale."
		""
		"&aRight-click a tank with a bucket of Cod, Salmon or Pufferfish&r to add the fish, and you keep the empty bucket. One tank can hold all three. Breaking the tank sets the fish free."
		""
		"&7Cats will sit and stare at it for hours.&r"
	]
	quest.551A358EBAD361AF.quest_subtitle: "The cat has opinions"
	quest.551A358EBAD361AF.title: "&bSomething Fishy"
	quest.551BFBBB211497CE.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Seared Chute&r lets hoppers and pipes feed items into the Smeltery. A &6Seared Duct&r is a drain with a &bfilter slot&r: it only outputs the fluid you pick."
		""
		"&6Seared Channels&r carry fluid sideways and downhill, never up. In this port, drains and ducts also work with &afluid pipes from other mods&r, including Create's."
	]
	quest.551BFBBB211497CE.quest_subtitle: "Hoppers in, pipes out"
	quest.551BFBBB211497CE.title: "&eDucts in a Row"
	quest.55230C8044653CDF.quest_desc: [
		"&6Foxhounds&r roam the Nether Wastes and Basalt Deltas (a rare blue kind lives in Soul Sand Valleys). They are hostile and set you on fire."
		""
		"To tame one, drink a &dPotion of Fire Resistance&r, then feed it &eCoal&r. Each piece has a small chance, so bring plenty."
		""
		"A tamed Foxhound fights like a wolf, and if it &anaps on a Furnace&r it speeds up smelting."
		""
		"&7Wraiths in Soul Sand Valleys drop Soul Beads that fly toward the nearest Nether Fortress.&r"
	]
	quest.55230C8044653CDF.quest_subtitle: "Hot dog"
	quest.55230C8044653CDF.title: "&4Playing With Fire"
	quest.55246DB5340409FE.quest_desc: [
		"The &cDead King&r sits on his throne as a skeleton. &aHit it or right-click it&r and he rises. He has &b500&r base health, and more when several players gang up on him."
		""
		"He drops lots of essence and has a &b50%&r chance at a &eNecronomicon&r or &eBlood Staff&r. &aEveryone who fought&r gets a &eBone Key&r to open a Bone Vault once."
		""
		"&7Want a rematch? Phylactery Shards from the Catacombs and vaults make a Phylactery to wake his soul. Do it with Bad Omen for a tougher, richer Ominous King.&r"
	]
	quest.55246DB5340409FE.quest_subtitle: "He's not dead, just resting"
	quest.55246DB5340409FE.title: "&4Long Live the King"
	quest.554A67577191E5FD.quest_desc: [
		"In this pack every &6End Portal Frame&r is unstable, and a production line can fix that. Build the &dEnd Portal Stabilizer&r with &6sequenced assembly&r:"
		""
		"&6- Create:&r a &6sequenced assembly&r on a &eNether Star&r: &b3 loops&r of Netherite Ingot, Precision Mechanism, Eye of Ender, &b1,000 mB&r Liquid Experience and an Echo Shard, then a press."
		""
		"&7Spouts handle the Liquid Experience, Deployers the parts. The rest of the road to the End is in &6Into the Unknown&7.&r"
	]
	quest.554A67577191E5FD.quest_subtitle: "Engineering the End"
	quest.554A67577191E5FD.title: "&6Assembly Required"
	quest.556290828A142A09.quest_desc: [
		"This plate uses everything you've built. Bake &eRoasted Corn&r on the Stove (two corn and butter), then combine &eany bread&r, &eBacon with Eggs&r and the corn in a crafting table."
		""
		"&eFarmer's Breakfast&r restores &b12 hunger points&r (six drumsticks), the best value in Farm \\& Charm, and you can place it on a table to share."
		""
		"&aYour kitchen is up and running.&r Bakery and Candlelight branch off from here."
	]
	quest.556290828A142A09.quest_subtitle: "The most important meal of the day"
	quest.556290828A142A09.title: "&6Breakfast of Champions"
	quest.558E24BA4CBCED96.quest_desc: [
		"Build a &bT&r of four soul sand and place the three skulls on top. The &cWither&r explodes when it spawns and smashes blocks, so &csummon it far from anything you love&r: deep underground or out in the Nether."
		""
		"Below half health it grows armour that &cblocks arrows&r, so switch to melee. &aSmite&r works well, and milk clears the Wither effect."
		""
		"It drops a &eNether Star&r, the heart of a &6Beacon&r. &7The quest counts for whoever lands the killing blow, and their team.&r"
	]
	quest.558E24BA4CBCED96.quest_subtitle: "Do not summon indoors"
	quest.558E24BA4CBCED96.title: "&8Withering Heights"
	quest.55D7DADD64FCB653.quest_desc: [
		"At a tier IV altar, &dAwakening Empyrite&r (&b2,500 ƒ&r, 9x9) takes a &eGold Block&r, &e2 Glowstone&r and &e4 Blaze Powder&r. &aLay your empyrite gear on the ground inside the circle&r: it isn't consumed and keeps its enchantments."
		""
		"Awakened pieces glow gold and grow stronger with use through &dResonance I-V&r."
		""
		"Each awakened piece can then take one &dimbuement&r, another tier IV rite: Veinsense, Kilnheart, Skystep, Siphon and six more. Check the Grimoire for layouts."
	]
	quest.55D7DADD64FCB653.quest_subtitle: "Awakening Empyrite, tier IV"
	quest.55D7DADD64FCB653.title: "&6Wake the Metal"
	quest.560F42E3CE954E72.quest_desc: [
		"The &eTrowel&r (a stick and 2 iron ingots) places a &brandom block from your hotbar&r each time you use it."
		""
		"Fill the hotbar with gravel, cobble and moss and you get a natural rubble path. Put a block in more slots to make it more likely. It is &aunbreakable&r in this pack."
	]
	quest.560F42E3CE954E72.quest_subtitle: "Let chaos design your path"
	quest.560F42E3CE954E72.title: "&eRandom Acts of Building"
	quest.561BD899B72600DE.quest_desc: [
		"Witches throw &cSplash Potions&r of Harming, Poison, Slowness and Weakness, and drink their own potions to heal, speed up or shrug off fire. They take &bfar less damage from magic&r, so the harming potions you loot here barely tickle them. Close the gap fast and use a sword or an axe."
		""
		"&aBring milk&r to clear the poison and weakness. Inside the village, &bwitches are the only monster that spawns&r in the dark (no zombies, skeletons or slimes), so leave the lights off if you want a steady supply of redstone, glowstone and sugar."
	]
	quest.561BD899B72600DE.quest_subtitle: "Trick question. All of them."
	quest.561BD899B72600DE.title: "&5Which Witch Is Which"
	quest.56369BC287278CBF.quest_desc: [
		"&6Shibas&r live in mountain biomes. Tame one with &eBones&r, like a wolf, and it becomes a loyal friend that &afetches the arrows you shoot&r."
		""
		"Best trick: hold a &eTorch&r and your Shiba &bbarks at dark spots&r that need lighting. Light the spot it finds to complete this quest."
	]
	quest.56369BC287278CBF.quest_subtitle: "Much light. Very safe."
	quest.56369BC287278CBF.title: "&eGood Boy, Bright Ideas"
	quest.565C5109E92D7E4C.quest_desc: [
		"Wear an affix item in &ball four armor slots&r and hold an affixed weapon to unlock &6Frontier&r. Unlocking isn't enough: open &bCtrl+T&r, select it and press &aActivate&r."
		""
		"Monsters get &b+4 armor&r and &cApothic Invaders&r start showing up. In return you gain &b+35%&r XP and loot rolls better rarities: Uncommon becomes the norm and Rare turns up more often. Your enchanting cap rises from &b30&r to &b45&r."
		""
		"&7Struggling? You can step back down a tier at any time in the same screen.&r"
	]
	quest.565C5109E92D7E4C.quest_subtitle: "World Tier: Frontier"
	quest.565C5109E92D7E4C.title: "&2Venture Forth"
	quest.566B55C2301ED298.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Quiver&r has no recipe. Look in &epillager outposts&r, woodland mansions and dungeons, or kill one of the rare &cSkeletons wearing a quiver&r (they show up on harder difficulty)."
		""
		"It holds &b6 stacks of arrows&r and works from anywhere in your inventory or the &bCurios belt slot&r."
		""
		"&cKeybind clash!&r The Quiver key defaults to &bV&r, which is also &bVoice Chat push-to-talk&r and a key in Ars Nouveau, Iron's Spells and Just Dire Things. Open &bControls&r, find &bQuiver&r and move it to a free key. Then hold it and pick an arrow with the &bscroll wheel or number keys&r."
		""
		"&7The same trick works for the Lunch Basket (6 stacks of food). Rope Arrows carry up to 32 rope and leave a climbable line where they land.&r"
	]
	quest.566B55C2301ED298.quest_subtitle: "Six stacks, zero fuss"
	quest.566B55C2301ED298.title: "&6Quiver Me Timbers"
	quest.56C0BBD5BBAD56C1.quest_desc: [
		"Every house is a little potion shop, with &6Brewing Stands&r and a stack of &ebarrels&r full of brewing ingredients (redstone, glowstone, spider eyes, sugar, mushrooms, now and then a Rabbit's Foot or a Pufferfish) and a few &cSplash Potions&r to throw back. Some houses also keep a chest of drinkable potions: Healing, Regeneration, Fire Resistance, Swiftness and Water Breathing. One of the larger houses has attic chests with the odd emerald."
		""
		"Grab a &eFermented Spider Eye&r. The barrels sometimes have them ready-made; otherwise craft one from a Spider Eye, Sugar and a Brown Mushroom, all three found in the same barrels. &aIt turns good potions bad&r: Swiftness into Slowness, Healing into Harming."
	]
	quest.56C0BBD5BBAD56C1.quest_subtitle: "Raid the witches' pantry"
	quest.56C0BBD5BBAD56C1.title: "&dEye of Newt"
	quest.56E8E2416820FE3B.quest_desc: [
		"Cut a &eShaft&r with a &6Mechanical Saw&r to get a &6Shear Pin&r. It works like a shaft, but &csnaps when the network overstresses&r, splitting it in two. Keep spares: it is single use."
		""
		"The &6Overstress Clutch&r does the same job and resets: fix the problem, then &bwrench it&r or give it a redstone pulse."
		""
		"&7More clutches: Inverted (couples only when powered), Centrifugal (couples above a set RPM) and Freewheel (one direction only). The Brake halts a network on a redstone signal.&r"
	]
	quest.56E8E2416820FE3B.quest_subtitle: "Better a pin than the whole factory"
	quest.56E8E2416820FE3B.title: "&cBlow a Fuse"
	quest.56F776CA91D18A0E.quest_desc: [
		"Six &eDried Kelp&r make a &6Mechanical Belt&r. Right-click one shaft with it, then a second shaft in line with the first. A belt can be &b2 to 20 blocks&r long, and one belt item covers the whole length."
		""
		"Belts carry items, mobs and you, and both shafts turn at the same speed. Right-click a belt with an empty hand to take items off; sneak-right-click cancels a half-placed belt."
		""
		"&7Here's kelp for a second belt.&r"
	]
	quest.56F776CA91D18A0E.quest_subtitle: "Snack-based logistics"
	quest.56F776CA91D18A0E.title: "&eKelp Drive"
	quest.57015C9828A55684.quest_desc: [
		"Beach bar stocked, fishing box full, Enderbag on your back. One trip left."
		""
		"Every &bEnd City&r treasure chest holds an &5Enderpack&r. Like the Enderbag, it &aopens your Ender Chest&r from your back, in a fancier &6Camping&r pack."
		""
		"Pack a Sleeping Bag, a stack of grilled food and a few cocktails, cross the Outer Islands and bring one home."
		""
		"&7You have truly seen the great outdoors. All of them.&r"
	]
	quest.57015C9828A55684.quest_subtitle: "The farthest campsite of all"
	quest.57015C9828A55684.title: "&5The Great Search"
	quest.573422BC2F7D8022.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Tesla Coil&r charges FE items and runs &bcharging&r recipes on items &abelow it&r on a Depot or belt. Mechanical-craft it with Copper Spools, Andesite Alloy, Capacitors (recipe in the Motor quest), Brass Sheets, a Brass Casing and an Electron Tube."
		""
		"Charging a &eGold Ingot&r costs &b36,000 FE&r and makes an &eElectrum Ingot&r. No mod here adds Silver Ingots, so charging is how you get Electrum."
		""
		"&cGive it a redstone signal and it zaps every mob (and player) within 3 blocks.&r"
	]
	quest.573422BC2F7D8022.quest_subtitle: "Gold, but with more zap"
	quest.573422BC2F7D8022.title: "&6Shocking Gold"
	quest.57692FB2843ED1C6.quest_desc: [
		"Place &e2 Patterns&r on top of &e2 Planks&r to make a &6Part Builder&r. It takes on the look of the wood you used."
		""
		"Put a Pattern in, pick a part from the grid, then add material. It shapes &bsoft materials&r: wood, any stone, flint, bone, cactus, leather and even &eCopper&r. Later it also makes &esand casts&r and salvages old tools."
	]
	quest.57692FB2843ED1C6.quest_subtitle: "Measure twice, carve once"
	quest.57692FB2843ED1C6.title: "&6Cut to Fit"
	quest.577A7F08DDB5F6C6.quest_desc: [
		"Every beer and whiskey needs &eYeast&r: the same yeast that goes into dough, cooked in the Farm \\& Charm &6Cooking Pot&r, &b12&r per batch."
		""
		"Grain must be &adried first&r. Load wheat, barley, oats or corn into a Farm \\& Charm &6Silo&r, then follow its info panel to open the hatch and take out &eDried Barley&r and friends."
		""
		"&7The &6From Farm to Table&7 chapter covers the pot, the yeast recipe, the silo and growing barley, oats and corn.&r"
	]
	quest.577A7F08DDB5F6C6.quest_subtitle: "The boring bits that make it all work"
	quest.577A7F08DDB5F6C6.title: "&eMalt and Yeast"
	quest.5790A8EC6D424DB0.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Display Link&r is a &eTransmitter&r on &eBrass Casing&r. &eAndesite Alloy&r and an &eElectron Tube&r make &b2&r &6Display Boards&r; boards need rotation to run."
		""
		"Right-click the &bdisplay first&r, then place the link on the source block, within &b64 blocks&r. A link on a &6Train Station&r shows live arrival times; one on a &6boiler&r reports its status."
		""
		"&7Two Electron Tubes make four Nixie Tubes, a smaller display for short messages.&r"
	]
	quest.5790A8EC6D424DB0.quest_subtitle: "Departures board not included. Oh wait."
	quest.5790A8EC6D424DB0.title: "&bNow Arriving"
	quest.57D7D9FE00A760D8.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Millstone&r (Cogwheel, Andesite Casing, Stone) grinds whatever you drop in from the &btop&r. Power it from the side with cogwheels; faster spin grinds faster."
		""
		"Good inputs: &eWheat&r to Flour, &eCobblestone&r to Gravel, &eGravel&r to Flint, Bones to Bone Meal, flowers to dyes."
		""
		"&7It won't touch raw ores. Ore crushing comes with Crushing Wheels in the next Create chapter.&r"
	]
	quest.57D7D9FE00A760D8.quest_subtitle: "Grind it 'til you make it"
	quest.57D7D9FE00A760D8.title: "&eEmbrace the Grind"
	quest.57ED5C17E350834D.quest_desc: [
		"Copper makes a &6Wrench&r. &aRight-click a block to rotate it&r around the face you clicked; sneak to turn the other way. Stairs, signs, chests and heads all spin."
		""
		"In your main hand it rotates instead of opening GUIs, so you can turn a chest without opening it. &7It also makes a surprisingly brisk club.&r"
		""
		"This branch covers the redstone gadgets. Have a &6Crank&r for later."
	]
	quest.57ED5C17E350834D.quest_subtitle: "Righty tighty, lefty loosey"
	quest.57ED5C17E350834D.title: "&6Engineer Gaming"
	quest.5833AAEB90F9F574.quest_desc: [
		"Grapes come in &b8 varieties&r: red and white of the plains, the &6taiga&r, the &6savanna&r and the &6jungle&r. Each region's bushes grow wild in its own biome, and each juice ferments into different wines."
		""
		"&eRed Taiga Grapes&r grow in taigas and mountains, &eRed Savanna Grapes&r in savannas and wooded badlands. Plant their seeds on stems at home so you never have to travel twice."
		""
		"&7The Wandering Winemaker sells every kind of seed if you'd rather shop than hike.&r"
	]
	quest.5833AAEB90F9F574.quest_subtitle: "Every biome has its vintage"
	quest.5833AAEB90F9F574.title: "&6Terroir"
	quest.58B811E51E1EFE3C.quest_desc: [
		"&6Just Dire Things&r has no ores. Instead you craft a living &eGoo&r block that slowly &atransforms the storage blocks touching it&r into brand new materials."
		""
		"Four goo tiers, one per 'dimension': Overworld, Nether, End and the Deep Dark. Each tier unlocks a new material, a better coal, a tool set with &bupgrade slots&r and new machines. At the very end you bend &dtime&r itself."
		""
		"Once you have a &ePrimogel Goo&r, craft it with a &eBook&r for the &6Just Dires Guide&r. Goo conversions and fluid tricks may not show in EMI here, so the guide is your reference. Hold &bShift&r on any JDT tool to see which upgrades it takes."
	]
	quest.58B811E51E1EFE3C.quest_subtitle: "Things Direwolf20 wanted, now yours"
	quest.58B811E51E1EFE3C.title: "&6Just Dire Things"
	quest.592FFFFA307E2709.quest_desc: [
		"&6Lootr&r gives every player their own loot from every structure chest, barrel, minecart, pot and item frame. You already opened your first one in &6Kitted Out&r. Now keep going: open &b50 Lootr containers&r."
		""
		"&cNever break a loot chest&r on the server: sneak-breaking destroys it for everyone. Loot it and leave it. Nothing respawns, so new chunks mean new loot."
		""
		"&7Many of these chests hide wearable treasure. The &6Finders Keepers&7 chapter covers the Relics and Artifacts.&r"
	]
	quest.592FFFFA307E2709.quest_subtitle: "Fifty chests, zero arguments"
	quest.592FFFFA307E2709.title: "&6Treasure Hunter"
	quest.5931E5E760ECDDA6.quest_desc: [
		"Relics earn &drelic XP&r mostly by doing their job. The &bExperience Sources&r tab lists how: seconds spent skating, blinks taken, damage soaked. Each relic level gives &b1 upgrade point&r."
		""
		"Spend a point plus some &bplayer XP&r to level an ability up. You can also &areroll&r an ability's stats for XP (it can get worse!) or reset it (for a little XP) to get the points back."
		""
		"&7On a server, check each ability's &bTargeting&7 tab so it doesn't zap your teammates or pets. &bLeft Alt&7 opens the active abilities menu for switching modes.&r"
	]
	quest.5931E5E760ECDDA6.quest_subtitle: "Use it, level it, spend it"
	quest.5931E5E760ECDDA6.title: "&aPoints Well Spent"
	quest.59353D0289F459DD.quest_desc: [
		"When a hit would kill you, the &eChorus Totem&r &ateleports you away&r and leaves you with a bit of health. &cIt is used up&r, so keep a spare."
		""
		"It's the most common artifact in &6End city&r treasure, and woodland mansions sometimes have one. See the &6Into the Unknown&r chapter for reaching the End."
		""
		"&7Belt slot, so it competes with the Cloud and the Heart. Swap it in for risky trips.&r"
	]
	quest.59353D0289F459DD.quest_subtitle: "A Totem of Undying with a travel plan"
	quest.59353D0289F459DD.title: "&5Exit, Stage Left"
	quest.593D60B7A296D5D7.quest_desc: [
		"Workstations still hand out the usual jobs, and MCA adds &6Guards&r and &6Archers&r who protect the village. &6Adventurers&r arrive at a village &6Inn&r and stay a couple of days."
		""
		"Talk to an adventurer and &aHire&r them for &e5&r or &e10 Emeralds&r (short or long contract) to get a mercenary, or ask them to &astay&r and move in for good."
		""
		"&7A Monarch can turn any adult into a Guard or Archer from the Professions button.&r"
	]
	quest.593D60B7A296D5D7.quest_subtitle: "Swords for hire"
	quest.593D60B7A296D5D7.title: "&eEveryone Has a Job"
	quest.598C8116985324D3.quest_desc: [
		"Make a &6Smeltery Controller&r by placing a &eSeared Bricks&r block in a &6Casting Basin&r and pouring &b4 ingots&r (360 mB) of molten &ecopper&r over it."
		""
		"A &6Seared Drain&r (4 bricks and 2 copper ingots) is where fluid comes out, so put a faucet on it. A &6Seared Fuel Tank&r (8 bricks around a glass block) holds &b4 buckets&r of lava fuel."
		""
		"&7Make plenty of Seared Bricks blocks too. The walls eat them.&r"
	]
	quest.598C8116985324D3.quest_subtitle: "Brains, drains and a fuel tank"
	quest.598C8116985324D3.title: "&6Controlling Interest"
	quest.598E5CEE5FB41FDC.quest_desc: [
		"Three cosy &6Let's Do&r mods share this chapter:"
		"&6Beachparty&r: palm trees, coconuts, sandcastles and cocktails."
		"&6Lili's Lucky Lures&r: new ways to fish, from floating junk to fish traps."
		"&6Camping&r: tents, sleeping bags, backpacks and a barbecue grill."
		""
		"None of them has a guide book. &bEMI&r shows the crafting recipes, plus &bTiki Bar Mixing&r (cocktails) and &bMini Fridge Mixing&r (freezing). &cFish Trap baits are not in EMI&r, so the quest that needs them lists them."
		""
		"Pick any of the three branches. They meet again at the end."
	]
	quest.598E5CEE5FB41FDC.quest_subtitle: "Sunscreen not included"
	quest.598E5CEE5FB41FDC.title: "&6The Great Outdoors"
	quest.59AA07A43C898F88.quest_desc: [
		"&6Galleons&r are pirate ships crewed by &cPlunderers&r and pillagers. They spawn out in the &bocean&r, well away from villages, so pack a boat and go looking."
		""
		"&cThe deck cannons come pre-loaded&r and the crew will use them. Bring a shield, a bow and some bombs of your own."
		""
		"Aboard: chests of rope, gunpowder, bombs and gold, a cobwebbed chest holding the ship's &eKey&r, and a locked &6Safe&r. Board the ship and take down at least one Plunderer."
	]
	quest.59AA07A43C898F88.quest_subtitle: "Yo ho, yo ho, a plunderer's life for me"
	quest.59AA07A43C898F88.title: "&cSails on the Horizon"
	quest.59CFE712C6BD5584.quest_desc: [
		"Blooming Nature adds &b10 new trees&r: Aspen, Baobab, Chestnut, Cypress, Ebony, Fan Palm, Fir, Larch, Swamp Cypress and Swamp Oak. Each brings a full wood set: planks, doors, boats and the rest."
		""
		"&eAspen&r grows only in Aspen Forests, which take over patches of Birch Forest. Gather some."
		""
		"&7It adds four building stones too: Laterit, Marlstone, Slate and Travertin.&r"
	]
	quest.59CFE712C6BD5584.quest_subtitle: "Ten new woods to build with"
	quest.59CFE712C6BD5584.title: "&2Branching Out"
	quest.59D1DD875F90D72B.quest_desc: [
		"Upgrade your Pickarang at a &6Smithing Table&r with a &eNetherite Upgrade&r template and a &eNetherite Ingot&r to get the &eFlamarang&r."
		""
		"It mines at &bnetherite level&r, has &b1040 durability&r, and &aanything it carries is fire and lava proof&r. Throw it across a lava lake at a Nether ore vein and the loot still comes home. &7(Like the Pickarang, it can't break obsidian or Ancient Debris.)&r"
		""
		"Get it back while it carries a burning item and you have finished the tour. &aQuark: done, bit by bit.&r"
	]
	quest.59D1DD875F90D72B.quest_subtitle: "The Pickarang, forged in netherite"
	quest.59D1DD875F90D72B.title: "&6Fly to the Sky, Fire Bird"
	quest.5A7A962012C514C9.quest_desc: [
		"&eShafts&r carry rotation in a straight line: two Andesite Alloy stacked make &b8&r. A &eCogwheel&r is a Shaft plus a plank, and passes rotation to cogs beside it."
		""
		"Two small cogs touching side by side turn in &bopposite directions&r at the same speed. A &eLarge Cogwheel&r (one more plank) changes speed; more on that later."
	]
	quest.5A7A962012C514C9.quest_subtitle: "Spin goes in, spin comes out"
	quest.5A7A962012C514C9.title: "&eGetting Into Gear"
	quest.5B459A0763C51D35.quest_desc: [
		"The &eWhistle&r is a &eGold Block&r and &e4 Iron Ingots&r. &aRight-click&r it to open &bCall Family Member&r and pick someone: they are brought straight to you."
		""
		"Perfect for a spouse who wandered off, or for bringing the kids home from the fields. They do need to be somewhere in the area for the whistle to find them."
	]
	quest.5B459A0763C51D35.quest_subtitle: "Come home, honey"
	quest.5B459A0763C51D35.title: "&eDinner's Ready!"
	quest.5B77150AEAD3078A.quest_desc: [
		"The &eExperience Disperser&r can drop from &aany chest in any dimension&r, so it's often your first relic."
		""
		"Wear it in the &bcharm&r slot: it shares a slice of &devery relic XP gain&r with all your other equipped relics, so the slow ones level along. At rank 3 it also turns some ordinary XP orbs into relic XP."
		""
		"&aWear it early&r. It pays off the whole game."
	]
	quest.5B77150AEAD3078A.quest_subtitle: "Charm slot, team player"
	quest.5B77150AEAD3078A.title: "&aShare the Wealth"
	quest.5BD561B1B3C0E7D8.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Stock Link&r (a &eTransmitter&r on an &eItem Vault&r; the Transmitter is a Lightning Rod, Copper Sheets and Redstone) placed on a Packager adds that chest to a &bnetwork&r with unlimited range. Then craft a &6Stock Ticker&r (&eGlass&r, a Stock Link and a &eGold Ingot&r), right-click your link with it, and place it."
		""
		"Seat a mob in front of the ticker, or put a &6Blaze Burner&r there: that's your &6Stock Keeper&r. Right-click it to browse everything on the network and order items to an address."
		""
		"&cOn a shared server, lock the network in the keeper's screen&r, or anyone can order from your chests."
		""
		"&7A Redstone Requester (Iron Ingot, Redstone and a Stock Link) places a preset order on every redstone pulse.&r"
	]
	quest.5BD561B1B3C0E7D8.quest_subtitle: "A shopkeeper for your own stuff"
	quest.5BD561B1B3C0E7D8.title: "&6Taking Stock"
	quest.5C887436217910ED.quest_desc: [
		"&6Relics&r show up in about &bone chest in five&r, anywhere: dungeons, villages, ruins, modded structures. Which relic you get depends on the &bdimension&r, the &bbiome&r around the chest and the &bkind of chest&r."
		""
		"The &eRoller Skate&r can come from any Overworld chest. Wear it on your feet and keep running: your speed &abuilds up&r the longer you go."
		""
		"&7Every relic's stats are rolled at random when it's found, and its quality is shown as 1 to 5 stars.&r"
	]
	quest.5C887436217910ED.quest_subtitle: "Your first relic, probably"
	quest.5C887436217910ED.title: "&eRolling Start"
	quest.5CB2958EBBBF1232.quest_desc: [
		"&6Herbal Brews&r is a cosy tea and coffee mod. You grow or forage leaves, dry them, then brew them in a &6Tea Kettle&r. Every drink gives a buff, and several of them buff your friends too."
		""
		"There is no guide book. Check &bEMI&r instead: the &bKettle Brewing&r and &bCauldron Brewing&r tabs show every recipe. The heat each brew needs is in these quests."
		""
		"It all starts with &eTea Blossoms&r. &aBreak a small vanilla flower with &eShears&r (poppy, dandelion, any tulip, oxeye daisy, allium, cornflower and so on) and it drops a &eTea Blossom&r instead of the flower."
	]
	quest.5CB2958EBBBF1232.quest_subtitle: "Welcome to Herbal Brews"
	quest.5CB2958EBBBF1232.title: "&dSnip, Snip, Sip"
	quest.5CCA5B912837CAE6.quest_desc: [
		"Brew &eLavender Blossom&r or &eHibiscus&r with &eSugar&r and a &eGlass Bottle&r. These barely need any heat, so a plain stove is plenty."
		""
		"&dLavender Tea&r gives &aFeral&r: you hit harder and get extra max health."
		"&cHibiscus Tea&r gives &aLifeleech&r: every few seconds each hostile mob near you loses a little health and you gain it. &aThe bigger the swarm, the more you heal.&r"
	]
	quest.5CCA5B912837CAE6.quest_subtitle: "Feral and Lifeleech"
	quest.5CCA5B912837CAE6.title: "&dFloral Arrangements"
	quest.5CDA28EF2771C903.quest_desc: [
		"&6First Light&r got you a &6Copper Furnace&r. Craft it with &eIron Ingots&r and &eGlass&r into an &6Iron Furnace&r, then with &eGold Ingots&r and a &eGold Block&r into a &6Golden Furnace&r."
		""
		"Ticks per item: vanilla &b200&r, Copper &b180&r, Iron &b160&r, Gold &b120&r, Diamond &b80&r, Emerald or Crystal &b40&r, Obsidian &b20&r, Netherite &b5&r. Every step also has an &eupgrade kit&r for a placed furnace, used just like the copper one."
		""
		"&cThere is no Silver or Rainbow Furnace here: this pack has no silver.&r"
	]
	quest.5CDA28EF2771C903.title: "&6Turning Up the Heat"
	quest.5CF03285F1E47EC6.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Mushroom Mines&r burrow under &bforests&r. Only a few armoured zombie miners and skeleton archers live here, but there are &bdozens of chests&r to open."
		""
		"The biggest chests always hold an &eenchanted pickaxe&r and can have diamond armour. The rest hold mineshaft loot, ores, coal and food."
	]
	quest.5CF03285F1E47EC6.quest_subtitle: "Forty-four chests and a pickaxe each"
	quest.5CF03285F1E47EC6.title: "&7We All Dig Together"
	quest.5D11F427DF64CFF7.quest_desc: [
		"&eSticks&r, &eString&r, a &eRabbit Hide&r and a &eSlimeball&r make a &6Slingshot&r. Hold right-click to charge it, and it fires the item from your offhand (or inventory)."
		""
		"&aBlocks place themselves where they land&r, so you can build at range. &eBuckets&r work too and pour out on impact. It accepts &dQuick Charge&r, &dMultishot&r and the mod's own &dStasis&r enchant (no gravity; books only from End City chests)."
		""
		"&7Bombs, pearls and splash potions are disabled for slingshots here. Parrots, however...&r"
	]
	quest.5D11F427DF64CFF7.quest_subtitle: "Why walk when you can throw?"
	quest.5D11F427DF64CFF7.title: "&aSlingin' Blocks"
	quest.5D161426C00A0769.quest_desc: [
		"Place a &ePlate&r on a Candlelight &6Table&r, then a dish on the plate. Add a &eNapkin&r, glasses and a cloche with right-click."
		""
		"Food eaten from a set table fills you &b1.3x&r as much and gives &bWell Served&r (your hunger won't drop below 4 drumsticks). Every napkin, glass and filled drink adds a minute, up to &b10 minutes&r. &aA lit candle beside it counts too.&r"
	]
	quest.5D161426C00A0769.quest_subtitle: "Elbows off the table"
	quest.5D161426C00A0769.title: "&6Set the Scene"
	quest.5D239F359DCA7A94.quest_desc: [
		"Your children get a &bWork&r button: &aFishing&r, &aHarvesting&r, &aHunting&r and &aChopping&r."
		""
		"Put the right tool in their &bInventory&r first: a fishing rod, a hoe, a weapon or an axe. &cWhen the tool breaks they stop&r, so leave them a spare."
	]
	quest.5D239F359DCA7A94.quest_subtitle: "Make light work"
	quest.5D239F359DCA7A94.title: "&eMany Hands"
	quest.5D3F2C653FA3895F.quest_desc: [
		"Half-buried in the &bdesert&r lies the &6Ceryneian Hind&r: the giant skeleton of a deer, built from bone and quartz. &aNothing guards it.&r"
		""
		"Look for its chest (desert-temple loot and enchanted iron armour) and the two &eblocks of gold&r set into the build."
	]
	quest.5D3F2C653FA3895F.quest_subtitle: "Something big died here. A long time ago."
	quest.5D3F2C653FA3895F.title: "&fOh Deer"
	quest.5D5DD4AB1B5DCF28.quest_desc: [
		"Brew &eDried Oolong Tea&r with a &eGlass Bottle&r at &b40% heat&r."
		""
		"Its &aFortune&r effect raises your &bLuck&r for 1:30, so &afishing&r turns up more treasure and less junk. Brew one before a long session at the pond."
		""
		"You have now mastered the whole drying chain: green, black and oolong. &7Spare Dried Black and Dried Oolong Tea also craft into dyes.&r"
	]
	quest.5D5DD4AB1B5DCF28.quest_subtitle: "The finest leaf in the garden"
	quest.5D5DD4AB1B5DCF28.title: "&6Fortune Favours the Steeped"
	quest.5D6B7C6BEE71163E.quest_desc: [
		"The &5Enderbag&r can't be crafted. It is added to every &bStronghold&r chest that uses the classic corridor, crossing or library loot. &7YUNG's Better Strongholds gives many rooms their own loot instead, so open every chest you pass.&r"
		""
		"Wear it like any backpack and press &bB&r: it opens &ayour Ender Chest&r, so your safest storage travels with you wherever you camp."
		""
		"&7While you're down there, keep your Sleeping Bag handy. It won't drag your spawn into the Stronghold.&r"
	]
	quest.5D6B7C6BEE71163E.quest_subtitle: "The real camping trip"
	quest.5D6B7C6BEE71163E.title: "&5Hell Week"
	quest.5D7F494335289C4F.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Sophisticated Storage Create Integration&r does the same for Sophisticated chests and barrels. On a contraption they keep working like any mounted chest, so a drill or harvester rig has somewhere big to put its haul."
		""
		"Their upgrades keep working while moving, and you can &aopen the mounted storage&r to check its contents and settings on the go."
	]
	quest.5D7F494335289C4F.quest_subtitle: "Sophisticated Storage on the move"
	quest.5D7F494335289C4F.title: "&eFreight Forwarding"
	quest.5DADCA6BDD7AEEEC.quest_desc: [
		"Upgrade your table with a &eNetherite Ingot&r, &b2 Arcane Sands&r and Nether Bricks to make the full &6Reforging Table&r. It handles &5Epic&r and &6Mythic&r reforges."
		""
		"Epic costs &b30 levels&r, 2 Arcane Sands and 4 sigils; Mythic &b50 levels&r, 3 Godforged Pearls and 5 sigils. Epic items carry an &dAbility&r, and that's the Pinnacle set sorted."
	]
	quest.5DADCA6BDD7AEEEC.quest_subtitle: "Epic and Mythic"
	quest.5DADCA6BDD7AEEEC.title: "&5Reforged in Fire"
	quest.5DB7513C262B96FB.quest_desc: [
		"Time to show off everything XyCraft taught you. Build an &eImmortal Aluminum&r and &eImmortal Glass Viewer&r room: a showroom for your tanks and machines that &aonly players can break&r."
		""
		"&eImmortal Aluminum&r takes a &fLight&r cloud Aluminum block with obsidian and aluminum ingots. The &eImmortal Glass Viewer&r is the same frame around a &eReinforced Glass Viewer&r."
		""
		"&7You'll need about 56 aluminum ingots and 48 obsidian, so this is a real project. Withers, dragons and creepers can only look in.&r"
	]
	quest.5DB7513C262B96FB.quest_subtitle: "A showroom no wither can touch"
	quest.5DB7513C262B96FB.title: "&5Unbreakable"
	quest.5DC249A6310485C3.quest_desc: [
		"A &ePathfinder's Quill&r finds a biome for you. &6Wandering Traders&r always carry one; Expert and Master &6Cartographers&r may sell them too."
		""
		"Use the quill and it &bsearches&r (progress shows on screen). When it finds the biome it becomes a map with an &cX&r. Follow it to the spot."
		""
		"&7Nature's Compass (in the Kitted Out chapter) does a similar job. The quill is the pretty, old-fashioned way.&r"
	]
	quest.5DC249A6310485C3.quest_subtitle: "X marks the biome"
	quest.5DC249A6310485C3.title: "&eRoad to Tomorrow"
	quest.5E0E96FB30E8B689.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Sophisticated Backpacks Create Integration&r lets a backpack &bplaced as a block&r ride along on a contraption and keep working. Glue it to a train, a cart or a drill rig."
		""
		"Its upgrades keep ticking while it moves: a &ePickup&r or &eMagnet Upgrade&r collects items around its current position. You can open it on the contraption too."
		""
		"&7Your first backpack is in First Light; tiers and upgrades are in Kitted Out.&r"
	]
	quest.5E0E96FB30E8B689.quest_subtitle: "Sophisticated Backpacks on the move"
	quest.5E0E96FB30E8B689.title: "&aHitchhiker"
	quest.5E12770062A9A6BF.quest_desc: [
		"&6Reindeer&r herd through the same cold biomes. &cThey have 40 health and hit back hard&r, so bring armour. They breed with &eSweet Berries&r."
		""
		"Cook their meat, then craft &eCooked Reindeer&r with a &eBaked Potato&r, a &eBrown Mushroom&r and a &eBowl&r into &b2&r hearty &eCooked Reindeer Dishes&r."
	]
	quest.5E12770062A9A6BF.quest_subtitle: "Sorry, Rudolph"
	quest.5E12770062A9A6BF.title: "&6Warmth on a Winter's Night"
	quest.5E1E3E62E3F09ED0.quest_desc: [
		"&ePaper&r (or Create &eCardboard&r) makes a &6Present&r. Put a stack inside, &aaddress it to a player&r and add a note. Only you and the recipient can open it."
		""
		"Add a &eTripwire Hook&r for a &cTrapped Present&r, a prank box for your friends."
		""
		"&7Great for SMP birthdays, trades and bribes.&r"
	]
	quest.5E1E3E62E3F09ED0.quest_subtitle: "For me? You shouldn't have!"
	quest.5E1E3E62E3F09ED0.title: "&dIt's a Wrap"
	quest.5E30FF1F692A63B6.quest_desc: [
		"Four tabletop pieces that &aopen vanilla workstation menus&r, for a tidier workshop:"
		""
		"&6Blueprints&r (&ePaper&r and &eLight Blue Dye&r): a &bCrafting&r grid. &6Tool Box&r (&eIron Nuggets&r around a &eSmithing Table&r): a &bSmithing&r menu. &6Sewing Kit&r (&eSticks&r around a &eLoom&r): a &bLoom&r. &6Explorers Box&r (&eChest&r and &eCartography Table&r): a &bCartography Table&r."
	]
	quest.5E30FF1F692A63B6.quest_subtitle: "Workstations, but make them cute"
	quest.5E30FF1F692A63B6.title: "&6A Cosy Workshop"
	quest.5E4AE0AD23E68C2B.quest_desc: [
		"Unclaimed builds can be griefed. &6FTB Chunks&r protects them: open the &bClaim Manager&r sidebar button, then &bleft-drag&r over the map to claim and &bright-drag&r to unclaim."
		""
		"In your claims only your team and its &aallies&r can break, place or use things, and &cexplosions can't break blocks&r. Each team gets &b500&r claimed chunks and &b25&r force-loaded ones (&bShift+drag&r)."
	]
	quest.5E4AE0AD23E68C2B.quest_subtitle: "Creepers not welcome"
	quest.5E4AE0AD23E68C2B.title: "&aThis Land Is My Land"
	quest.5E5210F1E8FD0823.quest_desc: [
		"&6Integrated Dungeons and Structures&r (IDAS) adds dozens of hand-built structures made with &6Create&r, &6Quark&r and &6Supplementaries&r blocks: wizard towers, inns, farmhouses, hunters' cabins, castles and more."
		""
		"The common ones turn up all over &bforests and plains&r. Their chests are full of Create goodies like raw zinc, rose quartz, builder's tea and experience nuggets, a nice head start for the Create chapters."
		""
		"&7Supplementaries road signs point to villages and some IDAS buildings.&r"
	]
	quest.5E5210F1E8FD0823.quest_subtitle: "Inns, towers and the odd castle"
	quest.5E5210F1E8FD0823.title: "&6Integrated Adventures"
	quest.5E9D3286A134DD13.quest_desc: [
		"Craft an unattuned &eAffinity Ring&r from Mithril Scrap and a Bucket, or loot one already attuned. In the &6Arcane Anvil&r, combine it with a scroll to attune it to that spell: wear it for &b+1 level&r."
		""
		"Rings go in your &bCurios&r ring slots. Worth a look in EMI: Ring of Mana (&b+100 mana&r), Ring of Recovery (+15% cooldown reduction) and Ring of Expediency (+15% cast speed)."
	]
	quest.5E9D3286A134DD13.quest_subtitle: "+1 level to one spell"
	quest.5E9D3286A134DD13.title: "&dRing of Fire (or Ice, or...)"
	quest.5EB84B8742885001.quest_desc: [
		"Magic armor is made on the Apparatus: a vanilla armor piece in the centre and &e4 Magebloom Fiber&r on pedestals. There are three sets:"
		""
		"&6Sorceror's&r from &egold&r: lowest defence, best thread slots. &6Arcanist's&r from &eiron&r: the middle ground. &6Battlemage's&r from &ediamond&r: most defence, fewest slots."
		""
		"Every piece boosts mana regen and slowly repairs itself."
	]
	quest.5EB84B8742885001.title: "&eDress for the Job"
	quest.5EE3EBAEDBFAF099.quest_desc: [
		"Five relics come from the &6End&r. Its chests roll them, and so do many of the chests in &6Better Strongholds&r, so you might get one on the way to the portal."
		""
		"The &eChorus Staff&r lets you &ablink forward&r up to &b10-15&r blocks with a right-click. It holds a few charges that refill over time."
	]
	quest.5EE3EBAEDBFAF099.quest_subtitle: "End chests, held"
	quest.5EE3EBAEDBFAF099.title: "&5Blink and You'll Miss It"
	quest.5F13F342D9539E0D.quest_desc: [
		"A pickaxe needs a &ePick Head&r (&b2&r units of material), a &eTool Handle&r (&b1&r) and a &eTool Binding&r (&b1&r). Make all three in the &6Part Builder&r."
		""
		"Put a material in the Part Builder to see its stats and trait. &eFlint&r and &eStone&r are fine for a first pick. &aCopper is the hidden gem&r: it mines at iron tier, and its &bdwarven&r trait makes it faster the deeper you dig."
		""
		"&7Iron can't be carved. It has to be melted and cast, which comes later.&r"
	]
	quest.5F13F342D9539E0D.quest_subtitle: "Pick head, handle, binding"
	quest.5F13F342D9539E0D.title: "&eSpare Parts"
	quest.5F78BB2BB582EE29.quest_desc: [
		"The &eNetherite Lance&r takes &e3 Netherite Ingots&r, crafted in a normal crafting table (no smithing). It has by far the most durability, &b2550&r, with a solid &b5.5&r attack and a weight of &b2.2&r, a touch heavier than iron."
		""
		"&7A lance for the long campaign. Your horse will be proud.&r"
	]
	quest.5F78BB2BB582EE29.quest_subtitle: "Built to last"
	quest.5F78BB2BB582EE29.title: "&8Knight of the Nether"
	quest.5F90151BEB365929.quest_desc: [
		"Smelt Grout in a &6Furnace&r or &6Blast Furnace&r to get &eSeared Bricks&r, one for one. Four of them make a &eSeared Bricks&r block."
		""
		"Budget: the Melter takes &b9&r, the Heater &b8&r, the Casting Table and Basin &b7&r each, and &b3&r bricks make 3 Faucets."
		""
		"&7Once your Melter is running there is a cheaper way. See the casting quests.&r"
	]
	quest.5F90151BEB365929.quest_subtitle: "Baked to perfection"
	quest.5F90151BEB365929.title: "&eBrick by Brick"
	quest.5F9444599B2C12FF.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Steam Whistle&r is a &eGolden Sheet&r over a &eCopper Ingot&r. Glue one onto your train before assembly, then press &bSprint&r while driving to sound it."
		""
		"&7On a heated tank it plays when powered; stack more whistles onto it for a deeper note.&r"
	]
	quest.5F9444599B2C12FF.quest_subtitle: "Choo choo!"
	quest.5F9444599B2C12FF.title: "&eWhistle Stop"
	quest.5FBA5B6C0A9668E0.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a &6Tea Kettle&r from &e4 Iron Ingots&r and &e2 Sticks&r (or Copper Ingots for the copper look; they work the same). Put it on your &6Stove&r and right-click it."
		""
		"&bWater:&r a water bottle adds &b25%&r, a water bucket &b50%&r. &cAny potion in the water slot counts as water and is used up&r, so keep real potions out of it."
		""
		"&bHeat:&r on a stove the kettle holds at least &b30%&r. &eBlaze Powder&r (from Nether blaze rods) in the heat slot adds &b35%&r and is used automatically whenever heat drops below &b70%&r, so leave a few in there while you brew. &7It keeps using powder even when idle, so take it out when you're done.&r"
		""
		"Most brews also need a &eGlass Bottle&r in an ingredient slot, and each one takes only a few seconds."
	]
	quest.5FBA5B6C0A9668E0.quest_subtitle: "The heart of every brew"
	quest.5FBA5B6C0A9668E0.title: "&6Put the Kettle On"
	quest.5FBFFFD99652C4B2.quest_desc: [
		"A &ePrecision Mechanism&r on top of &eBrass Casing&r makes a &6Rotation Speed Controller&r. Feed it rotation, put a &6Large Cogwheel&r on top, and set the output on its panel anywhere from &b-256 to 256 RPM&r."
		""
		"It adds no stress of its own, but &cit can't create power&r: the network still needs enough SU for the speed you ask for. &aGreat for running crushers at a full 256 RPM&r or calming a belt down."
	]
	quest.5FBFFFD99652C4B2.quest_subtitle: "Exactly 256, please"
	quest.5FBFFFD99652C4B2.title: "&eCruise Control"
	quest.5FDE4BF3F675A005.quest_desc: [
		"Melt &eIron&r, put your Pick Head Sand Cast on the Casting Table and pour. A pick head takes &b2 ingots&r (180 mB) of metal. A handle or binding takes 1."
		""
		"Build a new pickaxe around the iron head. Iron's &bmagnetic&r trait pulls nearby drops toward you when you hit things, and the head has much more durability than stone."
		""
		"&aAny meltable metal works the same way&r: copper, gold, and every alloy you make later."
	]
	quest.5FDE4BF3F675A005.quest_subtitle: "Iron, at last"
	quest.5FDE4BF3F675A005.title: "&eHeavy Metal"
	quest.60221F3A27F75DFA.quest_desc: [
		"&6Create: Copycats+&r adds dozens of copycat shapes: slopes, boards, bytes, layers, catwalks, doors and more. Most are cut from &eZinc Ingots&r in a &6Stonecutter&r (one ingot makes 2 Slopes or 8 Boards); a few, like Catwalks, are crafted from Boards."
		""
		"Right-click a copycat with a block to &askin it&r, and click again to rotate. A &bWrench&r takes the material back. &bShift-right-click with an empty hand&r toggles connected textures. Hold &bLeft Alt&r to fill every part of a multi-part copycat at once."
	]
	quest.60221F3A27F75DFA.quest_subtitle: "Copycats+"
	quest.60221F3A27F75DFA.title: "&aCopy Cat"
	quest.6060D7B7A76DA4C3.quest_desc: [
		"Five relics come from the Nether, but you don't have to go there: &6ruined portal&r chests, &aeven in the Overworld&r, count as Nether loot. Fortresses roll them too."
		""
		"The &eReflective Necklace&r sometimes &dstores part of the damage you take&r in orbs. Your next attacks fire those orbs back at the target."
		""
		"&7The Nether trip itself is covered in the &6Kitted Out&7 chapter.&r"
	]
	quest.6060D7B7A76DA4C3.quest_subtitle: "Ruined portals are secretly Nether chests"
	quest.6060D7B7A76DA4C3.title: "&cReturn to Sender"
	quest.607A27E5666C1B29.quest_desc: [
		"Flowers fill pools slowly. For heavy loads, build machines."
		""
		"The &6Astral Font&r (&e4 Astralite Ingots&r, &e3 Fluxite&r, &e1 Glass&r) needs only open sky: &b75 ƒ/s&r by day, &b150 ƒ/s&r at night, halved in rain, halved again in thunder. &cAnything solid above it stops it.&r"
		""
		"The &6Fluxia Dynamo&r burns any furnace fuel dropped on top at &b300 ƒ/s&r. An Amethyst Coal runs it for 160 seconds."
		""
		"&7A bank of fonts plus a dynamo for bad weather is a classic setup.&r"
	]
	quest.607A27E5666C1B29.quest_subtitle: "Astral Font and Fluxia Dynamo"
	quest.607A27E5666C1B29.title: "&9Beyond Flowers"
	quest.607E6BD2599A4F91.quest_desc: [
		"In this pack a block's physics stats (&bmass&r, Light or Heavy, Bouncy, Airtight...) only show in its tooltip &awhile you wear goggles&r. Goggles also read out propeller thrust, balloon volume and lift."
		""
		"&6Engineer's Goggles&r do the job. Craft them with any &eLeather&r for &eAviator's Goggles&r: same readouts, far more swagger."
		""
		"&7Scarf sold separately.&r"
	]
	quest.607E6BD2599A4F91.quest_subtitle: "Goggles, but make it Biggles"
	quest.607E6BD2599A4F91.title: "&eAviator Chic"
	quest.6083AC563682B8E2.quest_desc: [
		"&aPrime a pact&r by throwing it into a pool with a &eGhast Tear&r (&b5,000 ƒ&r). Then right-click a willing creature with the &ePrimed Soul Pact&r to bind it."
		""
		"Only four answer: &6Allay&r, &6Axolotl&r, &6Frog&r or &6Bat&r. Anything else refuses, unharmed, and the pact isn't spent."
		""
		"&7Frogs and bats live in the Willow Fen and axolotls in lush caves. Allays sit caged at pillager outposts, or the Starlight Cross rite at tier III summons one.&r"
	]
	quest.6083AC563682B8E2.quest_subtitle: "Allay, Axolotl, Frog or Bat"
	quest.6083AC563682B8E2.title: "&dWho Answers?"
	quest.60A85FB2FCEDEB20.quest_desc: [
		"&6Bastion&r chests roll the &ePiglin Mask&r almost half the time they roll a relic. With it on, &apiglins won't attack first&r, and bartering gives more per gold ingot."
		""
		"From relic level 5, kills drop &eGolden Teeth&r: three make a gold ingot, and piglins love them."
		""
		"&cA bastion is still a dangerous place&r, mask or not. Bring blocks and food."
	]
	quest.60A85FB2FCEDEB20.quest_subtitle: "Bastion chests, head slot"
	quest.60A85FB2FCEDEB20.title: "&6Pig in Disguise"
	quest.60B47FE03789CCE7.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Jam Pot&r (slabs and an iron ingot) has no menu. Set it on a stove or campfire and right-click in &efruit and sugar&r."
		""
		"When it bubbles up, &astir with an empty hand&r, then &abottle it with empty Jars&r. Too early and it's runny, too late it caramelizes, far too late it burns. &bPerfect jam&r gives an extra piece when you decorate with it."
		""
		"&7Sneak-right-click with an empty hand to tip out a ruined batch.&r"
	]
	quest.60B47FE03789CCE7.quest_subtitle: "Watch the pot"
	quest.60B47FE03789CCE7.title: "&dJam Session"
	quest.60B6FE857C713E11.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a &6Jug&r from &e7 Glass Panes&r and &bsneak + right-click&r to place it. Right-click it with up to &b3 drinks&r to pour them in."
		""
		"Right-click with an &aempty hand&r to drink everything at once. You get every effect, but only for &b45 seconds&r."
		""
		"&7In hand it also works as a one-time glass club. Use it wisely.&r"
	]
	quest.60B6FE857C713E11.quest_subtitle: "Three drinks, one gulp"
	quest.60B6FE857C713E11.title: "&bOne for the Road"
	quest.60E84C7CD71ACC8A.quest_desc: [
		"Have all &bseven&r brew effects at once: &aBalanced, Tough, Fortune, Feral, Lifeleech, Bonding and Deeprush&r."
		""
		"Line up the cups in your hotbar and drink them back to back; each lasts &b1:30&r. A &6Jug&r saves sips: fill it with three, drink the other four cups first, then the Jug, whose effects last only &b45 seconds&r."
		""
		"The mod rewards you with &dMiss Lilitu's special Mixture&r, a potion packed with buffs."
	]
	quest.60E84C7CD71ACC8A.quest_subtitle: "Seven buffs, one breath"
	quest.60E84C7CD71ACC8A.title: "&dA Sip of Infinity"
	quest.61074AEF7E9F7FEC.quest_desc: [
		"Some End Cities have an &6End Ship&r docked beside them, and on its deck an item frame holds a pair of &eElytra&r. Thanks to &6Lootr&r, that frame is &aper-player&r: everyone on the server can take their own wings from the same ship."
		""
		"Wear them in the &bback slot&r (see &6First Light&r), jump off something high and glide. &aFirework rockets&r give you a boost in flight."
		""
		"You've been to the bottom of the sea, the heart of the Nether and the end of the world. &aThe whole map is yours now.&r"
	]
	quest.61074AEF7E9F7FEC.quest_subtitle: "The unknown, seen from above"
	quest.61074AEF7E9F7FEC.title: "&6Into the Wild Blue Yonder"
	quest.614F17F343084D1C.quest_desc: [
		"&6Better Jungle Temples&r turns the tiny vanilla temple into a trap-filled ruin with challenge rooms, a pit and a &etreasure room&r (gold, emeralds and diamonds). Find it in &bjungles&r."
		""
		"Bring a &eBrush&r: suspicious gravel inside hides emeralds. &7Some explorer got here before you. Their old campsite might have a saddle.&r"
	]
	quest.614F17F343084D1C.quest_subtitle: "Mind the tripwires"
	quest.614F17F343084D1C.title: "&2Temple of Doom-ish"
	quest.6195D430B59CF369.quest_desc: [
		"&eWhite Chalk&r is &e1 White Concrete Powder&r over &e3 Water Bottles&r. Add one vanilla dye for each of the other &b15 colours&r. Rites tell all 16 apart, so light grey is not grey."
		""
		"&aRight-click the top of a block&r to draw a &dBase&r glyph. Click it again to cycle &bBase → Runes → Star → Triad → Serpent → Eclipse → Hex&r, and sneak-click to step back. Each draw and each click costs &b1&r of the chalk's &b128&r uses."
		""
		"&cGlyphs must sit at the altar's own height&r, and circles don't rotate: a lopsided circle drawn sideways never matches."
	]
	quest.6195D430B59CF369.quest_subtitle: "Base, Runes, Star, Triad, Serpent, Eclipse, Hex"
	quest.6195D430B59CF369.title: "&fChalk It Up"
	quest.61A8AAB532E55BCF.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a &6Sand Bucket&r from &e5 Dried Kelp&r around a &eWooden Shovel&r and right-click sand to fill it. Right-click the ground with the full bucket to build a &eSandcastle&r, then use more full buckets on it to add towers."
		""
		"&aPour a Water Bottle on it&r to harden it. &cZombies love knocking sandcastles down&r and will seek them out from about 16 blocks away."
		""
		"&7Sneak while placing to set the bucket itself down as decoration.&r"
	]
	quest.61A8AAB532E55BCF.quest_subtitle: "Slip into the sea, eventually"
	quest.61A8AAB532E55BCF.title: "&eCastles Made of Sand"
	quest.61B360894EE46B27.quest_desc: [
		"Backpack upgrades start on a backpack &eUpgrade Base&r (iron, leather, string). A &ePickup Upgrade&r (string, redstone, sticky piston) grabs items you walk over; add &eEnder Pearls&r, lapis, iron and redstone for the &eMagnet Upgrade&r, which pulls items from &b3 blocks&r away (&b5&r for the advanced one)."
		""
		"More favourites: &eFeeding&r (eats when you're hungry), &eRestock&r / &eDeposit&r (hold the backpack and sneak + right-click a chest to fill the backpack from it, or empty it into the chest), &eTool Swapper&r and &eCrafting&r. &bAlt+Z&r / &bAlt+X&r toggle the first two upgrades."
	]
	quest.61B360894EE46B27.quest_subtitle: "Everything comes to you"
	quest.61B360894EE46B27.title: "&6Sticky Fingers"
	quest.61DB6FB239E8C5FF.quest_desc: [
		"Combine an &eEnder Pearl&r with &eBlaze Powder&r to make an &eEye of Ender&r. Throw one and it flies toward the nearest &6Stronghold&r; each throw has a &b20%&r chance to shatter."
		""
		"Make plenty. In this pack each portal frame block has only a &b10%&r chance to already hold an eye, so you'll need nearly a full set of &b12&r to light the portal, and the frames have to be &5stabilized&r first."
		""
		"&7Strongholds sit in a ring roughly 1,300 to 2,800 blocks from the world centre.&r"
	]
	quest.61DB6FB239E8C5FF.quest_subtitle: "Follow the bouncing eyeball"
	quest.61DB6FB239E8C5FF.title: "&aEye Spy"
	quest.61EE5EFF62C3F5B0.quest_desc: [
		"Illagers have taken to the sea. The &6Illager Corsair&r and the &6Illager Galley&r sail the &boceans&r; either one counts. Campsite maps sometimes point to a Corsair."
		""
		"Expect pillagers and vindicator spawners on deck (and the odd &cEvoker&r on the Corsair). Below deck: quartz, diamonds, emeralds and enchanted iron gear."
		""
		"&7Come alongside in a boat and climb up the hull. A fall into deep water is the safest kind of fall.&r"
	]
	quest.61EE5EFF62C3F5B0.quest_subtitle: "Raids, now with sails"
	quest.61EE5EFF62C3F5B0.title: "&3Pillagers of the Caribbean"
	quest.620558C528F79588.quest_desc: [
		"A normal key's password is just its name, so anyone with an anvil can forge it. The &6Heavy Key&r fixes that: craft a &6Key&r with a piece of &eNetherite Scrap&r."
		""
		"When crafted it gets a &brandom, secret password&r. Renaming another key won't match it, so it's the &aonly real lock&r on a server. It works on Safes, Netherite Doors and Lock Blocks like any key."
		""
		"&cLose it and the lock is gone for good.&r Keep it in your belt slot."
	]
	quest.620558C528F79588.quest_subtitle: "No locksmith can copy this one"
	quest.620558C528F79588.title: "&8Heavy Is the Key"
	quest.622FFF275F002BD3.quest_desc: [
		"A &eRing of Potential&r (8 Iron Nuggets + a Source Gem) is the base for magic rings. Upgrade it on the Apparatus with Diamonds, Ender Pearls and Source Gems into a &eRing of Lesser Discount&r: &b-10 mana per cast&r. A Greater ring makes it -20."
		""
		"Rings, belts and amulets go in your &bCurios&r slots. &7Also worth it: the Amulet of Mana Boost (+50 max mana) and Amulet of Mana Regen, both built on a Dull Trinket.&r"
	]
	quest.622FFF275F002BD3.quest_subtitle: "Every cast, now on sale"
	quest.622FFF275F002BD3.title: "&eBargain Bling"
	quest.6236B97DF8D5BD75.quest_desc: [
		"The &eSpectral Pumpkin Pie&r is the best sanity food: &b+10&r sanity and a proper meal on top."
		""
		"Mix a &eSpectral Pumpkin&r, &eSugar&r and an &eEgg&r. Spectral Pumpkins sit in piles all over the biome; the glowing ones in each pile are Spectral Jack o'Lanterns."
	]
	quest.6236B97DF8D5BD75.quest_subtitle: "+10 sanity, extra whipped dread"
	quest.6236B97DF8D5BD75.title: "&ePie of Sound Mind"
	quest.624AEA10EE451435.quest_desc: [
		"&6MmmMmmMmmMmm&r adds the &6Target Dummy&r: a &eHay Bale&r on top of an &eArmor Stand&r. Hit it to see floating &bdamage numbers&r and a live &bDPS&r readout."
		""
		"Your weapon takes &ano durability damage&r on the dummy, so test builds freely."
		""
		"&aTip:&r put a &epumpkin&r on its head and it becomes a &6scarecrow&r that keeps animals out of a &b12-block&r radius. Handy next to a field."
	]
	quest.624AEA10EE451435.quest_subtitle: "It never fights back"
	quest.624AEA10EE451435.title: "Punching Bag"
	quest.62513AF3EA07FB9F.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Simple Coal Generator&r (Ferricore, Redstone, Coal and a Blast Furnace) burns any furnace fuel into FE and pushes it into the blocks touching it."
		""
		"Plain coal gives &b24,000 FE&r at 60 FE/t. Each JDT coal tier gives more in total and &adoubles the rate&r: Primal Coal is 72,000 FE at 120 FE/t."
		""
		"You'll need FE for Celestigem gear and every advanced machine later on."
	]
	quest.62513AF3EA07FB9F.quest_subtitle: "Fuel in, FE out"
	quest.62513AF3EA07FB9F.title: "&6Burn Notice"
	quest.626C47FA8E8B3ED5.quest_desc: [
		"&eFlux Cores&r (flux dust, Eye of Ender, obsidian) and more dust make a &eFlux Block&r, then a &6Flux Plug&r (block and core) and a &6Flux Point&r (core and redstone block)."
		""
		"Right-click a device, open the &bCreate New Network&r tab (name, colour, security), then select that network on every device. Put the &6Plug&r against your generator furnace's &bOutput&r side; the &6Point&r pushes power into a machine. No cables, any distance, even across dimensions."
		""
		"&cFlux moves power, it doesn't make it.&r"
	]
	quest.626C47FA8E8B3ED5.title: "&6Plug and Play"
	quest.62A0D3C726A24847.quest_desc: [
		"Two small stops from the &bplains and meadows&r. The &6Wishing Well&r holds a lingering cloud with one random effect: &aSpeed II, Regeneration, Resistance or Haste&r... or &cWither&r. &cYou can't tell which from the outside&r, but the Wither only lasts 10 seconds."
		""
		"The &6Bathhouse&r (plains, taigas, savannas and snowy biomes) is full of barrels of food, with a rare oddly named drink. Some have a &ahot tub&r that gives &bRegeneration II and Resistance II&r. Spawners of skeletons and husks guard it."
	]
	quest.62A0D3C726A24847.quest_subtitle: "Toss a coin, then take a soak"
	quest.62A0D3C726A24847.title: "&bWishes and Washes"
	quest.62A42BCE33B7057E.quest_desc: [
		"The Summit asks for a full set of &9Rare&r or better and a dead &cWither&r. You have to be credited with the kill, so get your hits in at the end."
		""
		"Up here monsters gain heavy armor, armor pierce and &b10%&r damage reduction. The payoff: &5Epic&r becomes the most common rarity, gems roll purer, and your enchanting cap rises to &b75&r."
		""
		"&aTip:&r a &6Simple Reforging Table&r rolls any item up to Rare. That's the reliable way to finish the set."
	]
	quest.62A42BCE33B7057E.quest_subtitle: "World Tier: Summit"
	quest.62A42BCE33B7057E.title: "&9Reach the Summit"
	quest.62B777855CE8A7C7.quest_desc: [
		"&6Asterism Arcanum&r adds a tenth school, &dAstral&r: starlight spells built around keeping your distance."
		""
		"Its home is the &6Astral Observatory&r on high mountains, peaks and meadows. The &6Astromancer&r there is a &aneutral&r merchant with astral scrolls and ink deals; the same chest rule applies. &cDragonflies&r nest inside and attack intruders."
		""
		"&7Watch for Lunar Moths fluttering around the frozen, jagged and stony peaks.&r"
	]
	quest.62B777855CE8A7C7.quest_subtitle: "Asterism Arcanum"
	quest.62B777855CE8A7C7.title: "&9Stargazing"
	quest.62D213E0B3AF5769.quest_desc: [
		"&6Arcane Essence Block&r adds storage for Iron's materials. &aNine Arcane Essence&r make an &eEssence Sack&r, and it unpacks back into nine."
		""
		"Nine &eArcane Ingots&r likewise make an &eArcane Ingot Block&r, and that one comes apart again too."
		""
		"&cCareful:&r smelting a sack turns it into an &eArcane Essence Block&r, which is pure decoration. There is &cno recipe back&r, so keep sacks out of furnaces."
	]
	quest.62D213E0B3AF5769.quest_subtitle: "Arcane Essence Block"
	quest.62D213E0B3AF5769.title: "&6Bag of Tricks"
	quest.630CAF9719FF49E7.quest_desc: [
		"Craft the &6Willow Altar&r from &e3 Amethyst Shards&r and &e4 Willow Planks&r. Every rite is cast here: draw the circle around it, drop the reagents inside, then &aright-click the altar&r."
		""
		"It holds &b20,000 ƒ&r but &cmakes none of its own&r, so it must be fed through a link."
		""
		"Once a second it reads the ground. &bGhost glyphs&r mark missing chalk, &cred sparks&r mark wrong shapes or colours, and the reagents it still wants orbit above it. &aFluxia and reagents are only spent when a cast succeeds.&r"
	]
	quest.630CAF9719FF49E7.quest_subtitle: "Where every circle begins"
	quest.630CAF9719FF49E7.title: "&5The Willow Altar"
	quest.632F5292910D7C95.quest_desc: [
		"Four Iron Sheets around Netherrack make an &6Empty Blaze Burner&r. Take it to the Nether and &bright-click a Blaze&r (or a Blaze spawner) with it to trap one inside. Blazes haunt Nether Fortresses; this pack uses &6YUNG's Better Nether Fortresses&r."
		""
		"Place it &bdirectly under a Basin&r and feed it any furnace fuel to make the basin &bHeated&r. An unfed burner just idles and doesn't count."
		""
		"&7Blaze Cakes and superheating come in the next Create chapter. Have some fuel for now.&r"
	]
	quest.632F5292910D7C95.quest_subtitle: "Contains one (1) Blaze"
	quest.632F5292910D7C95.title: "&cSentient Fireplace"
	quest.638ABEB2AA2C384E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Apothic Attributes&r adds the stats affix gear rolls: crit chance and damage, life steal, armor pierce, dodge, draw speed, mining speed and more."
		""
		"Click the &bsword button&r at the top-right of your inventory to see them all. Hover a stat for its base value and modifiers."
		""
		"&7Armor works a little differently here: high armor has diminishing returns, and Toughness now resists armor pierce. Crit chance over 100% can crit twice.&r"
	]
	quest.638ABEB2AA2C384E.quest_subtitle: "Apothic Attributes"
	quest.638ABEB2AA2C384E.title: "&bKnow Your Numbers"
	quest.63A8363BEA0A9754.quest_desc: [
		"Upgrades go into the extracting end's GUI, and each tier adds a feature:"
		"&eBasic&r: redstone modes. &eImproved&r (+gold): distribution - nearest first, furthest first, round robin, random. &eAdvanced&r (+diamond): &bfilters&r. &eUltimate&r (+netherite): pure speed."
		""
		"Speed climbs from &b4 items a second&r with no upgrade to &b64 items every tick&r with Ultimate."
	]
	quest.63A8363BEA0A9754.title: "&6Faster, Smarter Pipes"
	quest.63EA9FE30C1E8766.quest_desc: [
		"Upgrade your Novice book into the &5Mage's Spell Book&r: Novice Spell Book, an &eObsidian&r, 3 &eDiamonds&r, 2 &eBlocks of Quartz&r and 2 &eBlaze Rods&r. &cThe Blaze Rods mean a trip to the Nether.&r"
		""
		"Your spells carry over, your mana pool grows and you can now cast &dTier II&r glyphs. Think Heal, Explosion, Luck (Fortune), Smelt and Accelerate."
		""
		"&7Spell books can be dyed any colour in a crafting grid.&r"
	]
	quest.63EA9FE30C1E8766.quest_subtitle: "Tier II, now with fire"
	quest.63EA9FE30C1E8766.title: "&5Second Edition"
	quest.6414BF56FDC7209C.quest_desc: [
		"The &cWilden&r are Ars' hostile mobs. &cHunters&r drop &eWilden Horns&r, &cStalkers&r drop &eWilden Wings&r and &cDefenders&r drop &eWilden Spikes&r. You need them for Air and Conjuration Essence, Drygmys, several glyphs and the Flight ritual."
		""
		"They roam around &bWilden Dens&r in forests and taigas, mostly at night. The reliable route is the &dSummon Wilden&r ritual: its &aalternate tablet&r (Vexing log, Emerald Block, Iron Sword, Bow, Lapis Block) needs no Wilden drops."
	]
	quest.6414BF56FDC7209C.quest_subtitle: "Horns, spikes and wings"
	quest.6414BF56FDC7209C.title: "&cWhere the Wild Things Are"
	quest.642E99DCCEF3DAC8.quest_desc: [
		"&eSuper Glue&r (Slimeballs, an Iron Sheet and an Iron Nugget) marks which blocks move together. &bClick two corners&r to glue the box between them; punch a glued area while holding glue to remove it."
		""
		"Glued blocks must touch each other. Glue is the first step to every &6contraption&r: blocks that move as one."
		""
		"&7Spare slime for the next pot.&r"
	]
	quest.642E99DCCEF3DAC8.quest_subtitle: "Sticky situations"
	quest.642E99DCCEF3DAC8.title: "&eArea of Connect"
	quest.6462054B9B70B50C.quest_desc: [
		"&6Lili's Lucky Lures&r makes the water more interesting. Every few minutes, &bFloating Debris&r, &bFloating Books&r and &bFish Pools&r drift up near players."
		""
		"The &eBamboo Fishing Rod&r is the cheap way in: &eBamboo&r and &eString&r. It only has half a vanilla rod's durability, but any rod works for everything in this branch."
	]
	quest.6462054B9B70B50C.quest_subtitle: "Lili's Lucky Lures"
	quest.6462054B9B70B50C.title: "&9Gone Fishing"
	quest.6495FF4551691401.quest_desc: [
		"Put a &6Seared Faucet&r on the side of the Melter and a &6Casting Table&r or &6Casting Basin&r under it (7 bricks each). Melt something, then &bright-click the faucet&r to pour."
		""
		"The &6Table&r casts ingots, nuggets and tool parts. The &6Basin&r casts whole blocks. A &blever on the faucet&r pours nonstop, and a redstone pulse pours until one side is full or empty."
		""
		"&aMelting beats smelting:&r one raw ore gives &b12 nuggets&r (1 1/3 ingots), and a silk-touched ore block counts double."
	]
	quest.6495FF4551691401.quest_subtitle: "Right-click to pour"
	quest.6495FF4551691401.title: "&6Tap Dance"
	quest.649662BD1311F0EA.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Tea Kettle&r only heats up when it sits on a stove. Craft the &6Stove&r from &e3 Iron Nuggets&r, &e5 Cobblestone&r (or blackstone or cobbled deepslate) and a &eCampfire&r."
		""
		"It also works as a &bSmoker&r. The kettle only cares that it sits on a stove block, so it doesn't need fuel."
		""
		"&7Already own a Farm \\& Charm, Candlelight or Meadow stove? Those heat a kettle too.&r &cA lit stove burns anyone standing on it.&r"
	]
	quest.649662BD1311F0EA.quest_subtitle: "Mind your toes"
	quest.649662BD1311F0EA.title: "&6A Warm Start"
	quest.649AA99BD7FBE162.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Portable Engine&r is your on-board power plant: an &eIron Sheet&r over an &eEngine Assembly&r over a &eBlast Furnace&r. The assembly is a sequenced assembly on an Iron Sheet (&6Saw&r then &6Press&r, &b8 loops&r, about half succeed)."
		""
		"Feed it any &efurnace fuel&r by hand or by automation. It turns at &b32 RPM&r (about &b2048 SU&r) and a &eBlaze Cake&r superheats it to &b64 RPM&r."
		""
		"&7Craft it with a dye to repaint it. Sadly, the red ones don't go any faster.&r"
	]
	quest.649AA99BD7FBE162.quest_subtitle: "Steamless, not powerless"
	quest.649AA99BD7FBE162.title: "&6Engine Room"
	quest.64AE7877700E10F8.quest_desc: [
		"&6Camping&r is all about trips away from home. A &6Tent&r is wool and sticks, and a &6Sleeping Bag&r is three wool. Both come in all 16 colours."
		""
		"Sleep in the bag to skip the night, with a short burst of &bRegeneration&r as you lie down. &aIt does not move your spawn point&r, so you can camp anywhere and still respawn at home. The tent is a cosy 2x2 decoration around it. &cWith mob griefing on, monsters that walk into a tent wreck it.&r"
		""
		"&7Also handy: a Walking Stick (3 sticks) for a little extra speed, and a Multitool to rotate blocks.&r"
	]
	quest.64AE7877700E10F8.quest_subtitle: "Camping, at last"
	quest.64AE7877700E10F8.title: "&2Pitch Perfect"
	quest.64B77DDE8456BCEE.quest_desc: [
		"Craft an &6Enchanting Table&r from a &eBook&r, &e2 Diamonds&r and &e4 Obsidian&r, then enchant anything with &eLapis Lazuli&r."
		""
		"&6Apothic Enchanting&r reworks the table: instead of plain levels it shows three stats, &dEterna&r, &dQuanta&r and &dArcana&r. Bookshelves still raise them, and special shelves push far past vanilla."
		""
		"&7The &6Apotheosis&7 chapter explains the stats and the shelves in depth.&r"
	]
	quest.64B77DDE8456BCEE.quest_subtitle: "Some assembly (and lapis) required"
	quest.64B77DDE8456BCEE.title: "&dThe Enchanter's Desk"
	quest.64D46A6A5087692D.quest_desc: [
		"&eTomatoes climb&r: on their own they stay short, but with &eRope&r hanging just above the bed they climb &btwice as high&r. Craft &eBarley&r and &eString&r into &b6 rope&r."
		""
		"Rope needs something to hang from, such as a fence or a solid block. Run it down over the tomato seeds and let the vine find its way up."
		""
		"&7Brewery's hops climb rope too; see the Cellar chapter.&r"
	]
	quest.64D46A6A5087692D.quest_subtitle: "Tomatoes are social climbers"
	quest.64D46A6A5087692D.title: "&aLearning the Ropes"
	quest.64EDABE9B7C6CC14.quest_desc: [
		"Kill a &cWarden&r for a &eWarden Tendril&r, then combine it with an Echoing or Soul-Touched Deepshelf, 4 Sculk and a &eSculk Catalyst&r (both need Silk Touch)."
		""
		"&6Sculkshelves&r give &b10 Eterna&r up to &b80&r, plus Quanta, Arcana and an extra clue. Summit caps you at 75, so their last 5 levels only count at Pinnacle."
		""
		"&aTip:&r infuse one Echo Shard at &b70 Eterna, 50%+ Quanta and 50%+ Arcana&r to get four."
	]
	quest.64EDABE9B7C6CC14.quest_subtitle: "Sculkshelves"
	quest.64EDABE9B7C6CC14.title: "&3Whispers of the Warden"
	quest.64FB0A76FDF6C3D1.quest_desc: [
		"&eNether Cobalt Ore&r appears in netherrack all over the Nether, with the biggest veins between &bY 8 and 32&r. Look for its blue tint in walls and ceilings."
		""
		"&cYou need a diamond-tier pickaxe.&r A slimesteel head works, or put the &eDiamond&r modifier on any tool. Melt raw cobalt in a lava-fuelled melter or smeltery, or blast it into ingots."
		""
		"Cobalt heads are &blightweight&r: they swing and dig faster."
	]
	quest.64FB0A76FDF6C3D1.quest_subtitle: "Deep in the Nether walls"
	quest.64FB0A76FDF6C3D1.title: "&9Cobalt Blue"
	quest.64FFA8E2B31B15BF.quest_desc: [
		"The dark machine. The &6Fluid Void&r is &e4 Dark gems&r, Kivi, iron bars, a &eBucket&r and a &6Machine Base&r."
		""
		"It &astops fluids flowing into the six blocks touching it&r and deletes any fluid already sitting in them. Right-click it with a full bucket to empty the bucket. A row of them holds back water for a doorway or a mine shaft, or tidies up a lava mistake."
	]
	quest.64FFA8E2B31B15BF.quest_subtitle: "Where does it go? Nobody asks"
	quest.64FFA8E2B31B15BF.title: "&8Down the Drain"
	quest.650D8130E1C64907.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Aviary&r is the toughest build in &6When Dungeons Arise&r. It only appears on the &bEnd's outer islands&r (End highlands and midlands), so you need the dragon dead and the gateway open (see &6Into the Unknown&r). Only about one big End find in four is an Aviary."
		""
		"&cPhantoms spawn all over it.&r Skeletons in &cnetherite armour&r with Power bows and Fire Aspect swords hold the halls, and &cEnd Crystals&r are built into the structure: &cthey explode&r when hit, so mind your shots."
		""
		"Your reward: &enetherite ingots&r, piles of diamonds, enchanted diamond gear, &eEnchanted Golden Apples&r and, with luck, a &eTotem&r in the barrels. &aYou've raided the best Dungeons Arise has to offer.&r"
	]
	quest.650D8130E1C64907.quest_subtitle: "Where the phantoms go to nest"
	quest.650D8130E1C64907.title: "&5The Last Roost"
	quest.651F577DA771B6AA.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Simple Reforging Table&r rerolls &aany&r valid gear, affixed or not, into a fresh affix item, up to &9Rare&r. Item in the middle, rarity material top-left, &dSigils of Rebirth&r bottom-right."
		""
		"You get three choices. Each costs levels, materials and sigils: Uncommon starts at &b5 levels&r, 2 Fabric and 1 sigil; Rare at &b15&r, 2 Shards and 2 sigils. The 2nd and 3rd choices need 2x and 3x the levels and materials, but each choice only spends 1, 2 or 3 levels' worth of XP."
		""
		"&aThis is how you build the full sets the World Tiers ask for.&r"
	]
	quest.651F577DA771B6AA.quest_subtitle: "Reforging"
	quest.651F577DA771B6AA.title: "&aForged Anew"
	quest.653DBFECE3170782.quest_desc: [
		"&eGlass&r with a &eWooden Slab&r for a lid makes a &6Jar&r. It holds:"
		"&a- &rup to &b12 bottles&r of any liquid: water, lava, honey, milk, soups, potions, XP and more (fill and empty with bottles, bowls and buckets)"
		"&a- &rup to 12 cookies"
		"&a- &ra &bsmall mob&r: click a Bee, Slime, Magma Cube, Frog, Allay or baby Rabbit with an empty jar"
		""
		"&7You can't drink straight out of a jar in this pack. Craft a Jar with any boat for a ship in a bottle.&r"
	]
	quest.653DBFECE3170782.quest_subtitle: "Put a bee in it"
	quest.653DBFECE3170782.title: "&bJar Jar Things"
	quest.6544A91C97532FAC.quest_desc: [
		"&6Drygmys&r are rare, shy creatures that tend animals. &aThrow a Wilden Horn&r near a wild one to get a &eDrygmy Token&r, then use the finished charm on &eMossy Cobblestone&r to make a &6Drygmy Henge&r."
		""
		"It collects mob drops and XP from creatures within &b10 blocks&r &awithout killing them&r. More mobs and more species means more loot. Containment Jars count, so a row of jarred mobs works great. It needs a &echest&r and a &6Source Jar&r next to the henge."
	]
	quest.6544A91C97532FAC.title: "&aMoose Dance"
	quest.656678C8229897A2.quest_desc: [
		"Time to brew. &aRight-click the kettle with a &eWater Bucket&r, feed the &6Oven&r any fuel, add &e2 Hops&r and &eYeast&r to the kettle, then press the &6Timer&r. A brew takes &b60 seconds&r."
		""
		"Every few seconds something goes wrong. &bOverflowing kettle:&r take water out with an empty bucket. &bWeak heat:&r add fuel. &bRinging timer:&r press it. &bSteaming whistle:&r top up with a water bucket."
		""
		"Fix &b4 or more&r without missing one for top quality. Ignore them and you get weak beer. &cMiss more than half, or leave the kettle overflowing, and angry Booze elementals pop out&r."
		""
		"Collect beer with &eBeer Mugs&r (8 from planks). &7Try Barley Beer (villagers give discounts) and Oat Beer (Haste that grows the deeper you mine).&r"
	]
	quest.656678C8229897A2.quest_subtitle: "Sixty seconds of panic"
	quest.656678C8229897A2.title: "&6Hopstacle Course"
	quest.659B5A4C3DBBD663.quest_desc: [
		"&e4 Ash&r, a &ePorkchop&r and a &eWater Bucket&r make &e6 Soap&r. Ash falls where fire burns blocks, drops from mobs that burn to death and turns up in urns."
		""
		"Soap &aundoes things&r: it strips dye from wool, terracotta and leather, scrubs &bwax and oxidation&r off copper in one click, turns sticky pistons back into pistons, tipped arrows into arrows, filled maps into blank maps, and Quark's dirty glass into clear glass."
		""
		"&cDo not eat the soap.&r &7(There's an advancement for it.)&r"
	]
	quest.659B5A4C3DBBD663.quest_subtitle: "Undo button in a bar"
	quest.659B5A4C3DBBD663.title: "&bSqueaky Clean"
	quest.659FCE7D0B8E9CD7.quest_desc: [
		"Light a &eSoul Campfire&r in front of a fan and the air turns ghostly. &eSand&r becomes &eSoul Sand&r, so after one trip to the Nether the soul fire pays for itself."
		""
		"Other tricks: Cobblestone to Blackstone, Ink Sacs to Glow Ink Sacs, Torches to Soul Torches."
		""
		"&cCareful: haunting Stone or Stone Bricks makes infested blocks full of Silverfish.&r"
	]
	quest.659FCE7D0B8E9CD7.quest_subtitle: "Soul campfire not included"
	quest.659FCE7D0B8E9CD7.title: "&dSpooky Scary Airflow"
	quest.65B04B5E77249C49.quest_desc: [
		"An &eEmpty Upgrade Orb&r takes &e4 Arcane Ingots&r, &e4 Cinder Essence&r and a &eMithril Ingot&r. Arcane Ingots are &e8 essence&r around an iron, copper or gold ingot."
		""
		"Fill it with &e8 runes&r: a school rune gives &b+5%&r power in that school, Arcane Runes make a &bMana Orb&r (+50 max mana), and Recovery or Protective runes cut cooldowns or harden you against spells."
		""
		"Apply orbs in the &6Arcane Anvil&r to spell books, armor and staffs, up to &b3 per item&r."
	]
	quest.65B04B5E77249C49.quest_subtitle: "Three upgrades per item"
	quest.65B04B5E77249C49.title: "&dOrb-ital Upgrade"
	quest.6620B4691F970117.quest_desc: [
		"The &eAstrolabe&r is the astral spell book: &b12 slots&r, &b+200 mana&r, +20% astral power and +5% mana regen."
		""
		"Craft it from a &eMithril Ingot&r, &e4 Chains&r, a &eClock&r and a &eTarnished Crown&r. Every Necromancer wears that crown, but drops it only about &b15%&r of the time."
		""
		"&7The &eCelestial Staff&r&7 (an Affinity Ring, arcane ingots and mithril scrap) completes the stargazer look.&r"
	]
	quest.6620B4691F970117.quest_subtitle: "12 slots, +20% astral power"
	quest.6620B4691F970117.title: "&9Charting the Heavens"
	quest.66504ECB883F8E9E.quest_desc: [
		"A ruined &6Citadel&r stands in the &cNether&r, guarded by Ancient Knights. The way there is a &eFurled Map&r: &e2 Ancient Knowledge Fragments&r, &e2 Cinder Essence&r and &e5 Paper&r."
		""
		"&aUnroll it in the Nether&r for a map with a red X. It finds nothing in the Overworld."
	]
	quest.66504ECB883F8E9E.quest_subtitle: "X marks the Citadel"
	quest.66504ECB883F8E9E.title: "&cEchoes of Fire"
	quest.665451FC681A49F7.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Alternator&r turns rotation into FE. It is a &6Mechanical Crafting&r recipe built from &eAndesite Alloy&r, &eIron Sheets&r, &eCopper Spools&r and an &eIron Rod&r."
		""
		"It needs at least &b32 RPM&r and gives &b360 FE/t&r at 256 RPM. It is thirsty, though: &b64 SU per RPM&r, so plan a big power source. It has a shaft on both ends, so you can chain several on one line."
	]
	quest.665451FC681A49F7.quest_subtitle: "Spin goes in, power comes out"
	quest.665451FC681A49F7.title: "&6Alternating Currents"
	quest.666E3E72D5A2C561.quest_desc: [
		"&eCorundum&r crystals grow in caves between &bY 0 and 64&r, two colours per deposit, nine colours in all. Deep down they &aslowly grow upward&r; wax one with &eHoneycomb&r to stop it."
		""
		"Corundum ringed with &eRedstone&r makes a &6Crystal Lamp&r that glows when powered. A &eCorundum Cluster&r placed in a beacon beam &bbends&r it in a new direction."
		""
		"&7Collect every colour of cluster for a Quark advancement.&r"
	]
	quest.666E3E72D5A2C561.quest_subtitle: "They grow when you're not looking"
	quest.666E3E72D5A2C561.title: "&dCrystal Clear"
	quest.66748814A357FBCB.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Scribe's Table&r (Archwood Slabs, Logs and Gold Nuggets) is a two-block desk where you craft new &dglyphs&r."
		""
		"Use your spell book on it, pick a glyph from the list (filter by tier or search) and press Select. Then &athrow the listed items onto the table&r, or let it pull them from nearby inventories. Pay the XP and the glyph pops out."
		""
		"Costs: &bTier I 27 XP points&r, &bTier II 55&r, &bTier III 160&r (3, 5 and 10 levels if you start from zero)."
	]
	quest.66748814A357FBCB.quest_subtitle: "Where glyphs are born"
	quest.66748814A357FBCB.title: "&6Take Note"
	quest.6686A07450179984.quest_desc: [
		"Ferricore makes the usual tool set plus a &ebow&r and a full &earmor&r set. A pickaxe has &b500&r durability, double iron, at iron mining level."
		""
		"The real point is the &bupgrade slots&r. Hold &bShift&r on the tooltip to see which upgrades each piece accepts."
		""
		"&7Till dirt with a Ferricore Hoe for Primogel Soil: crops grow faster and it can't be trampled.&r"
	]
	quest.6686A07450179984.quest_subtitle: "Upgrade slots included"
	quest.6686A07450179984.title: "&eBetter Than Iron (Barely)"
	quest.66B7D4BF4A44E01C.quest_desc: [
		"Make a &6Bench&r from &eOak Slabs&r and &eSticks&r, and a &6Desk Chair&r from &eOak Slabs&r and an &eIron Nugget&r. Both recipes make two."
		""
		"&aRight-click any seat to sit down.&r Benches placed side by side join into one long bench, and &bSneak-right-click&r a Bench to add or remove its backrest."
	]
	quest.66B7D4BF4A44E01C.quest_subtitle: "Finally, somewhere to sit"
	quest.66B7D4BF4A44E01C.title: "&aTake a Load Off"
	quest.66CA52D1F8DC8463.quest_desc: [
		"Time to put it together. A classic andesite-age loop:"
		"&eCobblestone&r into a &6Millstone&r gives Gravel."
		"Gravel through a &bwashing fan&r gives Flint, plus a chance of &eIron Nuggets&r."
		"Flint, Gravel and Lava in a &6Press over a Basin&r give Andesite."
		"Andesite and Nuggets in a &6Mixer&r give &eAndesite Alloy&r at half the hand-crafting cost."
		""
		"Link the steps with belts, funnels and chutes, or carry things by hand at first. Mined andesite and spare nuggets work too. Either way, let the machines make the stack."
		""
		"&aYou now run an engine that feeds itself.&r"
	]
	quest.66CA52D1F8DC8463.quest_subtitle: "Your first real production line"
	quest.66CA52D1F8DC8463.title: "&6The Factory Floor"
	quest.671124D95FA01949.quest_desc: [
		"Three herbal teas brew in the &6Cooking Pot&r: &btwo&r of one herb, a &eWater Bucket&r and a &eGlass Bottle&r in the container slot."
		""
		"&eWild Nettle&r and &eWild Ribwort&r grow in forests and swamps and drop themselves when broken. &aBone meal on a wild plant&r often pops out an extra one. The third tea uses &eStrawberries&r."
		""
		"&7Each tea gives a different short boost; hover them in EMI. For a whole mod of teas and coffee, see &6Steeped in Tradition&7.&r"
	]
	quest.671124D95FA01949.quest_subtitle: "Pinkies out"
	quest.671124D95FA01949.title: "&aTea for Three"
	quest.673EB76A24FBD684.quest_desc: [
		"Some skeletons in the &bdark depths below Y=0&r are &6Forgotten&r: tougher, with arrows that cause &cBlindness&r, and a sword for when you close in."
		""
		"Beat one for the &eForgotten Hat&r: &b+2 reach&r for blocks and entities, plus a little armour and luck. Builders love it."
	]
	quest.673EB76A24FBD684.quest_subtitle: "Old bones, nice hat"
	quest.673EB76A24FBD684.title: "&8This Belongs in a Museum"
	quest.674056D16082369B.quest_desc: [
		"Pour &eRed Grapejuice&r into the barrel, add &eSugar&r and put an empty &eWine Bottle&r in the bottle slot. Fermenting takes &b5 minutes&r per bottle, so leave it running and go do something else."
		""
		"&6Red Wine&r only uses &b10%&r juice, so one full barrel makes &b10 bottles&r if you keep it stocked with sugar and bottles. It gives &bSlow Falling&r."
		""
		"There are over two dozen wines, each with its own juice, ingredients and effect. Check the &bBarrel Fermentation&r tab in EMI. &cCareful with Creeper's Crush&r (you explode) and &cVillager's Fright&r (Bad Omen)."
	]
	quest.674056D16082369B.quest_subtitle: "Your first vintage"
	quest.674056D16082369B.title: "&4The Noble Drop"
	quest.6746320BAA7ADCE8.quest_desc: [
		"Mix &eSweet Dough&r (egg, water bucket, flour, sugar) and put it on the Caking Station: it splits into dough cubes."
		""
		"&aCut a cube with a knife&r for cupcake blanks. For cookies, flatten a cube with a &eRolling Pin&r (or knead it with bare hands), then cut. &aSpread jam on the blanks&r and take your treats with an empty hand."
		""
		"Sweets give &bSugar Rush&r, a speed boost that stacks the more you eat."
		""
		"&7Next up: jam rolls and cornets, and the Bakery's own completion banner.&r"
	]
	quest.6746320BAA7ADCE8.quest_subtitle: "One more can't hurt"
	quest.6746320BAA7ADCE8.title: "&dCookie Cutter"
	quest.6773D92BF6148FCA.quest_desc: [
		"Chests in &bmountain, peak and hill biomes&r usually roll the &eSpringy Boot&r. &bSneak and jump&r to launch yourself away from where you're looking, and &abounce&r on landing instead of taking fall damage."
		""
		"&7Hold jump or sneak to stop bouncing. Great for getting around mountains.&r"
	]
	quest.6773D92BF6148FCA.quest_subtitle: "Mountain chests, feet slot"
	quest.6773D92BF6148FCA.title: "&aBoing"
	quest.67D25BED9DFA77BE.quest_desc: [
		"&eCopper&r, &ePlanks&r, &eCobblestone&r and &eRedstone&r make a &6Turn Table&r. While powered, it &arotates the block it faces&r; a stronger signal spins faster. Right-click to reverse it."
		""
		"Pointed up, it spins anything standing on it, including you. Turning a container sideways &bshuffles its contents&r."
		""
		"&7Stand on one while it runs for a little advancement.&r"
	]
	quest.67D25BED9DFA77BE.quest_subtitle: "You spin me right round"
	quest.67D25BED9DFA77BE.title: "&bHow the Turn Tables"
	quest.67DD0035AEBC2CD8.quest_desc: [
		"Mix a &eCoconut Cocktail&r in the &6Palm Bar&r: &eOpen Coconut&r, &eIce&r and a &eHoney Bottle&r."
		""
		"Each cocktail gives a short buff: Coconut &bStrength&r, Sweet Berry &bAbsorption&r, Cocoa &bRegeneration&r, Pumpkin &bFire Resistance&r, Honey &bHaste&r, Melon &bLuck&r."
		""
		"&aDrink it from your hand&r, or place it down and take sips from it."
	]
	quest.67DD0035AEBC2CD8.quest_subtitle: "Little umbrella optional"
	quest.67DD0035AEBC2CD8.title: "&dShaken, Not Stirred"
	quest.67EC6BC5C8C6D85A.quest_desc: [
		"&6Apothic Enchanting&r gives the table three stats, first met in the &6Kitted Out&r chapter. Here are the real numbers: &dEterna&r is your max level (a bookshelf gives 2), &dQuanta&r is randomness in power (base 15%), and &dArcana&r favours rarer enchantments and guarantees 2 or 3 at &b25%&r and &b75%&r."
		""
		"The &b?&r button in the table lists every possible enchantment and its odds. You pay the exact XP for a level, not the top of your bar."
		""
		"&cYour World Tier caps your Eterna:&r Haven &b30&r, Frontier &b45&r, Ascent &b60&r, Summit &b75&r, Pinnacle &b100&r. You have to activate the tier, not just unlock it."
	]
	quest.67EC6BC5C8C6D85A.quest_subtitle: "Apothic Enchanting"
	quest.67EC6BC5C8C6D85A.title: "&dBeyond Thirty"
	quest.67F6B81E623DF47A.quest_desc: [
		"Welcome! This &6quest book&r is a guided tour of the pack. Most chapters teach one mod step by step, in the order you'll actually use it."
		""
		"Open the book any time from the &bsidebar buttons&r at the top left of your inventory. You can also bind &bOpen Quests&r to a key under &bControls > FTB Quests&r."
		""
		"Rewards are &aclaimed by clicking&r the quest. In a &6party&r, one member finishing a quest finishes it for everyone, and &beach member&r then claims their own reward. No chapter is locked behind another, so do them in any order."
		""
		"&7The cat is Duff, the pack mascot. Duff does nothing. Duff is perfect.&r"
	]
	quest.67F6B81E623DF47A.quest_subtitle: "Grab a snack, this is the tutorial"
	quest.67F6B81E623DF47A.title: "&eWelcome to IsItSMP"
	quest.67FF7295FF2250CE.quest_desc: [
		"To break a limit, start with an item whose enchantment is &balready at its maximum&r, then add a matching &eAncient Tome&r in an &6Anvil&r. The result goes &aone level past the cap&r."
		""
		"&cApotheosis raises the maximums in this pack&r (the tome's tooltip shows the real cap), so this is a late-game goal: first reach the top level at an Apotheosis enchanting table."
		""
		"Going past the cap costs &b20 more levels&r than a normal tome upgrade, so bank some XP first."
	]
	quest.67FF7295FF2250CE.quest_subtitle: "Rules are made to be broken"
	quest.67FF7295FF2250CE.title: "&5One Step Beyond"
	quest.6806736A9723CE5E.quest_desc: [
		"&6Copper Pipes&r (Copper Ingots and Glass, 6 at a time) carry items. Feed them with a &6Hopper&r or Dropper, or toss items into an open end."
		""
		"Items prefer to go &bdown&r, then &bforward&r, then a random side, and &bup&r only as a last resort. A &bredstone signal&r switches a pipe off, and a Comparator reads how full it is."
		""
		"&cA pipe holding more than 16 items breaks.&r Don't flood them. For heavy hauling, use &6Pipez&r from the &6Kitted Out&r chapter."
	]
	quest.6806736A9723CE5E.quest_subtitle: "Gravity's favourite logistics"
	quest.6806736A9723CE5E.title: "&6A Series of Tubes"
	quest.681EF01C304A34C5.quest_desc: [
		"Find any &6Artifact&r. Good early odds per chest: big ocean ruins (&b45%&r), the rare chest minecarts in Better Mineshafts (&b30%&r), buried treasure and pillager outposts (&b25%&r), and Better Dungeons chests (&b15%&r). Desert and jungle temples have their own sets, and &abrushing suspicious sand&r in desert temples and wells can turn one up too."
		""
		"&cVillage chests here almost never have them&r: the villages use their own loot."
		""
		"&7The toggle keys (Night Vision Goggles, Scarf of Invisibility, Universal Attractor, the two Charms) are unbound: set them under Options > Controls > Artifacts.&r"
	]
	quest.681EF01C304A34C5.quest_subtitle: "Some assembly not required"
	quest.681EF01C304A34C5.title: "&eAmateur Archaeologist"
	quest.685146C48FA19AD4.quest_desc: [
		"&6MCA: Quests&r adds a &bQuests&r button to the villager menu. Each adult offers up to &b3 quests&r a day: deliveries, escorts, monster hunts, building jobs and more. &aTurn in to the villager who gave it&r (the Gift button works for deliveries)."
		""
		"Rewards are &eEmeralds&r, XP and, best of all, &ahearts&r with the giver. Declining costs nothing."
		""
		"Press &bJ&r to toggle the tracker. Active targets also get markers and &6Xaero's&r waypoints. The &bQuest Log&r and &bJournal&r keys are unbound, so set them in Controls."
	]
	quest.685146C48FA19AD4.quest_subtitle: "Villagers with to-do lists"
	quest.685146C48FA19AD4.title: "&6MCA: Quests"
	quest.689F4E8E973C1EE5.quest_desc: [
		"&6Better Ocean Monuments&r are bigger, with a new layout every time. They sit in &bdeep oceans&r and are rarer than vanilla ones. A Cartographer's &eOcean Explorer Map&r leads straight to one."
		""
		"Bring &dWater Breathing&r potions, Respiration and Aqua Affinity. Guardians patrol the halls, and &eTridents&r wait in the lower middle chambers."
		""
		"&7Here's a bucket of milk. You'll want it in a minute.&r"
	]
	quest.689F4E8E973C1EE5.quest_subtitle: "Holding your breath is not a strategy"
	quest.689F4E8E973C1EE5.title: "&3Twenty Thousand Blocks Under"
	quest.689FE6CCA650DD51.quest_desc: [
		"Open any chest: Quark adds small buttons next to the grid to &bsort&r it, &binsert&r everything that matches, or &bextract&r it all. Your own inventory gets a sort button too."
		""
		"More tricks: &bZ&r (default) swaps your hotbar with an inventory row, &bF12&r is a screenshot camera mode, and the chat screen has &aemote&r buttons. Click items into a held &eShulker Box&r like a bundle, or onto a &eLava Bucket&r to bin them."
		""
		"&7Keys clash in a big pack. Check Controls if Z does something else.&r"
	]
	quest.689FE6CCA650DD51.quest_subtitle: "Your chests called. They want order."
	quest.689FE6CCA650DD51.title: "&bTidy Up"
	quest.68B3754504EA6902.quest_desc: [
		"&ePortal Fluid Catalyst&r (Chorus Fruit and Lapis) dropped into Polymorphic Fluid makes &eUnstable Portal Fluid&r. &cIt only survives in End biomes&r, so carry a bucket of Polymorphic Fluid and a &6VoidShimmer Goo&r to the End and let the goo stabilise it into &ePortal Fluid&r there."
		""
		"The &eAdvanced Portal Gun&r (Blazegold, Celestigem, a Portal Fluid Catalyst and a &eFluid Canister&r, which is 4 Ferricore around Glass) runs on FE and Portal Fluid and can open a portal to a &asaved location&r. Right-click a Portal Fluid source with it to fill it."
		""
		"&7The basic Portal Gun (Blazegold and an Eye of Ender) just shoots a blue and an orange portal.&r"
	]
	quest.68B3754504EA6902.quest_subtitle: "Blue portal, orange portal"
	quest.68B3754504EA6902.title: "&dPortal Combat"
	quest.68EC883ABE4B532B.quest_desc: [
		"Imbue an &eAmethyst Shard&r or &eLapis Lazuli&r to get a &eSource Gem&r (&b500 Source&r each). An &eAmethyst Block&r becomes a whole &eSource Gem Block&r for 2000, the same price as its 4 shards but in one go."
		""
		"Source Gems go into almost every Ars recipe. &b4&r craft into a &eSource Gem Block&r (and it breaks back into 4), which relays, the Ritual Brazier and the Enchanted Spell Turret need. &aStart a stockpile.&r"
		""
		"&7Later, a Ritual of Awakening performed next to Budding Amethyst gives you an Amethyst Golem that farms amethyst for you.&r"
	]
	quest.68EC883ABE4B532B.quest_subtitle: "The currency of Ars"
	quest.68EC883ABE4B532B.title: "&eGemology"
	quest.6924C3B1BDF8405D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Waystones&r are teleport points. You'll find them in some &bvillages&r and out in the wild, styled to the biome. &aRight-click one&r to activate it, then right-click any activated waystone to travel to the others."
		""
		"&cEach player activates a waystone for themselves.&r Travel costs a little experience: about &b1 XP point per 100 blocks&r, never more than &b27 points&r. Every waystone you activate also becomes a minimap waypoint."
		""
		"&7A Warp Stone that takes you to your waystones from anywhere comes later, in &6Kitted Out&7.&r"
	]
	quest.6924C3B1BDF8405D.quest_subtitle: "Fast travel, the scenic way"
	quest.6924C3B1BDF8405D.title: "&dSet in Stone"
	quest.6954B6D2CF9DC86D.quest_desc: [
		"Collect all &b7 milks&r in wooden buckets:"
		"&ePlain&r: a Cow or Highland Cattle."
		"&eSheep&r and &eGoat Milk&r: milk a vanilla Sheep or Goat."
		"&eBuffalo Milk&r: a &6Water Buffalo&r, found in savannas, rivers and swamps."
		"&eGrain Milk&r: cook &b3 Wheat&r with an empty Wooden Bucket."
		"&eAmethyst Milk&r: cook an &eAmethyst Cluster&r, Salt and milk. &cClusters only drop with Silk Touch.&r"
		"&eWarped Milk&r: &cNether only.&r Milk a &6Warped Cattle&r in a Warped Forest."
		""
		"&7Keep them in buckets: you'll want every one of them for the next quest.&r"
	]
	quest.6954B6D2CF9DC86D.quest_subtitle: "Seven buckets, one wooden pail at a time"
	quest.6954B6D2CF9DC86D.title: "&fMilking the Possibilities"
	quest.69803516A8455E5E.quest_desc: [
		"Somewhere in the biome stands a &6Cemetery&r: a fenced graveyard with tombs, houses, crypts lined with &6Coffins&r full of loot and, at its centre, a &6Pedestal&r."
		""
		"Cemeteries only generate inside this biome and are &bwell spread out&r, so a small patch of Hollow may not have one. Keep exploring the fog. The &6Pedestal&r is &cunbreakable&r, so the boss fight happens here. Clear the area and light it up before you start anything."
		""
		"&7Creaky Hollow Planks in the buildings can be cleansed with a right-click from an axe, but that wakes a fully armoured guardian.&r"
	]
	quest.69803516A8455E5E.quest_subtitle: "The neighbours are very quiet"
	quest.69803516A8455E5E.title: "&6Grave Matters"
	quest.69DC532DF3A9DEA6.quest_desc: [
		"This book is cast, not crafted. Put a &eBook&r on a &6Casting Table&r and pour &b250 mB&r of &eSeared Stone&r fluid over it. One melted Grout gives 500 mB."
		""
		"&eMighty Smelting&r covers the &6Smeltery&r, alloys, the &6Anvil&r and melting mobs. That's where you're headed next."
	]
	quest.69DC532DF3A9DEA6.quest_subtitle: "Book three: Mighty Smelting"
	quest.69DC532DF3A9DEA6.title: "&eSmelting 201"
	quest.6A2110A0E61A948C.quest_desc: [
		"The &eBlueprint&r is &e8 Paper&r around &eBlue Dye&r. Right-click it in a village for the &bMap&r, the &bCatalog&r (what every building type needs), &bVillagers&r, your &bRank&r and the village &bRules&r."
		""
		"&cAuto scan is off in this pack.&r When you finish a room, stand inside it and press &aAdd Building&r, or switch on auto scan under &bAdvanced&r. A village needs at least &b3 buildings&r."
	]
	quest.6A2110A0E61A948C.quest_subtitle: "Paperwork, the fun part"
	quest.6A2110A0E61A948C.title: "&6Village Planner"
	quest.6A26893EB37B2666.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a &6Cutting Board&r from &cbirch planks&r (only birch!) and a stick, and an &eIron Cleaver&r from an iron ingot and a stick."
		""
		"&aPut the cleaver on the board, then hold right-click with food&r to chop it: iron takes &b5 chops&r, diamond &b3&r, netherite &b1&r. With no tool on it, stack ingredients and right-click with an empty hand to &aassemble&r feeds, sandwiches and salads. An axe on it strips logs."
		""
		"&7Zombies, skeletons, wither skeletons, creepers and piglins killed with a cleaver in hand always drop their head.&r"
	]
	quest.6A26893EB37B2666.quest_subtitle: "Mind your fingers"
	quest.6A26893EB37B2666.title: "&6Chopping Block"
	quest.6A35341729151A8C.quest_desc: [
		"Make a &ehoe&r, till dirt within four blocks of &bwater&r and plant some seeds (break grass for &ewheat seeds&r)."
		""
		"&6Serene Seasons&r is on: crops grow at full speed only in their &bfertile seasons&r and about &c6x slower&r out of season. A new world starts in &bEarly Spring&r, where &acarrots and potatoes&r thrive. &eWheat&r is a summer and autumn crop."
		""
		"Hover any seed to see its fertile seasons."
	]
	quest.6A35341729151A8C.quest_subtitle: "Mind the calendar"
	quest.6A35341729151A8C.title: "&aA Seedy Start"
	quest.6A36D5C0B79CA409.quest_desc: [
		"In this pack every &6End Portal Frame&r is unstable, and your magic can fix that. The &6Enchanting Apparatus&r makes the &dEnd Portal Stabilizer&r:"
		""
		"&d- Ars Nouveau:&r an &6Enchanting Apparatus&r with a &eNether Star&r in the middle and a &eWilden Tribute&r, 2 &eNetherite Ingots&r, 2 &eEcho Shards&r, 2 &eEyes of Ender&r and a &eSource Gem Block&r on the pedestals (&b10,000 source&r)."
		""
		"&7The rest of the road to the End is in &6Into the Unknown&7.&r"
	]
	quest.6A36D5C0B79CA409.quest_subtitle: "Sorcery for the End"
	quest.6A36D5C0B79CA409.title: "&5A Stable Gate"
	quest.6A6AAF71C55DA269.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Scorched Mines&r dig under the &bdesert&r. Their spawners are straight out of the Nether: &cWither Skeletons&r with Fire Aspect swords, skeletons with Flame bows, and husks."
		""
		"The treasure chests hold enchanted diamond armour, netherite scrap and sometimes a &eWither Skeleton Skull&r, without a trip to a fortress. &7Fire Resistance helps.&r"
	]
	quest.6A6AAF71C55DA269.quest_subtitle: "The Nether, delivered to your desert"
	quest.6A6AAF71C55DA269.title: "&cHot Under the Collar"
	quest.6A9A2EA30E39CD18.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Chef's Outfit&r is a hat, jacket, pants and boots made from wool, leather, a gold ingot and rabbit hide."
		""
		"Wear all four for a &b25% chance of an extra portion&r from Candlelight's Cooking Pan and Cooking Pot."
		""
		"&7Dining out instead? A suit or dress makes table meals even better, and a Gold Ring in your ring slot gives Luck.&r"
	]
	quest.6A9A2EA30E39CD18.quest_subtitle: "Yes, chef!"
	quest.6A9A2EA30E39CD18.title: "&fDressed to Grill"
	quest.6ABFF0B805111321.quest_desc: [
		"Pick up any &eaffixed item&r: chest loot, monster drops and &6Wandering Traders&r all carry them. The name colour is the rarity: &7Common&r, &aUncommon&r, &9Rare&r, &5Epic&r and &6Mythic&r."
		""
		"Your first one unlocks the &6Haven&r tier. Press &bCtrl+T&r, read the tutorial and click &aDone&r. Until a tier has been activated once, affix items stay &cUnidentified&r."
		""
		"Hold &bShift&r over gear to compare it with what you're wearing, and press &bShift+T&r to link the hovered item in chat."
		""
		"&7Each player has their own tier. Most spawns and loot follow the nearest player's.&r"
	]
	quest.6ABFF0B805111321.quest_subtitle: "World Tier: Haven"
	quest.6ABFF0B805111321.title: "&aA Touch of Affix"
	quest.6B1F2135FC7322DF.quest_desc: [
		"&eCandy Corn&r is the cheap sanity snack: &aput Sugar on a Campfire&r. Each one restores &b4 sanity&r."
		""
		"Every sanity food can be eaten &aeven when you're full&r. &eDusk Berries&r from the bushes in the biome give &b2&r, so pick them as you go."
		""
		"&7Keep a stack in your hotbar whenever you head into the fog.&r"
	]
	quest.6B1F2135FC7322DF.quest_subtitle: "Sugar, but make it spooky"
	quest.6B1F2135FC7322DF.title: "&eTrick or Treat Yourself"
	quest.6B3F14AFED3C8920.quest_desc: [
		"&6Elephants&r, &6Giraffes&r and &6Hippos&r drop &eThick Leather&r. &cElephants and Hippos defend themselves, and Hippos attack boats.&r"
		""
		"&aDrop Thick Leather on the ground&r, hold &eShears&r and right-click while looking at it to cut it into &b3 Leather&r."
	]
	quest.6B3F14AFED3C8920.quest_subtitle: "Big animals, big hides"
	quest.6B3F14AFED3C8920.title: "&6Thick Skinned"
	quest.6B5663F73180034C.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Weighted Ejector&r (Golden Sheet, Depot, Cogwheel) throws items, mobs or players up to &b32 blocks&r. While holding it, &bsneak-right-click&r the landing spot, then place it in line with that spot."
		""
		"Rotation charges it. Its value panel sets a stack size to wait for before launching."
		""
		"&7Ride one more than 30 blocks for the 'Springboard Champion' advancement.&r"
	]
	quest.6B5663F73180034C.quest_subtitle: "Yeet as a service"
	quest.6B5663F73180034C.title: "&aSpringboard"
	quest.6B63EB9D2C92B9A4.quest_desc: [
		"&6Train Track&r is another &6Sequenced Assembly&r: start with a &eStone Slab&r, &eSmooth Stone Slab&r or &eAndesite Slab&r, deploy an &eIron&r or &eZinc Nugget&r onto it, then another, then &6press&r it."
		""
		"To lay track, right-click a placed track and then a second spot: the curve or slope between them is built for you, up to &b32 blocks&r at a time. Turns max out at &b90 degrees&r; &bhold Sprint&r for the widest bend, and blocks in your &boffhand&r get paved underneath."
		""
		"&7Shift-click into the air to cancel a selection.&r"
	]
	quest.6B63EB9D2C92B9A4.quest_subtitle: "Slab, nugget, nugget, press"
	quest.6B63EB9D2C92B9A4.title: "&eMaking Tracks"
	quest.6BA1246AA4573796.quest_desc: [
		"A &eWarp Scroll&r is Blank Parchment, 4 Lapis and 4 Source Gems. &bSneak-use&r it to record where you stand, and use it later for a one-way trip back."
		""
		"For a permanent link, build a rectangular frame of &eSourcestone&r (1x1 up to 21x21), put a &bfull&r &6Source Jar&r nearby and &athrow the written scroll into the frame&r. The portal costs nothing to use afterwards, but a plain Warp Scroll only links &bwithin one dimension&r."
		""
		"&7A Stabilized Warp Scroll is reusable and can cross dimensions; thrown into a frame it makes a cross-dimension portal, but is used up.&r"
	]
	quest.6BA1246AA4573796.quest_subtitle: "Wrong game, right idea"
	quest.6BA1246AA4573796.title: "&dThinking With Portals"
	quest.6BC824E0A7DB436C.quest_desc: [
		"&eBlazing Blood&r is the hottest fuel at &b1500°C&r, and the top alloys need it. To get it, &cmelt live Blazes&r in a fuelled smeltery. Lure them in, or carry one in a &ePiggybackpack&r."
		""
		"A &eBlaze Head&r from a charged creeper melts into &b100 mB&r, and piglins sometimes barter lanterns of it. Right-click the drain with an empty bucket to fill it."
	]
	quest.6BC824E0A7DB436C.quest_subtitle: "1500 degrees of trouble"
	quest.6BC824E0A7DB436C.title: "&cHot Blooded"
	quest.6BCEFA2ECA2C104D.quest_desc: [
		"&6Bin&r (7 &eIron Nuggets&r, makes two): &aright-click it with an item to throw one away for good&r. Iron and gold tools and armour come back as nuggets. A nearly full bin stinks and a full one draws flies. The next item you throw in empties it, and &b1 time in 4&r a &eTrash Bag&r of random junk (and the odd treasure) pops out. &bSneak-right-click&r with an empty hand for quiet decoration mode."
		""
		"&6Boat in a Jar&r (any &eBoat&r and a &eGlass Bottle&r): right-click to shake it, and a &eWater Bottle&r starts a tiny storm inside. &cShake it about five times in a row and the mast snaps&r (a &eStick&r fixes it)."
		""
		"&6Terrarium&r: a little world under glass, made from &eGlass&r, a &eSapling&r, &eShort Grass&r (bring Shears), &eDirt&r and &eCobblestone&r. &6Display&r (&ePlanks&r and &eGlass&r): the item on it slowly spins."
	]
	quest.6BCEFA2ECA2C104D.quest_subtitle: "Every shelf needs clutter"
	quest.6BCEFA2ECA2C104D.title: "&aBits and Bobs"
	quest.6BDB9CA5EF2D0FC0.quest_desc: [
		"The last tier: a full set of &5Epic&r or better, and an &cEnder Dragon&r kill of your own. If the dragon is already dead, place &b4 End Crystals&r on the exit portal to bring it back for the next player."
		""
		"Pinnacle monsters are brutal (+16 armor, +25 armor pierce, 15% damage reduction). Loot is &b25%&r &6Mythic&r, gems are mostly &bFlawless&r or better, and the enchanting cap is finally lifted to &b100&r."
		""
		"&7The full Reforging Table builds Epic gear when the drops won't cooperate.&r"
	]
	quest.6BDB9CA5EF2D0FC0.quest_subtitle: "World Tier: Pinnacle"
	quest.6BDB9CA5EF2D0FC0.title: "&5Stormy Peaks"
	quest.6BE894E8245AC894.quest_desc: [
		"&6Jellie Wine&r is the finest bottle in Vinery. It ferments from &eWhite Grapejuice&r with three other wines as ingredients, &eApple Wine&r, &eBolvar Wine&r and &eChenet Wine&r, plus an empty Wine Bottle."
		""
		"Chenet Wine comes from &eRed Jungle Grapejuice&r with a &eSpider Eye&r and a &eHoney Bottle&r."
		""
		"The reward is the &dJellie&r effect, which works like a golden apple, only stronger. &aAge a few of these in your cellar&r and they get better still."
	]
	quest.6BE894E8245AC894.quest_subtitle: "Three wines walk into a barrel"
	quest.6BE894E8245AC894.title: "&dFine Vintage"
	quest.6C43F19C291C2A2A.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Supply Cart&r carries a chest, and the &6Plow&r tills two rows as it rolls and harvests crops in its path. &aRight-click a cart to pull it yourself&r, or right-click a tamed horse or donkey to hitch it up. &bSneak-right-click&r opens the cart's chest or switches the plow on and off."
		""
		"&7A Seeder cart sows farmland as you drive. Horse Fodder from the Cutting Board tames horses and gives them speed and jump.&r"
	]
	quest.6C43F19C291C2A2A.quest_subtitle: "Hitch it and ditch the walking"
	quest.6C43F19C291C2A2A.title: "&6Horsepower"
	quest.6C66C472EEA95010.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Navigation Table&r (Brass Sheet, Precision Mechanism, Brass Casing) holds a &enavigation item&r and sends a redstone signal out towards its target, weaker the further the table points off course."
		""
		"It reads a &eCompass&r, a &eRecovery Compass&r, &eexplorer and buried-treasure maps&r, and even &6Nature's Compass&r. Wire it to your steering for an autopilot. &6Display Links&r can show distance and ETA."
	]
	quest.6C66C472EEA95010.quest_subtitle: "Thataway!"
	quest.6C66C472EEA95010.title: "&bPlotting a Course"
	quest.6CDB1A354D3A1AAB.quest_desc: [
		"&aRight-click your spell book&r to wear it in its own &bCurios&r slot. Then press &bV&r to cast the selected spell, &bhold R&r for the Spell Wheel, or hold &bLeft Alt&r and scroll to flip through the spell bar."
		""
		"Casting drains &dmana&r (you start with &b100&r). The mana bar sits by your hunger bar and shows whenever you hold a magic item or aren't full. You respawn with an &cempty&r tank."
		""
		"&cKey clash:&r other mods in this pack (voice chat, Ars Nouveau, shaders, Quark) also use V and R. Rebind them under &bControls > Iron's Spells 'n Spellbooks - General&r; the &eToo Many Keys&r quest in &6First Light&r shows every clash."
	]
	quest.6CDB1A354D3A1AAB.quest_subtitle: "Point the pointy end at the enemy"
	quest.6CDB1A354D3A1AAB.title: "&dMagery"
	quest.6D0D10E20E338036.quest_desc: [
		"At &b66%&r health the Horseman's &6pumpkin head&r leaps off and flees. While it's loose the &cHorseman can't be hurt&r, and he keeps raising armoured skeletons."
		""
		"Hunt the &6Fleeing Pumpkin Head&r down: &b100 HP&r and heavy armour. It calls zombies and archers and flashes &cBlindness&r at anyone close. Each hit stuns it for a moment. Kill it and the Horseman glows, &avulnerable again&r."
		""
		"&7It happens twice, at 66% and 33%.&r"
	]
	quest.6D0D10E20E338036.quest_subtitle: "Literally. Away from you. Quickly."
	quest.6D0D10E20E338036.title: "&6Heads Will Roll"
	quest.6D3C5B543840E28C.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a &eBook&r with a piece of &eGrout&r to get &ePuny Smelting&r, the guide to the Melter, faucets, casting and every upgrade modifier."
		""
		"&aKeep it handy&r: it explains the melting and casting steps that EMI won't show you."
	]
	quest.6D3C5B543840E28C.quest_subtitle: "Book two: Puny Smelting"
	quest.6D3C5B543840E28C.title: "&eRequired Reading"
	quest.6DB3BA566DE1BE8B.quest_desc: [
		"A &eBlank Rune&r is a pool infusion: &e1 Fluxite&r + &e1 Astralite Nugget&r for &b1,000 ƒ&r."
		""
		"Altar tiers come from &bcomplete rings of runes laid one block BELOW the altar&r. For &btier II&r, replace the 8 blocks around the block under your altar with runes. Chalk sits on top, so runes and glyphs never clash."
		""
		"&cRunes beside the altar don't count, and a ring with one gap counts for nothing.&r"
	]
	quest.6DB3BA566DE1BE8B.quest_subtitle: "Eight runes, one ring"
	quest.6DB3BA566DE1BE8B.title: "&7Laying the Foundation"
	quest.6DE8825C081C6E71.quest_desc: [
		"The Nether hides &6Ancient Battlegrounds&r littered with &eArmor Piles&r. &cMine one and an Ancient Knight climbs out&r."
		""
		"Kill it yourself for a &eCinder Essence&r, plus a small chance at &eNetherite Scrap&r. Burial chests nearby can hold more cinder."
		""
		"&eCinder Essence&r is the Nether-side ingredient for the Alchemist Cauldron, upgrade orbs and the way to the final boss."
	]
	quest.6DE8825C081C6E71.quest_subtitle: "Someone is still inside"
	quest.6DE8825C081C6E71.title: "&cArmor Piled High"
	quest.6E10CE5ADD3F872F.quest_desc: [
		"Eight &eIron Ingots&r make an &6Iron Chestplate&r, the toughest piece of the iron set. Add a &6Shield&r (six planks and one iron ingot) and &bhold right-click&r to block arrows and creeper blasts."
		""
		"With iron tools and armour you're ready for caves, villages and the rest of the book."
		""
		"&7Fill out the rest of the set when you have the iron.&r"
	]
	quest.6E10CE5ADD3F872F.quest_subtitle: "Tools: check. Armour: check."
	quest.6E10CE5ADD3F872F.title: "&6Ironclad"
	quest.6E236043A977E268.quest_desc: [
		"Stabilize all &b12&r frames, fill them with eyes and step through. &6YUNG's Better End Island&r has redesigned the arrival platform, the pillars and the island itself."
		""
		"&cThe dragon isn't waiting for you.&r She is summoned when someone walks up to the &6bell tower&r in the middle of the island, so look around, set up a safe spot and get ready before you go near it."
		""
		"&cBeds explode in the End.&r"
	]
	quest.6E236043A977E268.quest_subtitle: "Not quite"
	quest.6E236043A977E268.title: "&5The End?"
	quest.6E4B2CDE38A78431.quest_desc: [
		"&6Apple Wood Rebarked&r adds a full wood set for Vinery's apple trees: planks, shingles, doors and boats, plus a whole house of &6apple furniture&r, apple wine racks and an apple lattice."
		""
		"&cStrip apple logs with an axe first.&r Unstripped logs can craft into oak planks; &eStripped Apple Logs&r always give &e4 Apple Planks&r."
		""
		"&7Look for the Grandfather Clock, Wardrobe and Dresser in EMI, and the produce crates made from planks and a bag of fruit or veg.&r"
	]
	quest.6E4B2CDE38A78431.quest_subtitle: "The apple doesn't fall far"
	quest.6E4B2CDE38A78431.title: "&6Rebarked"
	quest.6E525D7DD161608D.quest_desc: [
		"Build a &bhollow box&r, at least &b3x3x3&r and at most &b13x13x13&r counting the walls (cuboids work too). &bEdges and corners&r can be almost any full solid block without an inventory, but not glass or soft blocks like dirt, sand, gravel, wool, leaves or ice. &bWalls&r follow the same rule, except that &aglass and Glass Viewers are allowed&r. The inside must be &bempty&r; only XyCraft lamps, Aluminum or Copper Torches and Create Placards may go inside."
		""
		"Put a &6Valve&r in a wall and &aright-click it&r. Chat says &aFormed!&r when it works. If not, check the edges, walls and inside against the rules above."
		""
		"Each hollow block holds &b8 buckets&r: a 3x3x3 holds 8, a 5x5x5 holds 216, and a full 13x13x13 holds &b10,648&r. &cOne fluid per tank.&r A comparator on the Valve reads the fill level, and &bJade&r shows the contents."
	]
	quest.6E525D7DD161608D.quest_subtitle: "A bucket the size of a house"
	quest.6E525D7DD161608D.title: "&bTank You Very Much"
	quest.6EBBF7A0527A7694.quest_desc: [
		"&eJungle grapes&r are fussy: their seeds only grow on a &6Lattice&r. Craft lattices from sticks and planks of any vanilla wood, dark cherry or apple, place them, and &aright-click with jungle grape seeds&r."
		""
		"Wild jungle grapes hang like vines in jungles and wooded badlands. Harvest a ripe lattice by right-clicking it or with &eShears&r."
		""
		"&7Lattices are also climbable, so a lattice wall doubles as a ladder.&r"
	]
	quest.6EBBF7A0527A7694.quest_subtitle: "Jungle grapes climb, they don't sit"
	quest.6EBBF7A0527A7694.title: "&2Overgrown Lattices"
	quest.6ED7BCC44F1F0099.quest_desc: [
		"&eRaubbau&r is a shovel that gives itself &bEfficiency VIII&r and keeps it. Dirt, sand and gravel barely slow you down."
		""
		"Like Shatterbrand, it only comes from &eLoot Bags&r."
	]
	quest.6ED7BCC44F1F0099.quest_subtitle: "Somebody's very old shovel"
	quest.6ED7BCC44F1F0099.title: "&eDig It"
	quest.6EE1978CB79DD82B.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Hot Air Burner&r: Iron Sheets around a &eBlock of Coal&r, over Andesite Alloy and Redstone. Place it under your envelope shell."
		""
		"It runs on a &bredstone signal&r, not fuel. Signal strength sets the output, so an &6Analog Lever&r becomes an altitude knob. Its panel caps output at up to &b500 m³&r, and each m³ of hot air lifts &b1.5 kpg&r."
		""
		"The ship climbs until &blift equals weight&r and settles there. Several burners can share one balloon."
	]
	quest.6EE1978CB79DD82B.quest_subtitle: "No fuel, just feelings (redstone)"
	quest.6EE1978CB79DD82B.title: "&6Hot Air Rises"
	quest.6F1C68E333152F87.quest_desc: [
		"&6Create Offroad&r adds land vehicles. The &6Wheel Mount&r is Andesite Casing over a &eSpring&r over an Iron Sheet (a Spring is an Iron Nugget between two Iron Sheets)."
		""
		"Right-click its front with a tire, then &bgive it rotation&r to drive (&b16 SU per RPM&r). Redstone from the &btop brakes&r, from a &bside steers&r toward that side. Its panel sets suspension."
		""
		"&7Water wheels, flywheels and crushing wheels fit on a mount too.&r"
	]
	quest.6F1C68E333152F87.quest_subtitle: "Create Offroad"
	quest.6F1C68E333152F87.title: "&6Hit the Road"
	quest.6F2F5F0E6E338850.quest_desc: [
		"&eSticks&r make &6Timber Frames&r, Braces and Cross Braces. Place one and &aclick it with any full block&r to fill it in; an axe strips the frame off again."
		""
		"&eClay Balls&r and &eFlax&r (or Wheat) make &6Daub&r. Daub in a frame gives classic &6wattle and daub&r walls."
		""
		"&7Supplementaries Squared adds Metal Frames and Daub stairs and slabs.&r"
	]
	quest.6F2F5F0E6E338850.quest_subtitle: "Tudor-ly delightful"
	quest.6F2F5F0E6E338850.title: "&eHalf-Timbered"
	quest.6F99979451CF425E.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Water Sprinkler&r (iron ingots, planks and a &eWater Bucket&r) keeps farmland within &b8 blocks&r watered so it never dries out. Right-click it to change its look."
		""
		"&aOnions and lettuce&r with water within 4 blocks or a Sprinkler within 2 sometimes grow &bbig&r or even &bgiant&r, for a bigger harvest."
		""
		"&7Need water without a lake? A Timber Well pumps it up from below.&r"
	]
	quest.6F99979451CF425E.quest_subtitle: "Never water by hand again"
	quest.6F99979451CF425E.title: "&bMaking It Rain"
	quest.6FDC6AE4A69CB6EC.quest_desc: [
		"&6Candlelight&r is about fine dining: fancy dishes, dinner tables and dressing the part. Its dishes cook on the Farm \\& Charm &6Stove&r, &6Roaster&r and &6Cooking Pot&r; its copper Pan and Pot and stone stoves are prettier twins."
		""
		"Begin with &eMozzarella&r: a milk bucket and a water bucket in the &6Crafting Bowl&r make 6."
		""
		"&dMany dishes take a potion&r (or Vinery wine) as an ingredient and pass its effect on to the meal."
	]
	quest.6FDC6AE4A69CB6EC.quest_subtitle: "Candlelight lays the table"
	quest.6FDC6AE4A69CB6EC.title: "&6Dinner by Candlelight"
	quest.6FEF8159C3F36E60.quest_desc: [
		"&eSkyslime Balls&r come from the blue &bSkyslimes&r that live around &6skyslime islands&r. Those islands float high above the Overworld, and some sit in the ocean. The islands hold &eCongealed Skyslime&r blocks, and each one crafts into 4 balls. Crystals from underground &bskyslime geodes&r also blast into balls."
		""
		"Craft a &eBook&r with a Skyslime Ball to get &eModern Foundry's Gadgetry&r, the exploration guide. &7Slimy saplings and seeds sometimes turn up in loot chests.&r"
	]
	quest.6FEF8159C3F36E60.quest_subtitle: "The sky is full of slime"
	quest.6FEF8159C3F36E60.title: "&bBlue Goo"
	quest.702BB37A9276C185.quest_desc: [
		"You made your first &eBrass&r at the end of &6Spin Cycle&r, the Andesite Age chapter. Now make more and spend it: &6precision parts&r, &6steam power&r, &6package logistics&r and &6trains&r all live here."
		""
		"Quick recap: &eCopper&r and &eZinc Ingots&r in a &6Basin&r, mixed over a fuelled &6Blaze Burner&r, give &b2 Brass Ingots&r per pair."
		""
		"&7Reminder: EMI doesn't show Create's machine recipes in this pack&r (mixing, pressing, sequenced assembly and the rest), so these quests spell out every machine step in words. For everything else, hover a Create item and hold &bW&r for its &6Ponder&r scene."
	]
	quest.702BB37A9276C185.quest_subtitle: "Create, part two"
	quest.702BB37A9276C185.title: "&6The Brass Age"
	quest.70AD01C6285BA55C.quest_desc: [
		"Lay a second complete ring of &b16 runes&r around the first, still one block below the altar: &b24 runes&r in all. &cRings are read from the inside out&r, so a gap in ring one wastes ring two."
		""
		"Tier III unlocks &dLunar Gate&r (Eyes of Ender), &dVerdant Wilds&r (bees), &dStarlight Cross&r (it summons an &6Allay&r!), &dThe Whole Spectrum&r and the &dVigils&r of the Gathering Storm and the Warding Light."
	]
	quest.70AD01C6285BA55C.quest_subtitle: "Tier III: 24 runes"
	quest.70AD01C6285BA55C.title: "&dA Wider Circle"
	quest.70D1E1165F04A514.quest_desc: [
		"&eLeather&r and &eWooden Slabs&r make a set of &6Bellows&r. Give it a redstone signal and it pumps air out of its front."
		""
		"&aIt speeds up a furnace in front of it&r, keeps fires in front of it burning and &apushes mobs and items&r up to &b5 blocks&r away. A stronger signal pumps faster."
		""
		"&7Stepping on unpowered bellows squashes them with a wheeze.&r"
	]
	quest.70D1E1165F04A514.quest_subtitle: "And blow your furnace faster"
	quest.70D1E1165F04A514.title: "&eHuff and Puff"
	quest.70DDB67ABBC9B4E1.quest_desc: [
		"A &eBrass Ingot&r, &eElectron Tube&r and &eDried Kelp&r make &b2&r &6Brass Funnels&r or &b2&r &6Brass Tunnels&r. A &6Smart Chute&r is a &eChute&r with an Electron Tube and a &eBrass Sheet&r."
		""
		"Brass funnels and smart chutes have a &bfilter slot&r and a value panel for how many items move at once (a brass funnel pulls up to a full stack). Tunnels take a filter on each side and a distribution mode, like &bRound Robin&r or &bSynchronize Inputs&r, for splitting belts evenly."
		""
		"&7Filters: Iron Nuggets and Wool make a List Filter; Brass Nuggets and Wool make an Attribute Filter, which matches whole categories.&r"
	]
	quest.70DDB67ABBC9B4E1.quest_subtitle: "Smart parts for picky items"
	quest.70DDB67ABBC9B4E1.title: "&eSort It Out"
	quest.70DF494DEBCB80E4.quest_desc: [
		"Every &6End Portal Frame&r in this pack is an &5Unstable End Portal Frame&r: cracked, leaking void and &cunable to hold an Eye of Ender&r. The portal only lights once &ball 12&r frames have been stabilized."
		""
		"&cDon't force an eye in.&r The eye shatters and the void strikes back, harder each time. The first try stings; the &cfourth kills you&r, straight through armour, potions and even a &eTotem of Undying&r. It calms down by one step every &b20 minutes&r."
		""
		"&7Eyes already sitting in the frames are safe. They count again once their frame is stable.&r"
	]
	quest.70DF494DEBCB80E4.quest_subtitle: "Do not feed the portal"
	quest.70DF494DEBCB80E4.title: "&5Cracks in the Frame"
	quest.714C85B86043E27F.quest_desc: [
		"A &eBrass Hand&r is &eAndesite Alloy&r over &eBrass Sheets&r. Stack an &eElectron Tube&r, an &eAndesite Casing&r and the hand in a column for a &6Deployer&r."
		""
		"It acts like a player on the block &b2 blocks in front&r of it: placing blocks, using items, harvesting, even attacking. Right-click its front to hand it an item. Aim it at a &6Depot&r or &6Belt&r and it &aapplies its held item to whatever passes underneath&r."
		""
		"&cA Deployer that fills up with leftovers stops working&r, so pull them out with a funnel. &7Build three: the next quest needs them.&r"
	]
	quest.714C85B86043E27F.quest_subtitle: "A robot that thinks it's you"
	quest.714C85B86043E27F.title: "&aLend Me a Hand"
	quest.71710E5CEB7DBD94.quest_desc: [
		"&6Iron's Spells 'n Spellbooks&r is RPG-style magic: well over a hundred &dspells&r across nine schools. Spells come on &escrolls&r, scrolls get written into a &espell book&r, and casting costs &dmana&r."
		""
		"It all starts with &eArcane Essence&r. Look in dungeon, mineshaft, temple, outpost and shipwreck chests, magic structures, and the pockets of spellcasting mobs such as &cNecromancers&r and wizards."
		""
		"&aCraft a Book with one Arcane Essence&r to get &6Iron's Guidebook&r, the mod's own pamphlet. EMI has the crafting recipes; the guidebook and this chapter explain the stations."
		""
		"&7Iron's Lib comes along as a library. Its Patreon Transmog Table only offers cosmetics to the author's Patreon supporters.&r"
	]
	quest.71710E5CEB7DBD94.quest_subtitle: "There's more than meets the eye"
	quest.71710E5CEB7DBD94.title: "&5Spellbound"
	quest.71F727DE2C7DEA67.quest_desc: [
		"Willows don't grow wild. &aDrop an &eOak Sapling&r and a block of &eDeepslate&r close together into a &bwater source&r block. After a few sparks and a chime, a &eWillow Sapling&r floats up."
		""
		"&7It has to be plain Deepslate, not Cobbled Deepslate: smelt the cobbled kind or mine it with Silk Touch.&r You only do this once, since the tree drops more saplings."
		""
		"&aTip:&r use a &eGlass Bottle&r on a &eWillow Log&r for &eWillow Sap&r. It strips the log, and the sap tames &6Willow Hounds&r later."
	]
	quest.71F727DE2C7DEA67.quest_subtitle: "Some trees have to be asked nicely"
	quest.71F727DE2C7DEA67.title: "&2Coaxed from Still Water"
	quest.71FF3EF539AA0C44.quest_desc: [
		"&6Awoo Pie Moonshine&r ferments in the &6Fermentation Barrel&r from &eApple Juice&r with &eSugar&r, a &eHoney Bottle&r, &eCocoa Beans&r and a &eWine Bottle&r. It uses &b30%&r juice, so pour in a couple of apple juices first."
		""
		"Drink it for &bFerocity&r: for &b80 seconds&r every hit you land is a &acritical hit&r. Perfect before a boss fight."
		""
		"&7It ages like wine, so a cellar-aged bottle lasts longer.&r"
	]
	quest.71FF3EF539AA0C44.quest_subtitle: "Awoo!"
	quest.71FF3EF539AA0C44.title: "&cHowling Good Moonshine"
	quest.72037B367E7470EF.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Cooking Pot&r (5 iron ingots and a wooden shovel) has &b6 ingredient slots&r plus a slot for the bowl or bottle the meal is served in. A dish takes about &b45 seconds&r."
		""
		"&cIt needs heat below:&r set it on a Stove, a campfire or a magma block."
		""
		"Start with &eYeast&r: sugar, wheat and a water bucket, with a bowl in the container slot, makes &b12&r. Every dough needs it."
	]
	quest.72037B367E7470EF.quest_subtitle: "Yeast mode"
	quest.72037B367E7470EF.title: "&6Rising Action"
	quest.721DA607D2BF8731.quest_desc: [
		"Cook &aevery Farm \\& Charm dish&r, &b30&r in all: the soups, teas, roasts and bakes from the Stove, Cooking Pot, Roaster and Crafting Bowl, plus the Farmer Salad and the Farmer's Breakfast. EMI lists them all."
		""
		"The mod rewards you with &b2 Scarecrows&r, which can't be crafted from nothing. A scarecrow gives crops within &b8 blocks&r an extra growth tick every so often. After that, a &eBarley Bale&r, a scarecrow and 4 sticks craft two more."
		""
		"&7Still hungry? Bakery and Candlelight have their own collect-them-all advancements, each with a banner that buffs everyone standing near it.&r"
	]
	quest.721DA607D2BF8731.quest_subtitle: "The whole menu, start to finish"
	quest.721DA607D2BF8731.title: "&6From Farm to Table"
	quest.72800A344A63D036.quest_desc: [
		"Every finished quest also earns &bvillage reputation&r: &b2&r for easy, &b4&r for medium and &b7&r for hard. Your standing climbs from Stranger to &aAcquaintance&r (25), &aFriend&r (75), &aHonored&r (150) and &aRevered&r (300); the last two also earn you a title."
		""
		"Check it in the &bJournal&r. Bigger goals come from &6Village Projects&r, which everyone can help with, and &6Situations&r such as raids or a missing child. Some quests even send you to a &6Bountiful&r bounty board."
	]
	quest.72800A344A63D036.quest_subtitle: "Everybody knows your name"
	quest.72800A344A63D036.title: "&aA Pillar of the Community"
	quest.72B0A39797291E51.quest_desc: [
		"&6Noble&r needs &b800 hearts&r plus a &eGraveyard&r (3 headstones), an &eInn&r (4 beds, a jukebox and a smoker) and an &eInfirmary&r (brewing stand, cauldron, bed and flower pot). It unlocks the &aBirth limit&r rule."
		""
		"Beyond that: &6Mayor&r (1200 hearts, 20 villagers, a Library and an Armory; unlocks the Marriage limit) and &6Monarch&r (2500 hearts, 30 villagers, a Prison, a Blacksmith and the &cGrim Reaper&r slain). &aGift a Cake&r to a married villager couple to grow the population."
	]
	quest.72B0A39797291E51.quest_subtitle: "Rank: Noble"
	quest.72B0A39797291E51.title: "&6Blue Blood"
	quest.72E8795B65D6E4C9.quest_desc: [
		"Duck your head under &dLiquid Fluxia&r and the stone lets go of you: you &bsink through solid blocks&r. Sneak to drop faster, jump to rise."
		""
		"&cIt lasts 6 seconds after your eyes leave the Fluxia, about 15 blocks of drift. If you're still inside rock when it runs out, you suffocate.&r Pop out into open air and it ends at once. Bedrock and &eWarded Slate&r stop you."
		""
		"Under the oasis pool lies a sealed vault: two chests of shards, fluxite, amethyst coal, astralite and diamonds beside a &eBlock of Astralite&r, each with a chance of a &eFluxia Tablet&r or even an &eEnchanted Golden Apple&r. The pool floor is warded, but one of its four &dweeping stones&r has nothing behind it. Look for the one the willow shades."
	]
	quest.72E8795B65D6E4C9.quest_subtitle: "Something is sealed under the pool"
	quest.72E8795B65D6E4C9.title: "&bUnmoored"
	quest.72F2EF8A4F1F930B.quest_desc: [
		"The light machine. The &6Light Field&r is &e4 Light gems&r, glass, Kivi, a &eGlowstone&r block and a &6Machine Base&r."
		""
		"It &aprevents natural mob spawns in a cube&r around itself, reaching &b24 blocks&r out in this pack (hover over it in your inventory and hold &bLeft Ctrl&r to see the radius). It also stops zombie sieges, keeps Endermen from teleporting into the area and stops Phantoms spawning on players inside it."
		""
		"&7One of these makes a base far safer, no torches required.&r"
	]
	quest.72F2EF8A4F1F930B.quest_subtitle: "Monsters not welcome"
	quest.72F2EF8A4F1F930B.title: "&fNo Vacancy"
	quest.73105A450856754E.quest_desc: [
		"Want to fly on day one? The &6Balloon on a Stick&r needs no XyCraft materials at all: just a &eLead&r, any &eWool&r and any &eLog&r, shapeless."
		""
		"Place it and a balloon ties itself to you, giving you &acreative-style flight&r while you stay within &b9 blocks&r of the stake. &cStray too far and the string snaps&r, and down you go."
		""
		"&7Perfect for building tall things. Pick it up and move it as you go.&r"
	]
	quest.73105A450856754E.quest_subtitle: "How did you inflate a wool balloon?"
	quest.73105A450856754E.title: "&bUp, Up and Away"
	quest.737501122E774D21.quest_desc: [
		"Broad tools need heavy parts: a &eHammer Head&r (8 units), a &eTough Handle&r and &eTough Binding&r (3 each) and a &eLarge Plate&r (4)."
		""
		"The &eVein Hammer&r is a hammer head, a tough handle, a tough binding and a large plate. It &abreaks connected blocks of the same type&r around the one you mine, perfect for ore veins. Want a 3x3 instead? Build a &eSledge Hammer&r."
		""
		"&7Other options: the Excavator (shovel), Broad Axe (fells trees), Scythe and Cleaver.&r"
	]
	quest.737501122E774D21.quest_subtitle: "Stop! Mining time"
	quest.737501122E774D21.title: "&aHammer Time"
	quest.73775A0B6D7F7D83.quest_desc: [
		"Combine any &eleather armor&r piece with one &eArcane Essence&r for &eWandering Magician&r gear. Each piece adds &b25 max mana&r, &b100&r for the full set."
		""
		"Running dry mid-fight? Brew an &eAwkward Potion&r with &eArcane Essence&r for &dInstant Mana&r, then step it up with Glowstone Dust, an Amethyst Shard and finally an Amethyst Cluster."
		""
		"&7The &eAmethyst Resonance Charm&r&7 (an amethyst shard and leather) is the cheapest necklace: +15% mana regen.&r"
	]
	quest.73775A0B6D7F7D83.quest_subtitle: "+25 max mana per piece"
	quest.73775A0B6D7F7D83.title: "&eRobes on a Budget"
	quest.7381677620619DF3.quest_desc: [
		"Your village rank depends on your &btotal hearts&r with everyone living there, plus the buildings the village has."
		""
		"&6Merchant&r needs &b400 total hearts&r, a &eBig House&r (4 beds) and a &eStorage&r room (a lectern and 4 chests). Register both with the Blueprint. It unlocks &aTaxes&r in the Rules tab."
	]
	quest.7381677620619DF3.quest_subtitle: "Rank: Merchant"
	quest.7381677620619DF3.title: "&aMoving Up"
	quest.738D73328A305C13.quest_desc: [
		"&eAncient Tomes&r each hold one enchantment. Combine a tome with an item that &balready has&r that enchantment in an &6Anvil&r for &a+1 level&r, up to &bone level past the maximum&r. The tooltip shows the cap."
		""
		"Find them in &bMonster Boxes&r below Y=0, and in bastion treasure, dungeon, stronghold library and mansion chests."
		""
		"&7Protection, Mending and Silk Touch have no tomes. For the rest of enchanting, see the Apotheosis chapter.&r"
	]
	quest.738D73328A305C13.quest_subtitle: "Old books, new tricks"
	quest.738D73328A305C13.title: "&dTome Raider"
	quest.740F35C08AA09BD0.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Willow Fen&r takes over the wettest swamps: dark water, mist and drooping fen trees. A &6Nature's Compass&r finds it fastest."
		""
		"Pick up &eMoonlilies&r (you'll want them in the Spirit Realm much later) and &ePeat&r, which burns as fuel and turns cobblestone into &eFenstone&r. &6Frogs&r and &6Bats&r live here, and both can become familiars. Tame a &6Willow Hound&r with &eBottles of Willow Sap&r and it fetches loose items to your feet."
		""
		"&7Sunken Ruins hide a cache of peat, sap and moonlilies that sometimes holds a few Amethyst Coal, and now and then an empty Fluxia Tablet.&r"
	]
	quest.740F35C08AA09BD0.quest_subtitle: "The Willow Fen"
	quest.740F35C08AA09BD0.title: "&2Where the Water Stands Still"
	quest.7421CC513EE98C87.quest_desc: [
		"Vanilla villages are gone. &6Integrated Villages&r adds &b12 themed villages&r chosen by biome: tavern towns with windmills in taigas, a marketstead in the plains, an oasis kingdom in the desert, clockwork towns in the badlands, a sunken village in swamps and more."
		""
		"Look for the village &6Waystone&r (most villages have one) and activate it, so you can warp back later. The villagers are full &6MCA&r villagers (see &6Starting a Family&r), and some villages have working &6Create&r machines."
		""
		"&7Don't bother searching jungles, mushroom fields or snowy plains: no ground village grows there.&r"
	]
	quest.7421CC513EE98C87.quest_subtitle: "Twelve flavours of neighbour"
	quest.7421CC513EE98C87.title: "&aNot Your Average Village"
	quest.7427FA2A8BFCE380.quest_desc: [
		"The &cIllusioner&r never spawns on its own in vanilla, but Illager Forts usually hold a few (Abandoned Temples can too). It turns invisible, splits into &bdecoy copies&r and casts &cBlindness&r on you, then snipes with a bow."
		""
		"The copies are only illusions: keep moving, keep your shield up and go for the one you can actually hit. &7The Pirate Junk ships in the Seven Seas branch can have Illusioner spawners too.&r"
	]
	quest.7427FA2A8BFCE380.quest_subtitle: "...and now there are five of you"
	quest.7427FA2A8BFCE380.title: "&9Now You See Me"
	quest.7472A99AB27E4F94.quest_desc: [
		"Three &eIron Ingots&r and two sticks make an &6Iron Pickaxe&r. It's the key to the good ores: &egold&r, &eredstone&r and &ediamonds&r."
		""
		"&7Diamonds, the Nether and enchanting are the first stops in &6Kitted Out&7, the next chapter.&r"
	]
	quest.7472A99AB27E4F94.title: "Pick of the Litter"
	quest.74749CF00FF224E2.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Storage Request Table&r (crafting table, gold and a &eStorage Inventory&r) shows everything on the network. Take, deposit and craft - the grid pulls ingredients straight from storage."
		""
		"Search tricks: &b@mod&r, &b#tooltip&r and &b$tag&r."
		""
		"&aNext steps:&r Import, Export and Processing cables automate furnaces and farms, and a &eStorage Remote&r (bind it by right-clicking the Root) opens the network from anywhere - even other dimensions, as long as the Root's chunk stays loaded."
	]
	quest.74749CF00FF224E2.quest_subtitle: "Never dig through chests again"
	quest.74749CF00FF224E2.title: "&6Ask and You Shall Receive"
	quest.748A53D3597FD3BD.quest_desc: [
		"&eTraveler's Gear&r is modifiable armor you make in a normal &bcrafting grid&r from &eLeather&r and ingots of a meltable metal like &eCopper&r, &eIron&r or &eGold&r. The metal you use becomes the plating. The &eGoggles&r also need glass panes."
		""
		"Like your tools, the set takes &bmodifiers&r, and the boots come with built-in snow walking. &7It's a cheap set to carry you until Plate Armor.&r"
	]
	quest.748A53D3597FD3BD.quest_subtitle: "Leather, metal and a dash of style"
	quest.748A53D3597FD3BD.title: "&eDressed for the Road"
	quest.74DAF8BB4DEE29F8.quest_desc: [
		"&eHauntbound&r armour has &bdiamond-tier&r protection and toughness, and &cno crafting recipe&r. Pieces come from &eLoot Bags&r, the tombstone skeletons (chestplate, leggings and boots only) and the armoured skeleton guards the Horseman raises, who wear the full set."
		""
		"Each piece you wear has a &b25%&r chance to block each point of sanity loss. The &afull set&r gives &dMental Fortitude&r: your sanity &bstays at 100&r, fog or no fog."
		""
		"&7Collect all four and the mod's advancement hands you two Completionist Banners.&r"
	]
	quest.74DAF8BB4DEE29F8.quest_subtitle: "Armour for the mind, too"
	quest.74DAF8BB4DEE29F8.title: "&5Hauntbound and Ready"
	quest.7506F0F8E4268B9E.quest_desc: [
		"A &ePrecision Mechanism&r and a &eStock Link&r make &b2&r &6Factory Gauges&r, the brains of an automated factory."
		""
		"On a &6Packager&r, a gauge &akeeps that inventory restocked&r from the network. Anywhere else it watches the network: when an item drops below your target (&bhold right-click&r to set it), it &arequests the ingredients&r be sent to an address so a machine can make more. The products must come back into a linked inventory."
		""
		"Chain gauges into a board for multi-step recipes. For crafting-table recipes, a gauge can &aauto-arrange the ingredients&r so its packages unpack straight into a &b3x3, wrench-connected&r grid of Mechanical Crafters."
		""
		"&7A Re-Packager (a Packager converted in the crafting grid) merges split orders back into one box.&r"
	]
	quest.7506F0F8E4268B9E.quest_subtitle: "High Logistics"
	quest.7506F0F8E4268B9E.title: "&6The Factory Must Grow"
	quest.755C00A94A7B00E1.quest_desc: [
		"&6Highland Cattle&r are shaggy. &aShear them&r for &b1-3 Rustic Wool&r, and the coat grows back after they graze."
		""
		"Their cousins have different coats: &6Umbra Cattle&r in Dark Forests give &eChambray Wool&r, and &6Warped Cattle&r in the Nether's Warped Forests give &eWarped Wool&r."
		""
		"&7Patterned wool makes beds, carpets and Pine Sofas.&r"
	]
	quest.755C00A94A7B00E1.quest_subtitle: "They grow it back, honest"
	quest.755C00A94A7B00E1.title: "&6Hair of the Cow"
	quest.757925D92D8DC937.quest_desc: [
		"Craft a &eDormant Deepshelf&r from Cracked Deepslate Tiles and Books, then infuse it at &b60 Eterna, 40%+ Quanta and 40%+ Arcana&r."
		""
		"A &6Deepshelf&r gives 5 Eterna up to &b70&r plus Quanta and Arcana. Add an &eEcho Shard&r and Candles for an Echoing Deepshelf (more Arcana), or a &eSoul Lantern&r and Sculk for a Soul-Touched one (more Quanta). Both reach max &b75&r, so Summit."
	]
	quest.757925D92D8DC937.quest_subtitle: "Deepshelf"
	quest.757925D92D8DC937.title: "&3Delving Into Darkness"
	quest.75A2881A9EC0557B.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Enchantment Library&r (4 Ender Chests, 4 infused shelves, an Enchanting Table) eats enchanted books and stores their enchantments as points."
		""
		"&bClick&r an entry to pull out one level at a time, &bShift-click&r for the most you can. You can only extract up to the highest level you ever put in, and it holds up to level &bXVI&r."
		""
		"&7At Pinnacle it can be infused into the Library of Alexandria (level XXXI).&r"
	]
	quest.75A2881A9EC0557B.quest_subtitle: "Enchantment Library"
	quest.75A2881A9EC0557B.title: "&5Shelf Storage"
	quest.75F03B7EC595A39F.quest_desc: [
		"A small ruined temple in &btaigas, windswept hills and mountains&r. &cStrays&r spawn around the &6Abandoned Temple&r, so expect Slowness arrows, along with armoured skeletons and sometimes an &cIllusioner&r."
		""
		"It's a &atreasure-map hub&r: its map chest holds a map to a &6Monastery&r, the &6Mining Complex&r or the &6Thornborn Towers&r."
	]
	quest.75F03B7EC595A39F.quest_subtitle: "The congregation has gone a bit stray"
	quest.75F03B7EC595A39F.title: "&7Forgotten Faith"
	quest.7643BF2F63CD4932.quest_desc: [
		"On a server you can marry another &aplayer&r. Type &b/mca propose <name>&r; they answer with &b/mca accept <your name>&r or &b/mca reject <your name>&r."
		""
		"Married players can use &b/mca procreate&r (your partner has &b10 seconds&r to accept), and &b/mca separate&r ends it. &cYou can't do any of this while married to a villager.&r"
	]
	quest.7643BF2F63CD4932.quest_subtitle: "Server romance"
	quest.7643BF2F63CD4932.title: "&dTwo Players, One Heart"
	quest.7648A6DECCEB4750.quest_desc: [
		"Coloured clay balls shape into coloured pottery on the Table. Make &aall nine Red pieces&r: Vase, Bud Vase, Cupella, Garden Pot, Square Pot, Plant Bowl, Planter, Urn and Amphore. That's 9 Red Clay Balls, about three blocks' worth."
		""
		"&7Smelt spare coloured clay into bricks for colourful walls (and Timber Frame fillings). Each colour has its own complete-set advancement if you want to collect them all.&r"
	]
	quest.7648A6DECCEB4750.quest_subtitle: "The full red set"
	quest.7648A6DECCEB4750.title: "&cRuby Row"
	quest.7660BC6C968DBF21.quest_desc: [
		"&6Ore Geysers&r are small XyCraft structures scattered across the Overworld, mostly on the surface in plains, forests, hills, deserts and similar biomes, with rarer ones underground."
		""
		"&7Right now they're scenery: the geyser block drops nothing and the machine meant to tap it hasn't been added to XyCraft yet. Still, it's a nice thing to stumble on.&r"
	]
	quest.7660BC6C968DBF21.quest_subtitle: "A landmark from the future"
	quest.7660BC6C968DBF21.title: "&6Thar She Blows"
	quest.7684914F94FB8CCE.quest_desc: [
		"Wild &6Starbuncles&r roam wooded areas and are shy, but they let you approach while you hold a &eGold Nugget&r. Toss one the nugget: it grabs it and vanishes, leaving a &eStarbuncle Token&r. Put the token on the Apparatus with &e4 Gold Ingots&r for a &eStarbuncle Charm&r, then use the charm on the ground."
		""
		"With the &6Dominion Wand&r: Starbuncle → chest to &adeposit there&r; chest → Starbuncle to &atake from it&r. Item Frames or Item Scrolls on chests filter what moves."
		""
		"&7Use another charm on one to stack them, and it carries more per trip.&r"
	]
	quest.7684914F94FB8CCE.quest_subtitle: "Paid in gold nuggets"
	quest.7684914F94FB8CCE.title: "&eThe Cutest Hopper"
	quest.76B86C70AE4E2B36.quest_desc: [
		"Put a &6Mechanical Press&r over a &6Basin&r instead of a depot and it &bcompacts&r: any filled 2x2 or 3x3 crafting recipe, like 9 Iron Nuggets into an Ingot."
		""
		"It also has special recipes. &eRenewable Andesite&r: 2 Flint, 1 Gravel and a bit of Lava (pour a bucket into the basin) make Andesite, feeding straight back into your alloy."
	]
	quest.76B86C70AE4E2B36.quest_subtitle: "Press, meet Basin"
	quest.76B86C70AE4E2B36.title: "&eCompactification"
	quest.76C60DFBA0DF5A57.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Geode-Encased Bookshelf of Stability&r grants &dQuantic Stability&r: Quanta can only push power up, never down. Max out Quanta with no downside."
		""
		"It needs &eBudding Amethyst&r, which you make by infusing an &eAmethyst Block&r at &b60 Eterna, 30-50% Quanta and 50%+ Arcana&r. Add a Bookshelf and Calcite."
	]
	quest.76C60DFBA0DF5A57.quest_subtitle: "No more bad rolls"
	quest.76C60DFBA0DF5A57.title: "&eQuantic Stability"
	quest.76CB138022DBFEA6.quest_desc: [
		"A &eDiamond Block&r on &6VoidShimmer Goo&r becomes &eRaw Celestigem Ore&r in &b48 seconds&r. It drops &eCelestigem&r directly, no smelting."
		""
		"Celestigem gear swaps durability for &bForge Energy&r (&b10,000 FE&r each), so it never breaks, it just runs flat. Keep your &ePocket Generator&r fuelled."
		""
		"It also unlocks &aDrop Teleport&r (bind a tool to a chest and its drops go there), Elytra and Night Vision upgrades, and the Advanced machines (all but the Swapper, which needs Eclipse Alloy)."
	]
	quest.76CB138022DBFEA6.quest_subtitle: "Tier 3 material"
	quest.76CB138022DBFEA6.title: "&bDiamonds Are a Goo's Best Friend"
	quest.76DF13402EC7B00B.quest_desc: [
		"Smith your copper station with a &eNetherite Ingot&r and a &eNetherite Upgrade&r template for the &6Netherite Brewing Station&r."
		""
		"It &askips the brewing events entirely&r and always brews at top quality, so you can start a batch and walk away."
		""
		"It also unlocks the strongest recipes: &6Jameson Malt&r, &6Smokey Reverie&r and the throwable &6Dark Brew&r."
	]
	quest.76DF13402EC7B00B.quest_subtitle: "No more panic"
	quest.76DF13402EC7B00B.title: "&5Master Brewer"
	quest.7723007F047C6ABB.quest_desc: [
		"The &eFlimsy Journal&r is the cheapest spell book: &e2 Copper Ingots&r, &e6 Paper&r and a &eString&r. It holds &b5 spells&r and gives no bonuses."
		""
		"The &eIronbound Tome&r (chains, leather and paper) holds &b6&r. For casting, any spell book you find in a chest works too."
		""
		"&7Don't get attached. Better books come soon, and even a journal can later be expanded with slot upgrades.&r"
	]
	quest.7723007F047C6ABB.quest_subtitle: "5 spell slots"
	quest.7723007F047C6ABB.title: "&eDear Diary"
	quest.7763161666E74801.quest_desc: [
		"You met &6Waystones&r in &6First Light&r. A &eWarp Stone&r (emerald, amethyst shards, ender pearl) takes the network with you: &bhold right-click&r to warp to any waystone you've activated, from anywhere."
		""
		"It costs the same XP as walking up to a waystone. A one-use &eWarp Scroll&r or a warp plate is &afree&r, and so is any trip to a Global waystone."
		""
		"&eSharestones&r link to same-colour sharestones for everyone with no activation - great for a server hub. Carry an &eEpitaph&r and dying leaves a one-use waystone where your Corpse lies."
		""
		"&7Want one at home? A Warp Stone with &eObsidian&7 and &eStone Bricks&7 makes your own &eWaystone&7.&r"
	]
	quest.7763161666E74801.quest_subtitle: "Have stone, will travel"
	quest.7763161666E74801.title: "&dWarp Speed"
	quest.776F8F158580D52D.quest_desc: [
		"The biome is dotted with &6Tombstones&r, and most of them are &cawake&r (the big ones stand in Cemeteries). &aRight-click an awake one with an empty hand&r and up to &b3 skeletons&r climb out, wearing Spectral Jack o'Lanterns and swinging &eSpectral War Axes&r. Some wear &eHauntbound&r armour, which they can drop."
		""
		"As long as at least one skeleton rises, the grave &aalways drops an Essence of Undead&r, sometimes with Spectral Essence, a &eLoot Bag&r or Luminous Water."
		""
		"&cDon't punch an awake tombstone&r: it still raises the skeletons, but costs you &b5&r damage. A raised tombstone goes quiet. Feed it a &eSpectral Essence&r to wake it again, or stay nearby after dark and it may wake on its own."
	]
	quest.776F8F158580D52D.quest_subtitle: "Rest in pieces"
	quest.776F8F158580D52D.title: "&cThey're Coming Out of the Ground"
	quest.77AEBFEDC5178921.quest_desc: [
		"&6Blazes&r spawn in &6Nether Fortresses&r - in this pack those are &6YUNG's Better Fortresses&r: bigger, meaner and full of loot. Kill Blazes for &eBlaze Rods&r."
		""
		"A rod makes the &6Brewing Stand&r; ground into &eBlaze Powder&r it fuels brewing and turns Ender Pearls into &eEyes of Ender&r, which &6Flux Networks&r needs."
		""
		"&7Blazes hate snowballs. The &6Into the Unknown&7 chapter has more on fortresses.&r"
	]
	quest.77AEBFEDC5178921.quest_subtitle: "Blazing a trail"
	quest.77AEBFEDC5178921.title: "&6Rod Trip"
	quest.77C0617E2A95E4A5.quest_desc: [
		"&eHot Air Envelopes&r are the skin of a balloon: &e2 Wool&r and &e2 Sticks&r make &b4&r (a &6Deployer&r pressing sticks into wool gives 3 per wool). Coloured wool gives coloured envelopes."
		""
		"Build a hollow, &aairtight shell&r above the spot where your burner will sit: hot air fills it from the top down. Envelopes weigh almost nothing, plain wool is airtight too, and anything inside the shell eats into its volume."
		""
		"&7Shafts can be encased in envelope to pass through the balloon wall without leaking. Shears take envelopes down fast.&r"
	]
	quest.77C0617E2A95E4A5.quest_subtitle: "Wool, sticks, ambition"
	quest.77C0617E2A95E4A5.title: "&eFabric of the Sky"
	quest.7800B20C709CB9FC.quest_desc: [
		"&6Village&r and &6pillager&r chests have their own relics. The &eChef's Hat&r makes the mobs you kill sometimes drop &eRaw Meatballs&r: cook them for a decent meal."
		""
		"The same chests give the &eHunting Belt&r (stronger pets, extra charm slots) and the &eRider Flute&r, which stores a tamed mount so you can call it back anywhere. The flute also shows up in chests in cave biomes."
	]
	quest.7800B20C709CB9FC.quest_subtitle: "Village chests, head slot"
	quest.7800B20C709CB9FC.title: "&fKiss the Cook"
	quest.7806E39A82F33883.quest_desc: [
		"Every network has a stress &bcapacity&r in SU, set by its sources at their own speed, and an &bimpact&r from its machines. Impact is &bper RPM&r, so spinning a machine twice as fast costs twice the stress. Gears never create power."
		""
		"If impact beats capacity the network is &cOverstressed&r and &call of it stops&r. Fix it by adding sources or slowing machines down."
		""
		"A &6Speedometer&r is a Compass on Andesite Casing; convert it to a &6Stressometer&r in the crafting grid. Look at one with Goggles on for exact numbers."
	]
	quest.7806E39A82F33883.quest_subtitle: "SU times RPM, the one rule"
	quest.7806E39A82F33883.title: "&bStress for Nerds"
	quest.7815E6C6101019D5.quest_desc: [
		"Reach the &6Citadel&r and bring a &eCinderous Soulcaller&r: &e6 Cinder Essence&r, &e2 Netherite Scrap&r and an &eEcho Shard&r."
		""
		"Find the &dCinderous Soul Rune&r deep inside and &aright-click the Soulcaller near it&r. It's used up and the boss appears. Anywhere else, nothing echoes back."
		""
		"&7Search the bookshelves on the way for Ruined Books and fragments.&r"
	]
	quest.7815E6C6101019D5.quest_subtitle: "Something answers"
	quest.7815E6C6101019D5.title: "&cCalling the Cinders"
	quest.78394E8452713AF6.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Alchemist Cauldron&r is a cauldron, &e4 Iron Ingots&r, &e2 Arcane Essence&r and a &eCinder Essence&r. It holds water, potions, inks and blood. A &eglass bottle&r scoops out &b250 mB&r."
		""
		"&aRecycle scrolls:&r right-click a water-filled cauldron with a spare scroll for a &b50%&r chance at a bottle's worth of ink of the scroll's rarity."
		""
		"&aUpgrade ink:&r four bottles of one ink plus a catalyst make one bottle of the next rarity: Copper Ingot for Uncommon, Iron for Rare, Gold for Epic, an Amethyst Shard for Legendary. It also brews &delixirs&r on top of potions."
	]
	quest.78394E8452713AF6.quest_subtitle: "No fire needed"
	quest.78394E8452713AF6.title: "&6Toil and Trouble"
	quest.785C42C4C5FA9DC2.quest_desc: [
		"&6Meadow&r doesn't add a new biome. It rebuilds the vanilla &bMeadow&r: the grassy slopes just below the mountain peaks."
		""
		"Look for &ePine&r and &eAlpine Birch&r forests, cotton-grass, &eLimestone&r boulders and herds of shaggy &6Highland Cattle&r. Chalets, chapels, logging camps and observation posts are built only here."
		""
		"&7Wilder Nature's tiny Minisheep also live in Meadows, and nowhere else.&r"
	]
	quest.785C42C4C5FA9DC2.quest_subtitle: "Alpine Paradise"
	quest.785C42C4C5FA9DC2.title: "&aThe Hills Are Alive"
	quest.78913A9B1FDD0D3E.quest_desc: [
		"Add &e3 Iron Ingots&r to a log, two planks and a stick. The &eIron Lance&r hits for &b6&r instead of 3, with nearly double the durability of the wooden one."
		""
		"Every lance shows its &bAttack&r and &bWeight&r in the tooltip: heavier lances shove targets further, but the charge runs out sooner. &cHitting a raised shield&r costs your lance durability instead of hurting the target."
		""
		"&7Meet another lancer head-on and it becomes a joust: the faster, harder rider unhorses the other.&r"
	]
	quest.78913A9B1FDD0D3E.quest_subtitle: "A proper weapon"
	quest.78913A9B1FDD0D3E.title: "&fLance Corporal"
	quest.789311C776C803D9.quest_desc: [
		"The biome is a builder's graveyard. &eHollow Logs&r give dark planks with a full wood set and &eHollow Windows&r. &eGravestone&r, the local stone, makes bricks, chiseled, cracked and mossy blocks."
		""
		"Mining Gravestone gives &eCobbled Gravestone&r, which works as stone for tools and furnaces. &aSmelt it&r back into Gravestone, then craft &b4&r Gravestone into &b4&r &eGravestone Bricks&r. EMI and the stonecutter have the rest."
		""
		"&7For the full look, add a Coffin (a Chest ringed with Gravestone) and some Wrought Iron Fence.&r"
	]
	quest.789311C776C803D9.quest_subtitle: "Gothic chic"
	quest.789311C776C803D9.title: "&6Home Sweet Hollow"
	quest.78ACC716C44332E4.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Crafting Bowl&r (wooden slabs, a stick and an iron ingot) mixes things by hand. Right-click the ingredients in, then &ahold right-click to stir&r. It takes &b200 stirs&r; fast, steady stirring finishes in about &b8 seconds&r, and stopping just pauses it."
		""
		"&eDough&r: flour, yeast and a water bucket. &eButter&r: one milk bucket makes 4, and nearly every roasted dish wants it."
		""
		"&7Chop dough on the Cutting Board (or mince it) for Raw Pasta.&r"
	]
	quest.78ACC716C44332E4.quest_subtitle: "Two hundred stirs and counting"
	quest.78ACC716C44332E4.title: "&6Whisk Business"
	quest.78C1FC8FE1CFB362.quest_desc: [
		"&6Oak Shingles&r come from &eOak Slabs&r and &eOak Planks&r, and craft into stairs and slabs for proper roof slopes. &6Terracotta Shingles&r are stonecut from plain &eTerracotta&r, and mixing both kinds makes &6Patchwork Shingles&r."
		""
		"Or go rustic: &e4 Wheat&r make four &6Thatch&r blocks. Thatch &bages on its own&r (fresh, weathered, drying, aged), but very slowly. A &eWater Bottle&r pushes it one stage on, a &eHoe&r takes it one stage back, and &eWheat&r makes it fresh again."
		""
		"Frame, fill, roof: &ayou can now build a real Let's Do cottage.&r"
	]
	quest.78C1FC8FE1CFB362.quest_subtitle: "A house is only as good as its hat"
	quest.78C1FC8FE1CFB362.title: "&6Raise the Roof"
	quest.78DFFEFDBCDABCE6.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Gramophone&r takes &eGold Ingots&r, &eWooden Slabs&r and a &eJukebox&r. Insert a disc and play it. Its horn pulses to the beat."
		""
		"&aRight-click toggles repeat mode&r and &bSneak-right-click&r takes the disc out. It gives off a redstone signal while it plays."
		""
		"&7Furniture adds two discs of its own. Like the vanilla discs, they drop when a Skeleton's arrow kills a Creeper, and a Trash Bag very rarely hides one. Try disc 11 if you like being spooked.&r"
	]
	quest.78DFFEFDBCDABCE6.quest_subtitle: "Now that's what I call furniture"
	quest.78DFFEFDBCDABCE6.title: "&dEarworm"
	quest.7901B3E19A1EB8C8.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Plague Asylum&r is &bburied deep, around y 0&r, under forests, taigas and mountains. You won't see it from the surface: a &eSmall Blimp&r map or a &eWoodland Explorer Map&r helps."
		""
		"&cMind the evoker-fang trap&r, the witches, the Wither Skeletons and the skeletons that arrive with a splash of &cHarming&r. The potion chests are full of odd brews like &dStrange Concoction&r and &dQuickest Way Out&r. &7Read the label before you drink.&r"
		""
		"Other chests hold diamonds, music discs and Woodland Mansion loot."
	]
	quest.7901B3E19A1EB8C8.quest_subtitle: "Take two of these and don't call me"
	quest.7901B3E19A1EB8C8.title: "&2Bedside Manner"
	quest.79702A2C4DB07E04.quest_desc: [
		"Build a working machine that moves: a sweeping crop harvester, a tree-felling saw, or a drill bore on a piston."
		""
		"Glue a &eChest&r or &eBarrel&r onto it and it &acollects everything the tools break&r. Keep contraptions under &b2048 blocks&r; Obsidian can't be moved at all."
		""
		"&aYou now know how to make the world do the work.&r"
	]
	quest.79702A2C4DB07E04.quest_subtitle: "It's alive! (And it works)"
	quest.79702A2C4DB07E04.title: "&6Moving with Purpose"
	quest.797035AE991660DB.quest_desc: [
		"Combine a &eWater Bucket&r with a &eSpectral Essence&r for &b4&r &eLuminous Water&r (you keep the bucket)."
		""
		"Drink one for &b+6 sanity&r, or &aright-click an infected plant&r with it to cleanse every plant within &b4 blocks&r of it."
		""
		"&7More importantly, it's half of the key to the Horseman. Keep some aside.&r"
	]
	quest.797035AE991660DB.quest_subtitle: "Holy water, minus the priest"
	quest.797035AE991660DB.title: "&bLiquid Light"
	quest.797075B70D8F1BCC.quest_desc: [
		"&6Sophisticated Backpacks&r: four &eLeather&r, four &eString&r and a &eChest&r make a &6Backpack&r with &b27 slots&r."
		""
		"Right-click it in hand or press &bB&r to open it. &bSneak and right-click&r the ground to place it as a block."
		""
		"Bigger tiers and upgrades (pickup, magnet, feeding...) are in the &6Kitted Out&r chapter."
	]
	quest.797075B70D8F1BCC.quest_subtitle: "Pockets, but bigger"
	quest.797075B70D8F1BCC.title: "&6Pack It Up"
	quest.79780653C0004A32.quest_desc: [
		"&eOre Miner&r mines an entire connected vein at once (up to &b64 blocks&r on Ferricore). To install it, put the pickaxe and the upgrade into a &6Smithing Table&r. &aNo template needed.&r"
		""
		"Press &bV&r to switch all of a tool's abilities off and on. &bShift + right-click&r the tool opens &6Tool Settings&r: left-click an icon to toggle it, right-click it to bind a key or tweak it."
		""
		"&7Ability 'stopped working'? You probably pressed V.&r"
	]
	quest.79780653C0004A32.quest_subtitle: "One block in, the whole vein out"
	quest.79780653C0004A32.title: "&aVein Glory"
	quest.79B97494A034B74E.quest_desc: [
		"Mix a &eDye&r with &b250 mB&r of water in an unheated &6Mechanical Mixer&r to get &eLiquid Dye&r. Heated mixing turns it back into the dye item."
		""
		"Items and mobs that touch it get &acoloured&r (sheep included). A fan blowing through it does &bBulk Coloring&r, and even dyes the armour mobs are wearing. Liquid Dye meeting lava makes &eConcrete&r of that colour."
		""
		"&7Liquid Black Dye is the ink for Enchantment Industry's Printer.&r"
	]
	quest.79B97494A034B74E.quest_subtitle: "Paint, by the bucket"
	quest.79B97494A034B74E.title: "&eDye Hard"
	quest.79FA14B5F1FD76E8.quest_desc: [
		"The &eAnglers Hat&r can't be crafted. It turns up rarely in &bFloating Debris&r, in the &eFishing Net&r's bonus loot and in &eSoaked Bags&r, usually a bit worn. &aThe Fishing Net's bonus roll is your best bet&r, so keep scooping."
		""
		"Wear it for &b+1 Luck&r. &aLuck stacks&r with fish meals, the &eMelon Cocktail&r and Lili's Completionist Banner for the best fishing loot."
	]
	quest.79FA14B5F1FD76E8.quest_subtitle: "It's not a fashion choice"
	quest.79FA14B5F1FD76E8.title: "&aLucky Hat"
	quest.7A16E51109FFE4BA.quest_desc: [
		"XyCraft's signature look: &e2 Kivi&r and &e2 gems&r of one colour, placed diagonally in a 2x2, make &e2 cloud Kivi Bricks&r in that colour. The same trick with &eAluminum&r makes cloud Aluminum Bricks."
		""
		"Put any cloud block in a &6Stonecutter&r to swap between &atiles, pillars and trims&r of the same colour. Plain Kivi also cuts into bricks, tiles, smooth Kivi and more."
		""
		"&7This quest asks for the blue ones, but every colour works the same way. Four gems in a 2x2 make Inverted Bricks, which cut into matte and shiny Xychorium blocks.&r"
	]
	quest.7A16E51109FFE4BA.quest_subtitle: "Kivi with a glow"
	quest.7A16E51109FFE4BA.title: "&bOn Cloud Nine"
	quest.7A34B2DA8C7C239B.quest_desc: [
		"&6Pipez&r moves items, fluids and power. &eItem Pipes&r (iron, redstone, dropper) come &b16&r at a time; &eFluid&r pipes use a bucket and &eEnergy&r pipes a redstone block."
		""
		"Pipes connect on their own but &cmove nothing&r until you set an extracting end: &asneak + right-click the pipe end touching the source with the Pipe Wrench&r. Click that end for its settings."
		""
		"&7The Gas Pipe needs Mekanism, which isn't in this pack.&r"
	]
	quest.7A34B2DA8C7C239B.quest_subtitle: "It's a series of tubes"
	quest.7A34B2DA8C7C239B.title: "&6Plumbing 101"
	quest.7A426D0A1D2F4916.quest_desc: [
		"Back in the &cNether&r (you opened the portal in &6Kitted Out&r), look for a &6Better Nether Fortress&r: a huge complex of bridges, lava halls and a central keep. Some pieces are even built with &6Create&r parts."
		""
		"Blazes, &cwither skeletons&r and magma cubes spawn inside its walls. The chests in the quarters, worship rooms and storerooms can hold &ediamonds&r, the keep has saddles and horse armour, and item frames may hold more loot."
		""
		"&7Fortresses never generate right next to a bastion.&r"
	]
	quest.7A426D0A1D2F4916.quest_subtitle: "Now with more bridges to fall off"
	quest.7A426D0A1D2F4916.title: "&cA Better Terrible Fortress"
	quest.7A4EBF0D8803024D.quest_desc: [
		"Three pool infusions turn a &eWillow Sapling&r into a working flower. &aLink each to a pool&r: it draws Fluxia only when it does something."
		"&dVerdant Bloom&r (&eBone Block&r + &eMoss Block&r, &b6,000 ƒ&r): bonemeals one growable block within 5 blocks every 2 seconds."
		"&dGathering Bloom&r (&eHopper&r + &eEnder Pearl&r, &b6,000 ƒ&r): pulls loose items within 6 blocks into the inventory below it."
		"&dWarding Bloom&r (&eGolden Apple&r + &eWither Rose&r, &b8,000 ƒ&r): removes freshly spawned hostiles within 12 blocks."
		""
		"&7The Verdant Bloom works on anything bonemeal works on, other mods' crops included.&r"
	]
	quest.7A4EBF0D8803024D.quest_subtitle: "Functional blooms"
	quest.7A4EBF0D8803024D.title: "&aFlowers That Spend"
	quest.7AE7CB08AF8EC092.quest_desc: [
		"Craft an &6Arcane Core&r and an &6Enchanting Apparatus&r, then &aplace the Apparatus on top of the Core&r."
		""
		"Put ingredients on &6Arcane Pedestals&r &bwithin 3 blocks&r, then right-click the Apparatus with the centre item. Some recipes also draw Source from nearby jars."
		""
		"It can also &dadd or raise enchantments&r on your gear with Source and items, one level at a time. That includes Ars' own &dMana Boost&r, &dMana Regen&r and &dReactive&r enchantments."
	]
	quest.7AE7CB08AF8EC092.quest_subtitle: "The heart of every Ars workshop"
	quest.7AE7CB08AF8EC092.title: "&6Some Assembly Required"
	quest.7B02F19A38BD4F78.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Hellshelf&r is a Bookshelf in Nether Bricks with a &eBlaze Rod&r and a &ePotion of Regeneration&r. Each gives &b3 Eterna&r (up to 45) and &b+3% Quanta&r."
		""
		"15 bookshelves plus 5 Hellshelves is exactly &b45 Eterna and 30% Quanta&r: the recipe for an &dInfused Hellshelf&r. You'll need &6Frontier&r active for that."
		""
		"&7Pick fire, water or both. Either path leads on.&r"
	]
	quest.7B02F19A38BD4F78.quest_subtitle: "Hellshelves bring Quanta"
	quest.7B02F19A38BD4F78.title: "&cThe Path of Fire"
	quest.7B2DB39A23BBA494.quest_desc: [
		"The &eAncient Codex&r is the top crafted book: a &eNetherite Ingot&r, a &eRuined Book&r, &e2 Blood Vials&r, a &eBottle o' Lightning&r and &e4 Arcane Cloth&r. &b12 slots&r and &b+200 mana&r."
		""
		"&eRuined Books&r come from Ancient City chests, and later from the Citadel's bookshelves. For the bottle, &aright-click a charged creeper&r with an empty glass bottle."
		""
		"&7Ruined Books also start the Dragonskin, Frostbranded and Vampiric books. Each one boosts a single school instead.&r"
	]
	quest.7B2DB39A23BBA494.quest_subtitle: "12 slots, +20% cooldown reduction"
	quest.7B2DB39A23BBA494.title: "&6Ancient Knowledge"
	quest.7B306876E5B8E7D6.quest_desc: [
		"&6Villages and Pillages&r adds the &6Witch Village&r: a cluster of mossy witch houses on oak stilts just above the water, linked by spruce boardwalks. Some of the boards have rotted away, so watch your step."
		""
		"It only grows in &bswamps and mangrove swamps&r, and it needs a big, fairly flat one, so small swamps rarely have one. Point a &eNature's Compass&r at the nearest swamp and look for rooftops."
		""
		"&cThe residents are hostile.&r Witches stand guard at the village centre and the boardwalk crossings, and every house has its own witch and a cat."
	]
	quest.7B306876E5B8E7D6.quest_subtitle: "Population: witches, cats and a few unlucky neighbours"
	quest.7B306876E5B8E7D6.title: "&2Coven Town"
	quest.7B44DDA02F1F9A03.quest_desc: [
		"&6Modern Foundry&r is a port of &6Tinkers' Construct&r. You build tools from &eparts&r, and the &ematerial&r of each part sets its stats and gives it a &btrait&r. Then you upgrade the tool with &bmodifiers&r."
		""
		"You spawned with &eMaterials and You&r, the first of the mod's guide books. If you lost it, craft a &eBook&r with a &ePattern&r. Five more books unlock as you go, and this chapter tells you how to get each one."
		""
		"&cDon't count on EMI for melting, casting or alloying.&r This port only ships a JEI plugin, so these quests spell those steps out in words. &7Tip: put your books on a lectern next to your workbench.&r"
	]
	quest.7B44DDA02F1F9A03.quest_subtitle: "Tinkers' Construct, under a new name"
	quest.7B44DDA02F1F9A03.title: "&6Materials and You"
	quest.7B96CF8EB905A86A.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Redstone Link&r sends a redstone signal without wires, up to &b256 blocks&r. Craft a &eTransmitter&r (Lightning Rod, Copper Sheets, Redstone), then put it over Andesite Casing for two links."
		""
		"Put the same two items in the slots of both links to pair them. &bSneak-right-click with an empty hand&r to switch a link between sending and receiving."
	]
	quest.7B96CF8EB905A86A.quest_subtitle: "Redstone, minus the dust"
	quest.7B96CF8EB905A86A.title: "&cWireless Wizardry"
	quest.7BAFF02974C418B2.quest_desc: [
		"Night comes fast. Wall yourself in, light the place with &etorches&r and craft a &6Chest&r for your stuff."
		""
		"A &6Bed&r (three &ewool&r on three &eplanks&r) sets your &brespawn point&r, and the night is skipped once enough players on the server are asleep. Sleep in it once to finish this quest."
		""
		"&7Sheep are the easy source of wool. Shears get you more per sheep.&r"
	]
	quest.7BAFF02974C418B2.quest_subtitle: "Monsters hate this one simple trick"
	quest.7BAFF02974C418B2.title: "&eNight Shift"
	quest.7BB47BCDD39ACC83.quest_desc: [
		"&6Create: Ultimate Factory&r has no items. It adds dozens of Create recipes that make hard-to-get resources renewable. A few favourites:"
		""
		"Compact &eGravel&r with Bone Meal for &eCalcite&r, or compact Stone with a little Lava for &eDeepslate&r. Haunt a &ePoppy&r (fan through soul fire) for a &eWither Rose&r. Mix Netherrack, Flint and Lava into &eRedstone&r."
		""
		"&7Crushing End Stone gives End Stone Powder and sometimes Ender Pearls.&r"
	]
	quest.7BB47BCDD39ACC83.quest_subtitle: "Create: Ultimate Factory"
	quest.7BB47BCDD39ACC83.title: "&eRock Alchemy"
	quest.7BBE3094DD7EB137.quest_desc: [
		"&6Create&r is a tech mod with no batteries and no FE. Everything runs on &brotation&r: shafts spin, presses stamp, fans blow, belts carry, and whole buildings can move."
		""
		"Its manual is &6Ponder&r. Hover over any Create item in your inventory or in EMI and &bhold W&r to watch an animated scene of it working. Tooltips also have a summary when you hold &bShift&r."
		""
		"&cEMI doesn't show Create's machine recipes in this pack&r (pressing, mixing, fan processing, casings and the rest; there is no Create plugin for it). EMI still shows Create's crafting-table recipes, and these quests describe every machine step in words."
		""
		"This chapter takes you from your first shaft to your first &eBrass Ingot&r."
		""
		"&7Carry On can't pick up Create blocks. The Wrench, a few quests in, can.&r"
	]
	quest.7BBE3094DD7EB137.quest_subtitle: "Here be contraptions"
	quest.7BBE3094DD7EB137.title: "&6Welcome to Create"
	quest.7BD46D8912683BD7.quest_desc: [
		"Shipwrecks, buried treasure and other &bocean, beach or river&r chests favour two relics. The &eJellyfish Necklace&r gives extra health and regeneration &ain water or rain&r, and charges &delectric arcs&r that zap whatever you touch."
		""
		"Its partner is the &eCut Glass Boot&r: hold it as a bucket for several fluids, then wear it to &awalk on the fluids stored inside&r."
	]
	quest.7BD46D8912683BD7.quest_subtitle: "Ocean chests, necklace slot"
	quest.7BD46D8912683BD7.title: "&3Shocking Jewellery"
	quest.7BE80CE3D7617D3B.quest_desc: [
		"&6Sophisticated Storage&r chests and barrels start small but can be &atier-upgraded&r and take &aupgrades&r, keeping their contents."
		""
		"Craft a chest from &e8 Planks&r around a &eLever&r (or a vanilla chest plus a lever). Barrels use planks, slabs and a lever."
		""
		"&7Full vanilla chest already? Craft a &eBasic Tier Upgrade&7 (sticks and a lever) and right-click the chest to convert it in place.&r"
	]
	quest.7BE80CE3D7617D3B.quest_subtitle: "A chest with ambition"
	quest.7BE80CE3D7617D3B.title: "&6A Sophisticated Chest"
	quest.7BEB531889B2A460.quest_desc: [
		"&6Ars Creo&r connects Ars to &6Create&r. The &6Starbuncle Wheel&r (a Starbuncle Charm + a Create Water Wheel) is a generator with a Starbuncle running inside. It turns at &b16 RPM&r, or &b24 RPM&r with a &eBlock of Gold&r in front of it, and &auses no Source&r. Check its stress capacity with Goggles."
		""
		"Ars Creo also lets &6Spell Turrets&r and &6Source Jars&r work on moving contraptions, lets a Display Link read a jar's Source, and lets potions flow through Create pipes. &7See the Create chapters for the basics.&r"
	]
	quest.7BEB531889B2A460.quest_subtitle: "Spin, little buddy, spin"
	quest.7BEB531889B2A460.title: "&6Ars Creo&r: Hamster Power"
	quest.7C5181B81F1E1BB4.quest_desc: [
		"&6Boars&r in forests, taigas and savannas root around in the dirt and turn up &eTruffles&r. &eHollow Caches&r (squirrel stashes in old tree stumps) hide them too."
		""
		"&aTruffling:&r craft a Truffle with &bany food&r that isn't truffled yet to refine it: &b+20% hunger and saturation&r. EMI doesn't show this recipe well, but it works with nearly anything edible."
		""
		"&79 Truffles pack into a Truffle Bag.&r"
	]
	quest.7C5181B81F1E1BB4.quest_subtitle: "Follow the snout"
	quest.7C5181B81F1E1BB4.title: "&6Truffle Shuffle"
	quest.7C53A14073BFF530.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Mechanical Press&r is a Shaft over Andesite Casing over a &eBlock of Iron&r. Put a &6Depot&r (Andesite Alloy plus Casing) &btwo blocks below it&r, with one air gap, and drop an ingot on the depot."
		""
		"It stamps &eIron&r, &eGold&r and &eCopper Ingots&r into &eSheets&r, and sheets go into the Wrench, Goggles, Fans, Mixers, Chutes and Super Glue."
		""
		"It costs &b8 SU per RPM&r, so a Hand Crank at 32 RPM runs exactly one press."
	]
	quest.7C53A14073BFF530.quest_subtitle: "The machine that unlocks the others"
	quest.7C53A14073BFF530.title: "&6Bonk!"
	quest.7C629E4610BD335F.quest_desc: [
		"A &6Chute&r (planks and sticks) takes items from a hopper or dropper and &adrops them straight down&r into the open air below it."
		""
		"It only works with &bempty space underneath&r: a block below or a &bredstone signal&r stops it. Use it to drop items onto a water stream, a Create belt, or a hopper a block or two lower."
	]
	quest.7C629E4610BD335F.quest_subtitle: "Straight down, no detours"
	quest.7C629E4610BD335F.title: "&6Down the Chute"
	quest.7C83562EF3EE71E2.quest_desc: [
		"&eEnergy Pipes&r (iron, redstone, redstone block) carry &bFE&r from your generator furnace to whatever needs it."
		""
		"Set the furnace side touching the pipe to &bOutput&r, and wrench that pipe end to extract. A bare pipe moves &b256 FE/t&r; upgrades take it far higher."
	]
	quest.7C83562EF3EE71E2.title: "&cPower Lines"
	quest.7CA0EA0B909D9B33.quest_desc: [
		"Put a magic armor piece in the &6Enchanting Apparatus&r centre with &e2 Blaze Rods&r on pedestals and &b2500 Source&r nearby to raise it to &dTier 2&r."
		""
		"Each tier adds a thread slot to every piece and raises some slot levels. At Tier 2, &6Sorceror's&r and &6Arcanist's&r robes and leggings already get a &blevel 3&r slot. &aSorceror's pieces end up with the best slots.&r"
	]
	quest.7CA0EA0B909D9B33.title: "&dUpgraded Threads"
	quest.7CBEE715428EA777.quest_desc: [
		"The green machine. The &6Accelerated Planter&r is &e4 Green gems&r, dirt, Kivi, a &eWater Bucket&r and a &6Machine Base&r."
		""
		"It's a soil block: plant straight onto its face and it &aspeeds up the growth&r of wheat, potatoes, beetroot, sugar cane, cactus, bamboo, nether wart and more. Planters lined up in a row behind it &badd to the boost&r, up to &b16&r in a line."
	]
	quest.7CBEE715428EA777.quest_subtitle: "Grow, grow, grow your crops"
	quest.7CBEE715428EA777.title: "&aGreen Thumb"
	quest.7D02D2952021BED8.quest_desc: [
		"Level &b18&r is the cap, and all three limits have to reach it:"
		"&b- Size:&r 72 tank blocks, for example a 3x3 base, 8 tall."
		"&b- Heat:&r 9 Blaze Burners under the 3x3 base, all &csuperheated&r."
		"&b- Water:&r 180 mB/tick. A single pump at full speed falls short, so &arun two pumps facing the same way&r."
		""
		"Hang &b18 Steam Engines&r on it for a whopping &b294,912 SU&r. A &6Mechanical Arm&r handing out cakes keeps the whole thing running hands-free."
	]
	quest.7D02D2952021BED8.quest_subtitle: "Boiler level 18"
	quest.7D02D2952021BED8.title: "&6Full Steam Ahead"
	quest.7D6D90CDE5BDD133.quest_desc: [
		"Time to prove you rule the skies. First, &achristen your ship&r: place a &eNameplate&r on your assembled contraption and right-click it to write a name."
		""
		"Then fly up to &bcloud height&r in the Overworld (&bY 192-196&r) and toss any &emusic disc&r overboard. After a few seconds it turns into something new and &bfloats&r in the clouds, so you'll have to fly to catch it."
		""
		"Lift and thrust are weaker up there: bring plenty of balloon."
		""
		"&7Congratulations, Captain. The sky is no longer the limit.&r"
	]
	quest.7D6D90CDE5BDD133.quest_subtitle: "Every ship needs a name and a theme tune"
	quest.7D6D90CDE5BDD133.title: "&6Captain of the Clouds"
	quest.7D706AA1BD273D41.quest_desc: [
		"Point a &6Mechanical Arm&r at a &6Blaze Burner&r as an output and give it fuel to take from: it keeps the burner fed for you. &aOne arm can tend a whole row of burners&r under a boiler or a line of basins."
		""
		"&7Later, let it hand out Blaze Cakes for superheat without lifting a finger.&r"
	]
	quest.7D706AA1BD273D41.quest_subtitle: "Self-serve barbecue"
	quest.7D706AA1BD273D41.title: "&cFeeding Time"
	quest.7DC3368D01C65289.quest_desc: [
		"An &eElectron Tube&r, &eBrass Casing&r and a &eCrafting Table&r in a column make &b3&r &6Mechanical Crafters&r. Place them as a grid facing you and give them rotation."
		""
		"Use a &6Wrench&r to point each crafter's &barrow&r: every path must lead to one exit, where the result pops out. Fill the slots (right-click the front, or use funnels and arms) and crafting starts when all are full. Half-empty recipes need a &bredstone pulse&r, and &eCrafter Slot Covers&r mark a crafter as a deliberate blank."
		""
		"&7Crafters also do any normal crafting recipe, and gadgets like the Extendo Grip, Potato Cannon and Wand of Symmetry are made here.&r"
	]
	quest.7DC3368D01C65289.quest_subtitle: "A crafting table that scales"
	quest.7DC3368D01C65289.title: "&6Table for Nine"
	quest.7E30D793F1492007.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Machine Base&r is &e2 Aluminum Ingots&r and &e2 Kivi&r in a 2x2 checkerboard, which makes two."
		""
		"Every colour machine, the &6Valve&r, the &6Item IO&r and the &6Fabricator&r is built around one. &aKeep a few spare&r, you'll go through them quickly."
	]
	quest.7E30D793F1492007.quest_subtitle: "Every machine starts here"
	quest.7E30D793F1492007.title: "&6Base Camp"
	quest.7ED10F403A3DA98F.quest_desc: [
		"&cTyros&r is an echo of an ancient flamebearer, and a far tougher fight than the Dead King. Stock elixirs, wear your best upgraded robes and bring friends."
		""
		"He drops a &dDivine Soulshard&r, plenty of Cinder Essence, and sometimes a Decrepit Scythe or the Signet of the Betrayer. Each fighter gets a &eDecrepit Key&r for a Cinderous Vault, which always holds a &ePyrium Ingot&r."
		""
		"&aWhat's next:&r Pyrium and Soulshards go into the &ePyrium Staff&r, the &eInfernal Sorcerer&r and &eLightbringer&r chestplates and &eBoots of Speed&r. Spellbound indeed."
	]
	quest.7ED10F403A3DA98F.quest_subtitle: "Echo of Tyros, First Flamebearer"
	quest.7ED10F403A3DA98F.title: "&6The Flame Still Burns"
	quest.7EF964D43E8523A7.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Augmenting Table&r (Enchanting Table, &eNether Star&r, 2 Godforged Pearls) works on one affix at a time. &aUpgrade&r it for 2 &dSigils of Enhancement&r and &b225 levels&r, or &areroll&r it for 1 sigil and &b175 levels&r."
		""
		"It's meant for Mythic gear you plan to keep forever."
		""
		"&7Feeling lucky? A &dSigil of Malice&r&7 (invader drop) pushes one random affix to 200% and drops another to 0%.&r"
	]
	quest.7EF964D43E8523A7.quest_subtitle: "Augmenting"
	quest.7EF964D43E8523A7.title: "&6Fine-Tuning Fate"
	quest.7F035CB93ED62C45.quest_desc: [
		"&eFlax&r is this mod's starter crop and the root of the whole chapter. You need &eFlax Seeds&r first:"
		"&a- &rbreak &6Wild Flax&r, a rare plant that grows on &bsand right beside water&r: beaches, sandy riverbanks, desert pools"
		"&a- &rsmash &6Cave Urns&r underground, or loot dungeon and mineshaft chests"
		"&a- &rbuy them from the &eWandering Trader&r"
		""
		"Plant the seeds on farmland. Flax grows into a &btwo-block-tall&r crop, so leave headroom above it."
		""
		"&7Flax makes Rope, Sacks, Doormats, Awnings and String. Pack 9 into a Flax Bale for storage.&r"
	]
	quest.7F035CB93ED62C45.quest_subtitle: "The humble crop that ties it all together"
	quest.7F035CB93ED62C45.title: "&aFlax to the Max"
	quest.7F27CC30605D7A39.quest_desc: [
		"A big pack means lots of mods fighting over the same keys. Out of the box, &bM&r, &bB&r, &bU&r, &bN&r, &bG&r, &bV&r, &bC&r and &bZ&r each do two or more things at once."
		""
		"&6Studious Keybinds&r gives &bControls&r a visual keyboard: &cred&r keys are shared, green are fine. &aRebind the clashes you care about&r before they ambush you mid-fight."
		""
		"&7Top offenders: B opens your backpack and makes a waypoint, U opens Death History and the waypoint list.&r"
	]
	quest.7F27CC30605D7A39.quest_subtitle: "M, B and U walk into a bar"
	quest.7F27CC30605D7A39.title: "&bToo Many Keys"
	quest.7F4056A3379CBA45.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Dominion Wand&r (Stick on the Apparatus with 2 Source Gems and a Gold Ingot) is Ars' wrench. &aClick the source, then the target&r to link things: relays, creatures, lecterns. &bSneak-click&r clears it."
		""
		"You'll use it constantly from here on, especially to put magical creatures to work."
	]
	quest.7F4056A3379CBA45.title: "&6Wand of Command"
	quest.7F54042EC49FE7B1.quest_desc: [
		"&6Create: Enchantable Machinery&r lets you enchant machines like tools, at an &6Enchanting Table&r or &6Anvil&r: Drill, Saw, Harvester, Plough, Encased Fan, Millstone, Crushing Wheel, Press, Mixer, Roller and Spout."
		""
		"&bEfficiency&r speeds up every one of them. The Drill, Saw, Harvester and Plough also take mining enchantments like &bFortune&r and &bSilk Touch&r: a Harvester with Fortune reaps more crops, and a Saw's enchantments apply to the trees it fells."
		""
		"&7Engineer's Goggles show a placed machine's enchantments.&r"
	]
	quest.7F54042EC49FE7B1.quest_subtitle: "Create: Enchantable Machinery"
	quest.7F54042EC49FE7B1.title: "&dFortune Favours the Drill"
	quest.7F54D42F93FC8897.quest_desc: [
		"The &dVigil of the Open Way&r (tier IV) opens a gate above your altar: &b25,000 ƒ&r up front, then &b30 ƒ/s&r for 30 minutes. &cThat's more than a bare 20,000 ƒ reserve&r, so lay at least 3 Water Runes or bind a Wisp familiar first."
		""
		"When the vigil ends you're put back where you stepped through, and a return gate stands next to where you land if you want to leave early. Tamed pets near you come along (sitting ones stay), familiars never do."
		""
		"Shear &6Glimmerfawn&r for &eSpirit Down&r and weave it into &eGlimmerweave&r cloth armor. &aBring Moonlilies from the fen&r: they tame and breed the fawns and regrow a shorn coat at once, and none grow in the realm. &7Soulwood has no sapling.&r"
	]
	quest.7F54D42F93FC8897.quest_subtitle: "The Spirit Realm"
	quest.7F54D42F93FC8897.title: "&bThe Open Way"
	quest.7F719B573EFC8D38.quest_desc: [
		"Everything comes together: a &b6+ carriage&r train with a conductor and a schedule, running on a &6signalled&r network, with a &6Display Board&r at the station counting down to its arrival."
		""
		"Each carriage is its own glued structure on one or two bogeys; line them up on the station track and assemble them together. Fuel it, seat a driver, and let it haul your ore, your packages or your friends."
		""
		"&7Your trains also show up on Xaero's World Map (M). Congratulations, engineer: the Brass Age is yours.&r"
	]
	quest.7F719B573EFC8D38.quest_subtitle: "Mind the doors, please"
	quest.7F719B573EFC8D38.title: "&6Grand Central"
	quest.7FE056D6BBB0D0B3.quest_desc: [
		"&eFlippers&r make you swim &b70% faster&r. Big &6ocean ruins&r are the place to look: almost half their big chests have an artifact, and Flippers and the &eSnorkel&r are the most common picks. Buried treasure works too."
		""
		"&7Sea kit: the Snorkel gives 30 s of Water Breathing that refills at the surface, &eAqua-Dashers&7 let you sprint on water and the &eCharm of Sinking&7 lets you walk on the sea floor.&r"
	]
	quest.7FE056D6BBB0D0B3.quest_subtitle: "The ocean's best-kept secrets"
	quest.7FE056D6BBB0D0B3.title: "&3Fish Out of Water"
	quest.7FEBCEE826D2689F.quest_desc: [
		"Craft &e9 Dried Green Tea&r into a &6Dried Green Tea Leaf Block&r and place it to dry again. It darkens into a &6Black Tea Leaf Block&r, which breaks into &e2 Dried Black Tea&r."
		""
		"&cThat is a lot of leaves:&r one block (27 leaves) makes just 2 Dried Black Tea, so each costs about &b13.5 Green Tea Leaves&r. Now is a good time to grow a bigger tea field."
	]
	quest.7FEBCEE826D2689F.quest_subtitle: "Dry it twice"
	quest.7FEBCEE826D2689F.title: "&8Fade to Black"
